INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112710','A Hybrid Fast Gauss Transform algorithm for Doppler Broadening of neutron cross section at extremely high temperatures','초고온에서 중성자 단면적 도플러 확장을 위한 하이브리드 고속 가우스 변환 알고리즘','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112710','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112710',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112724','A neutron transport calculation method based on Monte Carlo–Deep learning–interface current coupling and its validation in assembly problems','몬테카를로–딥러닝–경계면 흐름 결합 기반 중성자 수송 계산 방법 및 집합체 문제 검증','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112724','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112724',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112738','CFD–DEM investigation of drag mapping and discharge-rate effects in the HTR-10 moving pebble bed','HTR-10 이동 페블베드에서 항력 매핑 및 배출 속도 영향에 대한 CFD–DEM 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112738','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112738',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;AU','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112741','Chaotic characteristics and state classification of pressure fluctuations in phase-change condensation water hammer','상변화 응축 수격현상에서 압력 변동의 혼돈 특성 및 상태 분류','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112741','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112741',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112723','Cross-domain generalization for nuclear power plant classification using large language models','대규모 언어모델을 이용한 원자력발전소 분류의 교차 도메인 일반화','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112723','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112723',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;US','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112703','Research on the efficient and lightweight surrogate model for Probabilistic Safety Margin analysis of SBLOCA in nuclear power plants integrating DL-TL','DL-TL을 통합한 원자력발전소 SBLOCA 확률론적 안전여유도 해석용 고효율 경량 대리모델 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112703','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112703',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112742','Validation and reliability analysis of CFD-based atmospheric dispersion modeling against wind tunnel experiments at a nuclear power plant site with irregular buildings and complex terrain','불규칙 건물 및 복잡 지형을 갖는 원자력발전소 부지에서 풍동실험 대비 CFD 기반 대기확산 모델링의 검증 및 신뢰성 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112742','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112742',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115158','Multiobjective optimization methodology for the design of a 10-kW-class space nuclear fission power system','10 kW급 우주 원자력 핵분열 전력계통 설계를 위한 다목적 최적화 방법론','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115158','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115158',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','FR','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115154','Seismic analysis of TMSR graphite core with viscous damping','점성감쇠를 고려한 TMSR 흑연 노심의 지진 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115154','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115154',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104656','Is grid-based intraoperative electron radiotherapy (IOERT) a potential solution for surface dose enhancement in breast cancer treatment?','격자 기반 수술 중 전자선 방사선치료(IOERT)는 유방암 치료에서 표면선량 증가를 위한 잠재적 해법인가?','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','Surface under-dosage is a challenge during breast intraoperative electron radiotherapy, especially at low energies (below 10 MeV). Current study tries to overcome this limitation by adding a grid to distal end of the employed electron applicator and producing a mixed electron-photon field. LIAC12 head, a dedicated IOERT Linac, along with attached applicator were simulated by MCNPX code. Then, a dedicated grid with fill factor of 0.1 was attached to distal end of applicator. Finally, PDD curves, TDPs and isodose curves were calculated in presence and absence of the grid. Inserting the grid improves surface dose at low electron energies (6 and 8 MeV), while it is not efficient at higher energies (10 and 12 MeV). Field symmetry and flatness were within recommended criteria at 6 and 8 MeV electron energies, while were not satisfied at higher energies. Isodose curves were affected within target superficial parts in grid presence. Adding the grid to distal end of IOERT applicator is efficient in surface dose enhancement and dose uniformity improvement at low electron energies (less than 10 MeV). In return, it doesn’t considerably increase surface dose at higher electron energies. Hence, the introduced method is only suitable, viable and effective for low energies.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104656','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104656',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104650','Optimization of a BWR bundle performance for reactor-grade plutonium and minor actinides recycling','원자로급 플루토늄 및 부악티늄 재활용을 위한 BWR 핵연료다발 성능 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study investigates the feasibility of recycling reactor-grade plutonium and minor actinides (MAs) in a boiling water reactor (BWR) using modified mixed-oxide (MOX) fuel compositions as an alternative to conventional burnable absorber rods. Six fuel compositions are proposed, requiring minimal modifications to the standard BWR fuel bundle design. Neutronic analyses were performed using the Serpent Monte Carlo code in conjunction with the ENDF/B-VII.0 nuclear data library. The analyses demonstrated that all proposed MOX configurations are capable of sustaining criticality over extended irradiation periods while delivering an energy output comparable to that of reference UOX fuel. The required 235 U enrichment per assembly is reduced from 3.67 wt.% in the UOX case to approximately 3.16 wt.% for most MOX configurations. Effective transmutation performance is achieved, with up to 86% of the initial MAs inventory and 32.2% of the initial plutonium inventory consumed over the fuel cycle. Key safety-related reactivity coefficients, including the fuel temperature coefficient, moderator temperature coefficient, void reactivity worth at 40% and 70% void fractions, and control rod worth, remain negative on average, indicating acceptable reactivity feedback and stable reactor behavior. These results confirm that the proposed MOX fuel concepts provide a viable and safe option for plutonium and minor actinide recycling in BWRs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104650','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104650',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','EG;RU','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712744','Financing Nuclear Decommissioning in Ghana: An Evaluation of Public-Private Partnership Models','가나의 원자력시설 해체 재원 조달: 민관협력 모델 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This review looks at how Ghana can use public-private partnership (PPP) models to obtain long-term funding for the decommissioning of its current research reactor and upcoming nuclear installations. Ghana’s current legal framework would benefit from strengthened institutional capacity, clearer financial assurance procedures, and the establishment of dedicated decommissioning funds.This review uses a comparative legal institutional analysis alongside international best practices from other countries and lessons learned from Ghanaian industries. The paper outlines a phased set of policy recommendations by identifying the technical, financial, regulatory, and sociopolitical risks associated with nuclear decommissioning. These recommendations include the creation of a national coordinating institution, long-term capacity building initiatives, and legal reforms to integrate decommissioning finance within nuclear safety regulations.The results demonstrate that well thought out PPP mechanisms can improve safety performance, lower uncertainty, and bring Ghana’s nuclear program into line with global best practices. These mechanisms are bolstered by transparent fund governance, robust regulatory oversight, and innovation-driven contracting.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712744','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712744',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','GH;PK','GH','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106546','Divergent and moderating determinants of social and local acceptance of high-level radioactive waste facilities: The role of nuclear power risk perceptions','고준위방사성폐기물 시설의 사회적·지역적 수용성의 상이한 결정요인 및 조절요인: 원자력 위험인식의 역할','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106546','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106546',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/s0149-1970(26)00329-x','Editorial Board','편집위원회','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-12','','','편집물','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0149-1970(26)00329-x','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0149-1970(26)00329-x',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106536','Sensitivity analysis of fast neutron flux calculations for the RPV extended beltline region','원자로압력용기 확장 벨트라인 영역 고속중성자속 계산의 민감도 분석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106536','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106536',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106555','Site selection procedure in Germany: Considerations on a depth limit for a high-level radioactive waste repository in claystone','독일의 부지선정 절차: 점토암 내 고준위방사성폐기물 처분장의 심도 한계에 대한 고찰','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-12','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The depth of a repository for high-level radioactive waste is an important aspect with respect to both long-term and operational safety. In contrast to the minimum depth, no relevant constraints are given in the German legal regulations for a maximum value. To define such a limit, various safety-related aspects of claystone host rock are considered. This evaluation takes place within an early stage of the German site selection process. The available data are evaluated, and the respective assessments are discussed, ranging from aspects of construction and operation of the repository to its post-closure period. Furthermore, tunneling experience in relevant claystones is evaluated. It is concluded that a favorable depth is neither the maximum depth of existing underground excavations nor the maximum achievable with available techniques. Instead, it is the depth for which experience indicates that under the current assumptions, the extended operation of a nuclear waste repository can be well conducted without jeopardizing operational and long-term safety. The major argument for limiting the repository depth is robustness, which means that the repository as a whole can be operated safely, requires no extraordinary measures like resources, techniques, or time, and can be built with well-established techniques. It can be summarized that those requirements are unlikely to be met for a repository in claystone at depths greater than 1000 m.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106555','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106555',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','DE','DE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112735','Analysis of the proliferation resistance of re-enriched reprocessed uranium on multiple recycling in nuclear reactors','원자로 내 다중 재활용 시 재농축 재처리우라늄의 핵확산저항성 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The intrinsic features of spent nuclear fuel (SNF) could enhance the proliferation resistance (PR) of plutonium (Pu) to minimize proliferation risk. One key intrinsic PR feature is the presence of the isotope 238 Pu in Pu. Increased 238 Pu content helps minimize proliferation risk owing to its high spontaneous fission neutron (SFN) emission rate and decay heat (DH). This study focused on the PR assessment of reprocessed uranium (RepU) that is recycled multiple times as fuel in nuclear reactors. The growth of the uranium (U) isotope, 236 U, in SNF and its co-enrichment while re-enriching RepU resulted in the enhanced production of 238 Pu supporting the intrinsic PR of Pu. In addition to enhancing the intrinsic PR of Pu, the presence of 236 U in SNF denatures U, which enables the minimization of the proliferation risk of U to a large extent because it limits the 235 U enrichment.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112735','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112735',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112727','Central-Difference method based on consistent Half-Node linear approximation for the neutron diffusion equation','중성자 확산방정식을 위한 일관된 반노드 선형근사 기반 중심차분법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112727','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112727',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112688','Design and analysis of secondary-side passive residual heat removal system to enhance inherent safety of lead-bismuth fast reactor STELLAR-EX','납-비스무트 고속로 STELLAR-EX의 고유안전성 향상을 위한 2차측 피동잔열제거계통 설계 및 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112688','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112688',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112734','Development of a benchmark experimental method for large angle scattering cross section of 14 MeV neutrons using compound targets – Application to fluorine benchmarking using PTFE','복합 표적을 이용한 14 MeV 중성자 대각도 산란 단면적 벤치마크 실험법 개발 – PTFE를 이용한 불소 벤치마킹 적용','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','In fusion reactors, large angle neutron scattering reactions significantly affect neutronics calculations, especially for the reactor blanket. Previous studies highlighted discrepancies in evaluated nuclear data, emphasizing the necessity for benchmarking large angle scattering cross sections. While the authors’ group previously developed a benchmark experimental system using the foil activation method, gaseous elements like fluorine could not be validated. This study introduces a new method that uses solid compounds containing the gaseous element to indirectly evaluate its large angle scattering cross section. Applying this method, benchmark experiments for fluorine were performed using graphite and polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) as the targets, and the fluorine contribution was extracted. The results were then compared with MCNP5 simulations using different nuclear data libraries and an excellent agreement was observed for ENDF/B-VIII.0 and JEFF-3.3. Future work will aim to reduce experimental uncertainties.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112734','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112734',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112698','Effect of burnup-dependent gap conductance on fuel–clad mechanical interaction and PCI risk during transient power excursions','과도 출력 급상승 시 연소도 의존 간극 열전도도가 핵연료-피복관 기계적 상호작용 및 PCI 위험에 미치는 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112698','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112698',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112739','Multiresolution Photon Dose Reconstruction using FLUKA and Resolution-Adaptive Physics-Informed Neural Networks','FLUKA와 해상도 적응형 물리정보신경망을 이용한 다중해상도 광자 선량 재구성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','AI·디지털','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112739','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112739',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112678','Numerical investigation on flow instability in casing once-through steam generators based on subchannel method','부수로 방법 기반 케이싱형 관류식 증기발생기의 유동 불안정성 수치해석 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112678','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112678',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112732','Seismic fragility analysis of multi-line transmission structure based on gas-insulated switchgear (GIS) equipment for nuclear power applications','원자력 적용을 위한 가스절연개폐장치(GIS) 기반 다회선 송전구조물의 지진 취약도 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The stable transmission of nuclear-generated electricity is vital for grid reliability and reactor external power supply. This study addresses this critical need by developing Finite Element Models (FEMs) of Gas-Insulated Switchgear (GIS) and a representative multi-line transmission structure to rigorously assess their seismic vulnerability through dynamic analysis and response evaluation. Based on the practical configurations of key substations system-level seismic fragility curves are constructed by integrating the failure probabilities of individual lines. The results indicate that, under identical structural dimensions, tapered bushings demonstrate superior seismic performance compared to uniform-section bushings. Furthermore, the maximum stress at spherical pipe joints is approximately three times that at right-angle joints, highlighting a critical structural vulnerability. Crucially, while a single transmission line is prone to failure under a given seismic excitation, increasing the number of parallel lines significantly enhances the seismic resilience and operational stability of the overall transmission system.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112732','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112732',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115161','CFD analysis of thermal mixing and stratification phenomena in a tee with a blind-end branch using URANS approach','URANS 접근법을 이용한 막힌 분기관 T자관의 열혼합 및 성층화 현상 CFD 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115161','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115161',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115162','Direct numerical simulation of thermal mixing in a T-junction with conjugate heat transfer in the solid walls','고체 벽 공액열전달을 고려한 T자 접합부 열혼합의 직접수치모사','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115162','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115162',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','NL;US','NL','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104654','Modeling and decoupler design for the OTSG feedwater control system of small modular reactors','소형모듈원자로 OTSG 급수제어계통의 모델링 및 비연성화기 설계','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104654','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104654',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104653','Properties of single-mode optical fibers under high-dose gamma-ray irradiation','고선량 감마선 조사 하 단일모드 광섬유의 특성','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104653','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104653',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104644','Uncertainty analysis for nuclear design parameters of VHTR-350','VHTR-350 핵설계 변수의 불확실성 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104644','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104644',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106560','Application of artificial neural networks in the identification of nuclear power plant accident and transient','원자력발전소 사고 및 과도상태 식별에 대한 인공신경망 적용','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-11','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106560','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106560',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112706','A parametric review of saturated pool boiling heat transfer over vertical tubes and tube bundles for passive residual heat removal systems','피동잔열제거계통을 위한 수직관 및 관다발 포화 풀비등 열전달의 매개변수별 고찰','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-10','','','리뷰·관점','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112706','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112706',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112730','Method research on the neutronic simulations of the bowed fuel rods in nuclear reactors','원자로 내 휜 핵연료봉의 중성자 해석 모의 방법 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Fuel rod bowing is a phenomenon that can alter power distribution in nuclear reactors. Accurate representation of bowed fuel rods is therefore essential for neutronic analysis. In this work, a geometry-modeling method for bowed fuel rods is proposed for Monte Carlo neutronic simulations, coupled with a delta-tracking algorithm enabling particle transport. By leveraging the delta-tracking routine, which does not require handling surface crossings, we implement particle transport on the proposed model. Verification of the proposed method is performed through comparison with two state-of-the-art semi-discrete models. The results indicate that the proposed model provides accurate neutronic simulations for bowed fuel rods, while reducing the computational cost compared to semi-discrete models.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112730','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112730',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112729','Nuclide number density prediction in molten salt reactors using dynamic mode decomposition with fractional-power snapshot transformation','분수 거듭제곱 스냅샷 변환을 적용한 동적 모드 분해를 이용한 용융염원자로 핵종 수밀도 예측','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112729','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112729',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112721','Numerical investigation of the effects of various non-condensable gases on steam condensation outside a vertical tube','다양한 비응축성 기체가 수직관 외부 증기 응축에 미치는 영향 수치해석 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','Steam condensation in the presence of non-condensable gases (NCGs) is widely encountered in industrial thermal systems, including power plants, desalination units, and nuclear reactor containment cooling. NCGs severely impair condensation heat transfer performance by accumulating near the condensation surface and impeding steam diffusion to the interface. Crucially, the physical properties (e.g. density and diffusion coefficient) lead to pronounced differences in natural convective mass transfer features and interfacial diffusion transport behavior. To gain a comprehensive understanding of the effects of various types of NCGs on the condensation heat transfer, a modified diffusion boundary layer model (MDBLM) is established. Systematic numerical simulations were conducted to investigate the effects of six NCGs, namely helium (He), neon (Ne), air, argon (Ar), carbon dioxide (CO 2 ), and krypton (Kr), under natural convection, using steam as the reference condensable vapor and contrasting He (lightest) and Ne to Kr (progressively heavier) as representative NCGs. Results demonstrate that the molar mass of NCG fundamentally determines the flow characteristics: heavier NCG (Ne to Kr) induces intensive downward natural convection, while He induces upward reverse convection and gas stratification. For heavy NCGs, the condensation heat transfer coefficient (CHTC) is positively correlated with the molar mass of NCGs. This is mainly attributed to the gas sweeping the wall, which effectively reduces the accumulation of NCG at the interface. Specifically, comparing the cases from Ne to Kr, the maximum flow velocity experiences a 119.51% increase, driving a concurrent 72.27% enhancement in the CHTC. Investigations across various thermal conditions demonstrate that the fundamental trends governing the influence of thermal parameters on the CHTC are independent of the NCG species. Finally, this study identifies an alternating dominant mechanism between molecular diffusion and macroscopic convection during the condensation heat transfer process.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112721','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112721',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104651','Acquisition-specific motion deblurring in X-ray radiography using a dual-acquisition residual-domain framework','이중 획득 잔차 영역 프레임워크를 이용한 X선 투과영상의 획득 특화 동작 흐림 제거','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','Motion blur in X-ray radiography can obscure fine anatomical structures and lead to repeat imaging. This study presents a dual-acquisition residual-domain framework that combines a normal-dose motion-blurred image with an auxiliary low-dose fast-acquisition image for acquisition-specific blur-kernel estimation and restoration. The estimated kernel and residual-domain input are used for residual-domain Richardson–Lucy (RL) restoration, followed by gain-controlled restoration and detail recovery. The method was evaluated through simulation studies using line-pair and ex vivo human dental phantoms and controlled C-arm experiments using an anthropomorphic chest phantom. Across 20 repeated ROI-based evaluations, dental phantom SSIM increased from 0.87 ± 0.02 to 0.94 ± 0.02 and PSNR from 33.81 ± 0.22 to 35.70 ± 0.26 dB, with higher SSIM and PSNR than Wiener, non-blind RL, and total variation–regularized RL deconvolution. In C-arm experiments, BRISQUE decreased from 19.40 to 9.51 in the upper-spine case and from 31.03 to 19.98 in the lower-spine case, while SNR remained near normal-dose levels. CNR remained comparable to the normal-dose level in the upper-spine case and increased in the lower-spine case. The framework improved visibility under small-amplitude, approximately linear motion blur, although sequential acquisition introduces registration and additional-exposure considerations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104651','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104651',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR;US','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104648','Corrosion behavior of 304 stainless steel in pressurized water reactor primary water chemistry controlled by LiOH and KOH','LiOH 및 KOH로 제어된 가압경수로 1차계통 수화학 환경에서 304 스테인리스강의 부식 거동','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','This study evaluates the effect of LiOH and KOH as pH-control agents on the corrosion behavior of 304 stainless steel in simulated pressurized water reactor primary water chemistry. Corrosion tests were performed in LiOH–H 3 BO 3 and KOH–H 3 BO 3 solutions at 593 K, and the exposed specimens were characterized in terms of corrosion rate, oxide morphology, phase constitution, and surface chemical states. In addition, the wettability and electrochemical behavior of 304 stainless steel were evaluated by contact angle measurement and potentiodynamic polarization tests. 304 stainless steel showed a slightly higher initial corrosion rate in the LiOH–H 3 BO 3 solution than in the KOH–H 3 BO 3 solution. However, the difference between the two solutions became smaller with increasing exposure time. Duplex oxide layers consisting of Fe-rich oxide particles and a Cr-rich inner oxide layer were formed in both solutions. No clear difference was observed in the overall oxide characteristics after long-term exposure. These results indicate that the type of pH-control agent slightly affected the initial corrosion behavior of 304 stainless steel, whereas its influence on the long-term oxide layer characteristics was minor under the present conditions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104648','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104648',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104649','Diffusion of tritium in Li4SiO4 crystal: A first-principles study','Li4SiO4 결정 내 삼중수소 확산: 제1원리 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Li 4 SiO 4 is a promising solid-state tritium breeder material due to its high lithium density and low tritium retention. Under irradiation, lithium vacancies are the predominant defects formed, influencing tritium release behavior. This study systematically investigates tritium adsorption and diffusion in different lithium vacancy configurations within Li 4 SiO 4 using first-principles calculations. The investigation covers three stages: first, adsorption and migration characteristics within vacancies; second, adsorption sites and migration behaviors after escape; finally, diffusion coefficients for both processes. The results show maximum adsorption energies of -1.597 eV (within vacancies) and -1.638 eV (after escape). The minimum migration energy barriers within the three vacancy configurations are 0.231 eV, 0.129 eV, and 0.091 eV, with corresponding optimal escape barriers of 0.236 eV, 0.373 eV, and 0.766 eV. The optimal migration pathways were identified as T Ⅳ →T Ⅲ →O37, P Ⅴ →P Ⅲ →P Ⅱ →O19, and O Ⅴ →O Ⅳ →O30. At 900 K, diffusion coefficients are 1.63×10 -7 m 2 /s (within vacancies) and 2.96×10 -8 m 2 /s (escape), with the former being approximately one order of magnitude higher, indicating greater mobility within the vacancies. The results provide an atomistic understanding of the individual stages of tritium migration and can indirectly inform subsequent breeder material design and fabrication.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104649','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104649',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104647','Full-scale vibration fatigue testing of 316L butt-welded small-bore piping in nuclear power plants and equivalent structural stress S-N curve','원자력발전소 316L 맞대기 용접 소구경 배관의 실규모 진동 피로시험 및 등가구조응력 S-N 곡선','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료',': To establish direct experimental evidence for vibration fatigue assessment of 316L stainless-steel small-bore piping butt-welded joints in nuclear power plants, full-scale TIG/GTAW butt-weld specimens (Φ16 mm × 3 mm) were tested using an electrodynamic shaker resonance excitation system. A total of 39 specimens were subjected to uniaxial constant-amplitude vibration fatigue tests at six nominal stress levels (130–210 MPa) with approximately fully reversed loading (R ≈ −1) and first-mode resonance frequencies of 55–83 Hz. Digital image correlation (DIC) was employed to measure the weld-toe strain field, X-ray diffraction (XRD) was used to determine residual stresses, scanning electron microscopy (SEM) was performed for fracture-surface analysis, and equivalent structural stress (ESS) was calculated by extracting nodal forces from ANSYS. The influence mechanism of weld reinforcement height on local mechanical states and fatigue life was systematically investigated. Specimens were classified into three groups according to weld reinforcement height: high reinforcement (h ≥ 1.0 mm), medium reinforcement (0.5 mm < h < 1.0 mm), and low reinforcement (h ≤ 0.5 mm). SEM observations on one failed specimen tested at 210 MPa indicated that crack propagation accounted for only ∼0.8% of the total life, supporting the approximation that leak-detection life was initiation-dominated. DIC measurements yielded weld-toe stress concentration factors (SCFs) of 1.26–1.47, which increased monotonically with reinforcement height. XRD results showed that reducing reinforcement height generally corresponds to a larger magnitude of compressive residual stress on the outer surface. Finite-element calculations gave bending ratios r ranging from 0.453 to 0.508 (mean 0.475); the mean r values for the high-, medium-, and low-reinforcement groups were 0.498, 0.472, and 0.458, respectively, indicating that reinforcement height affects fatigue performance through three coupled pathways: SCF, the load mode at the control section, and residual stress. Based on ESS S–N regression using 30 failed specimens, the fitted parameters were m = 7.88, A = 25.91, S logN = 0.331, and R 2 = 0.618; the P97.7% engineering design-line intercept was A d = 25.25. A supplementary right-censored maximum-likelihood analysis showed that, at N f = 10 6 , the mean-line ΔS s increased by only 4.2% compared with the baseline result, indicating local stability of the fitted curve within the observed life range. Compared with the ASME VIII Div. 2 Annex 3.F master S–N curve, the two mean lines intersect at ΔS s ≈ 417.4 MPa and N f ≈ 1.80×10 5 . At N f = 10 6 and 10 7 , the present mean line is higher than the ASME mean line by 39.2% and 116.9%, respectively, suggesting that the ASME master curve is conservative in the medium-to-high-cycle vibration fatigue regime covered herein. The scenario-specific ESS S–N design line developed in this work provides direct experimental support for vibration fatigue evaluation of 316L small-bore piping butt-welded joints under comparable material compositions, pipe dimensions, and resonance-bending loading conditions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104647','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104647',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104646','Neutronic and depletion analysis of a 5 MWth heat pipe cooled reactor with TRISO fuel and fluoride salt using MCS','MCS를 이용한 TRISO 핵연료 및 불화염 적용 5 MWth 히트파이프 냉각 원자로의 중성자 및 연소 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study investigates the neutronic performance, depletion behavior, and safety characteristics of a 5 MWth Sejong TRISO-fueled molten salt filled heat pipe cooled reactor. It employs tristructural-isotropic (TRISO) uranium-oxycarbide fuel, LiF-BeF 2 (FLiBe) molten salt coolant, and a beryllium-oxide (BeO) reflector. The Monte Carlo code MCS is used for three-dimensional burnup analysis over a 5 year cycle. The core adopts a pebble bed with 21,600 TRISO-embedded pebbles and 665 sodium heat pipes, achieving passive heat removal and a thermal spectrum that enhances neutron economy and control drum effectiveness. Depletion under all-control-drums-out shows smooth reactivity decrease from k-eff starting at 1.06075 at beginning-of-cycle and reaching 1.01138 at end-of-cycle. This is accompanied by limited spectral hardening and flattened radial power distributions, indicating benign fuel utilization and power peaking. Parametric studies clarify the roles of FLiBe, BeO, and carbon in shaping the spectrum, demonstrating pronounced BeO and carbon moderation and F-19 resonance absorption effects on the intermediate energy flux. Safety analyses of drum rotation, drum seizure, and shutdown rod insertion failure confirm sufficient control margin and fault tolerance. The combination of passive heat pipes, integrity fuel and coolant, and redundant shutdown systems supports a safety-driven microreactor concept.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104646','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104646',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104642','Vacuum leak detection and localization based on remote handling and laser spectroscopy coupling','원격취급과 레이저 분광 결합 기반 진공 누설 탐지 및 위치 추정','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','방사선·계측','For the leakage detection and localization in the vacuum chambers of future fusion reactors, this paper proposes a design method based on the coupling of remote operation and laser spectroscopy. By using a pulsed laser to ablate solid targets, the design excites leaked gases in the environment and generates a spectrum. Spectrometers and detectors are used to collect information on atomic spectral lines in the area, enabling leak detection. A remote-operated robot is then used to transport the spectrometer to different areas of the vacuum chamber for continuous sampling. The precise location of the leak can be determined based on the distribution trends of the leak gas concentration gradient. To fully validate the feasibility of leak location, this paper analysis the diffusion behaviour of the leaking gas under different gas types and background pressures using finite element software. The results show that the mass fraction distribution of the leaking gas within the vacuum chamber exhibits a monotonically decreasing spatial gradient along the primary direction of diffusion. This gradient exhibits a distinguishable decay pattern under various leakage gas conditions (air and water vapor) and at different background pressures, demonstrating the feasibility of using concentration gradients to locate leaks.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104642','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104642',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712097','Stabilization of Research Reactor Spent Nuclear Fuels: Pellet Formation Using Spark Plasma Sintering','연구로 사용후핵연료의 안정화: 방전플라즈마소결을 이용한 소결체 성형','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712097','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712097',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712089','Thermal Aging Analysis of RNS-NR Neutron-Shielding Material for Long-Term Storage of Spent Nuclear Fuel','사용후핵연료 장기저장용 RNS-NR 중성자 차폐재의 열적 노화 분석','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study evaluated the long-term stability of a boron-loaded resin, RNS-NR, developed as a neutron-shielding material for dry storage casks. A laboratory-scale cask system with four stainless steel chambers was constructed to replicate dry storage conditions. The system integrated mass monitoring to track the thermal aging behavior under controlled boundary configurations, and the mass change of RNS-NR was continuously monitored for 2000 h at 170°C under sealed and open configurations.The experimental results demonstrated that the sealed configuration exhibited a lower mass change (−0.436 wt%) than the open configuration (−1.574 wt%). These results confirmed the influence of the chamber geometry on the release of water generated during thermal aging and other volatile species. The system included a high-temperature reference chamber and an ambient control chamber, which verified the stable operation of the platform during the long-term test.Regression modeling projected that RNS-NR in sealed configurations would reach only ~1 wt% mass loss after nearly 3 decades, which demonstrated improved long-term stability relative to the commercial benchmark NS-4-FR. The consistently low mass change rates observed under dry storage–relevant conditions indicated robust thermal aging resistance and supported the use of RNS-NR as a durable neutron-shielding material for long-term dry cask storage.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712089','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712089',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106552','A framework for probabilistic risk assessment of nuclear power plants coupled with data centers using causal analysis','인과분석을 이용한 데이터센터 연계 원자력발전소의 확률론적 리스크 평가 프레임워크','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The rapid growth of Artificial Intelligence (AI) is driving an unprecedented increase in electricity demand from Data Centers (DCs). Nuclear Power Plants (NPPs) are increasingly being considered as reliable low-carbon energy sources capable of supplying the required baseload power. However, the coupling introduces new operational interdependencies that may affect the overall plant safety and reliability, which are not captured by traditional Probabilistic Risk Assessment (PRA) frameworks. This work proposes a Bayesian Network (BN)-based framework for the risk assessment of NPPs coupled with DCs. The BN structure explicitly captures the causal relationships from component failures and cyber-attacks to initiating events and their progression to core damage, consistent with standard PRA logic. The BN parameters are estimated through both literature-informed engineering judgment and data-driven learning from data generated with a system simulator integrated within a Monte Carlo Simulation, while epistemic uncertainty is propagated with probabilistic parameter modeling. The framework enables the estimation of the Core Damage Frequency (CDF) increase due to coupling, identification of the most impactful failures and cyber-attacks, and extraction of the most probable causal paths that lead to core damage. Application to multiple coupling configurations involving Pressurized Water Reactors (PWRs) and Small Modular Reactors (SMRs) demonstrates the capability of the approach to provide both quantitative risk estimates and interpretable insights, supporting risk-informed design and operation of integrated NPP-DC systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106552','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106552',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','GR;US','GR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106554','Corrosion and mitigation of structural materials in chloride-based molten salt reactors: Mechanisms, challenges, and design strategies','염화물계 용융염원자로 구조재료의 부식 및 완화: 메커니즘, 과제 및 설계 전략','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-10','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Chloride-based molten salt reactors are promising advanced nuclear systems because of their favorable neutronic characteristics and high actinide solubility, but their deployment is limited by severe corrosion of structural materials in chemically aggressive and irradiation relevant environments. This review aims to provide an integrated understanding of corrosion and mitigation in chloride-based molten salt reactors by connecting degradation mechanisms with broader materials challenges and design strategies. The analysis shows that corrosion is governed by the coupled effects of impurities, fission products, and irradiation rather than by a single factor. Moisture, oxygen, dissolved metallic ions, and other impurities destabilize salt chemistry, disturb redox balance, and accelerate selective dissolution and intergranular corrosion. Fission products further intensify degradation through distinct pathways: tellurium directly promotes embrittlement and grain boundary damage, whereas europium, antimony, and selenium contribute through redox perturbation or direct reaction layer formation. Irradiation adds another level of complexity by generating defects, elemental redistribution, phase instability, and gas accumulation, thereby altering both the material and its response to molten salt attack. These findings indicate that effective mitigation requires an integrated strategy combining salt purification and redox control with protective coatings, surface engineering, and alloy design. Overall, corrosion in chloride-based molten salt reactors should be understood as a coupled chemical and microstructural degradation problem, and reliable deployment will depend on structural materials and protection strategies validated under relevant reactors combined environments.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106554','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106554',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR;US','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112689','Integration of PID controller and reinforcement learning agents for core power control of small pressurized water reactors','소형 가압경수로 노심출력 제어를 위한 PID 제어기와 강화학습 에이전트의 통합','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-09','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','In this paper, a composite control strategy, integrating classical PID controller and multiple reinforcement learning agents, is proposed for the core power control of small pressurized water reactors. The control architecture exploits the PID controller to maintain the baseline steady-state performance of the system while introducing a feedforward nonlinear compensation signal generated by agents based on the twin delayed deep deterministic policy gradient algorithm with prioritized experience replay (PER-TD3). To overcome the generalization bottleneck of a single agent across the entire power range, independent local agents are trained at multiple discrete power points, and a dynamic scheduling function based on real-time power is designed to achieve smooth weighted optimization and integration of the compensation actions from each local agent. Simulation results demonstrate that the prioritized experience replay mechanism effectively overcomes the inefficiency of standard uniform sampling, significantly enhancing the convergence speed and global search capability of the agents’ training. Under conditions of step changes in power setpoint, coolant inlet temperature, reactivity and model parametric mismatches, the proposed composite control strategy outperforms comparative control methods in terms of dynamic tracking accuracy, overshoot suppression capability and anti-disturbance robustness.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112689','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112689',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;FR;IT','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112728','Precise location of failed fuel assembly in operating PWR-core based on fine nuclide evolution and deep metric learning','정밀 핵종 변화 및 심층 거리학습 기반 운전 중 PWR 노심 결함 핵연료집합체 위치 정밀 탐지','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-09','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112728','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112728',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112695','Strategies for re-enriching depleted uranium: Reducing the consumption of natural UF6 for fuel production in a nuclear power reactor','감손우라늄 재농축 전략: 원자력발전로 핵연료 생산을 위한 천연 UF6 소비 저감','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-09','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112695','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112695',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104643','Heterogeneity in community acceptance of urban SMR siting: A contingent valuation and latent class analysis','도심 SMR 부지선정에 대한 지역사회 수용성의 이질성: 조건부가치평가 및 잠재계층 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-09','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This study provides empirical evidence on community acceptance of small modular reactor (SMR) siting among urban residents using a double-bounded dichotomous choice contingent valuation survey of 2,456 respondents in South Korea. Among respondents with a finite reservation price, the median annual Willingness-to-Accept (WTA) was KRW 111,000 per person (95% bootstrap CI: KRW 99,000 to 124,000). Respondents were classified into three tiers according to their reactions to two sequential bids: bid acceptors (52.6%), price-conditional acceptors (25.4%), and non-compensatory rejectors (22.0%), who reject SMR siting regardless of the amount offered. Latent class analysis identified five policy-relevant groups based on their perception profiles. The classes differed substantially in their tier compositions and perceptions of risk, benefits, trust, fairness, and negative affect, whereas demographic characteristics had limited explanatory power. The findings show that community responses to urban SMR siting cannot be adequately represented by a simple binary distinction between acceptance and opposition. By integrating compensation-based valuation, behavioral response classification, and perception-based segmentation, this study provides evidence for differentiated community engagement and benefit-sharing strategies that extend beyond uniform policy approaches.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104643','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104643',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106550','Multi-objective optimization and thermodynamic limits of free-piston Stirling generators using physics-informed active learning','물리정보 능동학습을 이용한 자유피스톤 스털링 발전기의 다목적 최적화 및 열역학적 한계','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-09','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The free-piston Stirling generator (FPSG) provides a promising energy conversion solution for space nuclear power systems (SNPS) and deep space exploration. However, intense multiphysics coupling creates an extremely narrow steady-state operable domain. To ensure high-fidelity performance prediction, a third-order transient thermodynamic solver, previously validated against experimental benchmarks, is employed to capture nonlinear gas-solid heat transfer and fluid inertia effects. To overcome the high-dimensional optimization bottleneck, this study proposes a physics-informed active learning multi-objective optimization (AL-MOO) framework. This mechanism enforces strict thermodynamic conservation constraints and eliminates non-physical pseudo-optima frequently encountered in conventional data-driven methods. Macroscopic performance limits within strict safety constraints are precisely determined: maximum power output reaches 158.6 W (14.4% efficiency), and maximum efficiency peaks at 15.0% (114.9 W). Detailed energy flow breakdowns and entropy generation analysis reveal the underlying microscopic dissipation mechanisms. Pursuing maximum power inevitably triggers exponentially growing unsteady viscous hysteresis penalties, severe local thermal non-equilibrium, and regenerator enthalpy leakage. It simultaneously sacrifices impedance matching, causing significant electromagnetic reactive power losses. Monte Carlo analysis further confirms that the optimal design maintains robust performance under small manufacturing tolerances. This study quantifies the inherent competition between thermodynamic work capacity and energy efficiency, providing thermo-physical criteria for next-generation Stirling energy systems in nuclear applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106550','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106550',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112726','Coupled comparative simulation and comprehensive performance evaluation of steam-extraction schemes for CHP retrofit of HPR1000 nuclear power units','HPR1000 원자력발전소 열병합(CHP) 개조를 위한 증기 추기 방식의 연계 비교 모의 및 종합 성능 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-08','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112726','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112726',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112707','Diffusion-based phase space nodal method (PSN): Solving the neutron transport equation with a diffusion code','확산 기반 위상공간 노달 방법(PSN): 확산 코드를 이용한 중성자 수송방정식 풀이','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-08','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112707','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112707',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112705','Numerical study of a guide shell for enhancing steam–air condensation heat transfer outside a straight tube','직관 외부 증기-공기 응축 열전달 향상을 위한 가이드 쉘의 수치해석 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-08','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112705','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112705',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115153','Study on vibration reduction mechanism of steam generator tube stabilizers based on damping control','감쇠 제어 기반 증기발생기 전열관 안정화기의 진동 저감 메커니즘 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-08','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115153','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115153',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106547','Analysis of dynamics of fuel rods in pulsed fast reactor','펄스형 고속로 핵연료봉의 동특성 해석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-08','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106547','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106547',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106556','Fragility analysis of PCCV under internal pressure via probability density evolution method','확률밀도진화법을 이용한 내압 하 PCCV의 취약도 해석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-08','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Prestressed concrete containment vessel (PCCV) serves as the final barrier against the release of radioactive materials into the environment. Throughout the service life of a PCCV, time-dependent prestress losses happen due to the creep and shrinkage of concrete as well as the relaxation of tendons, which surely reduce the integrity of the PCCV and increase the failure probability correspondingly. Therefore, it is essential to investigate the fragility of the PCCV with different prestress loss levels under internal pressure. Firstly, a finite element model was established to simulate the experiment of a 1:4 scaled PCCV under increasing internal pressure at Sandia National Laboratories. Subsequently, the probability density evolution method (PDEM) was adopted for the probabilistic analysis of random structural responses, where material properties were assumed as the source of uncertainty. The ultimate state of the PCCV was evaluated using the global average strain, whose values of 0.4% and 1.5% corresponded to the functional failure and structural failure, respectively. Finally, a parametric sensitivity analysis was performed on the displacement response of the PCCV under internal pressure. The fragility of the PCCV under different prestress loss levels was also discussed. The results indicate that the Young''s modulus of the prestressing tendons and the concrete have significant influences on the PCCV response. As the level of prestress loss increases, the integrity of the PCCV decreases. When the prestress loss level rose from 10% to 50%, the functional limit pressure capacity decreased by approximately 19%, while the structural limit pressure capacity decreased by about 7%.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106556','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106556',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106559','Tailored potassium-alumino-borosilicate glasses for high-level immobilization of Cs+, Co2+, and Ni2+: Enhancing structural integrity, thermal and mechanical stability, and leaching resistance','Cs+, Co2+ 및 Ni2+의 고함량 고정화를 위한 맞춤형 칼륨-알루미노-붕규산염 유리: 구조적 건전성, 열적·기계적 안정성 및 침출 저항성 향상','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-08','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106559','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106559',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','SA;EG','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112719','Effect of different oxidation time on deuterium absorption behavior of titanium films for radiation-voltaic isotope batteries','방사선-전지형 동위원소 전지용 티타늄 박막의 산화시간에 따른 중수소 흡수 거동','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112719','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112719',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
