INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112711','Neutronic analysis of a two-region damaged reactor model based on the external source mode of the Serpent code','Serpent 코드 외부선원 모드 기반 2영역 손상 원자로 모델의 중성자 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112711','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112711',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112712','Rapid prediction of atmospheric radionuclide concentration at an AP1000 nuclear power plant with complex terrain using a neural network optimized by a quantum virus optimization algorithm','양자 바이러스 최적화 알고리즘으로 최적화한 신경망을 이용한 복잡 지형 AP1000 원자력발전소의 대기 중 방사성핵종 농도 신속 예측','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','AI·디지털','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112712','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112712',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112718','Study on the simultaneous impact of double droplets on a wetted cylindrical wall by the CLSVOF method','CLSVOF 방법을 이용한 젖은 원통 벽면에 대한 이중 액적 동시 충돌 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112718','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112718',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112708','Tungsten-based polymer composites for lead-free gamma-ray shielding: attenuation performance and mechanical trade-offs','무연 감마선 차폐용 텅스텐 기반 고분자 복합재: 감쇠 성능과 기계적 특성의 상충관계','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112708','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112708',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','ID','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115146','Analytical investigations on dynamic instabilities in large PHWRs','대형 PHWR의 동적 불안정성에 대한 해석적 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115146','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115146',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115155','Effect of leakage cavity geometry on the performance of a rim-driven high-load helium compressor','누설 공동 형상이 림구동 고부하 헬륨 압축기 성능에 미치는 영향','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','Conventional high-load helium compressors are prone to significant tip leakage and rotor dynamics issues. The rim-driven motor configuration effectively mitigates these challenges; however, it introduces a tip leakage cavity that alters the flow characteristics at the rim tip region of the high-load helium compressor. To analyze the influence of the leakage cavity geometry on the compressor performance and to provide practical design guidelines for optimization, numerical simulations were conducted to investigate the effects of radial clearance width, axial clearance width, and different sealing configurations. The results show that reducing the axial clearance from 1.5 mm to 0.5 mm increases the peak efficiency by 4.7%, while reducing the radial clearance over the same range yields a 3.7% improvement. Furthermore, the optimized sealing configuration (Case F) improves the peak efficiency point of high-load helium compressor by 5.7% without modifying the clearance widths.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115155','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115155',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;PK','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2694116','Supervisory Control of Nuclear Power Plants Using Finite State Automata','유한상태 오토마타를 이용한 원자력발전소 감시제어','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-07','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Reducing operation and maintenance expenses associated with energy generation costs for small reactors and microreactors is necessary for their economic viability. One avenue for reducing these expenses is the implementation of autonomous reactor control systems. Advanced reactor designs inherently support reduced human operator interventions and incorporate enhanced passive safety features, reduced source terms, and digital instrumentation and control systems. Thus, the introduction of supervisory control systems (SCSs) for dynamic operations creates an opportunity to further reduce dependence on human operators and fosters confidence in advanced control systems. SCSs, as a transition technology, serve as a strategic pathway toward fully autonomous nuclear power plant operations. Finite state automata provide a fully verifiable and validatable supervisory control framework and thereby facilitate the transition to autonomous control systems, serving as a foundational mathematical tool for modeling discrete event systems (DESs). Furthermore, a DES can directly model both nuclear power plant systems and their operational procedures, which can be arranged within a hierarchical architecture using a graded functionalization approach already employed in complex dynamic systems like self-driving vehicles. Here, low-level actuation is accomplished via feedback controllers, and high-level state transitions are controlled by the supervisory controller. In the absence of licensed advanced reactor designs and approved nuclear autonomous control systems, legacy light water reactors (LWRs) can be used as a case study for the phased-implementation of advanced control systems because they provide realistic feedback and controls within a more conservative operating margin than the proposed advanced reactors. A generic supervisory controller was developed as a transition technology toward autonomous nuclear power plant operations. This controller was then tailored and scaled for implementation on LWR simulators. The lessons learned from incorporating automated processes can guide the framework development for autonomous processes. Incorporating a holistic and scalable approach via transitional steps toward autonomy provides an opportunity for validating these processes while actively engaging the nuclear industry in the shift away from reliance on human operators.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2694116','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2694116',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112715','Acceleration methods for the preprocessing of three-dimensional discrete ordinates radiation shielding calculations','3차원 이산좌표 방사선 차폐 계산 전처리 가속 기법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112715','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112715',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112717','Analysis of severe accident progression in a BWR considering power uprates and ATF cladding materials','출력증강 및 ATF 피복관 재료를 고려한 BWR 중대사고 진행 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112717','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112717',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112684','Direct incorporation of up-scattering sources in the Resonance Spectrum Expansion (RSE) method','공명 스펙트럼 전개(RSE) 방법에서의 상향산란 선원 직접 반영','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112684','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112684',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112716','Hybrid deep learning and metaheuristic algorithms for contaminated zone prediction and source term inversion in nuclear safety','원자력 안전에서의 오염구역 예측 및 선원항 역산을 위한 하이브리드 딥러닝·메타휴리스틱 알고리즘','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112716','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112716',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112697','Neutronic analysis of Yttrium Hydride temperature feedback coefficient in HALEU UMo fuelled microreactors','HALEU UMo 핵연료 초소형원자로에서 수소화이트륨 온도 궤환계수의 중성자 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The emerging interest in terrestrial and space microreactors has highlighted the need for innovative core design solutions. Selecting an adequate moderator is challenging for solid-core microreactors operating at high temperatures, where few weight-efficient options are available. Yttrium hydride (YH) is an appealing candidate due to its high hydrogen content and superior high-temperature retention compared to other hydrides. However, YH exhibits a positive temperature feedback coefficient (TFC), posing a significant safety risk that could offset its advantages. This work studies the YH TFC across various configurations, from simple unit-cells (fuel pins, moderator pins, and layers) to a realistic space heat-pipe reactor (PoliMi-TASI design) modified with moderator layers. The TFC is broken down into contributions defined by the 4-factor and 6-factor formulas. Neutron transport is simulated employing a Monte Carlo approach via OpenMC. The thermal utilisation factor provides the predominant contribution to the TFC, leading to positive values for most analysed configurations. Furthermore, analysis of the moderated PoliMi-TASI design reveals the MTC depends not only on the moderator-to-fuel ratio but also on layer thickness: for a fixed ratio, thinner layers yield a smaller MTC. This analysis clarifies the physics behind the YH TFC, guiding future design improvements for the PoliMi-TASI reactor.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112697','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112697',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','IT','IT','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112700','Oxygen substitution-induced structural, mechanical, and electronic evolution in UC1-xOx: A first-principles study for TRISO UCO fuel applications','UC1-xOx의 산소 치환에 따른 구조·기계·전자적 특성 변화: TRISO UCO 핵연료 적용을 위한 제1원리 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Uranium oxycarbide (UCO) TRISO fuel kernels undergo irradiation-driven redistribution of carbon and oxygen, leading to the formation of oxygen-substituted carbide domains (U C 1 - x O x ). The intrinsic properties of these domains influence dimensional stability and fission-product behaviour. In this work, density functional theory calculations within the GGA + U framework were combined with special quasi-random structures (SQS) to investigate structurally disordered U C 1 - x O x with oxygen concentrations of 0–16 at.% on the anion sublattice. Occupation matrix control was applied to ensure consistent convergence of the uranium 5f states, and a 1 K-type antiferromagnetic configuration was used to examine magnetic behaviour. Oxygen substitution preserves the rock salt structure up to 16 at.% O and produces a non-monotonic lattice response, with an initial lattice contraction at low oxygen content followed by lattice expansion at higher concentrations. The formation enthalpy becomes increasingly negative with oxygen addition, indicating enhanced thermodynamic stability of the carbide lattice. Simultaneously, uranium magnetic moments increase, and the density of states at the Fermi level decreases, reflecting stronger 5f localization and enhanced U-O bonding interactions. Elastic calculations show that oxygen incorporation increases C 44 and shear-related moduli, while C 11 remains nearly unchanged, accompanied by a reduction in Poisson’s ratio. Overall, these results establish clear composition structure property relationships for U C 1 - x O x in the low-oxygen composition range relevant to irradiation conditions in TRISO UCO fuels.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112700','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112700',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112704','Statistical admissibility of diffusion and SPN closures in correlated-medium nonclassical transport','상관 매질 비고전적 수송에서 확산 및 SPN 근사의 통계적 타당성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','Deterministic particle transport closures such as diffusion and S P N approximations are widely used in nuclear transport analysis, but are typically derived under exponentially distributed free paths, implying Poisson collision statistics and the existence of all required free-path moments. In spatially correlated media, attenuation is generally nonexponential and may exhibit heavy-tailed behavior, raising the question of whether the corresponding closure coefficients are well defined. This work uses a renewal-based formulation to identify when moment-dependent deterministic closure coefficients remain well defined for correlated free-path statistics. Within this formulation, macroscopic equations arise as moment projections of an underlying renewal process, with closure coefficients determined by the hierarchy of free-path moments. We recast the established moment dependence of nonclassical closure coefficients as an explicit coefficient-admissibility criterion for correlated renewal media whose free-path moment hierarchy may be finite. For the correlated survival-law family considered here, diffusion requires finite first and second free-path moments, while the one-dimensional isotropic S P 2 -level scalar closure additionally requires the third moment. The asymptotic renewal expansion shows how higher-order deterministic projections introduce successively higher free-path moments, but the explicit coefficient-admissibility analysis is limited to diffusion and the S P 2 -level closure. Boundary conditions are treated only as a scope limitation and are left for future nonclassical half-space analysis. Classical transport is recovered in the exponential limit. Generalized linear Boltzmann equation benchmarks are consistent with the predicted diffusion and S P 2 coefficient thresholds.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112704','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112704',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US;BR','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115138','Semi-mechanistic modeling of moisture release from heated concrete for safety design under sodium fire accident conditions','소듐 화재 사고 조건의 안전설계를 위한 가열 콘크리트의 수분 방출 반기계론적 모델링','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115138','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115138',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104639','Comparative SRIM investigation of lutetium-based alloys and lead for alpha-particle shielding applications','알파입자 차폐 적용을 위한 루테튬 기반 합금과 납의 SRIM 비교 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Due to increasing concerns regarding the toxicity, high density, and environmental limitations of lead-based shielding materials, heavy rare-earth elements such as lutetium (Lu) are gaining attention as potential alternatives for radiation protection applications. In this study, the interaction of 10 MeV alpha particles with pure lutetium and two engineered lutetium-based alloys (Lu–B and Lu–W) was investigated using SRIM simulation. Key shielding parameters, including electronic and nuclear stopping powers, projected range, longitudinal straggle, and lattice displacement damage, were evaluated and compared with those of pure lead (Pb). The Lu–W alloy exhibited a projected range of 36.1 μm, slightly lower than that of Pb (36.5 μm), indicating superior stopping efficiency against 10 MeV alpha particles. In contrast, the Lu–B alloy achieved approximately 21.5% weight reduction while maintaining acceptable shielding performance. Radiation damage analysis further revealed that Lu–W produced the highest vacancy concentration due to enhanced collision cascades, whereas Lu–B showed comparatively reduced defect formation, suggesting improved radiation tolerance. Despite its lower atomic number compared with lead, lutetium demonstrated excellent attenuation behavior and structural stability, highlighting its potential as a lightweight and environmentally safer shielding material. These findings suggest that lutetium-based composites are promising candidates for advanced aerospace systems and next-generation nuclear shielding technologies.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104639','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104639',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','SD;SA','SA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104637','Experimental investigation of persistence spectra, spatial correlations, and vortex structures in a randomly packed pebble bed using time-resolved PIV','시간분해 PIV를 이용한 무작위 충전 페블베드 내 지속성 스펙트럼, 공간 상관 및 와류 구조 실험 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104637','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104637',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','','','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104641','Fuel cycle features of RFBB fast reactor with silicide fuel and lead coolant','규화물 핵연료 및 납 냉각재를 사용하는 RFBB 고속로의 핵연료주기 특성','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The development of innovative fast nuclear reactor systems offers a reliable and sustainable solution to the world''s growing energy demand. In particular, breed-and-burn systems that use uranium as an efficient fuel could help significantly reduce nuclear waste and eliminate the need for expensive fuel reprocessing plants. The purpose of the present paper is to design a core for a rotational fuel-shuffling breed-and-burn reactor with silicide fuel and lead coolant (RFBB-SL). Compared to other breed-and-burn reactor designs, RFBB offers a more practical pathway by combining high fuel burnup with manageable material constraints and operational flexibility. We reveal the core’s fuel cycle features by analysing reactor burnup parameters through neutronic calculations. First, core simulations fully loaded with natural uranium fuel were conducted to assess the feasibility of achieving a critical equilibrium state. The configuration and fuel enrichment for the start-up core were determined based on this equilibrium state condition. A start-up core fuelled by uranium silicide with enrichments ranging from natural to 12% could operate with different shuffling intervals for 750 MW th and 250 MW th power reactors. The worth of the six peripheral control rod assemblies was between -5% and -2.8% for both cores. Heat removal analyses showed that a small, low-power start-up core for an RFBB-SL design is viable and that the maximum temperatures of the fuel, cladding, and coolant in the hottest channel can remain below their safety limits for a 250 MW th power reactor. Hence, the reactor could achieve a subcritical state even in a one-rod stuck scenario. Based on the obtained results, a practical RFBB-SL core combining slightly enriched uranium in silicide fuel and lead coolant under appropriate operating conditions can achieve an equilibrium state and sustain breed-and-burn mode for a long period.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104641','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104641',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','MN;JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104636','Monte Carlo investigation of spectral modifications induced by a W/Al selective filter in 6 MV flattening filter-free photon beams','6 MV 평탄화 필터 제거(FFF) 광자선에서 W/Al 선택 필터에 의한 스펙트럼 변화의 몬테카를로 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This study investigated the impact of a selective tungsten/aluminum energy filter [SF (W/Al) ] on the spectral characteristics of 6 MV Flattening Filter-Free (FFF) photon beams. The analysis included the energy spectrum and fluence, pinpointing the photon and electron energy ranges that contribute most to energy deposition on the water phantom surface. Monte Carlo (MC) simulations were performed using GATE for a 10 × 10 cm 2 field size at a source-to-surface distance (SSD) of 100 cm. The simulation model was validated against Varian phase-space file (PSFs) data using the gamma index criterion of 2%/2 mm. Excellent agreement was obtained, with gamma pass rates reaching 99% for percentage depth-dose (PDD) curves and 98% for lateral dose profiles. The spectral analysis demonstrated that FFF beams substantially increased the contribution of low-energy particles to surface dose deposition compared with flattened (FF) beams. Relative changes of 139.68 ± 2.18% for photons and 60.35 ± 2.71% for electrons, relative to the FF beam, were observed within the energy ranges of 0.49–0.525 MeV and 0.28–0.315 MeV, respectively. After introducing the SF (W/Al) , the corresponding relative changes decreased to 114.76 ± 1.82% for photons and 38.24 ± 1.76% for electrons within the same energy ranges, corresponding to relative reductions of 17.84% and 36.64%, respectively. These findings demonstrate that using a dedicated filter to control low-energy fluence selectively is an effective strategy to reduce surface dose and improve the clinical safety of FFF photon beams while preserving their therapeutic properties.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104636','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104636',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','MA','MA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104638','Refined multiphysics coupling analysis in optimized isotope production','최적화된 동위원소 생산의 정밀 다중물리 연계 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','ABSTRACT Aiming to balance efficient Californium-252 (Cf-252) production with reactor safety, this study investigates the Ultra-high Flux Lead Bismuth Reactor (UFLBR) and develops six progressive core schemes: no target, targets only, targets with moderator, layered target-moderator arrangement, spectrum-optimized layered arrangement, and spectrum-optimized arrangement based on neutron unidirectional flow. A neutronics-thermal-hydraulics-structural mechanics coupling framework is used to evaluate Cf-252 yield, heavy-nuclide conversion, temperature distribution, stress, and deformation. Results indicate that targets alone produce negligible Cf-252 in the fast spectrum, whereas moderation and layered spectrum regulation greatly enhance production. The spectrum-optimized layered scheme achieves the highest conversion rate of 1.67%, but also induces severe local power and thermal-mechanical risks. By introducing neutron unidirectional flow, thermal neutron backflow is effectively suppressed while favorable target-region spectra are retained. This scheme yields 11.7 g Cf-252 per fuel cycle with a 1.22% conversion rate, about 3.94 times that of the HFIR C78 campaign. Meanwhile, maximum fuel, cladding, coolant, and target temperatures remain below safety limits, and deformation stays within engineering margins. The proposed iterative optimization strategy provides a general reference for isotope-production scheme design and feasibility assessment.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104638','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104638',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2704150','Core Deformation Reactivity Analysis Using a Neutronics–Thermal-Hydraulics–Structural Mechanics Coupled Method for FFTF LOFWOS TEST #13','FFTF LOFWOS TEST #13에 대한 중성자–열수력–구조역학 연계 방법을 이용한 노심 변형 반응도 해석','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','Accurate evaluation of reactivity feedback caused by core deformation—including core bowing and radial expansion—during power increases in sodium-cooled fast reactors requires comprehensive modeling of the interactions among neutronics, thermal-hydraulics, and structural mechanics in the core. Conventional evaluation methods for core design studies often lack accuracy due to oversimplified modeling. To address this, Japan Atomic Energy Agency has developed a high-fidelity evaluation method that couples multiple analysis codes to simulate these complex phenomena. In this study, the evaluation method was applied to analysis of the Fast Flux Test Facility (FFTF) loss of flow without scram (LOFWOS) TEST #13 using the experimentally measured core flow rate and inlet temperature as boundary conditions. The coupled analysis successfully reproduced the non-monotonic temporal variation of net reactivity observed experimentally. Sensitivity analyses of core design parameters related to core structural mechanics revealed that the S-shaped bowing of fuel assemblies, driven by specific contact conditions, is the primary mechanism of negative feedback. Notably, initial assembly pad gaps and pad compressive stiffness significantly influence the feedback magnitude and timing, highlighting the critical impact of core structural design. These results demonstrate that the developed coupled analysis method is a valuable tool for the design and licensing of fast reactors, supporting both safety and economic competitiveness.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2704150','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2704150',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2707603','Development and Deployment of a Machine Learning–Based Predictor of Moisture Carryover in Boiling Water Reactors','비등경수로 습분 이월 예측을 위한 기계학습 기반 예측기 개발 및 적용','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2707603','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2707603',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106537','Insensitivity of scenario-based seismic fragility to distance-based inter-SSC correlation variations up to 1000 m in multi-unit NPPs','다수기 원자력발전소에서 1000 m 이내 거리 기반 SSC 간 상관관계 변화에 대한 시나리오 기반 지진 취약도의 둔감성','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-06','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106537','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106537',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112713','Prediction of plutonium content of BWR/MOX fuel using a neural network','신경망을 이용한 BWR/MOX 핵연료의 플루토늄 함량 예측','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-05','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The Nuclear Material Balance (NMB) code is a comprehensive nuclear fuel cycle simulator developed by the Institute of Science Tokyo and the Japan Atomic Energy Agency. By modeling a fleet of reactors, fuel cycle simulators like NMB can help to optimize uranium and plutonium utilization, develop a reprocessing plan, and manage nuclear waste. However, a key challenge in this code is to simulate the fabrication of Mixed Oxide fuel, where the plutonium content must be properly tuned to achieve the targeted multiplication factor after irradiation. Traditionally, NMB’s prediction relies on predefined one-group cross sections and computationally intensive depletion calculations that involve solving burnup equations. This study addresses the inaccuracy due to the one-group cross-section as well as the computational burden by developing and integrating a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) model into NMB. A custom PyTorch MLP was trained on a dataset of 5,000 depletion calculations generated with the SERPENT code for an ATRIUM-10 Boiling Water Reactor geometry. The developed MLP, in conjunction with a dichotomy search algorithm, determined the plutonium content with an error below 1% and achieved calculation speed of approximately 60 times for determination of Pu enrichment and 4 times for overall calculation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112713','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112713',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','FR;JP','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2705813','Experimental Characterization and Statistical Analysis of Two Geiger-Müller Detectors After Several Years of Use','수년간 사용한 두 가이거-뮐러 검출기의 실험적 특성 평가 및 통계 분석','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-05','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','In general, radiation detectors are supplied at the time of acquisition with a user manual describing their technical characteristics and nominal operating conditions. However, these characteristics may evolve over time and gradually deviate from the original specifications after several years of use due to intensive operation, electronic component wear, gas aging, and cumulative irradiation effects.In this context, the present work aims to reidentify and analyze the evolution of the characteristics of two Geiger-Müller detectors used at the Nuclear Physics Laboratory of the Faculty of Sciences of Rabat, Morocco, after approximately 10 years of operation. A complete experimental recharacterization of the detectors was carried out in order to evaluate their current operational state and to compare their measured performances with those determined at the time of their first acquisition in 2016.In addition, an in-depth analysis of the archived experimental data collected between 2018 and 2025 was performed to investigate the temporal evolution of the main detector parameters. The exploitation of these historical data made it possible to propose a model for estimating the future evolution of detector performance and predicting their behavior over the period 2026 to 2033. Furthermore, this paper discusses the main techniques that could be implemented in laboratories to restore or improve the performance of aging detectors while also examining the practical and physical limitations associated with these approaches.Finally, this work also proposes a new experimental approach to investigate the detection efficiency as a function of energy in the case of Geiger-Müller detectors used for beta particle detection. Unlike the conventional method, which generally provides a global efficiency without energy discrimination, the proposed approach relies on the use of attenuation layers and on simulations of beta particle attenuation in order to explore the energy dependence of the detection efficiency.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2705813','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2705813',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','MA','MA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106548','Analysis of natural deposition and spray removal characteristics of aerosols in containment based on PISAA code','PISAA 코드 기반 격납건물 내 에어로졸의 자연침적 및 살수 제거 특성 분석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-05','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106548','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106548',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN;SG','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106549','From data to correlation: symbolic regression reveals a unified friction factor relation for upward single-phase flow in vertical rod bundles','데이터에서 상관식으로: 기호회귀로 도출한 수직 봉다발 내 상향 단상유동의 통합 마찰계수 관계식','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-05','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106549','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106549',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106545','Study of separation characteristics of corrugated-plate dryers under marine conditions','해양 조건에서 파형판 건조기의 분리 특성 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-05','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106545','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106545',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112709','Predicting independent fission yields of the JEFF-4.0 evaluation via physics-informed machine learning surrogate models','물리정보 기계학습 대리모델을 이용한 JEFF-4.0 평가 독립 핵분열 수율 예측','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Evaluating independent fission product yields is crucial for advanced reactor physics. In this study, physics-informed and explainable machine learning (ML) surrogate models were developed to predict these yields using the latest JEFF-4.0 evaluation for thermal and fast neutron-induced fission.. The dataset was systematically constructed from filtered yield records across 19 fissioning actinides, with the target variable modeled on a log arithmic scale (log 10 (Yind)). To assess cross-actinide transferability, GroupKFold and Leave-One-Actinide-Out (LOAO) validation protocols were implemented. The findings demonstrate that tree-based ensemble algorithms substantially outperform linear baselines in capturing the discontinuous, quantum–mechanical nature of nuclear data. The optimized Random Forest model achieved an R 2 ≈ 0.798 under GroupKFold validation and demonstrated high generalizability with an average R 2 ≈ 0.792 under the LOAO evaluation. Furthermore, the reconstructed isobaric mass chain distribution for U-235 thermal fission successfully captured the fundamental asymmetric, double-humped topology. To overcome the traditional “black-box” limitations of ML, SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP) and feature ablation analyses were integrated, revealing that the algorithm explicitly relies on fundamental physical constraints—specifically, the mass split fraction, Unchanged Charge Distribution (UCD)-based charge polarization, and odd/even nucleon pairing effects. Finally, point tests on critical reactor poisons demonstrated the model’s capability to generate preliminary predictions within the same order of magnitude for I-131 and Xe-135, although relative errors naturally widened for ultra-low yield isotopes such as Sm-149. Consequently, the proposed framework provides a rapid, physics-grounded surrogate for data screening workflows, intended to be coupled with decay chains and neutron capture equations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112709','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112709',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112692','Scaling analysis of primary coolant system under SBLOCA for a test facility according to a pressurized water test reactor: Part I – top-down scaling','가압경수형 시험로 기반 시험장치의 SBLOCA 시 1차 냉각재계통 척도해석: 제1부 – 하향식 척도해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112692','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112692',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115103','A simulation of the CAPRIX pin irradiation in comparison with experimental data: Illustration of the significance of accurate irradiation data','CAPRIX 연료봉 조사시험 모의 및 실험 데이터 비교: 정확한 조사 데이터의 중요성','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','Mixed oxide (MOX) fuels with high plutonium content are key candidates for sodium-cooled fast reactors (SFRs) aimed at maximizing plutonium burning and reducing minor actinide radiotoxicity. Within the CAPRA (Consommation Accrue de Plutonium dans les Rapides 1 ) program, MOX fuels with plutonium fractions up to 0.45 were developed and irradiated. This work focuses on the simulation of the CAPRIX 2 experimental fuel pin, composed of CAPRA pellets and irradiated in the PHENIX reactor between 1995 and 2006, and on the comparison between numerical predictions and post-irradiation examination (PIE) data. A comprehensive assessment of the experimental conditions used on input by the GERMINAL fuel performance code was carried out. Regarding the irradiation history, the linear heat rate profiles, the neutron fluxes and the cladding temperature fields were obtained from coupled TRIPOLI-4 neutronic and TrioMC thermal-hydraulic calculations. Simulations were performed using GERMINAL versions 2 and 3. The calculated results were compared with experimental measurements at pin scale (burn-up, fission gas release, internal pressure, and fuel column elongation) and pellet scale (fuel and cladding diameters, fuel restructuring, and radial actinide redistribution). The results demonstrate that GERMINAL is able to reasonably reproduce the overall behavior of a high‑plutonium MOX fuel pin, provided that the irradiation data are accurately defined. Remaining discrepancies concern burn-up (BU) overestimation, internal pressure prediction, limited fuel restructuring, and the inability to reproduce the experimentally observed plutonium redistribution near the central hole. These deviations highlight the limitations of current thermally activated and geometrical models. This study underlines the critical importance of well-defined irradiation conditions and identifies key areas for further model improvements when simulating high-Pu-content MOX fuels.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115103','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115103',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','FR','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115148','Numerical study on 7 to 61-rod LBE cooled wire-wrapped fuel rod bundles and the scalability to large-scale fuel assemblies','LBE 냉각 와이어랩 7~61봉 핵연료봉 다발의 수치해석 연구 및 대형 핵연료집합체로의 확장성','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115148','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115148',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104598','An equivalent source response matrix method for solving the neutron diffusion equation','중성자 확산방정식 풀이를 위한 등가 선원 응답행렬 방법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This paper presents an equivalent source response matrix method (ESRMM) for solving the neutron diffusion equation. Starting from Neumann boundary conditions, the prescribed boundary-source problem in a finite homogeneous node is reformulated, through equivalent source theory, as a superposition of source-response problems in an infinite homogeneous medium. The resulting source-response relation is expressed in a parametric form, enabling efficient response matrix generation via precomputed interpolation tables. The boundary-source-to-flux response matrix is directly compatible with discontinuity factors from generalized equivalence theory and response correction factors from the recently proposed response equivalent theory (RET). Numerical results for the IAEA 2D benchmark, the IAEA 3D benchmark, and a small PWR problem with discontinuity factors show that ESRMM with one node per assembly is more accurate than a 1 × 1 nodal discretization and approaches the accuracy of a 2 × 2 subdivision. The two-dimensional problems complete in milliseconds, and the IAEA 3D benchmark completes in 0.12 s.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104598','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104598',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104609','Applicability of regulatory Guide 1.99 Rev. 2 and ASTM E900-15 embrittlement trend curves to high-yield-strength RPV steels for small modular reactors','소형모듈원자로용 고항복강도 원자로압력용기강에 대한 Regulatory Guide 1.99 Rev. 2 및 ASTM E900-15 취화 경향 곡선의 적용성','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This study evaluates the applicability of Regulatory Guide 1.99 Rev. 2 (RG 1.99) and ASTM E900-15—candidate models for future regulatory adoption—to SA508 Gr.3 Class 2 high-strength steel, a reactor pressure vessel material under considered for innovative small modular reactors. As a regulatory-basis pre-assessment, materials from a combined Korean and U.S. surveillance database were classified as Class 1- or Class 2-equivalent based on the unirradiated yield strength and ultimate tensile strength, and the residuals of each model were statistically analyzed by product form. Under RG 1.99 Position 1.1, the forging residuals of Class 2 were significantly lower than those of Class 1. This result reflects a conservative overprediction of the transition temperature shift and is therefore acceptable from a regulatory safety standpoint. Under RG 1.99 Position 2.1, the unit-specific chemistry factor recalculation eliminated all significant class differences. ASTM E900-15 yielded similar conclusions while resolving the high-fluence underprediction bias of RG 1.99. No combination of model and product form exhibited a nonconservative bias for Class 2 within the analyzed surveillance database. These conclusions are limited to retrospectively classified Class 2-equivalent materials. Therefore, direct validation using actual SA508 Gr.3 Class 2 materials remains necessary.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104609','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104609',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104610','Investigation of the physicochemical responses and radical behavior of silk fabrics induced by gamma irradiation','감마선 조사에 따른 견직물의 물리화학적 반응 및 라디칼 거동 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Climate change has increased flood damage to cultural heritage, drawing attention to gamma irradiation as an eco-friendly disinfection technique for the biological control of heritage materials. However, comprehensive evaluations of the physicochemical responses of silk textiles to low-dose gamma irradiation (≤25 kGy) remain limited. Raw and degummed silk under dry and wet conditions were irradiated at 5–25 kGy and analyzed by colorimetry, breaking force and elongation testing, FT-IR, XRD, and ESR. As a result, no distinct changes in morphology, protein secondary structure, or Silk II crystalline structure were observed by stereomicroscopy, FT-IR, or XRD up to 25 kGy. In contrast, yellowness and color difference increased with dose, whereas mechanical properties exhibited nonlinear behavior depending on degumming and moisture. ESR analysis revealed that residual radicals increased up to 10 kGy and then decreased under dry conditions, whereas no stable radicals were detected under wet conditions. Notably, radical behavior and mechanical properties showed inflection points in similar dose ranges, suggesting that subsequent radical reactions may be associated with mechanical changes. These findings indicate that ESR, colorimetric, and mechanical analyses are more sensitive for evaluating the early responses of silk fabrics, providing fundamental data for biological control guidelines for silk cultural heritage.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104610','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104610',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104629','Removing oxygen-derived impurities from molten chloride fuel salts with aluminium chloride: Effectiveness and limitations','염화알루미늄을 이용한 용융 염화물 핵연료염 내 산소 유래 불순물 제거: 효과와 한계','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-04','','','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Growing electricity demand has renewed interest in chloride-based molten salt reactors. However, oxygen ingress during operation can raise the redox potential, accelerating corrosion and promoting fuel loss through uranium oxide formation, while removal methods for operating reactors remain underdeveloped. In this study, aluminium chloride is investigated for removing oxygen-derived impurities and inhibiting uranium oxide formation during operation. Within the salt, aluminium chloride was effective: the oxide ion removal efficiency exceeded 93%, UO 2 was effectively converted to UCl 4 after 24 h at 700 °C, while U 3 O 8 also underwent conversion to soluble uranium species. However, its ability to restore the redox state was limited. Using the Sm 2+ /Sm 3+ couple as an analogue for the U 3+ /U 4+ system, once the redox state had been disturbed by oxygen, it could not be recovered even after the oxo-species were removed. These results indicate that oxygen is better removed in the cover gas before it reacts with the molten salt. Given its high volatility, gaseous aluminium chloride is well suited to this purpose, as supported by thermodynamic calculations, although experimental verification remains future work. Some Al 2 O 3 inevitably remains in the salt, and its possible effects on the thermochemical properties of the molten salt require further study.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104629','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104629',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR;GB;UA','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112691','Comprehensive validation of subchannel analysis code SACOS-LMR with liquid-sodium and -lead benchmarks','액체 소듐 및 납 벤치마크를 이용한 부수로 해석코드 SACOS-LMR의 종합 검증','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112691','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112691',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112674','Innovative techniques in evaluating neutron fluxes of the multi-energy groups diffusion for homogeneous cubic and spherical reactors','균질 입방체 및 구형 원자로에 대한 다군 확산 중성자속 평가의 혁신적 기법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The study of neutron diffusion in nuclear reactors is pivotal for ensuring safe and efficient reactor operation. This paper presents a comprehensive analysis of multi-energy group neutron diffusion, focusing on the derivation of spatial functions for cubic and spherical reactor geometries and the development of volume-integrated multigroup point kinetics equations. Analytical solutions for the time-integrated multigroup point kinetics equations are derived using Hermite piecewise polynomial methods for one-energy group, two-energy groups, and four-energy groups, incorporating temperature feedback effects. Numerical results are provided for step and ramp reactivity insertions in cubic and spherical reactors, analyzing delayed supercritical, supercritical, and subcritical cases for the spherical reactor. The study further evaluates the impact of temperature feedback on reactor dynamics. Results demonstrate high accuracy in the proposed analytical solutions, with significant implications for reactor design and safety analysis. This work provides a robust framework for modeling neutron behavior in multi-energy group systems, offering valuable insights for both theoretical and applied nuclear engineering.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112674','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112674',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','EG;SA','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112702','Radiological site evaluation of the proposed Gosong Beach nuclear power plant site in Indonesia','인도네시아 고송 해변 원자력발전소 후보 부지의 방사선학적 부지 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112702','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112702',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','ID','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115136','Coupled flow-thermal analysis of an HTGR spent fuel dry storage system during transfer and storage','HTGR 사용후핵연료 건식저장계통의 이송 및 저장 중 유동-열 연계 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115136','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115136',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115149','Design and analysis of a bedrock-coupled passive heat removal system for a small modular reactor','소형모듈원자로용 암반 연계 피동열제거계통 설계 및 해석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The safety of small modular reactors (SMRs), particularly for district heating applications where reliable and simple decay heat removal is required, is best achieved with passive systems. This study presents a naturally circulating passive heat removal system that uses bedrock as an intermediate heat sink. The system has been designed for the LUTHER 24 MWth district heating reactor. TRACE system code is used to model the reactor core, containment atmosphere, and heat exchanger pipes embedded in crystalline granite bedrock typical to Nordic countries and Canada. The analysis focuses on the performance of the heat exchanger and the bedrock, considering thermal contact at the pipe-rock interface, heat exchanger pipe length, condensation in the presence of non-condensable gases, containment pressure response, and long-term heat dissipation inside the bedrock. The results show that an air gap between heat exchanger piping and bedrock reduces the heat transfer significantly. Concrete filling (grouting) would improve thermal coupling. Under the considered conditions, 300 parallel pipes of 20 m are sufficient to keep the containment pressure within acceptable limits and support long-term heat removal. Slow conduction in the bedrock keeps ground-surface temperature low enough for accessibility. The results indicate that bedrock can serve as a feasible intermediate heat sink for passive decay heat removal in underground small reactor applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115149','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115149',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','FI','FI','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104626','An uncertainty-aware machine learning framework for predicting cable and cabinet damage in switchgear room fire scenarios','개폐기실 화재 시나리오에서 케이블 및 캐비닛 손상 예측을 위한 불확실성 인지 기계학습 프레임워크','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Fires in the motor control center (MCC) of switchgear rooms in nuclear power plants can threaten operational reliability and safety by damaging safety-critical electrical cabinets and cable systems. This study proposes an integrated, reliability-consistent surrogate modeling framework for fire risk assessment in a switchgear room of a nuclear power plant. First, a sensitivity analysis is conducted using Consolidated Model of Fire and Smoke Transport (CFAST) simulations to investigate the effects of fire source, cable and cabinet locations, air change per hour (ACH), and ambient temperatures on cable and cabinet damage times. The results indicate that cables near the ceiling are damaged faster, while lower fire source locations cause earlier cable damage. Additionally, higher ACH accelerates damage to distant downstream cables. Second, an ML-based surrogate model was developed, with SHAP-based analysis to interpret feature contributions, indicating that the Light Gradient-Boosting Machine (LGBM) effectively predicts damage times, while SHAP analysis aligns with the sensitivity analysis, ensuring model interpretation. Third, uncertainty quantification evaluates the statistical consistency between predicted uncertainties and actual errors using Pearson, Spearman, and Kendall correlation. Uncertainty thresholds are calibrated against relative error criteria to provide trustworthy guidance for identifying scenarios where CFD simulations are needed, enabling robust, risk-informed tool for supporting conservative fire safety decisions in switchgear rooms.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104626','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104626',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104627','Analysis of low-level alarm for a lubricating oil tank based on flow characteristics and temperature in a nuclear power plant','원자력발전소 윤활유 탱크의 유동 특성 및 온도 기반 저수위 경보 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The lubrication of charging pump is critical in the RCV system in nuclear power plants and keeping the oil level stable is essential for safe plant operation. In this study, the reasons for the low-level alarm activation and recovery in the RCV system are investigated by the combination of both theoretical analysis and experimental testing. The results show that two flow characteristics cause fluctuations of liquid level, the maximum amplitudes respectively reach 0.92 mm and 5.73 mm for the initial liquid level of 290 mm. And temperature is a vital factor to the level of the tank, one is ambient temperature which causes lubricating oil to undergo thermal expansion and contraction, changing the level up to 2.6 mm with temperature difference of 10 °C. The other is oil temperature, lower temperatures result in higher lubricant viscosity at the beginning of charging pump startup, prolonging oil return time, which causes level to remain low for an extended period and the maximum level difference up to 3.24 mm between 15 and 25 °C for a D/4 back flow, increasing the likelihood of triggering the low-level alarm. As temperature rises, the liquid is more quickly back to the tank, making the level recovered.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104627','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104627',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104630','Computational assessment of the feasibility of conversion of the impulse graphite reactor to high-assay low-enriched uranium fuel','임펄스 흑연원자로의 HALEU 핵연료 전환 타당성에 대한 전산 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','A conceptual assessment of the conversion of the Impulse Graphite Reactor (IGR) from high-enriched uranium (HEU) fuel to high-assay low-enriched uranium (HALEU) fuel is presented. The proposed conversion concept is based on the expansion of the core and the application of uranium-impregnated graphite fuel using IG-430 graphite. The study investigates whether the key performance characteristics of the reactor can be preserved under HALEU conditions while maintaining the existing operational modes and addressing primary safety considerations. The analysis was performed using a previously validated methodology for coupled neutronic and thermal transient simulations of the IGR reactor. Five representative transient scenarios, including regulated pulses, long-duration transients, and self-terminating neutron bursts, were analyzed for both HEU and HALEU configurations. The performance criteria considered include neutron flux and fluence parameters, pulse kinetics, energy release in an experimental device (ED), reactivity margins, shutdown capability, and thermal limits of the graphite core. The results demonstrate that all required conversion criteria can be achieved for the proposed HALEU configuration without approaching limiting thermal conditions. The obtained reactivity margins and shutdown characteristics additionally provide significant tolerance to uranium concentration variations in graphite fuel blocks.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104630','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104630',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','KZ','KZ','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104628','Investigation into peak shaving technology for nuclear power systems utilizing SOEC technology','SOEC 기술을 활용한 원자력 계통의 첨두부하 저감 기술 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','ABSTRACT: The integration of Solid Oxide Electrolysis Cell (SOEC) technology and nuclear power systems is investigated in this study, with a focus on operational flexibility and efficiency during peak shaving periods. As renewable energy increasingly penetrate the power grid, the proposed Nuclear Power Plant-Solid Oxide Electrolysis Cell (NPP-SOEC) system addresses the need for flexible baseload operations by repurposing surplus electricity and thermal energy into hydrogen. The system is modeled and simulated under varying load conditions using Aspen Plus software, establishing two distinct thermal integration strategies. Findings reveal a profound thermodynamic contrast between the two configurations. While the Low-Grade Recovery Configuration maintains a slightly higher first-law thermal efficiency reaching up to approximately 80%, the High-Pressure Extraction Configuration demonstrates higher second-law performance. Specifically, the high-pressure strategy achieves a peak exergy efficiency of approximately 75% at a 50% generation load, compared to approximately 67% attained by the low-grade alternative. This highlights the necessity of matching high-grade thermal energy with the sensible heating requirements of the electrolysis process to minimize exergy destruction. Under these optimal conditions, the high-pressure configuration exhibits a hydrogen production capacity of 2711 kmol/h. Comprehensive techno-economic evaluations incorporating operation, maintenance, and stack replacement costs indicate financial viability, with the return on investment reaching up to approximately 340% over a ten-year lifespan. Furthermore, while continuous full-power reactor operation mitigates thermal-hydraulic fatigue risks, the safety assessment integrates quantitative regulatory constraints. It emphasizes that enforcing a safe stand-off distance against hydrogen detonation hazards, such as the 1 psi overpressure threshold, constitutes a primary source of economic uncertainty. Overall, the integration of SOEC technology with nuclear power offers a systematic framework for evaluating nuclear-SOEC coupling configurations, while acknowledging that site-specific factors—including electricity market structures, hydrogen storage economics, and seasonal demand variations—will determine the practical viability of deployment.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104628','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104628',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104634','Local lattice distortion-induced mechanical asymmetry and coupled magnetic-electronic responses in bcc iron: A combined experimental and first-principles investigation','bcc 철에서 국부 격자 뒤틀림에 의한 기계적 비대칭성과 자기-전자 연계 반응: 실험 및 제1원리 복합 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Dislocations and defect clusters critically influence the mechanical, magnetic, and electronic properties of body-centered cubic (bcc) iron, which is the foundational matrix for reactor pressure vessel (RPV) steels and low-activation ferritic alloys. Yet, the underlying mechanisms driving load-dependent asymmetry in these extreme-environment structural materials remain unclear. Here, motivated by experimental characterizations, we independently employ first-principles density functional theory (DFT) calculations to elucidate the effects of local lattice distortions in bcc Fe. Transmission electron microscopy and electron backscatter diffraction on a rolled Fe-Si model alloy reveal dense dislocation networks and heterogeneous residual stress fields. Informed by these microstructural heterogeneities, simplified DFT simulations of supercells with varying local atomic displacements (15–45% along the [001] crystallographic direction) demonstrate pronounced mechanical asymmetry: distortions enhance compressive stiffness but induce early tensile instability, with softening scaling to distortion magnitude. Electronic analysis shows defect-suppressed density of states near the Fermi level and reduced magnetic moments, weakening interatomic bonds under tension. These effects position severe local lattice distortions as stabilizers under compression but initiators of tensile failure. Our findings provide atomic-scale insights into defect-controlled asymmetry in iron-based materials, guiding microstructural engineering for improved strength, magnetic stability, and electronic performance in structural steels and soft magnetic devices.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104634','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104634',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104571','Neutron leakage spectra benchmark of spherical iron sample with a 252Cf fission source','252Cf 핵분열 선원을 이용한 구형 철 시료의 중성자 누설 스펙트럼 벤치마크','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','To provide complementary benchmark data for validating evaluated neutron nuclear data with time-of-flight techniques, a neutron leakage experiment for spherical natural-iron samples was conducted on a 252 Cf spontaneous-fission-source-based integral experiment platform established at Lanzhou University. Neutron leakage spectra from spherical natural-iron samples with diameters of 12, 24, and 36 cm were measured over the energy range of 0.15–8.00 MeV. The 0.15–0.80 MeV region was measured using a CLYC detector, while the 0.80–8.00 MeV region was measured using an EJ-309 liquid scintillation detector. Monte Carlo simulations were performed using the MCNP code with four evaluated nuclear data libraries: ENDF/B-VIII.1, CENDL-3.2, JEFF-3.3, and JENDL-5. The calculated leakage spectra were compared with the experimental results. The calculated-to-experimental (C/E) ratios indicate that JENDL-5 and ENDF/B-VIII.1 show comparatively good agreement with the measurements, whereas CENDL-3.2 and JEFF-3.3 exhibit larger deviations, particularly in the 0.80–8.00 MeV region. The NDPlot-based diagnostic analysis of 252 Cf-spectrum-weighted secondary-neutron emission spectra suggests that these deviations may be related to differences in the treatment and representation of elastic and discrete-level inelastic scattering processes in the evaluated nuclear data libraries and the numerical reconstruction procedure. However, since the measured leakage spectra represent integral responses involving multiple scattering and coupled reaction channels, further sensitivity and uncertainty analyses are required to identify the dominant contributors quantitatively. This work provides complementary modern TOF-based benchmark data for natural-iron shielding calculations using a 252 Cf-driven integral experiment platform. The measured leakage spectra provide additional experimental information for validating recently updated evaluated nuclear data libraries and may support future sensitivity, uncertainty quantification, and nuclear-data improvement for shielding applications in advanced nuclear energy systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104571','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104571',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104631','Regulatory readiness for SMRs in Greece: An institutional gap analysis of a latent EU newcomer','그리스의 SMR 규제 준비도: 잠재적 EU 신규 도입국의 제도적 격차 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','방사선·계측','Greece has begun to examine small modular reactors (SMRs) without holding any of the institutions of a declared nuclear program, which raises the question of whether it is a latent European Union (EU) newcomer rather than a conventional one. The 19 infrastructure issues of the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) Milestones framework are applied as a qualitative gap-analysis matrix, read through Euratom obligations, WENRA expectations, and comparator evidence from Poland, Estonia, and the United Arab Emirates, with issue-specific decision rules and named evidence anchors reported for every rating. Greece meets 4 issues, partially meets 8, and does not meet 7, so it is neither institutionally blank nor program-ready. EU-derived radiation protection, safeguards, and environmental permitting coexist with the absence of program ownership, a commercial nuclear framework act, financing architecture, and backend policy. Apparent readiness is therefore conditional rather than substantive, and the latent EU newcomer is proposed as an analytical category that separates inherited compliance from program-specific governance. The 12 to 15 year roadmap derived from the diagnosis is an institutional sequencing estimate, not a deployment forecast. Findings reflect Greek readiness as of mid-2026, including observer participation in the Nuclear Alliance meeting of 26 June 2026.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104631','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104631',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','GR;US','GR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104633','Strontium-90 determination in milk ash by cherenkov and gas-flow proportional counting: A comparison of three radiochemical separations','체렌코프 계수 및 기체유동 비례계수를 이용한 우유 회분 중 스트론튬-90 정량: 세 가지 방사화학적 분리법 비교','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','Strontium-90 is a long-lived fission product whose determination in milk is analytically demanding, requiring selective separation from excess calcium before beta counting. Three radiochemical procedures were compared for 90 Sr determination in a milk-ash matrix: solvent extraction of 90 Y into tributyl phosphate (TBP) with gas-flow proportional counting, extraction chromatography on Sr Resin, and molecular-recognition separation on AnaLig® Sr-01, both read out by Cherenkov counting of ingrowing 90 Y. Eight milk-ash aliquots were spiked at 10 Bq/L of raw-milk equivalent and analyzed by all three methods in a paired design. Cherenkov counting efficiency was characterized against a graded iron(III) color-quench series to define the optimal energy window. Mean chemical recoveries were approximately 90% for AnaLig® Sr-01, 85% for Sr Resin, and 75% for TBP. All three methods yielded statistically indistinguishable 90 Sr activity concentrations, as confirmed by repeated-measures ANOVA, the Friedman test, and pairwise comparisons. Method minimum detectable activity concentrations were 0.296 – 0.332 Bq/L. The principal differences were operational rather than analytical: TBP suited aged, equilibrated samples; Sr Resin remained the most established rapid option for emergency use; and AnaLig® Sr-01 was also suitable for fresh post-incident samples while offering routine-use advantages through sorbent regeneration and reduced waste generation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104633','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104633',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','SK','SK','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2704149','Balance of Plant Modeling and Real-Time Hardware-in-the-Loop Integration with the Microreactor Automated Control System','BOP 모델링 및 초소형원자로 자동제어계통과의 실시간 HIL(Hardware-in-the-Loop) 통합','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','열수력·유체','The advent of novel microreactor technology has driven a focused effort to explore safety and efficiency improvements that can be achieved through the use of automated system control. Development of control strategies, especially for initial demonstration, requires an adequate surrogate environment to safely research failure modes and control integration with realistic hardware delay. However, efficiency gains from control strategies are improved when the scope of controller action is expanded to include system-level dynamics such as downstream heat extraction and mass flow. For this reason, a balance-of-plant (BOP) model of a representative microreactor system has been developed using the TRANsient Simulation Framework of Reconfigurable Models library in Modelica. This model captures a reactor and primary NaK coolant loop that represent corresponding system components of the Microreactor Applications Research Validation and EvaLuation (MARVEL) design as well as a secondary coolant loop and heat extraction representative of the Microreactor Agile Non-Nuclear Experimental Test Bed (MAGNET). This model configuration allows for hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) integration with microreactor automated control system (MACS) hardware in real time through a Python-based gRPC client. Real-time simulation of model performance with emulated hardware and communication delay suggests that under independent proportional-integral-derivative control of BOP model drum dynamics and downstream heat extraction, stable power load following is achievable. A slight delay in load following, filtering of high-frequency dynamics, and localized temperature fluctation suggest room for improvement through the development of higher-level control strategies. The simulated coupling of the MAGNET facility lays the groundwork for future digital twin analysis with a coupled MACS-MAGNET HIL demonstration.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2704149','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2704149',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2699518','Evaluation of Neutron-Induced Radiation Generated by a Vehicle-Mounted System for Hazardous Material Detection','유해물질 탐지용 차량 탑재 시스템에서 발생하는 중성자 유발 방사선 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Compact neutron generators enable prompt gamma neutron activation analysis as an effective technique for subsurface material identification in applications such as unexploded ordnance and land mine detection. Their integration into mobile platforms introduces complex mixed neutron-photon radiation fields that require quantitative evaluation. In this study, neutron and secondary gamma radiation transport from a compact deuterium-tritium neutron generator integrated into the optionally manned ground vehicle TAERO, a platform adapted for off-road demining operations, is investigated using Monte Carlo simulations.Spatial distributions of neutron flux and gamma dose rate are analyzed at locations corresponding to the vehicle operator and onboard electronic systems within a material-representative vehicle geometry. Neutron-induced displacement damage in silicon is additionally evaluated as a metric of radiation exposure for electronic components. The analysis focuses on the influence of distance, structural scattering, and local shielding on radiation field characteristics and on the derivation of distance-dependent dose parameterizations relevant to operational deployment.The presented approach establishes a framework for characterizing the radiation exposure associated with compact neutron-based sensing systems deployed on mobile demining platforms. These outcomes are employed to establish operational limits and safety-relevant constraints for the engineering design and integration of mobile neutron-based systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2699518','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2699518',1,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','PL','PL','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2705814','Reliability Analysis and 30 Years of Operational Performance of the GHARR-1 Control Rod System','GHARR-1 제어봉 계통의 신뢰도 분석 및 30년 운전 성능','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This study evaluates the 30-year operational reliability of the Ghana Research Reactor-1 (GHARR-1) control rod drive mechanism (CRDM) from its criticality on December 17, 1994, to August 7, 2025. To address a 4.93-year left-truncation period (1994–1999) when records were undocumented, a conditional reliability framework was utilized to analyze 31 subsequent failure events. Failures were categorized by physical nature (mechanical versus electrical) and maintenance logic (repairable versus non-repairable). The results indicate that the system has transitioned from its stable useful-life phase into a definitive wear-out phase. The most frequent failure mode was the inability of the control rod to move upward (n = 12), exhibiting the highest failure rate (λ = 0.4668 yr−1) and a mean time between failures of 2.14 years. While electrical failures were more prevalent (n = 22), primarily involving instrumentation drift and circuit malfunctions, mechanical failures (n = 9) such as structural wire snaps and sudden rod drops emerged predominantly during the later operational stages (at 25–30 years). The clustering of safety-critical failures in the final five years demonstrates that after 30 years, the CRDM is nearing its design-life threshold. The study concludes that standard annual maintenance is insufficient for aging miniature neutron source reactor facilities and recommends a transition toward predictive, condition-based maintenance strategies. These empirical findings provide essential benchmarks for aging management and life extension protocols for similar research reactors globally.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2705814','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2705814',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','GH;ZM;PK','GH','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106544','Experimental and numerical study of the formation and breakdown of density stratification in an air-steam containment atmosphere with internal cooler and steam injection','내부 냉각기 및 증기 주입이 있는 공기-증기 격납건물 대기에서 밀도 성층의 형성 및 붕괴에 관한 실험 및 수치해석 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','','2026-08-03','','','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106544','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106544',0,'2026-08-16','2026-08-30','active','Crossref + publisher metadata','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106621','A transfer learning-assisted unsupervised clustering approach for unknown fault diagnosis of nuclear power plant equipment','원자력 발전소 장비의 알 수 없는 결함 진단을 위한 전이학습 지원 비지도 클러스터링 접근법','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Chiye Ma; Ting Yu; Hongxiao Chen; Xiaolei Pan; Jun Zhao; Wei Wang','2026-09-20','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Nuclear Power Plant (NPP) equipment works in a harsh, complex environment where distinct faults randomly occur and many of them are unknown to emerge, increasing the shutdown risk and maintenance cost. Advanced techniques are demanded with the capacity to train detection models independent of known fault mode constraints while being sensitive to new types of fault modes. In this study, we propose a transfer learning-assisted unsupervised clustering approach to identify unknown faults in NPP equipment. The approach is built on three modules: fault feature extraction, fault diagnosis, and unknown fault clustering. A feature extractor, based on a multi-scale convolutional neural network, is first employed to extract features from raw data, superior to the single-scale extractors in preventing potential losses of key features. A transfer learning model is then built to enhance the model’s generalization capability to new fault modes. Moreover, an unsupervised K-means clustering model is embedded to cluster unknown faults from known samples. To verify the robustness of the proposed approach, operational data from safety-critical service water pumps in a China commercial NPP are collected and tested. The results show that the proposed approach achieves higher accuracy and stronger robustness in diagnosing unknown faults compared to existing models.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106621','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106621',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','HK;CN','HK','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104726','A variable-domain integral weak solution deep learning method for neutron diffusion calculations in multi-material domains','다중 물질 도메인의 중성자 확산 계산을 위한 가변 도메인 통합 약한 솔루션 딥 러닝 방법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Yang Liu; Dong Liu; Junfeng Wang; Zhen Liao; Kangjun He; Zhenyu Liu; Chao Wu; Xiyan Zhai','2026-09-20','','2026-09','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Neutron diffusion calculations are an important part of reactor physics analysis. In reactor models involving multi-material domains, diffusion coefficients and macroscopic cross sections are typically defined piecewise. Their discontinuities at material interfaces result in discontinuous neutron flux gradients, posing challenges for deep learning-based solvers. In this work, the variable-domain integral weak solution (VIWS) theory is applied to neutron diffusion problems in multi-material domains. A VIWS formulation is derived for complex geometries and multigroup conditions. Based on this formulation, a meshless deep learning method is developed for both fixed-source and eigenvalue problems. A single neural network is used to represent the global neutron flux, while VIWS residual constraints are imposed over the entire computational domain, avoiding special numerical treatments at material interfaces. An antiderivative transformation is also introduced to convert weak-form integral terms with continuous kernels into differential constraints. Numerical results using finite element method (FEM) solutions as references show that VIWS achieves higher accuracy than the standard physics-informed neural network (PINN) and can solve two-dimensional and three-dimensional neutron diffusion problems in multi-material domains. This work provides a new deep learning approach for neutron diffusion problems in multi-material domains and shows its potential for extension to large-scale, complex reactor physics calculations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104726','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104726',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104729','A deployment-oriented single-channel integrity assessment and fault-subtype triage framework for in-core instrumentation loops','노내 계측 루프를 위한 배포 지향 단일 채널 무결성 평가 및 장애 하위 유형 분류 프레임워크','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Youngchul Cho; Keon Il Cha; Jung Hoon Choi; Kyoon Ho Cha','2026-09-20','','2026-09','연구논문','AI·디지털','This study proposes a deployment-oriented single-channel integrity assessment and fault-subtype triage framework for in-core instrumentation loops using only normal-operation data. It couples normal-only reconstruction screening with deterministic rule-based subtype triage, rather than treating the autoencoder as a standalone fault classifier, and is validated using HANARO experimental data. The results indicate that the proposed approach can identify induced single-loop degradation signatures in the tested dataset relative to the calibrated normal baseline, while an extrema-based rule layer provides traceable subtype cues. In addition, runtime integration with a LabVIEW–C# deployment environment was verified using the Open Neural Network Exchange (ONNX) format. These characteristics suggest potential applicability to commercial nuclear power plants only after plant- and loop-specific calibration and validation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104729','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104729',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115223','Investigation on the geometrical representation of an infinite array of bare rod bundle subchannels using Direct Numerical Simulations (DNS)','직접 수치 시뮬레이션 (DNS) 을 사용하여 베어로드 번들 부수로의 무한한 배열의 기하학적 표현에 대한 조사','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Akshat Mathur; Jacob Abraham; Marc Gerritsma; Ed Komen','2026-09-20','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Direct Numerical Simulations (DNSs) are widely considered as an accurate and reliable approach to generate high-resolution data. However, due to the very high computational costs involved, DNS is generally performed in scaled or simpler geometry and at lower Reynolds numbers, which is still representative of the real industrial-scale scenario. In order to represent the flow and heat transport between an array of fuel rods in a reactor core, simulations are conventionally performed in a smaller computational domain with periodic boundaries – often limited to a single interstitial subchannel space or domain around a single pin. The present study examines DNS at a bulk Reynolds number of 5300 for several configurations, including a periodic domain around a single pin, a single subchannel space, and an array of 2 × 2 subchannels. It is shown quantitatively that the proximity of the periodic boundaries in the smaller domains alters the flow physics. The mean flow statistics and integral quantities, which may be used for development and validation of lower-order models, seem to be largely unaffected, despite small differences. However, the periodic boundaries of the small domains cannot faithfully represent the large-scale flow interaction across subchannels. This is observed to have a significant effect on the mean secondary flows in the different geometries. Moreover, the local distribution of the wall shear stress and Nusselt number around the pin are also reported to be affected. Flow pulsations in the narrow gap, typically associated with low P/D ratios, are also observed for the present P/D ratio of 1.326. The frequency of these pulsations is also shown to be significantly affected by the selected flow domain.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115223','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115223',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','EE;NL','EE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112848','Elitism integrated genetic algorithm and differential evolution for in-core fuel management of the Dalat nuclear research reactor','달랏 원자로의 핵심 연료 관리를 위한 엘리트주의 통합 유전 알고리즘 및 차등 진화','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Giang T.T. Phan; Minh Duy Nguyen; Hoai-Nam Tran; Quang Binh Do','2026-09-20','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This study investigates the performance of elitism-integrated Genetic Algorithms (GA) and Differential Evolution (DE) for the in-core fuel management (ICFM) of the Dalat Nuclear Research Reactor (DNRR). An elitist strategy was implemented within both GA and DE frameworks to preserve high-fidelity solutions throughout the evolutionary process. The ICFM problem for the DNRR entails the strategic arrangement of 100 fuel bundles with diverse burnup levels, aiming to maximize fuel utilization while enhancing safety margins. Comprehensive computations were performed to evaluate the sensitivity of the algorithms to the ratio between the elitist archive size ( A ) and population size ( N P ). Results demonstrate that elitism significantly bolsters GA performance, with optimal convergence achieved at N P = 30 and an archive size of 25% of N P . Furthermore, the integration of elitism enables DE to utilize larger population sizes effectively, overcoming the inherent limitations of its basic scheme and yielding superior solution quality. Statistical analysis reveals that the DE variant outperforms GA in terms of both convergence rate and solution diversity for DNRR fuel management. Notably, the optimal core configurations identified by both metaheuristics exceeded the performance of the reference core across all primary objectives, extending reactor operation by approximately 1700 h and reducing the power peaking factor by nearly 4.0%.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112848','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112848',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','VN','VN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112849','Analysis of the ex-vessel phase of the Fukushima Daichi Unit 1 reactor accident using improved MCCI tools that incorporate major modeling contributions by J.M. Seiler','J.M. Seiler의 주요 모델링 기여도를 통합한 향상된 MCCI 도구를 사용하여 후쿠시마 다이치 1호기 원자로 사고의 선박 전 단계 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','M.T. Farmer; S. Mizokami; M. Naitoh','2026-09-20','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Forensics investigations continue at Fukushima Daiichi related to understanding and interpreting severe accident progression at the three affected units following the Great East Japan Earthquake on March 11, 2011. As part of this work, the U.S. Department of Energy sponsored a study in 2016 to examine ex-vessel accident progression in Unit 1 (1F1) based on what was known at the time using the MELTSPREAD and CORQUENCH codes developed by Argonne National Laboratory. Since then, TEPCO has adeptly utilized robot and drone technologies to gain a clearer understanding of conditions within the reactor containments, and for 1F1, these investigations have provided important insights related to MCCI. In parallel, progress has been made on improving melt spreading and MCCI/debris coolability models as part of the Reduction of Severe Accident Uncertainties (ROSAU) program using insights from the experiments as well as findings at Fukushima shared through numerous international collaborations and programs (FACE, ARC-F, …). The objective of this work is to apply these improved models to perform an integrated analysis of the 1F1 ex-vessel accident sequence to gauge their ability to replicate actual end-state debris conditions reported by TEPCO. The analysis spans the time from vessel failure up through cavity flooding and the follow-on debris cooling phase until cavity ablation is arrested. Since this paper is published in a special edition commemorating Jean-Marie Seiler, the MCCI/coolability analysis portion of this work makes note of his key contributions in this field that have been implemented in CORQUENCH as well as other severe accident codes.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112849','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112849',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US;JP','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115199','The history of reactor physics studies for fast-spectrum reactor application in Japan','일본에서 빠른 스펙트럼 원자로 적용을 위한 원자로 물리학 연구의 역사','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Go Chiba; Kenji Yokoyama; Masahiro Fukushima; Taira Hazama','2026-09-19','','2026-12','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The history of reactor physics studies for fast-spectrum reactor application in Japan is reviewed. As a starting point, Tone’s pioneering work on resonance self-shielding calculations for heterogeneous lattices is introduced to illustrate the research environment in the 1970s in Japan. Subsequent developments are then reviewed, including double heterogeneity treatment in power reactors, ultra-fine energy-group calculations for accurate resonance self-shielding treatment, and sodium void reactivity calculations incorporating the neutron streaming effect. Then, the theoretical development in nuclear data adjustment methodologies and reactor physics experiments carried out at the Fast Critical Assembly are reviewed. Finally the legacy acquired through the development of the Japanese prototype fast-spectrum reactor MONJU is referred.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115199','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115199',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115227','Research on a GPU-parallelized method for large-scale fault trees importance analysis in NPPs','NPP에서 대규모 고장수목 중요도 분석을 위한 GPU 병렬화 방법에 대한 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Shen Liu; Shaoxuan Wang; Zhixian Lin; Daochuan Ge; Jie Yu','2026-09-19','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Importance analysis is a key component of Probabilistic Safety Assessment (PSA) in nuclear power plants (NPPs). Based on the minimal cut sets (MCSs) obtained from fault tree analysis, importance analysis identifies the basic events that are important to plant safety. However, fault tree analyses at the scale of NPPs typically generate tens of thousands of MCSs, which impose a substantial computational burden on minimal-cut-set-based importance analysis. To address this issue, this study proposes a GPU-parallelized importance analysis framework. By restructuring the data organization and computational workflow, the proposed framework fully exploits GPU parallelism while maintaining the accuracy of the importance analysis results. To validate the effectiveness of the proposed method, fault tree models under four operating conditions of one Chinese 1000 MWe PWR were selected as case studies and compared with a conventional CPU-based method. The results show that the proposed method achieves a peak speedup of more than 400 times and demonstrates significant advantages in computational efficiency for importance analysis, thus being of great significance for the efficient implementation of PSA for NPPs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115227','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115227',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115218','Boron-containing deposits with tritium activity in the primary circuit of HTR-10: experimental measurements and source analysis','HTR-10의 1차 계통에서 삼중수소 활성을 갖는 붕소 함유 침착물: 실험적 측정 및 원천 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Rui Nie; Xuegang Liu; Liqiang Wei; Yu Wang; Naizhe Zhang; AiXin Zhu; Jianzhu Cao; Feng Xie','2026-09-19','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','The chemical environment of the primary coolant in high-temperature gas-cooled reactors (HTGRs) is complex, where the sources, chemical states, and migration behaviors of impurities affect safe reactor operation. In this study, white crystalline deposits with a mass of (881.70 ± 0.03) mg collected from the dust filter of HTR-10 were analyzed. The morphology of the deposits was analyzed by scanning electron microscopy, while the boron content was analyzed by energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy and inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry, yielding a boron mass fraction of (19.55 ± 0.24)%. Using X-ray diffraction, Raman spectroscopy, and Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy, the samples were found to be composed of NH₄B₅O₈·4H₂O, (NH₄)₃[B₁₅O₂₀(OH)₈]·4H₂O, and H₃BO₃. The thermal behavior of the crystalline deposits was examined by thermal analysis. Based on liquid scintillation counting and high-purity germanium gamma-ray spectrometry, the mass-specific activities of 3 H and 137 Cs, decay-corrected to the date of filter cutting (3 December 2013), were estimated to be (791.55 ± 21.40) and (0.0506 ± 0.0055) Bq/mg, respectively. Based on the structural materials and operating conditions of HTR-10, the boron in the deposits was inferred to originate mainly from boron-containing graphite bricks in the core and boron carbide absorber spheres. The ammonium ions may originate from hydrazine or its decomposition products in the secondary circuit, which could enter the primary circuit through trace cross-wall migration or the decomposition of nitrogen-containing chemicals introduced during maintenance or cleaning. The results reveal the phase characteristics, migration, and deposition behavior of boron-containing impurities in the primary circuit and demonstrate, for the first time, their significant tritium enrichment. This study provides useful guidance for impurity source tracing, coolant chemistry monitoring, purification strategy optimization, and radiation protection during maintenance and decommissioning of HTGRs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115218','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115218',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112834','Integral measurements of (γ,n) reactions and 238U photofission in bremsstrahlung fields','Bremsstrahlung 필드에서 (γ, n) 반응 및 238U 광분열의 적분 측정','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Marek Zmeskal; David Chvátil; Václav Olšanský; Jan Šimon; Michael Němeček; Zdenek Matej; Michal Košt’ál','2026-09-19','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Photonuclear activation and photofission reaction rates were measured in bremsstrahlung fields produced by the MT-25 microtron at primary electron energies of 14.25, 15.90, 17.80 and 19.55 MeV. A stack of activation detectors was used to study ( γ , n ) reactions on F, Ti, Mn, Ni, Co, Cu, Y, Nb, Tm, Au and U, the 169 Tm ( γ , 2 n ) reaction, and 238 U photofission. The photon field was calculated with Geant4 and independently checked with the deterministic code Radiant and with stilbene scintillation spectrometry. The measured reaction rates were compared with calculations based on ENDF/B-VIII.0, ENDF/B-VIII.1, IAEA/PD-2019, JENDL-5 and recent TENDL releases. Several ( γ , n ) reactions were reproduced within a few tens of percent, whereas larger discrepancies were found for threshold-sensitive channels, especially 46 Ti ( γ , n ) , 58 Ni ( γ , n ) and 169 Tm ( γ , 2 n ) . The 238 U ( γ , n ) and 238 U ( γ , f ) reaction rates were generally underestimated by the evaluated data, and the measured fission-to- ( γ , n ) ratio increased from 0.35 to 0.51 over the investigated energy range. The results provide integral benchmark data for photonuclear cross-section libraries in the giant-dipole-resonance region.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112834','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112834',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA;CZ','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112828','Assessment of multi-stage telescopic control rods in a pebble bed reactor, Part I: Mechanical design, neutronic assessment, and economic analysis','페블베드 원자로에서 다단계 텔레스코픽 제어봉 평가, 파트 I: 기계 설계, 중성 평가 및 경제 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ethan Fowler; Gabriel Paramucchio; Loic Durand; Sam Garcia; Ethan Chang; Peter Wilkinson; Farshid Shahrokhi; Hans Gougar; Ryan Stewart; Adrien Couet; Ben Lindley','2026-09-19','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The low power density of Pebble-Bed Reactors (PBRs) results in larger Reactor Pressure Vessels (RPVs) and reactor buildings in comparison to other Generation IV concepts. Multi-stage Telescopic Control Rods (TCRs) have been proposed to reduce both the size and complexity of both the RPV and reactor building to reduce construction costs. This work seeks to explore the neutronic feasibility and economic impact of a three-stage TCR design in the 200 MWth Generic Pebble Bed Reactor (GPBR-200). Modeling of the reactor from startup to the equilibrium core was conducted using Serpent 2 and kugelpy . A wide range of TCR geometries using fresh boron carbide were found to bring the core to a subcritical state following a steam ingress scenario, assuming a uniform distribution of steam throughout the core and no prompt change in core temperatures. Loss of Boron-10 in the control rods was found to be insignificant up to 20 years but became neutronically significant by the reactor’s 30-year maintenance period. However, the depleted control rods were still capable of bringing the core to a subcritical state following a steam ingress scenario. A top-down economic analysis based on cost estimates from the Modular High Temperature Gas-Cooled Reactor (MHTGR) program was then used to assess the economic impact of TCRs when introduced at various stages of reactor design completion. Subject to underlying assumptions, incorporation of TCRs resulted in an estimated 1.7%–4.3% savings, with earlier adoption of TCRs in the design phase resulting in greater savings.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112828','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112828',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106617','Laser welding of critical nuclear materials: A review of mechanisms, defect control, and advanced techniques','임계 핵 물질의 레이저 용접: 메커니즘, 결함 제어 및 고급 기술 검토','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Fajie Zhang; Peilei Zhang; Chao Fang; Maolong Zhang; Qinghua Lu; Xunzuo Su; Peixuan Lei','2026-09-18','','2027-01','리뷰·관점','열수력·유체','Laser welding offers distinct advantages for the fabrication and repair of critical components in Pressurized Water Reactors (PWRs), future Fusion Reactors (e.g., ITER), and Generation IV systems. Its concentrated energy density, minimal thermal distortion, and rapid processing speeds make it highly suitable for joining key nuclear materials. This paper systematically reviews the application of laser welding to: austenitic stainless steels (ASSs) used for PWR primary circuit components and reactor internals; reduced-activation ferritic/martensitic (RAFM) steels, the primary candidate for fusion reactor first wall/blanket modules; and zirconium alloys, the standard material for fuel cladding and assembly grids in light-water reactors. The study focuses on welding processes, weld quality, defect control, and the effects of post-weld treatments on joint performance. To meet nuclear industry demands for in-situ repairs of reactor internals and joining of thick-walled pressure vessels, recent advances in two specialized techniques—underwater laser welding and narrow-gap laser welding (NGLW)—are reviewed. In addition, numerical simulation methods for laser welding are summarized, with emphasis on thermal-field prediction, molten-pool behavior, residual stress and strain evolution, deformation control, and process optimization for nuclear-grade materials. Looking ahead, advancements in high-power lasers, intelligent control, and advanced inspection technologies are positioning laser welding as a cornerstone technology for enhancing the safety, longevity, and efficiency of nuclear power manufacturing and maintenance operations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106617','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106617',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106625','A PSA-informed methodology for alternative source term evaluation in HPR1000','HPR1000에서 대체 선원항 평가를 위한 PSA 정보에 입각한 방법론','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Pingwen Ou; Chao Guo; Peng Chen; Yong Ouyang','2026-09-18','','2027-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Accurate fission product source term assessment is crucial for nuclear safety analysis, equipment qualification, and emergency planning. Traditional deterministic approaches relying on a single conservative scenario fail to capture the enhanced safety features of advanced reactors such as the HPR1000. To address this, a PSA-informed methodology is developed to evaluate alternative source terms by characterizing variability across severe accident phases. Eleven dominant accident sequences (>1% individual, >90% cumulative probability) from Level 1 PSA are simulated using ASTEC to model core degradation through containment release. A PSA-Informed Bootstrap Method (PIBM) is applied to generate statistically robust samples while preserving sequence probabilities. Percentile analyses (5th–95th) reveal that high-frequency small break LOCAs dominate the statistical risk profile. Quantitatively, the gap release duration has a median of 0.066 h (95th percentile: 0.370 h), while in-vessel release dominates with volatile elements reaching 0.70–0.80 and noble gases up to 0.90–0.96. High-frequency sequences contribute over 60% of the total probability. The resulting alternative source term database provides a probabilistic characterization of release periods and radionuclide fractions, supporting the transition from deterministic to risk-informed regulation and enabling applications in equipment qualification, probabilistic source term input for risk-informed emergency planning, and advanced reactor licensing.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106625','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106625',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2724786','Machine Learning-Assisted Calibration of Fission Gas Parameters in the DART Code for U-Mo Fuel','U-Mo 연료에 대한 DART 코드에서 핵분열기체 매개변수의 기계 학습 지원 보정','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Zhi-Gang Mei; Gyuchul Park; Bei Ye; Abdellatif M. Yacout; A. T. M. Jahid Hasan; Benjamin Beeler','2026-09-18','2026-09-18','2026-09-18','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Accurate prediction of fission gas swelling in uranium-molybdenum (U-Mo) fuel is essential for fuel qualification. The primary objective of this work is to calibrate fission-gas-related DART parameters such that the model predictions match experimentally observed fission gas bubble concentrations measured from post-irradiation examination. This work presents a systematic methodology combining machine learning surrogate models with global optimization to calibrate fission gas parameters in the DART fuel performance code. High-throughput DART simulations using Latin Hypercube Sampling explored the DART parameter space for RERTR-5 fuel plates. A neural network surrogate (64-128-64 architecture) achieved exceptional accuracy (RMSE = 0.111, R2 = 0.999), representing 92% error reduction compared to the best tree-based method. Global optimization methods (Evolutionary Algorithm, Efficient Global Optimization) achieved 27% RMSE improvement over previous calibration, substantially outperforming local Pattern Search (18%). Validation against independent fuel plates confirmed parameter transferability with approximately 9% total RMSE reduction across varying fission densities, temperatures, and grain sizes. Bayesian calibration provided uncertainty quantification, revealing that nucleation and re-solution parameters exhibit different identifiability levels, informing priorities for future experiments. This methodology through integrating surrogate modeling, global optimization, and Bayesian uncertainty quantification provides an efficient, reproducible framework for multivariate parameter calibration in mechanistic fuel performance codes.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724786','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724786',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2727813','Assessment of a Physics-Based Model of Microcracking and Microstructural Evolution for Fission Gas Release and Swelling in Ceramic Nuclear Fuels with Multiple Data Sets','다중 데이터 세트를 사용한 세라믹 핵 연료의 핵분열기체 방출 및 팽윤을 위한 미세 분해 및 미세 구조적 진화의 물리 기반 모델 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Charles K. C. Lieou; Wen Jiang; Brian D. Wirth','2026-09-18','2026-09-18','2026-09-18','연구논문','핵연료·재료','We assess the enhanced version of the Simple Integrated Fission Gas Release and Swelling (SIFGRSX) model for fission gas swelling and release, recently developed in the fuel performance code BISON, with simulations of the Risø-AN3, Risø-AN4, and Risø-II3 light water reactor fuel rod irradiation experiments from the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development/Nuclear Energy Agency’s International Fuel Performance Experiments database, as well as the IFA-677.1 and IFA-716.1 tests of the Halden Reactor Project.The wealth of data corresponding to a broad range of operating conditions and initial grain sizes provides important insights that enable a rigorous assessment of the model for microcracking, microstructural evolution, and fission gas behavior beyond that of our earlier work in which we first proposed the model. Through this comprehensive assessment, we recalibrate the SIFGRSX model and identify a small handful of model ingredients that must be adjusted to properly describe the experimental measurements. Our findings provide meaningful improvements to the SIFGRSX model that will be useful for large-scale simulations of nuclear fuel performance.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2727813','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2727813',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104730','Impact of Depletion Chain Files on Isotopic Prediction Accuracy in OpenMC: Analysis of Fukushima Daini Unit 1 BWR Using SFCOMPO Data','OpenMC에서 연소 체인 파일이 동위원소 예측 정확도에 미치는 영향: SFCOMPO 데이터를 이용한 후쿠시마 다이니 1호기 BWR 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Peshwah Mostafiz Rafi; Ashim Mazumder Santo; Md Tanvir Ahmed; Tarikul Islam','2026-09-18','','2026-09','연구논문','핵연료·재료','This study evaluates the impact of depletion chain files on the isotopic prediction accuracy of OpenMC using post-irradiation examination data from five BWR 9×9-9 fuel samples irradiated in Fukushima Daini Unit 1. Six depletion chain files—ENDF/B-VII.1, ENDF/B-VIII.0, ENDF/B-VIII.1, JEFF-4.0, JENDL-5, and CASL—were assessed using a nodal power correction method. All chain files show good agreement (within 10% bias) for U-236, U-238, Pu-240, Pu-242, Pu-238, Nd-143–146, Nd-148, Eu-153, Pm-147, Sm-147, Mo-95, Ru-101, Rh-103, and Cs-133. ENDF/B-VII.1 exhibits higher errors in U-235 prediction, likely due to missing destruction pathways. ENDF/B-VIII.1 shows the widest Pu-239 bias range (37.47%). Nd-142 remains a consistent outlier across all chains, with large negative biases and biases attributed to isobaric interference. Eu, Gd, and Tc-99biases are largely chain-file independent. JENDL-5 shows poor performance for Pm-147 and Sm-154 due to additional production channels and differing fission yield contributors, including minor actinides. It also produces an anomalous overprediction for Sm-149 (∼+28%). JEFF-4.0 provides the best agreement for Ag-109 due to enhanced reaction pathways. Overall, JEFF-4.0 and ENDF/B-VIII.1 demonstrate the most consistent performance, supporting their application in BWR depletion analyses while highlighting areas for further chain file refinement.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104730','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104730',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','BD','BD','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112856','Preliminary conceptual design of a micro supercritical CO2-cooled pressure-tube reactor for unmanned underwater vehicles','무인 수중 차량용 초임계 CO2 냉각 압력 튜브 원자로의 예비 개념 설계','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zhuhan Ran; Chang Xu; Hao Yuan; Pan Wu; Jianqiang Shan','2026-09-18','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Nuclear reactors possess extremely high energy density and can continuously deliver high power within a compact, sealed system over long periods. Utilizing nuclear power as the main power source for Unmanned Underwater Vehicles (UUVs) is an ideal solution to overcome endurance limitations and enable long-term deep-sea missions. This paper proposes a preliminary conceptual design of a micro supercritical carbon dioxide (S-CO 2 )-cooled pressure-tube reactor for UUVs, and conducts core physics calculations and inherent safety characteristic analyses under extreme accident conditions to validate the safety features of this reactor. The reactor has a thermal power of 3.2 MW and a design life of 10 years. It uses heavy water moderation with UN fuel (25% enrichment), with reactivity controlled by control drums and Gd 2 O 3 burnable poison. Core neutronic calculations based on OpenMC show that the core exhibits negative feedback characteristics (fuel temperature coefficient of −1.18 pcm/K core, void reactivity of −1302 pcm), and the control drums provide sufficient shutdown margin (keff < 0.95). Heavy water moderation shifts the neutron energy spectrum towards the epithermal region, with a radial power peaking factor of only 1.044. Steady-state thermal–hydraulic analysis conducted using FLUENT indicates that under normal operation, the maximum cladding temperature is 1063.7 K and the maximum fuel pellet temperature is 1769.0 K, meeting design requirements. Studies on the extreme condition of a large-break loss-of-coolant accident with loss of emergency core cooling system (LBLOCA/LOECC) resulting in complete coolant loss show that the reactor can transfer decay heat from the fuel rods to the moderator solely by radiation and conduction, and then effectively remove the decay heat through convective heat transfer in the moderator. Under such extreme accident conditions, the maximum cladding temperature is 1578.0 K, which is lower than the temperature limit of 12YWT-type ODS steel. The results demonstrate that this design meets the requirements for compactness, long life, and inherent safety, presenting a promising core design concept for UUVs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112856','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112856',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112844','Impact of ideal scaling on BEPU uncertainty and sensitivity analysis of the ACME test facility','이상적인 스케일링이 ACME 테스트 시설의 BEPU 불확실성 및 민감도 분석에 미치는 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ye Yang; Qian Ye; Mengyan Hu; Xueyan Zhang; Jun Yang','2026-09-18','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','In applications of the BEPU approach, uncertainty analyses are typically performed only at the test facility or the reactor, and the impact of model scale on uncertainty quantification remains an open issue to be further investigated. As a first step toward addressing this issue, an ideal scale-up comparative uncertainty analysis scheme is proposed, in which models of different scales for the target test facility are evaluated under identical accident scenarios using the same sampling set. Firstly, the realistically constructed ACME integral test facility is taken as the reference, and its numerical model is rigorously scaled up to the prototype plant size in strict accordance with scaling laws. The nodalization strategy, physical models, boundary conditions, and accident scenarios are also consistently preserved across scales. Then, both models are subjected to the same set of uncertain input parameters and an identical sampling matrix, and a representative 2-inch cold-leg-break loss of coolant accident transient is simulated for direct multiscale comparison. The resulting distributions of key safety-relevant responses are compared in terms of central tendencies, uncertainty bands, and consistency of safety margins, thereby directly quantifying scale-induced effects. The analysis shows that the multiscale BEPU results exhibit good coherence, scale-related biases remain within acceptable limits, and the extrapolation from test facility to prototype is technically justified.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112844','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112844',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112816','Barriers for Adoption and Deployment of Digital Instrumentation and Control Systems for Advanced Reactors and Existing Reactor Modernization','첨단 원자로 및 기존 원자로 현대화를 위한 디지털 계측 및 제어 시스템의 채택 및 배치 장벽','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Edward Chen; Tate Shorthill; Congjian Wang; Ahmad Y. Al Rashdan; Svetlana Lawrence','2026-09-18','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Digital instrumentation and control (DI&C) systems are essential for advanced reactors and modernization of existing nuclear power plants (NPPs). These systems—such as field-programmable gate arrays and programmable logic controllers—are often developed by third-party vendors and provide advanced monitoring that enhances safety, reliability, and efficiency at lower cost than legacy analog components. Digital technologies are mature, widely used in other industries, and proven to improve reliability, flexibility, and cost-effectiveness. Despite these benefits, adoption in the nuclear sector faces major barriers, primarily uncertainties and high costs in licensing due to inconsistent regulatory requirements and lack of industry consensus on best practices. This paper presents findings from 78 stakeholder interviews on challenges and opportunities related to licensing, economics, risk methodologies, and regulatory compliance. While DI&C technologies are technically mature, inconsistent deployment strategies, economic planning issues, regulatory hurdles, and organizational debt have significantly slowed their widespread implementation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112816','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112816',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106586','Developing correlation for prediction of departure from nucleate boiling heat flux in subcooled flow boiling using artificial neural network-aided framework','인공 신경망 지원 프레임워크를 사용하여 아냉각 유동 비등에서 핵비등 열속으로부터의 이탈 예측에 대한 상관 관계 개발','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Thanh-Binh Nguyen; Yoshiyasu Hirose; Akira Satou; Satoshi Abe; Yasuteru Sibamoto','2026-09-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Departure from nucleate boiling (DNB) in subcooled flow boiling leads to an abrupt rise in the heat transfer surface temperature within a short time. In light water reactors, knowledge of DNB heat flux is essential to prevent the catastrophic failure of heating elements. However, accurately predicting DNB heat flux remains challenging due to the underlying physical complexities. Existing empirical correlations, mechanistic models, and AI-aided models in the open literature continue to exhibit certain limitations, such as disagreements on the dominant DNB mechanism or the inherent lack of transparency in black-box AI frameworks. In this study, an artificial neural network (ANN) is utilized to analyze the interrelationships between DNB heat flux and eight influential dimensionless parameters gathered from extensive literature resources. Subsequently, a minimal number of the most critical dimensionless quantities were extracted to develop a novel empirical correlation. The results demonstrate that the proposed model possesses superior characteristics, including high robustness, mathematical simplicity, broad applicability across diverse operating conditions, and independence from thermal–hydraulic parameters.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106586','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106586',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106596','Comprehensive analysis of thermal margins in Cr-coated accident tolerant fuel under steady state PWR conditions','정상 상태 PWR 조건에서 Cr 코팅 사고저항성핵연료(ATF)의 열적 여유도에 대한 포괄적 분석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','R. Deepak Selvakumar; Salem M. Alshehhi; Ahmed K. Alkaabi','2026-09-17','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106596','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106596',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2724780','Preliminary Thermal Analysis of Fort Saint Vrain HTGR Fuel Elements in a Transportation Overpack Configuration','운송 오버팩 구성에서 Fort Saint Vrain HTGR 연료 요소의 예비 열 분석','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Nilay Atul Kulkarni','2026-09-17','2026-09-17','2026-09-17','연구논문','열수력·유체','The Road-Ready Demonstration Project aims to demonstrate that Department of Energy (DOE) managed spent nuclear fuel (SNF) can be loaded into DOE Standard Canisters (SC) for interim storage at the Idaho Nuclear Technology and Engineering Center. The DOE-managed fuel evaluated in this paper is the Fort Saint Vrain (FSV) fuel element which was used in a high-temperature gas cooled reactor (HTGR). The DOESCs are envisioned to be loaded in a Type B transportation overpack designed to meet regulatory requirements in 10 CFR Part 71 which will be obtained from a commercial vendor. In this paper, the effect of two basket designs that hold the DOESCs in place inside the transportation overpack on thermal performance will be evaluated. It is important to conduct thermal analysis to ensure the fuel and overpack component temperatures are within safe range for operation and transportation. In this paper, the DOESC-transportation configuration is thermally evaluated for normal operating conditions and a hypothetical accident scenario as described under 10 CFR Part 71. Different thermal models are employed to understand their effect on the component temperatures including a mesh sensitivity analysis. Steady state analysis is conducted for the normal operating condition and a transient analysis is conducted for accident scenarios. Thermal analysis is carried out using the computational fluid dynamic (CFD) code StarCCM+.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724780','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2724780',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115205','Peridynamic assessment of damage evolution in a full UO2 fuel pellet under RIA-like equivalent thermal-expansion loading','RIA와 동등한 열팽창 하중 하에서 전체 UO2 핵연료 소결체의 손상 진화에 대한 주변 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Ekrem Gulsevincler','2026-09-17','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Reactivity-initiated accidents (RIA) in light water reactors subject UO 2 fuel pellets to rapid thermal transients that can induce fracture and fragmentation. Existing peridynamic (PD) models for nuclear fuel require coupled thermal solvers or imported temperature fields, limiting their utility for rapid parametric screening. The study does not propose a new peridynamic constitutive formulation; rather, it presents a numerically verified and sensitivity-assessed reduced-order peridynamic screening workflow for a full three-dimensional UO 2 pellet, in which the equivalent expansion magnitude and loading rate can be controlled independently. A bond-based peridynamic model with critical stretch-based bond breakage is applied to a full cylindrical pellet (radius 5 mm, height 10 mm) with a pre-existing crack. Equivalent radial thermal expansion is imposed by prescribing a radial velocity on the outer surface corresponding to target temperatures of 1000–2500 °C and loading durations of 10–80 ms, without solving the temperature field. Numerical sensitivity analyses showed that crack-extension and percentile-based local-damage measures were more robust than absolute global damaged-volume fractions, while the principal final-state metrics varied by less than approximately 3.1% over the investigated horizon-ratio range. Independent implementation-level benchmarks quantified the affine-displacement error of the baseline formulation as 10.49% and showed that the finite-width-corrected LEFM fracture stress was bracketed by microscopic first-bond failure and subsequent macro-damage onset. Uniform effective cold- and hot-side property envelopes changed the principal final-state damage metrics by no more than approximately 2.2%, while the normalized crack-extension measure remained unchanged. An axial-loading diagnostic showed that symmetric axial expansion increased the energy-corrected full-domain broken-bond fraction by 85.9%, while normalized crack extension and severe mid-plane damage remained unchanged. The results indicate that damage severity generally increases with target temperature, while loading duration modifies the damage morphology and local severity through the imposed radial velocity. The largest severe-damage fractions occur in selected high-temperature cases at shorter and intermediate loading durations. The equivalent thermal-expansion approach isolates pellet-scale damage sensitivity to prescribed displacement magnitude and loading rate, providing a preliminary screening tool for selecting cases that may require higher-fidelity multi-physics analysis. This work addresses a gap in the literature by demonstrating an equivalent-expansion damage map and computational triage methodology for RIA-like radial expansion conditions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115205','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115205',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115197','Fuel cycle performance of the Fort Saint Vrain reactor','포트세인트브레인 원자로의 연료 순환 성능','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Edan K. Estes-Lumpkin; Donald L. Doyle; Venkata S. Vallabhaneni; Nicholas R. Brown','2026-09-17','','2026-12','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','All modern fuel cycle analysis studies have not considered the historically operated high-enriched uranium (HEU) and thorium (Th) fuel cycles. This represents a significant gap in the literature as these reactors were operated both in the United States and internationally. The work discussed here fills that gap by determining the performance of the Fort Saint Vrain high enriched uranium thorium fuel cycle with respect to natural uranium resource utilization, high-level waste, low-level waste, radioactivity, land use, water use, and CO 2 production. The Department of Energy (DOE) Office of Nuclear Energy (NE) Evaluation and Screening (E&S) study provides information on several different figures of merit for many nuclear fuel cycles employing advanced reactors; however, the study does not include information on high-enriched uranium fueled systems. Fort Saint Vrain and Peach Bottom are the only commercially operated high temperature gas-cooled reactors in United States history, and they operated with a high enriched uranium‑thorium fuel cycle. Determination of the performance of the high enriched uranium thorium fuel cycle is a novel contribution due to the lack of similar investigations in the E&S study as well as in the literature. To understand the performance of the Fort Saint Vrain once-through fuel cycle, a full-core Serpent model with equilibrium fuel masses was created. This was depleted for a length of time determined by the quadratic reactivity model using 6 batches. The resulting burnups and discharge masses were used to compare performance to once-through cycles from the E&S study. There is a gap in similar modeling of the Fort Saint Vrain equilibrium core in the literature, as well as the necessary concentration of information to facilitate modeling Fort Saint Vrain. Once-through cycles from the E&S study for a pressurized water reactor using low-enriched uranium fuel (EG01), a high temperature gas-cooled reactor using high-assay low-enriched uranium fuel (EG02), and a high temperature gas-cooled reactor using high-assay low-enriched uranium and thorium fuel (EG05) were compared to Fort Saint Vrain. The results show that compared to the HTGR and HTGR-Th fuel cycles, Fort Saint Vrain performed better for the natural uranium required, 36.8% less than the HTGR and 33.2 less than the HTGR-TH, CO 2 produced, 21.8% less than the HTGR and 20.4% less than the HTGR-Th, and land use metrics, 20.2% less than the HTGR and 18.7% less than the HTGR-Th. For spent nuclear fuel and high level waste (SNF&HLW) produced, the Fort Saint Vrain fuel cycle produced 27.3% more mass than the HTGR and 2.8% more mass than the HTGR-TH. Compared to the LWR fuel cycle Fort Saint Vrain performed well requiring similar mass of natural uranium, 2.4% more, and land, 4.7% less, as well as producing similar amounts of CO 2 , 2.9% less, but producing 46.5% less SNF&HLW. The activity at 100,000 years is the main disadvantage of the Fort Saint Vrain fuel cycle. Mainly due to the presence of U-233 in the discharged SNF&HLW, Fort Saint Vrain produced significantly more activity at 100,000 years, with activity being 990.5% more than the LWR, 770.2% more than the HTGR, and 143.7% more than the HTGR-TH. The results show that Fort Saint Vrain had benefits regarding mass of natural uranium required and environmental impact; however, its main drawback was a high level of long term activity largely driven by the high U-233 content of the spent nuclear fuel. This suggests that the HEU-Thorium fuel cycle should be operated as a continuous recycle fuel cycle for which the thorium fuel was originally intended.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115197','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115197',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115201','Assessment of temperature-based and vapor-pressure-driven models for CFD simulation of volatile species deposition','휘발성 종 증착의 CFD 시뮬레이션을 위한 온도 기반 및 증기 압력 중심 모델 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Francesco Lobresco; Georg Tiebel; Gian Carmine Conigliaro; Patrick Steinegger; Olha Marinich; Nikolaos I. Prasianakis; Jörg Neuhausen; Bojan Ničeno','2026-09-17','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','The transport and deposition of volatile fission-product species under strong thermal gradients is a safety relevant issue in lead-bismuth eutectic (LBE) systems, yet reliable kinetic models for their treatment in computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulations remain limited. In this work, two complementary modeling strategies for the deposition of PbI 2 are implemented and assessed within a common CFD framework. The first approach is a phenomenological temperature-based model in which deposition is represented by temperature-activated source terms calibrated against experimental observations. The second approach is a vapor-pressure-based kinetic model derived from the Hertz–Knudsen–Schrage formulation, which explicitly links phase change to thermodynamic driving forces and allows for re-evaporation. Both models are implemented in the in-house solver T-Flows and assessed by comparison with thermosublimatography experiments under varying carrier-gas flow rates and experiment durations. The temperature-based model reproduces the main trends of the reference experiment and long-duration deposition profiles, and shows robust behavior within its calibration regime. The vapor-pressure-based model captures reversible phase-change effects and reproduces the experimentally observed decrease in deposition temperature with increasing experiment duration, but systematically predicts broader downstream deposition tails, indicating that the effective condensation kinetics remain slower than in the experimental system. The results highlight complementary strengths of the two approaches: the temperature-based model is well suited for robust engineering-oriented assessments after calibration, while the vapor-pressure-based formulation provides a more physically grounded framework for future extension toward multi-species and multi-phase thermodynamic coupling. The study provides a basis for further development of CFD models for volatile species behavior in complex LBE environments.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115201','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115201',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CH','CH','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112838','Small modular reactors in future energy systems: A study of grid support, distributed energy systems, non-electric applications, and economic drivers','미래 에너지 시스템의 소형모듈원자로(SMR): 계통 지원, 분산형 에너지 시스템, 비전기 응용 분야 및 경제 동인에 대한 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ali Hosin Naseri; Fulong Zhao; Shamsuddeen Lawal','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Small Modular Reactors (SMRs) are emerging as a potential low-carbon technology for grid decarbonization and industrial applications. This paper provides a comprehensive review and critical synthesis of SMR technology and its role in enabling operational flexibility and reliability in future energy systems. We systematically review 70 SMR designs, categorizing them by reactor type, technology readiness level, and operational characteristics. The literature is synthesized on four key aspects: (1) the technological capabilities of SMRs for grid support services, including inertia, frequency control, and load-following; (2) the potential for SMRs to enable non-electric applications such as hydrogen production, seawater desalination, district heating, and industrial process heat; (3) the role of SMRs in distributed energy systems, including microgrids, data centers, military installations, remote mining, and off-grid communities; and (4) the economic drivers and value of SMR integration with energy storage. The review identifies three main findings. First, SMRs demonstrate technical capability to provide essential grid stability services critical for enabling high-penetration variable renewable energy systems. Second, advanced SMR designs, particularly Generation IV reactors, offer high-temperature heat suitable for decarbonizing hard-to-abate industrial sectors, while micro-reactors provide viable solutions for remote and distributed applications. Third, economic analysis indicates that while SMRs show promise, their competitiveness depends on achieving sufficient deployment scale, learning rates of 10–20%, and supportive market frameworks for value-stacking. Significant challenges remain in licensing harmonization, fuel cycle infrastructure development (particularly for high-assay low-enriched uranium), material for high temperature operation, hybrid system control optimization, and public acceptance.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112838','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112838',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112852','Similarity analysis of flow and heat transfer characteristics in Fluid-to-Fluid natural circulation loops','Fluid-to-Fluid 자연 순환 루프에서 유동 및 열전달 특성의 유사성 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','W.B. Xiao; C.H. Dong; Z.B. Nan; B.H. Yan; L.S. Wang','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112852','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112852',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112862','GSA v3: an advanced and flexible approach for adjusting gamma-ray spectrum analysis results','GSA v3: 감마선 스펙트럼 분석 결과를 조정하기 위한 진보되고 유연한 접근법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Lahcen El Amri; Omar El Bounagui; Hamid Amsil; Hamid Bounouira; Abdessamad Didi; Brahim Elmokhtari; Abdelmajid El Badraoui; Abdelwahab Badague','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112862','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112862',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112813','Equivalent RIA Pulse Threshold for comparative assessment of solid fuel–cladding systems','고체 연료 피복관 시스템의 비교 평가를 위한 동등한 RIA 펄스 임계값','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ekrem Gulsevincler','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Reactivity-initiated accidents impose rapid thermo-mechanical loading on fuel–cladding systems and can compromise fuel-rod integrity through fuel heating, gap closure, pellet–cladding mechanical interaction (PCMI), and cladding stress buildup. This study presents a reduced-order framework for comparative screening of conventional and accident-tolerant fuel–cladding systems under an RIA-like power pulse. The model solves one-dimensional transient radial heat conduction in the solid fuel pellet using a lumped effective surface boundary condition, evaluates incremental thermal expansion and pulse-scaled swelling, tracks contact onset, estimates PCMI contact pressure, and calculates a normalized total hoop-stress indicator. An Equivalent RIA Pulse Threshold (ERPT) is defined from prescribed fuel-temperature, contact-pressure, and stress-utilization criteria, while gap closure is treated separately as a contact-onset indicator. The framework is applied to UO 2 , UN, U 3 Si 2 , U-Th MOX, U-Mo, and UC fuels with Zircaloy, SS316, FeCrAl, and SiC claddings. Under the baseline assumptions, finite ERPT values are 13.5 for U-Mo, 16.0 for UO 2 , 17.5 for U-Th MOX, and 20.0 for U 3 Si 2 , whereas UN and UC remain above the investigated range. All finite baseline ERPT values are temperature-controlled. Sensitivity analysis shows that fuel thermal conductivity and the prescribed temperature limit most strongly affect ERPT, while swelling, gap size, differential rod pressure, and cladding expansion mainly influence contact onset and PCMI severity. A tenfold increase in effective contact stiffness shifts UO 2 /Zircaloy and U 3 Si 2 /Zircaloy to pressure-controlled behavior. ERPT is intended as a transparent reduced-order screening metric, not an experimentally validated failure threshold.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112813','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112813',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112843','Development of depletion calculation method considering continuous reprocessing and fuel flowing for molten salt reactors analysis','용융염 원자로 분석을 위한 지속적인 재처리 및 연료 유동을 고려한 연소 계산 방법 개발','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hao Tang; Shunhang Yang; Shuo Li; Yiwei Wu; Qufei Song; Kunfeng Ma; Hui Guo; Jianhui Wu; Hanyang Gu','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','To achieve accurate simulation of the neutronic behavior in liquid-fueled Molten Salt Reactors (MSRs), this paper investigates a flow burnup calculation method of fuel flow effects and continuous refueling processes. Based on a Monte Carlo program, a non-homogeneous burnup matrix reconstruction equation was established according to the flow zones and nuclear reaction rates of the MSR. The Chebyshev Rational Approximation Method (CRAM) was employed to achieve efficient solving of the flowing depletion process. Simultaneously, continuous refueling and continuous reprocessing modules with customizable rates are developed. Using this model to perform numerical simulations on a Single-Fluid Molten Salt Breeder Reactor (MSBR), the results indicate that fuel flow significantly alters the spatial distribution of key nuclides. Specifically, compared to traditional static approximations, the dynamic flow-refueling mode reveals that the equilibrium inventories of short-lived isotopes, such as 135 Xe and 99 Mo, are approximately 60 % and 200 % higher, respectively. The research conclusions confirm that the computational framework constructed in this paper can accurately capture the unique physical characteristics of liquid-fueled reactors, providing a reliable numerical tool for the nuclear analysis and operational optimization of Thorium-based Molten Salt Reactors.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112843','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112843',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112812','Coupling of neutronics, discrete element method, thermal-hydraulics and Voronoï mesh for pebble bed reactor analysis','페블베드 원자로 분석을 위한 중성자 해석, 이산소자법, 열수력 및 보로노이 메쉬의 커플링','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ludovic Jantzen; Yves Robert; Massimiliano Fratoni','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','The simulation of pebble bed reactors (PBRs) is often simplified using homogenized spectral zones, limiting the accuracy of key parameters such as power distribution, fuel burnup and temperatures. To address this, the hyper-fidelity tool (HxF) is extended to incorporate detailed thermal feedback by coupling the Monte Carlo code Serpent with the porous media solver GeN-Foam and a discrete element model (DEM). A novel Voronoï-based mesh mapping strategy is developed to enable efficient and accurate transfer of power density and temperature fields between the coupled solvers, capturing the strong spatial heterogeneities inherent to PBR cores. The methodology is applied to the HTR-10 reactor at equilibrium conditions. Results show that the proposed approach captures significant intra-core power variations, with pebble-wise powers deviating by up to ± 20 % compared to the isothermal model. In addition, the coupled model provides a prediction of the temperature distributions for the core components. The coupling framework enables consistent multi-physics feedback at the pebble scale and demonstrate that the proposed Voronoï-based coupling significantly enhances the fidelity of PBR simulations, providing a robust tool for core design, safety analysis, and fuel management.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112812','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112812',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112832','Characterization of pressure drop in structured packed beds with a layer stacking model','층 적층 모델을 이용한 구조화된 포장층의 압력 강하 특성 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yilong Guo; Bo Li; Kejie Tian; Zhen Yan; Ming Ding; Zehua Guo; Zhongning Sun','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Packed beds are widely encountered in many energy and chemical process industries, where pressure drop directly impacts pumping power and operational efficiency. In recent years, structured packed beds have emerged as a promising option for reducing flow resistance and improving overall performance. This study employs computational fluid dynamics method to investigate the pressure drop characteristics of structured packed beds with cubic, rhombohedral, and orthorhombic configurations. In all three series, the pressure drop increases with superficial velocity, while the friction factor generally decreases with the modified Reynolds number. The effect of porosity on both quantities is rather complicated: the maximum values usually occur at the minimum porosity, whereas their minimum values are observed at intermediate porosity rather than at the maximum porosity. In the cubic and rhombohedral series, both pressure drop and friction factor decrease with increasing spacing between adjacent particles. In the orthorhombic series, however, the pressure drop and friction factor initially decline, then rise, and finally decline again as the spacing progressively increases. At a given porosity, the rhombohedral series exhibits the lowest flow resistance, followed by the orthorhombic series, with the cubic series having the highest. A comparison between the simulation results and classical empirical correlations indicates that existing porosity‑based models are unsuitable for structured packed beds, with average errors exceeding 20 % for each series. By analogy with flow resistance in sudden contraction‑expansion sections, a new correlation based on the layer stacking model is proposed. The correlation achieves better prediction accuracy than traditional models, with average errors of 11.68 % for the cubic series, 10.17 % for the rhombohedral series, and 4.18 % for the orthorhombic series. The results and models presented in this study are helpful for the optimal design of packed bed reactors.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112832','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112832',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112790','A study on post-discharge decay heat evolution &amp; isotopic contribution of uranium, thorium, and TRU-based zirconium hydride fuels in TRIGA Mark II reactor, Bangladesh','방글라데시 TRIGA Mark II 원자로에서 우라늄, 토륨 및 TRU 기반 지르코늄 수소화물 연료의 방전 후 붕괴열 진화 및 동위원소 기여에 관한 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Peshwah Mostafiz Rafi; Mohammad Khan; Ashim Mazumder Santo; Abdur Rahman Antor','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','This computational study investigates the decay heat characteristics and isotopic source term evolution of three nuclear fuel cycles using OpenMC particle transport and depletion: Conventional 235U cycle (Model 1), 233U–Thorium cycle (Model 2), and transuranic (TRU)-loaded cycle (Model 3). Simulations modeled an 800-day irradiation period at 3 MWth (discharge burnup ∼ 50 MWd/kg) across a 1,000-year cooling horizon. During operation, all models reached saturation within 5 days, led by Model 1 in peak decay heat (∼190 kW), followed by Model 3 (∼160 kW) and Model 2 (∼150 kW). Post-discharge decay heat increased with burnup and peaked immediately after discharge before decreasing over time. While all models decayed rapidly for 10 days, Model 3 maintained a long-term thermal burden above 10 3 W after 10,000 days, whereas Models 1 and 2 converged below 10 2 W. Isotopic analysis showed short-lived nuclides (134I, 138Cs, 91Rb) dominating immediately post- discharge. At 2–4 years, Models 1 and 2 consolidated around 90Y and 137mBa, while Model 3 remained driven by alpha-emitting actinides (244Cm, 238Pu, 241Am). By 100 years, Model 3 carried a significantly higher thermal burden dominated by 241Am (∼600 W), whereas Model 2 retained a unique 233U signature. The Wigner–Way approximation proved accurate for conventional cycles (within ± 5.22%) but failed for the TRU cycle (deviations exceeding −50.03% by day 10) due to uncharacterized minor actinide alpha-decay heat. Additionally, multi-percentile sensitivity analysis revealed a secondary isotopic diversity peak near 10^5 days in Model 2 from 4n + 1 neptunium series progeny.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112790','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112790',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','BD','BD','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112819','A coupled compressible multiphase thermohydraulic–neutronics solver for simulating rapid reactivity insertions in molten salt reactors','용융염 원자로에서 신속한 반응성 삽입을 시뮬레이션하기 위한 커플링된 압축성 다상 열수력-중성미자 솔버','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Anna Maître; Nathalie Seiler; Frédéric Bertrand; Axel Laureau; Elsa Merle','2026-09-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','International audience','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112819','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112819',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106615','Numerical correlations for thermal-hydraulic performance of He-Xe and He-Kr binary mixtures in pebble-bed geometries','페블베드 기하학에서 He-Xe 및 He-Kr 이진 혼합물의 열수력 성능에 대한 수치 상관 관계','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Salih Said Çatalbaş; Ali Ti̇fti̇kçi̇; Cemil Kocar','2026-09-16','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','A comprehensive CFD study was conducted to analyze the thermal and hydraulic behavior of He-Xe and He-Kr binary mixtures in pebble-bed geometries with varying Reynolds numbers (10 3 -5×10 4 ) and helium molar fractions (0.2-0.8). The simulations included both transitional and fully developed turbulent regimes, allowing for a systematic assessment of the effect of mixture composition on convective heat transfer and pressure drop. The results showed that the Nusselt number grows monotonically with Reynolds number, with helium-rich mixtures (≥60% He) showing improved heat transfer due to helium''s strong thermal conductivity, while heavier gas mixtures provide lower Nusselt numbers. Pressure drop trends show how gas density and velocity interact, with He-Kr combinations providing more hydraulic resistance than He-Xe at equal compositions. Both accurately predict Nusselt numbers and pressure drops across the studied parameter space, showing good agreement with well-established correlations in the literature. Two correlation models were developed: one that provides mixture-specific power-law relationships and another that generalizes the findings into a composition-dependent framework. Both accurately predict Nusselt numbers and pressure drops across the studied parameter space. The findings highlight the trade-off between thermal performance and hydraulic resistance, and they provide practical guidance for optimizing helium-heavy gas combinations in pebble-bed reactor cooling systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106615','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106615',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2726712','Water-Free and Low-Temperature Cutting Method for Nuclear Facilities: The Effect of Abrasive Hardness on the Cutting Efficiency of Low-Pressure Abrasive Air Jet','원자력 설비의 무수 및 저온 절단 방법: 연마 경도가 저압 연마 에어 제트의 절단 효율에 미치는 영향','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Tao Yang; Changjiang Chen; Huidong Zhang; Lijuan Wang; Yang Du; Chenxu Luo; Fei Huang; Dong Li; Yong Liu','2026-09-16','2026-09-16','2026-09-16','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726712','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726712',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2712102','Multigroup Cross-Section Generation Using OpenMC Fixed-Source Neutron Transport Simulation for Spent TRISO Fuel','사용후 TRISO 연료를 위한 OpenMC 고정 소스 중성자 수송 시뮬레이션을 사용한 다군 단면적 생성','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Brecken Allegood; Rodrigo de Oliveira; Joshua Hanophy','2026-09-16','2026-09-16','2026-09-16','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','One of the main tasks during repository studies is to demonstrate canister subcriticality under various conditions. If this task is tackled using deterministic codes, a suitable set of cross sections must be generated. In this work, OpenMC fixed-source neutron transport simulation was utilized to generate representative condensed and homogenized multigroup cross sections for spent fuel pebbles in a spent fuel canister. The results show a noticeable difference between reactor and canister cross sections. For isotopes of interest such as 235U and 239Pu, fission cross-section differences of up to 29.41% and 16.31% were seen, respectively, showing that such methodologies are necessary to accurately simulate spent fuel canisters via deterministic methods.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712102','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2712102',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2710042','Conceptual Proposal: Reactor Cooled by High-Temperature Sodium Vapor','개념 제안: 고온의 소듐 증기로 냉각된 원자로','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','William Vandyke Snyder','2026-09-16','2026-09-16','2026-09-16','연구논문','열수력·유체','This paper presents a conceptual proposal that uses new ideas and novel combinations of old ideas to construct an inherently and passively safe compact and simple boiling sodium reactor. There is no pretense of detailed neutronic, structural, or thermal-hydraulic analyses. The fuel is particles of metal nitride ceramic or an alloy containing beryllium or niobium. Liquid sodium coolant enters at the bottom, flows around the fuel particles, and sodium vapor exits at the top, circulated by its boiling, not by pumps.The device consists of a reaction region connected to a storage region in which criticality is impossible. There are no control rods. The power output depends on the amount of fuel in the reaction region, which is controlled by gas pressure or electromagnetic pumps, and by circulation velocity and void fraction, which are controlled by gas injection. If the gas pressure or electromagnetic pump fails, fuel flows passively under the influence of gravity from the reaction region to the storage region and the reaction stops.The reaction region is small. The volume of circulating coolant is small. Therefore thermal inertia is small and power output can be changed rapidly. If electricity is produced by magnetohydrodynamic generators or thermoelectric diodes, the entire plant has essentially no moving parts other than the fuel, coolant, and pumps and valves that control gas pressures above the regions.External electrical power is not necessary for safety. Small volumes of sodium vapor and fuel slurry are removed continuously for processing, the latter even during shutdown, which reduces or eliminates the “iodine pit” startup control instability. There is no need to shut down the reactor for refueling. The capacity factor should well exceed 95%. Very high burnup is possible.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2710042','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2710042',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104728','cGAN-Based Triaxial Vibration Data Augmentation and Random Vibration Analysis for Radioactive Material Transport','방사성 물질 운반을 위한 cGAN 기반 삼축 진동 데이터 증강 및 무작위 진동 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Gil-Eon Jeong; Hyun-Geun Song; Yun-Young Yang','2026-09-16','','2026-09','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104728','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104728',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104727','Technical Challenges and Operational Milestones in Scaling Proton Beam Current for Tandem Accelerator-Based BNCT','탠덤 가속기 기반 BNCT용 프로톤 빔 전류 스케일링의 기술적 과제 및 운영 이정표','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Bong Hwan Hong; Hyunwoo Jung; Kyeong Min Kim; Seungwoo Park; Minho Kim; Won Taek Hwang; Chawon Park','2026-09-16','','2026-09','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','High-current electrostatic tandem accelerators are considered a key technology for the development of compact hospital-based neutron sources for Boron Neutron Capture Therapy (BNCT). By employing charge-exchange stripping and SF 6 -gas insulation, these accelerator systems can efficiently generate 2.0–2.5 MeV proton beams for the 7 Li(p,n) reaction while maintaining a compact footprint. Although theoretical designs target beam currents of up to 10 mA to enable clinically practical treatment times, stable high-current operation remains a major technical challenge. As part of the staged development toward a full-scale accelerator system, the newly developed K-500 tandem accelerator at the Korea Institute of Radiological and Medical Sciences (KIRAMS) was successfully commissioned and its initial performance was evaluated. In this study, stable operation of a 500 keV proton beam under atmospheric conditions was demonstrated, achieving a maximum beam current of 7.3 mA. In addition, key technical limitations associated with high-current scaling were identified, and ongoing efforts toward achieving clinically relevant beam currents for accelerator-based BNCT (AB-BNCT) applications are discussed.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104727','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104727',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104724','Radiation dose analysis in the Lithium system rooms during beam-on and beam-off','빔-온 및 빔-오프 중 리튬 시스템 룸의 방사선량 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Gediminas Stankūnas; Andrius Tidikas; Benjaminas Togobickij; Simona Breidokaite; Egidijus Urbonavicius','2026-09-16','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','International Fusion Materials Irradiation Facility – DEMO-Oriented NEutron Source (IFMIF-DONES) is a d–Li neutron irradiation facility developed, which is being designed as part of the European roadmap to fusion-generated electricity. This work presents shielding analyses to support the design of the Test Cell floor and the safety assessment of lithium system rooms under beam-on and beam-off conditions. A detailed MCNP model of the Lithium Loop Cells (LLC) room, including the new Dump Tank baseline, Heat Exchanger, and electromagnetic pumps, has been developed and integrated into the main building model. The model includes the shielding barrier configuration and relevant piping. Shielding calculations are performed to estimate the required thicknesses of the cover and wall, considering space limitations in the LLC and the use of different materials, such as ordinary and heavy concrete. In addition, the radiation dose in the LLC is re-evaluated using updated Activated Corrosion Product (ACP) source terms. The results provide updated dose maps to support maintenance planning and safety assessment of the lithium systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104724','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104724',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115219','International study of fuel performance codes for failure predictions of pre-hydrided Zircaloy cladding during RIAs','RIA 중 사전 소수 지르칼로이 피복관의 고장 예측을 위한 연료 성능 코드에 대한 국제 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Seokbin Seo; Charles Folsom; Colby Jensen; David Kamerman; Vincent Georgenthum; Jerome Sercombe; Francisco Feria; Luis Enrique; Vincenzo Romanello; Anthony Kececioglu; Andras Vanyi; Tasaki Yudai; Charles Cheron; Wonkyo Cho; James Corson; Katalin Kulacsy; Martin Dostal; Asko Arkoma','2026-09-16','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','This paper summarizes the outcomes from the second part of the High Burnup Experiments in Reactivity Initiated Accidents (HERA) modeling and simulation (M&S) exercise. International collaboration was relied upon to assess fuel-cladding behaviors during reactivity-initiated accident (RIA) scenarios by using various fuel performance codes. The goal of this exercise was to provide data from well-characterized experiments for code validation and to compare fuel performance predictions between codes. Four as-run HERA experiments were carried out on unirradiated but oversized UO 2 fuel with pre-hydrided Zircaloy (Zr) cladding under transients simulating RIA. These experiments were replicated in the computational model, and thermo-mechanical simulations were performed using various fuel performance codes. While all simulations predict the expected fuel and cladding behaviors during RIA transients, comparison of the mechanical models utilized by each of the various codes reveals key differences that serve as the main drivers of deviations in predictions of fuel-cladding behaviors during the pellet cladding mechanical interaction (PCMI) phase. Furthermore, a comparison study of various failure models illustrated how different failure models vary in their cladding failure predictions. The outcomes from this work will improve the understanding of how different mechanical and failure models can be used to predict PCMI-induced failure. Future studies aim to reduce the uncertainties associated with thermal-hydraulic (TH) models during the post-PCMI phase in order to foster better interpretation of experimental data.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115219','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115219',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US;FR;ES;CZ;HU;JP;FI','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112830','Three-stage cascade fault detection for safety-class Motor-Operated Valves using vibration signals','진동 신호를 사용하는 안전 등급 모터 작동 밸브를 위한 3단계 캐스케이드 결함 감지','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Wenlei Jin; Wenbin Tang; Helin Gong; Jie Liu; Minggang Li; Yingting Luo','2026-09-16','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112830','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112830',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112857','Numerical study of the effects of interconnecting opening geometry on PCS-driven natural circulation and steam stratification in a multi-compartment containment','다중 구획 격납건물에서 PCS 구동 자연 순환 및 증기 층화에 대한 개구 기하학의 상호 연결 효과에 대한 수치 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jiahui Zhang; Zongwen Hu; Haozhi Bian; Feng Liu; Li Gao; Tongyu Wu; Yongan Ji; Song Ma; Zhongning Sun','2026-09-16','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112857','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112857',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112842','Forward ensemble machine learning for grouped source term prediction in nuclear emergency response','핵 비상 대응에서 그룹화된 선원항 예측을 위한 순방향 앙상블 머신 러닝','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Osamong Gideon Akou; Xuan Wang; Shuhuan Liu; Xinwei Liu; Boyang Liu; Ailing Zhang','2026-09-16','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Major nuclear accidents reveal critical limitations in rapid source term prediction during emergency response. Conventional high-fidelity simulation approaches are computationally expensive and unsuitable for near-real-time decision-making. This study develops a machine learning surrogate framework to predict grouped radionuclide source terms-noble gases, iodine, and particulates-under a hypothetical containment-bypass scenario for the CAP1400 reactor. Using 3000 RASCAL-generated simulation samples for training and testing, three ensemble models were evaluated: LightGBM, Stacking, and CatBoost. LightGBM achieved the best overall performance on unseen test data (R 2 = 0.714) with near-instantaneous inference (∼ 0.001 s). Noble gases showed the highest predictive accuracy (test R 2 = 0.762), whereas particulates remained the most challenging target (R 2 = 0.58–0.74). SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP) analysis identified mass number, core uncovered time and particulate concentration as dominant predictive features. The results demonstrate the potential of machine learning surrogate models to provide rapid and reliable source term estimates for near-real-time nuclear emergency response.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112842','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112842',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112853','Experimental investigation of single-bubble dynamics and apparent drag in a liquid metal under narrow-gap confinement','좁은 갭 구속 하에서 액체 금속의 단일 기포 역학 및 겉보기 항력에 대한 실험적 조사','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Xuanyou Yan; Xianghao Fu; Guangquan Zhu; Zhenhua Sheng; Fang Liu; Shengfei Wang','2026-09-16','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Gas–liquid two-phase flow is important to the thermal–hydraulic performance of liquid–metal-cooled nuclear systems, including liquid–metal-cooled reactors and compact heat-transfer channels in small modular reactors (SMRs). In narrow gaps, bubble confinement affects interfacial momentum exchange, pressure-drop behavior, and the reliability of interfacial drag models. To provide experimental data for confined liquid–metal bubbles, liquid gallium was selected as the working fluid and a visualization facility was developed. Single-bubble rising experiments were performed at channel gaps of 1.5–3.0 mm. High-speed imaging and image processing were used to obtain the projected-area equivalent diameter, aspect ratio, terminal velocity, and apparent drag coefficient. The results show that increasing geometrical confinement induces progressive bubble deformation. This deformation is accompanied by reduced terminal velocity and enhanced apparent drag resistance. The 2.0 mm gap exhibits transitional behavior between weak and strong confinement. Based on the experimental data, an empirical correlation for bubble morphology was established. By incorporating the geometrical confinement parameter β into the Re-Eo framework, a confinement corrected drag correlation was developed. The proposed correlation accurately predicted drag coefficients under different gap conditions, with all predictions falling within a ±15% error band. These results provide experimental data for evaluating and refining interfacial drag closure relations used in thermal–hydraulic models of compact channels relevant to liquid–metal-cooled reactor systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112853','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112853',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112845','Development of a 2D SLAM based radiation mapping system for surface contamination measurement','표면 오염 측정을 위한 2D SLAM 기반 방사선 매핑 시스템 개발','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Sujung Min; Sujin Kim; Bum Kyoung Seo; Sang bum Hong','2026-09-16','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','This study developed a SLAM-based radiation measurement system using an autonomous mobile robot and a LiDAR sensor to improve the quantitative accuracy of surface contamination assessments. Conventional fixed or manually operated radiation detection systems have limitations in performing precise evaluations over wide areas. To resolve these issues, the proposed system integrates autonomous navigation, real-time localization, and dynamic measurement correction. Correction factors derived from static experiments are applied in real time to compensate for CPS errors caused by variations in detector height and speed, enabling accurate measurements under various conditions. Scanning experiments were conducted using Co-60 radiation sources. After applying the correction factors, the average deviation was reduced to within 10%, with lower scanning speeds resulting in further error reduction. This system, equipped with a real-time correction algorithm, serves as a foundational technology for dynamic radiation mapping and has potential applications in facility decommissioning and precision measurement of radioactive contamination areas.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112845','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112845',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106610','Analysis of the source term and prediction of the radioactivity releases for a hypothetical accident at ETRR-2','ETRR-2에서의 가상의 사고에 대한 방사능 방출의 선원항 및 예측 분석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Magdy M. Zaky; Mohamed A. Elsaied; Ahmed Abdel-hameed; Mahmoud R. AboElross','2026-09-15','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Evaluating radioactive release and its impact is very important for the safety of research reactors, especially those located near populated areas. In this work, a deterministic and conservative analysis is carried out to study the source term and the possible radiological consequences of a hypothetical beyond design basis accident at the ETRR-2 Research Reactor. The accident scenario assumes a large break loss of coolant due to rupture of the tangential irradiation tube, together with failure of cooling systems, which may lead to severe core damage. The radionuclide inventory is calculated using the ORIGEN-S code in the SCALE package, assuming a maximum irradiation time of 220 full power days. The total uranium mass and irradiation history are based on equilibrium core conditions obtained from WIMS/CITATION fuel management calculations. Since no dedicated cross-section libraries are available for material testing reactors, different ORIGEN libraries are evaluated and compared with MCNP depletion results for the same irradiation conditions. The comparison shows that libraries representing softer neutron spectra provide better agreement, supporting the selection of an appropriate library and improving the reliability of the inventory estimation. A conservative assumption of 80% core damage is applied. The source term is developed based on the updated U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission Regulatory Guide 1.183, Revision 1 (2023), which introduces revised radionuclide grouping and release fractions compared to the older 2000 version used in most previous studies. Atmospheric dispersion is analyzed using the HOTSPOT code with site-specific meteorological data covering more than ten years. The results show that noble gases and iodine isotopes are the main contributors to the release. The maximum dose reaches about 1.9 Sv at around 400 m, and it is strongly affected by atmospheric stability conditions, highlighting the sensitivity of the results to atmospheric parameters.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106610','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106610',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','EG','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2726702','Heat Flux Partitioning Evaluation in Flow Boiling Interface Capturing Simulations','유동 비등 인터페이스 캡처 시뮬레이션에서의 열유속 분할 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Nicholas J. Mecham; Om Jagtap; Igor A. Bolotnov','2026-09-15','2026-09-15','2026-09-15','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726702','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726702',0,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104713','Reaction-dissolution characterization of corrosion products Ni and NiO under acid shutdown conditions','산성 셧다운 조건에서 부식 생성물 Ni 및 NiO의 반응-용해 특성 규명','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Genxian Lin; Lve Lin; Fuhai Li; Wentao Zhou','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','ABSTRACT The dissolution and release behavior of nickel (Ni) and nickel oxide (NiO), primary corrosion products in nuclear reactors, were investigated under acid shutdown conditions. This study employs thermodynamic and kinetic analyses to elucidate the dissolution mechanisms and their dependencies on water chemistry parameters across varied reactor shutdown scenarios. The equilibrium constants, reaction energy barriers, and rate constants were determined for key reactions involving Ni and NiO. Results indicate that dissolution kinetics are significantly influenced by boron and lithium concentrations, temperature gradients, and the presence of oxidants such as H 2 O 2 . Specifically, Ni dissolution is accelerated in oxidative environments, while NiO dissolution is hindered by prolonged reaction half-lives at lower temperatures. The study identifies optimal operational conditions to enhance dissolution efficiency, providing critical insights for mitigating radiation hazards during reactor maintenance. These findings contribute to a deeper understanding of corrosion product behavior, ensuring safer and more efficient nuclear reactor operations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104713','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104713',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104711','Laboratory evaluation of desiccation cracking and microstructure change of carbon fiber-reinforced bentonite subjected to thermo-hydro coupled environment for geological repositories','지층처분장의 열-수력 커플링 환경에 노출된 탄소섬유 강화 벤토나이트의 건조 균열 및 미세구조 변화에 대한 실험실 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Abdullah Azzam; Yong-Rak Kim; Jongwan Eun; Seunghee Kim','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','ABSTRACT Deep geological repositories that utilize bentonite clay as an engineered barrier material offer a promising solution for isolating and containing waste from the surrounding environment. However, desiccation cracking of bentonite under thermo-hydro coupled conditions may compromise its effectiveness as a barrier material. This study developed a laboratory testing method to evaluate the use of carbon microfiber reinforcement in reducing desiccation cracking under thermo-hydro environment. Bentonite samples containing varying carbon fiber contents and lengths were exposed to elevated temperatures (150°C) on one boundary to mimic heat from nuclear waste canisters, while water infiltration was introduced from the opposite boundary to represent surrounding host rock conditions. Temperature and moisture changes were continuously monitored, and internal microstructural changes were captured using X-ray computed tomography. Results showed that carbon microfiber reinforcement significantly reduced desiccation cracking. Samples with 1% carbon fiber and 12.5 mm fiber length performed best, exhibiting substantially lower crack geometry than plain bentonite. In contrast, 2% fiber content increased cracking, which may be attributable, in part, to localized fiber entanglement, though this requires further quantitative verification. Carbon fibers also improved thermal distribution and moisture retention, which delayed desiccation and can potentially enhance the performance of bentonite barriers in nuclear waste repositories.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104711','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104711',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104721','Integrating Compartment-Based Hydraulic Flood Propagation with Seismic Fragility for Dynamic Risk Assessment of Combined Events in Nuclear Power Plants','원자력 발전소의 복합 사건에 대한 동적 위험 평가를 위해 격실 기반 침수 전파와 지진 취약성 통합','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Sunghyon Jang; Jaehyun Cho','2026-09-15','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study presents a time-dependent dynamic probabilistic risk assessment (PRA) framework that integrates seismic equipment fragility, compartment-based hydraulic flood propagation, component water-height fragility, and event-tree quantification. The framework is applied to a combined earthquake and internal-flooding event in a nuclear power plant turbine building. The risk metric is the conditional core damage probability (CCDP); results are conditional on the specified combined initiating scenario and do not represent hazard-weighted core damage frequency (CDF). The analysis covers four peak ground acceleration (PGA) levels: 300, 600, 900, and 1,200 gal. At t = 1,500 s, the ratio of the emergency diesel generator (EDG)-failure core-damage sequence probability to the EDG-available core-damage sequence probability increases from 0.111 at 300 gal to 12.0 at 600 gal, indicating that the dominant core-damage sequence changes between these two analyzed ground-motion levels under the PGA-independent base leakage-area assumption. Under an illustrative PGA-dependent barrier-leakage scaling, the crossover interval shifts to 900–1,200 gal. The time margin between total CCDP reaching 0.5 and deterministic EDG submergence is quantified for each PGA. The framework supports combined-hazard scenarios not readily represented by static event trees.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104721','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104721',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','JP;KR','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104722','Few-shot class-incremental fault diagnosis in nuclear power plants via a static network-based method','정적 네트워크 기반 방법을 통한 원자력 발전소의 Few-Shot Class-Incremental Fault Diagnosis','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Meng Lin; Daizheng He; Jinpei Wang; Shiqi Zhou; Yanfeng Lv; Jiashu Li; Shilong Huang; Zongwei Yang; Ke Huang','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The operational safety of nuclear power plants (NPPs) imposes a lifelong adaptability requirement on fault diagnosis systems: they must recognize newly emerging fault types from very limited samples while retaining diagnostic performance on previously learned faults. However, conventional incremental learning methods typically rely on parameter fine-tuning or storage of historical data, which conflicts with the data minimization and algorithmic verifiability principles in nuclear safety regulation. To address this few-shot class-incremental fault diagnosis challenge, this paper proposes a static network-based approach that fundamentally circumvents catastrophic forgetting. After training a one-dimensional convolutional neural network feature extractor on base classes with a joint cross-entropy and center loss, all extractor parameters are frozen, and incremental class learning is accomplished solely by expanding a non-parametric K-nearest neighbor classifier. A dedicated joint preprocessing strategy combining data centering and logarithmic normalization is introduced to handle the multi-source heterogeneous sensor data exhibiting cross-order-of-magnitude scale disparities, thereby enhancing the saliency of weak fault signals. The feature extractor adopts grouped convolution to model individual sensor dynamics, followed by channel fusion and hierarchical abstraction. In a 3-way 5-shot class-incremental scenario on a CPR1000-based NPP simulation dataset covering 19 fault types, the proposed method achieves an average accuracy of 94% and a performance degradation as low as 0.08%, significantly outperforming mainstream dynamic-architecture methods such as EWC, LwF, iCaRL, and APISs. Ablation studies confirm the effectiveness of each component, including the preprocessing strategy, the 1D-CNN extractor architecture, and the KNN classifier.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104722','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104722',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104708','Factor effect analyses on radionuclide release rate from a spent nuclear fuel transport cask submerged in deep sea for surrogate model development','대리모형 개발을 위해 심해에 잠긴 사용후핵연료 수송통의 방사성핵종 방출률에 대한 요인효과 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Guhyeon Jeong; Sanghoon Lee','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','In Korea, maritime transportation of spent nuclear fuel (SNF) is considered as a highly plausible management option. It is necessary to develop technology to assess the radiological impact of SNF cask submersion accidents to manage the risk caused by the maritime transportation of SNF and to find the optimal transport route to minimize the risk. In our previous work, a computational fluid dynamics (CFD) model was developed to accurately evaluate the mass release rate of radionuclides from a submerged cask. The final goal of this study is to establish a methodological framework to develop a surrogate model of the developed CFD model and integrate it as a subroutine into the SNF maritime transportation risk assessment code. This paper addresses several key aspects, including the definition of the input space and the determination of the surrogate model''s validity domain, in order to ensure accurate predictions across a wide range of accident and transport scenarios. A comprehensive factor effect analysis was conducted to support efficient training data generation, identifying key factors that significantly influence the release rate and temperature of radionuclides when a SNF cask is lost at sea.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104708','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104708',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104723','Experimental investigation of damage mechanisms and limit states for nuclear power plant electrical cabinets using tri-axial shaking table tests','3축 진동대 시험을 이용한 원자력 발전소 전기 캐비닛의 손상 메커니즘 및 한계 상태에 대한 실험적 조사','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Bub-Gyu Jeon; Dong-Uk Park; Sung-Jin Chang; Young-Soo Jeong; Jae-Wook Jung; Seunghyun Eem','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Seismic fragility tests using tri-axial shaking table excitation were performed on representative safety-related electrical cabinets for nuclear power plants, namely two MCCs, two switchgears, an inverter, a battery charger, and a load center, to evaluate their ultimate limit states and dynamic damage mechanisms in this study. The results showed that the MCCs with complex internal structures exhibited a strong interaction between structural failure and malfunction. In contrast, power conversion devices such as inverters and battery chargers tended to experience malfunction before structural failure. Equipment containing heavy components, such as switchgear and the load center, sustained structural failure at corresponding sub-components and supporting structures. In particular, structural failure and malfunction were frequently observed when the peak acceleration at critical locations exceeded approximately 21 g. Resonance frequency analysis revealed that structural failure or malfunction was accompanied by the resonance frequency reduction of approximately 12% or more in most specimens. Unlike previous studies limited to a small number of specimens, this study presents ultimate-state data for seven types of full-scale electrical cabinets and is therefore expected to provide fundamental data for improving seismic fragility analysis, for optimizing equipment-specific seismic design and seismic retrofitting, and for establishing practical guidelines for field inspection and monitoring.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104723','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104723',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104718','Effects of microstructure fraction on J-R fracture resistance of SA508 Gr.1A low-alloy steels','미세조직 분획이 SA508 Gr.1A 저합금강의 J-R 파단 저항성에 미치는 영향','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Se-mi Hyun; Min-Chul Kim; Seokmin Hong; Jongmin Kim; Seok Su Sohn','2026-09-15','','2026-09','연구논문','핵연료·재료','SA508 low-alloy steel is a candidate material for main steam line piping, and its microstructure and mechanical properties are significantly influenced by the cooling rate after austenitizing. This study quantitatively analyzed the effect of cooling rate–induced microstructural changes on J -R fracture resistance. As the cooling rate increased, the fraction of coarse ferrite and pearlite decreased, while the formation of low-temperature transformation microstructure increased. As a result, the strength increased, whereas the J -R fracture resistance increased up to the air cooling (AC) and subsequently decreased with a further increase in the cooling rate. These changes in mechanical properties are considered to be associated with these low-temperature microstructures induced by the increased cooling rate. The relationship between microstructure and J Ic was quantitatively evaluated using a predictive model incorporating grain size and strength. For specimens with mixed microstructures of ferrite, pearlite, and bainite (FC, AC, AQ), the predicted values of J Ic showed good agreement with experimental results. However, for WQ, the experimental J Ic was approximately 140 kJ/m 2 lower than the predicted value.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104718','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104718',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR;JP','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104720','Development of stratification analysis capability in the SAFARI MCCI module and validation with the MOCKA 3.1 experiment','SAFARI MCCI 모듈의 층화 분석 기능 개발 및 MOCKA 3.1 실험을 통한 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Jun Sung Choi; Tae Hwan Kim; Jin-Woo Kim; Eung Soo Kim; Hyun Sun Park','2026-09-15','','2026-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study extends the MCCI analysis capability of the SAFARI (Safety Analysis Code for Severe Accident Risk Identification) code by enabling the evaluation of stratified corium behavior during Molten Core–Concrete Interaction (MCCI). The extended MCCI module considers Molten Corium Stratification (MCS) as a plausible late-phase configuration, the occurrence of which depends on reactor type and accident progression conditions, but remains important to evaluate in severe accident analyses. The MOCKA 3.1 experiment, which clearly demonstrates this stratification-induced ablation under dry cavity conditions, is used for validation. To represent stratified corium configurations within the SAFARI MCCI module, a stratification analysis framework was established, supported by essential modeling elements such as metallic crust representation and temperature treatment based on alumina-based oxide phase data. Simulation results successfully reproduce key thermal and ablation characteristics observed in the experiment, including intensified ablation beneath the metal layer following stratification. These findings demonstrate the applicability of the extended SAFARI MCCI module for analyzing stratification driven MCCI behavior in dry cavity scenarios.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104720','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104720',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112815','Structural design and heat transfer performance study of a diverging-converging sodium heat pipe via numerical simulation','수치 시뮬레이션을 통한 발산 컨버징 소듐 히트 파이프의 구조 설계 및 열전달 성능 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jiajun Zhao; Jian Liu; Yuqing Chen; Pengfei Liu; Dongjie Sheng; Chengsheng Xiao; Jinyang Zhao','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','This paper proposes a novel heat pipe with a diverging evaporator section and a converging condenser section to overcome the sonic limit of heat pipes and improve their heat transfer efficiency. The heat transfer performance and structural advantages of this design are systematically studied through a combination of theoretical modeling and numerical simulation. A three-dimensional transient heat transfer numerical model is established using ANSYS Fluent to analyze the thermal performance under different diverging-converging angles of 0° (traditional cylindrical), 0.2°, 0.4°, 0.6°, 0.8°, and 1.0° at heating powers of 300 W, 500 W, and 700 W. The research results indicate that the designed diverging-converging sodium heat pipe meets the structural design requirements. The diverging structure in the evaporator section effectively reduces the vapor flow velocity, avoids the sonic-limit effect during startup, and promotes full evaporation. The converging structure in the condenser section provides an accelerated channel for condensed liquid. The temperature difference of the heat pipe exhibits a nonlinear relationship with heating power, decreasing first and then increasing. At 500 W, the temperature difference is the smallest, indicating optimal heat transfer performance. Compared to traditional cylindrical heat pipes, the diverging-converging structure reduces the total thermal resistance by approximately 28.56 %, improves condensation heat-transfer coefficient by up to 47.23 %, and enhances the overall heat transfer coefficient by 39.98 %. This design offers significant application advantages in fields such as heat recovery, electronic cooling, and nuclear reactor core heat transfer.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112815','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112815',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112825','Assessing the value of future ZED-2 experiments for molten salt reactor temperature reactivity validation','용융염 원자로 온도 반응성 검증을 위한 향후 ZED-2 실험의 가치 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Stephen Marshall; Julian Atfield; David R. Novog','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Zero Energy Deuterium (ZED-2) reactor experiments at the Canadian Nuclear Laboratories have the potential to support the development of advanced power reactors. Relevant experimental data from ZED-2 could be used to validate code predictions of important quantities such as the reactivity temperature coefficient (RTC). However, ZED-2, was originally designed to support CANDU reactor applications, and its applicability to alternate designs is not well established. This work provides a thorough example of how a proposed experiment can be assessed based on its potential to reduce application response uncertainty within the TSUNAMI validation framework. A similar approach could be adopted by reactor designers and experimentalists to explore and optimize future benchmark experiments for novel applications. This work considers two potential ZED-2 experiments for validating predictions of molten salt reactor (MSR) RTCs. The results indicate that valuable experimental data can be gathered from appropriately designed ZED-2 experiments. However, configurations should minimize reliance on driver fuels as they significantly reduce the value of the experimental data.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112825','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112825',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112791','A novel component mode synthesis-proper orthogonal decomposition-reduced-order model for flow-induced vibration prediction of nuclear fuel rods using limited measurement samples','제한된 측정 샘플을 사용하여 핵연료봉의 유동유발진동 예측을 위한 신규 부품 모드 합성-정규 직교 분해-감소-차수 모델','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Shuguang Yang; Xiaohui Liu; Hongbin Peng; Chuan Lv; Chuan Wu; Guangyun Min','2026-09-15','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Flow-induced vibration of nuclear fuel rods is a critical issue affecting the structural integrity, operational safety, and long-term reliability of advanced nuclear energy systems. However, high-fidelity fluid–structure interaction simulations required for accurate flow-induced vibration prediction are often computationally expensive, limiting their use in rapid assessment and design optimization. To address this challenge, this study proposes a reduced-order model based on component mode synthesis and proper orthogonal decomposition for reconstructing full-field flow-induced vibration responses of fuel rods from sparse measurements. The fuel rod is first partitioned into subcomponents according to the locations of measurement and target points, and the structural degrees of freedom are reduced using the Craig-Bampton component mode synthesis method. Static loading cases are then designed to construct snapshot matrices, from which dominant modes are extracted. Based on sparse measured displacement responses, the corresponding mode coefficients are identified through Tikhonov regularization, enabling efficient prediction of full-field dynamic responses. The proposed method is applied to circular and helical cruciform fuel rods immersed in lead–bismuth eutectic coolant. Results show that the method accurately predicts both natural frequencies and flow-induced vibration responses, achieving model reduction ratios of 98.21 percent and 97.81 percent, respectively. Even under 20 percent measurement noise, the coefficients of determination remain as high as 0.957 and 0.934, demonstrating strong robustness and prediction accuracy. The proposed method provides an efficient and reliable tool for rapid flow-induced vibration response prediction and can support the vibration-resistant design and safety assessment of nuclear fuel rods in advanced energy systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112791','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112791',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2727815','Safe Use of AI as Part of the Control Loop in Nuclear Facilities','원자력 시설에서 제어 루프의 일부로 AI의 안전한 사용','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Emilie Greaker; Rune Winther; Sizarta Sarshar','2026-09-14','2026-09-14','2026-09-14','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2727815','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2727815',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','BG','BG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104705','Theoretical assessment of energy-selective transmutation in spent nuclear fuel','사용후핵연료에서 에너지-선택적 핵변환에 대한 이론적 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Alberto Mizrahy Campos; Bruno Melo Mendes; Tarcisio Passos Ribeiro de Campos','2026-09-14','','2027-02','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104705','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104705',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104712','Modeling of the high burnup structure formation in nuclear fuels: a bubble pressure-based approach','핵연료에서 고연소도 조직 형성에 대한 모델링: 기포 압력 기반 접근법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','JangSoo Oh; YongSik Yang; JuYeop Park; Ho Jin Ryu','2026-09-14','','2026-09','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','A bubble pressure-based model was developed to predict the formation of high burnup structure (HBS) in nuclear fuel pellets. In contrast to existing models that predominantly focus on burnup, the proposed model comprehensively considers physically relevant parameters, including fission gas concentration, bubble size, bubble density, and porosity, based on the hypothesis that HBS formation is driven by grain subdivision resulting from bubble over-pressurization. The model was implemented in the FRAPCON-4.0 Patch 1 fuel performance code and validated against in-pile experimental data. The influence of power history on HBS evolution was investigated, indicating that the onset and width of HBS are significantly affected by the time-dependent behavior of fuel temperature and fission gas distribution. These findings demonstrate that the coupled effects of power history, temperature, and fission gas behavior play a critical role in accurately modeling HBS formation, enhancing the reliability of high burnup fuel performance predictions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104712','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104712',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115210','An operating-experience–augmented fragility framework for SiC in TRISO fuel','TRISO 연료에서 SiC를 위한 작동 경험 증강 취약성 프레임워크','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Makuteswara Srinivasan','2026-09-14','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study develops an operating-experience (OpE)–augmented fragility framework to evaluate silicon carbide (SiC) layer degradation in TRISO fuel for pebble bed reactors. Intrinsic SiC fragility is anchored using a normalized hybrid synthetic brittleness index (NHSBI) regression as a deterministic material-state descriptor. OpE effects, including persistent thermal exposure, transient temperature gradients, and localized cycling, are represented through physically interpretable amplification multipliers. Parametric evaluations are performed under AVR-anchored operating conditions with explicit treatment of epistemic uncertainty arising from sparse high-temperature data. Results indicate that short-duration thermal excursions typically produce modest amplification when considered in isolation, whereas persistent boundary-condition degradation and coupled mechanical–chemical processes provide plausible pathways to risk-relevant tail behavior. The framework links intrinsic material state, operating phenomena, and functional performance loss, and identifies key data and modeling requirements needed to support quantitative fuel-performance assessment and comparative and bounding evaluations of operating conditions. A demonstrative calculation is provided to illustrate framework implementation and sensitivity to operating-experience conditions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115210','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115210',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112755','Polishing process of the TRISO particle fuel','TRISO 입자 연료의 연마 공정','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Z.M. Krajewska-Travar; E. Fontana; P. Lajarge; S. Gardeur; S. Pfirrmann; D. Freis','2026-09-14','','2027-02','연구논문','핵연료·재료','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112755','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112755',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112841','Bayesian Optimization-Based Machine Learning Inversion of 237NpTransmutation Depletion in ADS','ADS에서 237NpTransmutation 연소의 베이지안 최적화 기반 기계 학습 반전','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Feng Zhou; Peng Fang; Yanling Zhu; Shijie Du; Deliang Fan; Xunchao Zhang; Yongwei Yang; Xubo Ma','2026-09-14','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The Accelerator Driven Advanced Nuclear Energy System (ADANES) is a novel closed nuclear fuel cycle system consisting of an Accelerator Driven Sub-critical System (ADS) and a spent fuel recycling system. Its primary function is the transmutation of long-lived minor actinides. To monitor the depletion of 237 Np in the transmutation fuel rod of an ADS reactor core, this paper proposes an offline monitoring scheme based on a Bayesian-optimized machine learning model that integrate nuclide characteristic peak areas with operational parameters. The scheme establishes a nonlinear mapping relationship among 237 Np depletion, characteristic peak area counts of key nuclides, and known operational histories using a database generated from simulations of an ex-core measurement system equipped with a high-purity germanium (HPGe) detector, thereby enabling rapid inversion of the 237 Np transmutation state. Inversion results obtained from six Bayesian-optimized machine learning models demonstrate that the BO-XGBoost model achieves the best performance, yielding a mean relative error (MRE) of 1.47% and a maximum relative error (MaxRE) of 5.32%. Analysis of nuclide and operational parameter feature configurations reveals that burnup time is the dominant operational parameter governing prediction accuracy. When critical operational history information such as burnup history is unavailable, gamma-ray characteristic peak areas can effectively compensate for the deficiency in operational parameters and enhance prediction accuracy, underscoring the gamma-spectroscopic information as an essential source for high-precision inversion. Among the nuclide combinations examined, N3 ( 125 Sb, 134 Cs, 144 Ce, 154 Eu) exhibits the most favorable prediction stability.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112841','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112841',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112835','Application of data driven POD reduced order model to helical cruciform fuel rod bundle','나선형 십자형 핵연료봉 번들에 데이터 구동 POD 차수축소모델 적용','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Wanghong Han; Yue Zeng; Huandong Chen; Lei Zhao; Boyan Li; Hongqiang Ma; Fan Yu; Junkai Wu; Xiaosong Cheng; Jing Wu; Huilun Kang','2026-09-14','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','To enable efficient and accurate prediction of coolant thermal–hydraulic characteristics in helical cruciform fuel rod bundle channels, a data-driven rapid prediction framework is developed by combining proper orthogonal decomposition (POD) with surrogate models. Optimal Latin hypercube sampling (OLHS) was used to generate 34 operating conditions, and high-fidelity data are obtained through computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulations. The modal bases and coefficients of temperature, axial and two lateral velocity fields were extracted. With 99.99% energy retention, the minimum reconstructed modal numbers were determined as k T = 2, k w = 2, k u = 3, k v = 4, respectively. Multi-section reconstruction results demonstrate that the temperature error is within ± 2 K, while those of axial and lateral velocity fields are within ± 0.08 m/s and ± 0.001 m/s, respectively. The reconstruction accuracy is insensitive to axial position and rotation angle. Furthermore, the prediction performances of Kriging and radial basis function (RBF) surrogate models are compared. The Kriging model exhibited local high errors in regions with strong gradients, whereas the RBF model showed more uniform error distributions, with prediction errors below 0.5 K for temperature and below 0.002 m/s and 0.010 m/s for lateral and axial velocity fields, respectively. The maximum relative error is only 2.02%. Moreover, the POD-RBF framework reduced the computational time of a single case from 7200 s to 7.328 s, achieving a speed-up factor of 982.533. These results demonstrate that the POD-RBF model provides an efficient and accurate approach for rapid thermal–hydraulic prediction of helical cruciform fuel rod bundles.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112835','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112835',1,'2026-09-20','2026-09-21','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
