INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115244','Multi-stage optimization of spray flow characteristics and structural performance for a pressurizer spray valve in nuclear power plants','원자력 발전소의 가압기 스프레이 밸브에 대한 스프레이 흐름 특성 및 구조적 성능의 다단계 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Hongwei Xu; Yufeng Lang; Jianian Chang; Xizhuo Le; Jianfeng Mao','2026-10-04','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','To address abnormal flow increase and internal wear in the pressurizer spray valve (PSV) under small openings, this study conducts flow analysis and structural optimization. A CPO-SVR surrogate model combined with the hippopotamus optimization algorithm is proposed. The model achieves high accuracy with an R 2 of 0.95 for stress prediction and 0.99 for flow coefficient prediction, with prediction errors of 0.23% and 1.4%, respectively, while reducing computational cost by approximately 86%. After optimization, valve seat stress drops by 49.4% to 150.58 MPa, maximum flow velocity is reduced by 7.9%, and the abnormal flow plateau in the 0%–20% opening range is eliminated, yielding a smooth characteristic that closely follows the ideal equal-percentage curve. This study provides an effective method for the design of nuclear-grade valves.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115244','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115244',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112914','Safety assessment of a loss-of-pool-water accident in the spent fuel storage of a high-power research reactor','고출력 연구용 원자로의 소모 연료 보관 중 풀-물 손실 사고에 대한 안전성 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ehsan Boustani; Valiyollah Ghazanfari; Hassan Esmaeili','2026-10-04','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','As research reactors undergo power uprates to enhance medical isotope production and materials testing, higher fuel burnup and elevated decay-heat levels significantly reduce the thermal margins of spent fuel storage facilities under postulated accident conditions, necessitating a systematic reevaluation of their safety limits. This study presents a safety analysis of the spent fuel storage system of a 10 MW research reactor under a postulated loss-of-pool-water accident. A multiphysics framework combining neutronic analysis, transient thermal–hydraulic modeling, and radiation transport calculations is employed to evaluate the safety limits of a high-density two-tier rack configuration. The results show that the effective multiplication factor remains well below unity for all investigated configurations, indicating preserved subcriticality. However, thermal–hydraulic margins are significantly reduced for fuel with only 24 h of post-irradiation cooling, resulting in cladding blistering after approximately 5 h of air exposure. In contrast, a decay period of 144 h provides sufficient passive cooling to prevent cladding degradation under complete loss of pool water. Radiation shielding analysis further indicates that a water column of approximately 300 cm above the top of the spent fuel assembly rack is required to reduce the personnel dose rate below the adopted criterion of 10 μSv/h for the pool geometry and radiation source considered in this study. These findings provide quantitative guidance for safety evaluation and operational planning in high-power research reactor spent fuel storage systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112914','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112914',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112894','Investigation of the heat transfer of supercritical carbon dioxide in a vertical tube under high-temperature and high-pressure conditions','고온 고압 조건에서 수직 튜브에서 초임계 이산화탄소의 열전달 조사','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Fanghao Chen; Jinghui Wu; Xianjun Chen; Yangle Wang; Yu Tang; Yanlin Wang; Minyun Liu; Han Wang','2026-10-04','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','The design and refinement of the supercritical carbon dioxide (S-CO 2 ) direct cycle nuclear energy system are crucial for advancing the application of green energy and mitigating the energy crisis. The key to this lies in the research on the heat transfer characteristics of S-CO 2 fluid. Previous studies primarily focus on the heat transfer behavior of S-CO 2 near the critical point, leaving a significant gap in understanding its characteristics under high-temperature and high-pressure conditions. To address this gap, this paper investigates the heat transfer characteristics of S-CO 2 fluid in a vertical tube at pressure and fluid temperature up to 14 MPa and 451℃, respectively. By evaluating the classical heat transfer correlations, it was found that the Krasnoshchekov et al. (1964) correlation provides the most accurate predictions, while the Chen and Fang (2014) correlation is the most stable. The study found that the corrections of Gr number, density, and viscosity have a significant impact on the prediction results. The magnitude of these correction effects is influenced by heat flux. Based on these findings, a new heat transfer correlation was proposed, which demonstrates excellent accuracy and generalization capability for both the experimental data in this study and external data, providing a reliable tool for heat transfer prediction under high-temperature and high-pressure conditions. This paper can serve as a reference and provide data support for the design of S-CO 2 reactor fuel assembly.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112894','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112894',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112864','Application of machine learning for identifying plutonium diversion in molten salt reactors','용융염 원자로에서 플루토늄 전환을 식별하기 위한 기계 학습의 응용','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Branko Kovacevic; Andre Vidal Soares; Azaree T. Lintereur; William J. Walters; Amanda M. Johnsen','2026-10-04','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Molten salt reactors (MSRs) have advantages over traditional light water reactors; however, nuclear material safeguards remain an obstacle to their deployment. The nontraditional liquid fuel of the MSR designs examined in this work and additional material flow streams create challenges for safeguards. These properties not only preclude traditional item-counting safeguards but also create new material diversion pathways. The approach proposed here involves modeling a reactor similar to currently proposed molten salt reactors using Serpent and SCALE, simulating its operation under normal conditions and under various scenarios of plutonium removal. SCALE Sampler is used to introduce isotope-specific nuclear data uncertainty perturbations across 10,000 reactor operations for each scenario. Gamma-ray, neutron and alpha spectra measurement signatures are then collected from each perturbed reactor simulation to identify differences caused by plutonium removal. These signatures are then passed to a machine learning model that classifies each dataset as originating from either normal reactor operation or reactor operation during which plutonium diversion occurred. The highest performing developed machine learning model is capable of correctly classifying over 90% of all reactor simulations for most examined diversion scenarios. Alpha spectra features created by 242 Cm, 239 Pu, 240 Pu, along with gamma-ray spectra features created by 239 Np, 133 Xe, 132 I and other isotopes, proved instrumental for the classification process. The results indicate that, given appropriate measurement signatures, plutonium diversion can be recognized with confidence, complementing the proposed isolate-and-contain safeguards approach for MSRs. Accordingly, MSRs would particularly benefit from safeguards by design that enable collection of these signatures.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112864','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112864',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02072-4','New measurement of the 197Au(n, γ) cross section at the CSNS Back-n white neutron facility','CSNS Back-n 백색 중성자 시설에서 197Au (n, γ) 단면의 새로운 측정','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Zhan-Qiao Cui; Wei Jiang; Gao-Le Yang; Rui-Rui Fan; Jie Ren; Kang Sun; Han Yi; Qiu-Yue Luo; Yong-Qi Wang; Fan Wu; Yu-Bin Shi; Wei-Ping Liu','2026-10-03','2026-10-03','2026-10-03','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02072-4','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02072-4',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104759','Validation of a Hybrid Physics-Informed Machine Learning Model for Mobile Radiation Detection Using Monte Carlo N-Particle Simulations','몬테카를로 N-입자 시뮬레이션을 사용한 이동방사선 검출을 위한 하이브리드 물리 정보 기계 학습 모델의 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Nancy Ibrahim; Amin Amirlatifi; Somayeh Bakhtiari Ramezani','2026-10-03','','2026-10','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Accurate estimation of the Maximum Detectable Distance (MDD) is essential for reliable mobile gamma spectrometry in environmental radiation monitoring and post-remediation surveying. Conventional analytical and data-driven approaches may have limited predictive accuracy under dynamic conditions involving detector motion, photon attenuation, and varying background radiation. A physics-informed neural network (PINN) was developed to estimate MDD by integrating radiation transport relationships with simulation and field data. The model incorporates inverse-square geometric spreading and exponential photon attenuation through physics-based constraints in the training objective, while MCNP 5 -derived photon transport data inform attenuation behavior. Detector velocity, source-to-detector distance, and background count rate serve as primary inputs. The framework also incorporates velocity-dependent dwell-time effects and Monte Carlo-based uncertainty analysis. The approach was evaluated using field-acquired mobile gamma spectrometry measurements and site-specific MCNP 5 simulations representing 662 keV photon transport through silicate-rich soil. Results demonstrate that physics-based constraints and MCNP-informed attenuation behavior improve MDD prediction performance and generalization across varying survey conditions. Relative to conventional approaches, the hybrid model reduced MDD prediction errors by approximately 10-30%, with the greatest improvements observed at higher detector velocities. The proposed framework provides a physics-guided approach for MDD estimation to support mobile radiation detection, survey planning, and environmental radiological assessment.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104759','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104759',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115231','The evolution of computer codes for the analysis of severe accidents in light water reactors, WASH-1400 to present','경수로의 심각한 사고 분석을 위한 컴퓨터 코드의 진화, WASH-1400은','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Richard Denning; Randall Gauntt; Jeff Gabor','2026-10-03','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This paper describes the evolution of our understanding of the potential consequences of severe accidents in light water based on research and model development undertaken by the Nuclear Regulatory Commission through its contractors and by the U.S. nuclear industry. Major milestones were activities undertaken by Brookhaven National Laboratory in support of the WASH-740 study, based on a very limited experimental database, by AEC contractors in support of the Reactor Safety Study (WASH-1400), which was the first major attempt to quantify the risk to the public from severe accidents, to the follow-on NUREG-1150 risk study and most recently to the insights provided by the NRC''s SOARCA program. The Three Mile Island Unit-2 accident, which shortly followed after the release of WASH-1400, provided impetus to the regulatory authority and the regulated industry to perform research to better understand the potential frequency and consequences of severe accidents. This paper describes the development of the tools used to predict accident consequences based on research performed by the NRC (and its contractors) and by the nuclear industry (including the Electric Power Research Institute). Over time, these tools have matured, have been validated against research results, and have gained a level of configuration management enabling them to be used in demonstrating safety adequacy for the licensing and regulatory oversight of these reactors. This paper has been limited in its scope to severe accident analysis development activities in the U.S.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115231','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115231',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115230','Direct numerical simulation of turbulent natural convection in a heat generating fluid within a shallow horizontal enclosure','얕은 수평 인클로저 내의 열 발생 유체에서 난류 자연 대류의 직접 수치 시뮬레이션','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Michael Johnson; Barbara Bigot; Rémi Clavier','2026-10-03','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Core catchers are a significant safety feature of Generation-IV nuclear reactors for the safe dissipation of decay heat and maintaining the integrity of the reactor containment in the event of a severe accident. Direct numerical simulation is used to simulate turbulent natural convection in a shallow layer of dense oxidic corium, with significant internal heat generation ( R a i = 4.5 × 1 0 8 ), at the base of a core catcher. The simulation revealed a large persistent convection cell adjacent to the pitched lateral boundary, smaller eddies comparable in dimension to the fluid depth closer to the centre of the core catcher and enhanced dissipation of turbulent kinetic energy in the upper half of the fluid. Around 73 % of the heat generated within the fluid is dissipated from the upper boundary. The surface and time-averaged heat flux at the upper and lower boundaries are in good agreement with Emara and Kulacki predictions in the shallow limit. Significant spatiotemporal fluctuations in local Nusselt number are observed, with local flares in heat flux manifesting in local Nusselt numbers of several times the surface average. These local flares are less frequent at the lower and lateral boundaries but greater in amplitude relative to the surface-averaged heat flux. Further research is required into the duration and frequency of these flares, given the potential of persistent local flares to induce crust remelting or localised thermal attack of the core catcher.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115230','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115230',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','FR','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115255','Burnup-dependent nuclear safeguards and security assessment of HALEU-Fueled sodium-cooled fast reactors','HALEU 연료 소듐 냉각 고속 원자로의 연소 의존적 핵 안전 장치 및 보안 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Cihang Lu; Arantxa Cuadra','2026-10-03','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study presents a burnup- and cooling-time-dependent assessment of safeguards- and security-relevant characteristics of spent fuel from high-assay low-enriched uranium (HALEU)-fueled sodium-cooled fast reactors (SFRs). A physics-based framework is adopted to evaluate spent fuel in terms of three functions: material attractiveness, self-protection, and monitorability. Within this framework, decay heat, photon emission rate, spontaneous fission rate, and external dose rate are treated as key spent-fuel attributes that collectively determine safeguards and security functions. Burnup-dependent isotopic inventories were generated using the Serpent 2 Monte Carlo code and tracked through post-discharge decay. The resulting isotopic compositions were further used in photon and neutron transport calculations to quantify radiation signatures and dose rates over cooling times ranging from 1 day to 100 years. For reference and verification, analyses were also performed for a conventional low-enriched uranium pressurized water reactor (PWR) and a recycled-fuel SFR. Results show that material attractiveness, self-protection, and monitorability exhibit strong dependence on both discharge burnup and cooling time. The fast neutron spectrum of the HALEU-fueled SFR limits the buildup of higher-mass transuranic isotopes such as 244 Cm, resulting in comparatively weak spontaneous-fission neutron signatures and negligible neutron dose contributions. Consequently, radiological self-protection is dominated by photon-emitting isotopes, and passive neutron monitoring may be less effective than photon-based approaches. Higher-burnup fuel maintains greater decay heat, photon emission rates, and dose rates at long cooling times, resulting in stronger intrinsic barriers and enhanced monitorability. These results demonstrate the importance of accounting for the combined effects of discharge burnup and post-discharge cooling time on spent-fuel characteristics when developing safeguards and physical protection strategies for advanced reactor systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115255','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115255',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112890','Research on control rod cusping effect correction methods in the 2D/1D transport calculations','2D/1D 이송계산에서 제어봉 압착효과 보정방법에 관한 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jiada Chen; Zhouyu Liu; Zihuang Huang; Jun Chen; Guangwen Bi; Chuntao Tang; Liangzhi Cao; Hongchun Wu','2026-10-03','','2027-02','연구논문','핵연료·재료','The cusping effect is one of the critical challenges that must be addressed in the reactor core physics simulations involving control rod movement. This study proposes two improved methods for correcting the control rod cusping effect in the 2D/1D transport calculations. First, the conventional Both Axial and Radial Homogenization (BARH) method in NECP-X is enhanced by subdividing partially rodded axial planes into sub-planes, each undergoing independent radial homogenization. The radial leakage term of each sub-plane was then approximated using the leakage terms of its adjacent layers. Second, an Axial-Only Homogenization (AOH) method was developed, building on the material-region-based 2D/1D transport method. This method leverages high-precision axial fine-mesh fluxes from material regions to perform flux-volume-weighted axial homogenization. It initially approximates the radial leakage terms of sub-planes using those of adjacent layers, and further refines these terms via pre-calculated radial leakage correction factors. Validation of the proposed methods was performed on the VERA #4 and VERA #5 benchmarks, and on the SPERT 3 × 3 assembly and full-core problems. Results show that, compared with the conventional BARH method, the improved BARH method significantly improves the correction accuracy of the cusping effect and demonstrates strong potential for application to typical commercial PWR control rod clusters. For problems involving large, strong-absorber control rods in the research reactors, the AOH method combined with radial leakage correction achieves the highest accuracy, meeting the precision requirements for correcting the cusping effect in research reactors.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112890','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112890',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112889','Numerical study on capacitive metal rod position detector in double-layer medium','이중층 매질의 정전용량식 금속봉 위치검출기에 관한 수치연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yanlin Li; Benke Qin; Zijia Chen; Wei Xiong; Hanliang Bo','2026-10-03','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','Position signals of control rods are important parameters that should be measured during the operation of nuclear reactors. The performance of capacitive detectors for measuring control rod positions in a double-layer medium is numerically studied in this paper. According to the experimental results of concave electrodes capacitive detectors, the numerical model is verified. The mathematical expression of the detector signal is derived as a function of rod position and liquid level. The error characteristics of the capacitive detectors for measuring the eccentric metal rod are revealed. The method for evaluating measuring errors of capacitive detectors in double-layer medium is constructed. The relation between flare angles of electrodes and measuring errors is studied, and the optimization method of the flare angles is discussed. The design of the integrated capacitive metal rod position detector (CMRPD) is proposed. Measuring errors and performance of the detector are evaluated.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112889','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112889',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112866','Experimental investigation of corium top-flooding with sustained induction heating and MCCI','지속적인 유도 가열 및 MCCI를 이용한 코륨 상부 홍수에 대한 실험적 조사','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Sébastien Renaudière de Vaux; Viviane Bouyer; Christophe Journeau; Arthur Denoix','2026-10-03','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Top-flooding of molten prototypic corium is investigated experimentally, in the presence of sustained induction heating of the melt. The melt lays on the top of a concrete layer, and consecutively to the sustained heating, molten-core concrete interaction (MCCI) occurs. The experiment is conducted in the MERELAVA facility, which enables to melt and study oxidic and steel corium (using thermite reaction or thermite plus induction heating, with a maximum capacity of 80 kg of corium). The steam flowrate generated after corium flooding is quantified through a vapor line made of a condenser and condensate tank. In the present test, the initial corium mixture is composed of 54%UO 2 /23%ZrO 2 /8%Concrete/15%Steel (weight percentage). The water is injected in several batches. After an initial phase of dry ablation of the siliceous concrete, several water injections on the top of the melt have been realized with a total volume of 74 liters. We present an overview of the experimental setup and a summary of test conditions carried out in the facility. Steam flowrate is measured by condensing the steam and measuring the condensate mass flowrate. Heat flux estimates are provided, based on the mass flowrate analysis and heat exchanger data. Dismantling observations of the solidified ingot are also given.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112866','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112866',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','FR','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112892','CFD investigation of gas-core instability in axial swirl separators using a coupled VOF-two-fluid model','커플링된 VOF-투-플루이드 모델을 사용하여 축 방향 스월 분리기에서 가스 코어 불안정성에 대한 CFD 조사','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jiaming Li; Yanyou Ou; Xiaobo Zeng; Zongkun Li; Yicheng Ou; Guangming Fan','2026-10-03','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Unstable flow in gas–liquid separators significantly degrades separation efficiency and system reliability. While previous work has documented unstable flow phenomena, the statistical regularities of transient interfacial oscillations and their quantitative coupling with local flow parameters (swirl intensity, pressure gradient, and velocity slip) have not been fully quantified. To address these gaps, the present study develops and validates a coupled VOF-two-fluid model for axial swirl separators, incorporating the Reynolds Stress Model (RSM) to investigate the dynamic characteristics of transient gas-core behavior. The results show that under unstable conditions, the gas core exhibits quasi-periodic “necking-expansion” oscillations with bimodal probability distributions (peaks at 29.56 mm and 36.49 mm), contrasting sharply with the unimodal distribution observed under stable flow. The standard deviation of core diameter increases by 116% (from 1.8 mm to 3.9 mm), quantitatively confirming fluctuation amplification. Strong negative correlations are observed between core diameter and swirl intensity, with swirl intensity decaying by approximately 4% during an expansion event at Z/D = 8. Transient pressure-drop peaks reach 4.62 times the temporal mean and are synchronized with core oscillations, indicating strong pressure-interface coupling. Swirl intensity decays monotonically along the axis, by 47% from its maximum after an axial length of 10D, while velocity slip remains elevated in the region of Z/D = 3–13. This competition between weakening centrifugal constraints and sustained shear effects drives instability onset in the middle-to-downstream region, which is characterized by the proposed dimensionless stability indicator (We/Nc). These findings provide additional insight into gas-core instability behavior.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112892','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112892',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2727814','Investigation of Performance of a Large-Scale Water-Based RCCS Under Varying Decay Heat Loads','다양한 붕괴열 부하 하에서 대규모 수성 RCC의 성능 조사','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Qiuping Lv; Matthew J. Jasica; Darius D. Lisowski; Zhiee J. Ooi; Rui Hu','2026-10-02','2026-10-02','2026-10-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','The objective of the present study is to investigate the effects of varying decay heat loads and tank inlet elevations on the performance of a large-scale water-based reactor cavity cooling system (RCCS) utilizing the water-based Natural convection Shutdown heat removal Test Facility (NSTF) at Argonne National Laboratory. A power parametric series with prototypic decay heat loads of 1.4 MWt, 1.75 MWt, 2.1 MWt, and 2.4 MWt) (34.4 kWt, 43.0 kWt, 51.6 kWt, and 58.5 kWt scaled) with a low tank inlet configuration was tested.The system performance metrics at the two-phase quasi-steady state were compared, mainly the system flow, steam generation rate, system pressure, and liquid and structure temperatures. The effect of the decay heat power level on the boiling front progression was also investigated.It was found that lower decay heat loads caused delayed boiling front progression. The results were then compared to previous data sets collected at identical testing conditions but with chimney piping configured at the mid tank elevation configuration. Overall, the tank inlet elevation did not significantly influence the system two-phase quasi-steady-state performance at the studied decay heat levels. However, the tank inlet elevation had a significant impact on the two-phase flow instability characteristics and the boiling front propagation.A static flashing model identified from the literature predicted the flow oscillation period well but would result in high flashing superheating. Additional analysis also identified the presence of Type-I density wave oscillations (DWOs) in the present study. By plotting all the test results on the subcooling and Zuber plane, a chimney exit quality of ~0.3% was identified as a trigger for the onset of flow oscillations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2727814','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2727814',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104763','Structural integrity assessment and manufacturability-oriented design improvement of the HCCP TBM shield','HCCP TBM 차폐재의 구조적 무결성 평가 및 제조 가능성 중심 설계 개선','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Hyoseong Gwon; Seong Dae Park; Youngmin Lee; Dohyun Kim; Suntaek Lim; Jae Sung Yoon; Suk-Kwon Kim; Mu-Young Ahn','2026-10-02','','2026-10','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The Helium Cooled Ceramic Pebble (HCCP) TBM shield is a safety-important component (SIC-1) serving as a vacuum boundary and the first confinement barrier, and a design with a simplified internal structure has been proposed to improve its manufacturability. In this study, a structural integrity assessment of the simplified HCCP TBM shield was performed in accordance with RCC-MRx 2018, considering 15 single loads and 17 load combinations. The assessment covers all operating states, namely the normal operation state (NOS), the baking state, and the tritium outgassing state (TOS), as well as the electromagnetic and seismic loads. While sufficient margins were confirmed for the accidental loads, negative margins were found in the load combinations governed by the pressure in the baking state, identifying the baking state as the design driver of the TBM shield. The cause was analyzed to be the combination of the reduction in the allowable stress intensity at the elevated temperature of 240 °C and the increased bending stresses of the walls caused by the enlarged spacing between the internal plates. In the design improvement for the margin recovery, manufacturability was consistently applied as a decision criterion. Parameter studies on the side wall thickness, the front plate thickness, and the pipe casing layout were performed for an improved geometry in which the width of the shield block containing the pipe casing bends was increased, and it was confirmed that the combination of a 40 mm side wall and a front plate of 60 mm or thicker recovers the structural integrity in all shield blocks. In addition, it was quantitatively shown that the pipe casings act as structural stiffeners and that their reinforcing effect increases with the symmetry of the casing layout. These results provide a design solution reconciling the structural integrity with the manufacturability without reintroducing the internal plates, and a quantitative basis for the geometry optimization in the final design phase.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104763','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104763',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104755','Robustness of moving-window Ib-value analysis for acoustic-emission-based fracture precursor detection under severe background noise','심각한 배경 소음 하에서 음향-방출 기반 파단 전구체 검출을 위한 이동-창 Ib-값 분석의 견고성','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Doyun Jung; Byunyoung Chung; Youngchul Choi','2026-10-02','','2026-10','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Background noise in operating nuclear power plants masks the acoustic emission (AE) signals of micro-cracks and hinders early fracture-precursor detection. A moving-window Ib-value methodology is proposed and validated by a proof-of-concept tensile test on a notched SM45C carbon steel specimen. For 651 crack signals screened by source location, the energy-based b-value (Aki''s maximum likelihood method) and the Ib-value were evaluated, and detection-threshold elevation was emulated by removing up to 50% of the low-amplitude data. The cumulative approach diluted the precursor and never reached the alarm criterion of 1.0, whereas the 100-hit moving window immediately captured the shift of the crack mode from shear to tensile. Under increasing noise, low-amplitude micro-crack signals were selectively lost (survival 100% to 40%, against 100% for macro-cracks), biasing the b-value by up to −19.8%, while the Ib-value, which evaluates only the distribution''s statistical center, stayed within ±4.9%. Across 0–40% hit loss it still crossed the criterion 7.4–11.8 s before rupture, at 98.4–99.3% of peak stress. The moving-window Ib-value is therefore markedly less sensitive than the b-value to the selective loss of low-amplitude AE events caused by threshold elevation. Generalization to full background-noise robustness, which also involves waveform superposition and parameter distortion, requires further validation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104755','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104755',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104756','Geant4-Based Differentiable Optimization for Energy-Response Flattening of a Multi-Detector Neutron Long Counter','다중검출기 중성자 롱카운터의 에너지 응답 평탄화를 위한 Geant4 기반의 차별화된 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Ziyang Gan; Lizhen Liang; Bing Hong; Xiaohua Li; Cong Yang; Xin Xu','2026-10-02','','2026-10','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','To address the significant energy dependence of long neutron counter responses in wide-energy-range fluence measurements, this paper proposes a differentiable-optimization-based method for flattening the energy response of a multi-detector long neutron counter. A Geant4 model of the multi-detector long counter was developed, and the energy–position response matrix of this detector was constructed for the energy range of 1 eV to 20 MeV. The relative standard deviation (RSD) of the synthesized response was used as the flatness metric, and two optimization approaches—discrete combinatorial search and differentiable continuous optimization—were compared. The results show that multi-position response synthesis effectively improves the response flatness of the long counter across a broad energy range. For a detector array with K = 8, the sampled combinatorial-search benchmark identified a configuration with an RSD of 3.79%, whereas differentiable optimization yielded 2.98%, indicating a lower RSD under the present calculation settings. Additionally, embedding tungsten rods in the moderator of a long neutron counter was found to improve the overall flatness of its response. Independent verification simulations were performed by placing 6 Li micro-detectors at the eight optimized axial positions, yielding a verified RSD of 2.84%. This study demonstrates that the proposed method effectively enhances the wide-energy-range response consistency of the multi-detector long counter and provides a reproducible computational framework for position optimization in such detector systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104756','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104756',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;PL','PL','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104736','Development and Verification of an Efficient 3-D Finite Element Analysis Model for Irradiation Deformation of the Fast Reactor Fuel Assembly','고속 원자로 연료 어셈블리의 조사 변형을 위한 효율적인 3차원 유한 요소 분석 모델의 개발 및 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Haoyu Wang; Guangliang Yang; Zhifan Zhou; Junxian Cao; Yongzhong Huang; Jing Zhang; Yuanming Li; Lei Shi','2026-10-02','','2026-10','연구논문','핵연료·재료','The existing performance analysis of the fast reactor fuel assembly faces the challenge of balancing high-fidelity and computational efficiency. This study develops a 3-D irradiation deformation analysis model based on ABAQUS to address this conflict. The model employs shell elements to simulate claddings and the hexagonal duct, beam elements for wrap wires, and simplifies complex mechanical interactions using Tie Constraint, Axial Connector element, and General Contact. User subroutines are implemented to incorporate material irradiation behaviors and the non-uniform operating conditions. A parametric automatic modeling method is also developed to construct simplified structures and mechanical interactions. The analysis model has been verified against out-of-pile compression test for a 127-pin fuel bundle and an irradiation deformation benchmark case for a 169-pin fuel assembly, with verification parameters such as gap variation and ovalization. Results demonstrate good agreement with errors within 20%. Furthermore, compared with the simplified model in BAMBOO, the present model demonstrates higher accuracy in the simulation of mechanical interactions and possesses the capability to capture cladding circumferential effects; compared with the full-scale detailed model, the present model achieves comparable results while improving solution speed by over 100-fold for a 7-pin fuel assembly. This model is reliable, efficient and easily extensible for irradiation deformation analysis and design optimization of fast reactor fuel assemblies.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104736','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104736',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104751','Comparing advanced model and human observers for CT detectability index under varied tube currents and contrasts','다양한 튜브 전류 및 대조 하에서 CT 검출 가능성 지수에 대한 고급 모델과 인간 관찰자 비교','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Keyla G.A. Mulyana; Choirul Anam; Qidir M.B. Soesanto; Ariij Naufal; Noor Diyana Osman','2026-10-02','','2027-02','연구논문','기타 원자력','Objective This study aims to compare the detectability index (d′) between the human observer (HO) and advanced model observer (AMO) using the Non-Prewhitening Observer (NPW) and Non-Prewhitening Observer with Eye Filter (NPWE) for various tube currents and low-contrast objects. Methods Image data were obtained using the ACR 464 phantom at three different tube current levels (i.e., 80 mA, 140 mA, and 200 mA). The task object had contrast levels ranging from 3 HU to 15 HU, with a diameter of 3 mm. The task objects used a Gaussian profile model. The d′ values were measured using the AMO with NPW and NPWE models, while HO values were computed using the 2-AFC method. Each configuration consisted of 100 signal-present and 100 signal-absent images. Results The results demonstrated that the d′ values obtained from AMO displayed a trend similar to those derived from HO. Increases in the tube current and contrast resulted in higher d′ values across all observers. Correlation analysis revealed that NPW and NPWE showed a strong relationship with HO ( r = 0.979; p < 0.001) and ( r = 0.976; p < 0.001), respectively. Conclusion This study confirms that the AMO can effectively replicate object detection with accuracy comparable to that of HO. This behaviour was consistently observed across variations in tube current and low-contrast objects.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104751','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104751',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','ID;MY','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104745','Assessment of occupational radiation exposure from gamma-emitting rad ionuclides in the bio-shield of Kori Unit 1 during decommissioning','해체 중 Kori Unit 1의 바이오 실드에서 감마 방출 방사성 이온핵종으로 인한 작업 방사선 피폭 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Ja Yeong Yoon; Hyeonmin Lee; Seungbin Yoon; Min Ji Kim; Hee Reyoung Kim','2026-10-02','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','The external dose to the workers of bio-shield of the Kori Unit 1 was evaluated by using the VISIPLAN 4.0 code to secure the radiation safety of its decommissioning work. In particular, radionuclide-specific activity concentration data, derived from prior MCNP simulations, were used to model three-dimensional radiation work scenarios. Each scenario was simulated with shielding and sampling configurations to calculate the external dose rates. Worker operation times were estimated based on the ICRP-recommendation and Nuclear Safety Act of annual average dose limit of 20 mSv. Variations in worker role, position, and task duration resulted in substantial disparities in individual cumulative doses. The maximum dose rate in scenario 1 under the 8-year cooling condition was 2.3 × 10 −1 mSv/h at 3 m height, decreasing to 9.3 × 10 −2 mSv/h under the 15-year condition (∼60 % reduction). A 20 mm lead shield reduced the dose rate by ∼86 %. The total dose rate in scenario 2 under the 8 year cooling condition was 1.33 × 10 1 mSv of workers 1 and 2, ∼22 times that of Worker 3. The minimum required shielding thickness was estimated at 14.8 mm. The allowable number of complete sampling operations was 32 and 80 for the 8 and 15 year cooling conditions, respectively.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104745','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104745',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112886','Reinforcement learning for BWR fuel management','BWR 연료 관리를 위한 보강 학습','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Loukas Carayannopoulos; Koroush Shirvan','2026-10-02','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Boiling water reactor (BWR) core design is a highly constrained optimization problem that directly affects fuel costs in operating reactors. The problem consists of both fuel bundle design and core loading pattern design, each of which presents significant computational and combinatorial challenges. Historically, stochastic optimization methods such as genetic algorithms and simulated annealing have been the most widely used approaches for automated bundle and core design. More recently, reinforcement learning (RL) has emerged as a promising class of algorithms capable of solving complex design problems while exploiting underlying physics-based patterns. This work presents a reinforcement learning framework for both fuel bundle and loading pattern optimization and demonstrates a sequential approach to BWR core design. First, the performance of the loading pattern optimizer is evaluated independently by reproducing a historic fuel cycle from an operating reactor using industry-designed assemblies. The optimizer consistently meets all cycle constraints and statistically outperforms the reference loading pattern, as demonstrated by a Wilcoxon signed-rank test. The full sequential optimization framework is then applied to design new fuel bundles and corresponding loading patterns for the same cycle. These results demonstrate that reinforcement learning can effectively address the sequential bundle and core design problem and highlight its potential to reduce design time and fuel costs in BWR core optimization.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112886','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112886',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112873','Development of new lead-free borate glasses: Experimental evaluation for the impact of BaO on radiation shielding properties of glasses','새로운 무연 붕산염 안경 개발: BaO가 안경의 방사선 차폐 특성에 미치는 영향에 대한 실험적 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','M. Elsafi; M.I. Sayyed; K.A. Mahmoud','2026-10-02','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','This study investigated advanced glass compositions for gamma-ray shielding consisting of (78-x) B 2 O 3 -8MgO-13ZnO-1Eu 2 O 3 -xBaO, x = 23, 26, 29, and 32 mol%. Attenuation coefficients were calculated experimentally and simulated. The results between the two methods are fairly similar, with a ± 5 % experimental–measured data difference. The addition of BaO improves the shielding performance of the prepared BMZE glass. The progression of the BaO concentration from 23 to 32 mol% within the prepared BMZE glasses causes an improvement in their LACs from 0.299 to 0.319 cm −1 at 661.7 keV and shows a consistent improvement over the examined gamma-ray energy range of 59.5–1332 keV. It is shown that the BMZE1–BMZE4 glass samples exhibited superior protection performance to RS 323 G19 lead-based shielding commercial glass, which contains 33 % lead oxide and 1.8 % cerium oxide, while BMZE4 exhibited superior protection performance to RS 360 lead-based shielding commercial glass, which contains 45 % lead oxide. Therefore, the prepared BMZE4 glass represents a lead-free shielding glass alternative for hospital nuclear medicine applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112873','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112873',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','EG;JO;KW;RU','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106630','Numerical study of functionally graded material models for evaluation of thermomechanical loading on nuclear fuel particles','핵연료 입자에 대한 열기계적 하중 평가를 위한 기능 등급 물질 모델의 수치 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','S. Khajian; A. Zolfaghari; M. Aghaie; A. Minuchehr','2026-10-01','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Functionally graded materials (FGMs) are well suited for analyzing the thermomechanical behavior of dispersed fuel particles under severe thermal and mechanical conditions, due to their capability to exhibit continuously varying properties in the radial direction. In this study, the primary focus is placed on the numerical analysis of an FGM hollow sphere subjected to thermal loading and internal pressure, as this configuration is more relevant to higher burnup conditions and the associated buildup of internal gas pressure. Within this framework, the radial distribution of material properties is assumed to be continuous, and the influence of the inhomogeneity parameter, β, on the temperature field, radial displacement, and radial and circumferential stresses is investigated. The results show that variations in β play a decisive role in the thermomechanical response of the hollow sphere and can alter both the magnitude and the radial location of stress concentration. Accordingly, an appropriate choice of β can be used to optimize the mechanical response of the fuel particle and reduce stress concentration in critical regions. The FGM solid-sphere formulation is included as a complementary theoretical formulation representing a physically relevant configuration for the early stage of irradiation; however, the parametric numerical results and quantitative discussion of the present study are restricted to the hollow-sphere configuration.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106630','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106630',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106629','Effect of vertical heat exchange tube/tube-bundle condensation on aerosol diffusiophoretic deposition','수직 열교환 튜브/튜브 번들 응축이 에어로졸 확산성 증착에 미치는 영향','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','E. Xinnuo; Haifeng Gu; Junyan Chen; Hui Wang; Yanmin Zhou; Qingyang Sun; Jianqun Yu; Tianhao Tang','2026-10-01','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','During a severe accident, substantial amounts of radioactive aerosols are released into the containment. Upon activation of the Passive Containment Cooling System, these aerosols are driven by diffusiophoresis toward condensing heat exchange surfaces, thereby altering the distribution of radioactive inventory within the containment. This study experimentally investigates aerosol diffusiophoresis under single-tube and tube-bundle condensation conditions. A series of experiments on aerosol diffusiophoresis were conducted under systematically varied steam mole fractions, condensation rates, and system pressures, with real-time monitoring of the spatial aerosol concentration. The results indicate that particle size has a negligible effect on the diffusiophoresis velocity, an increased steam condensation rate enhances the deposition, while a reduction in steam mole fraction inhibits it. A higher steam density inhibits the diffusiophoresis velocity. Furthermore, the study investigates diffusiophoresis under both single-tube and tube-bundle condensation conditions. The effective deposition area coefficient (α), correlated with condensation rate and steam mole fraction, is proposed to modify the classical model, thereby improving its predictive accuracy. The study proposed the effective deposition area coefficient α, related to both the steam condensation rate and steam mole fraction, to modify the classical diffusiophoresis model. This correction effectively reduces the deviation between experimental data and model predictions, significantly improving the accuracy of diffusiophoresis decay constant forecasts under strong heat-sink tube-bundle condensation conditions. The findings provide essential experimental data and a refined model for assessing post-accident radioactivity distribution within the containment.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106629','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106629',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2732612','An Integer Programming Method for Maintenance Schedule Optimization in Nuclear Power Plants','원자력 발전소의 유지보수 일정 최적화를 위한 정수 프로그래밍 방법','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Ethan Deakins; Tim Gallacher; Najmaddin Akhundov; Anahita Khojandi; Jamie Coble; Diego Mandelli; Jim Ostrowski','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Maintenance scheduling in nuclear power plants (NPPs) is challenging because multicomponent systems exhibit strong interdependencies and must satisfy strict safety requirements. We present a two-tier framework that couples a mixed-integer programming (MIP) model with a probabilistic risk assessment (PRA) layer for at-power maintenance scheduling.The PRA module evaluates incumbent schedules, and through a solver callback, triggers additional constraints that exclude configurations violating PRA-derived risk thresholds, technical specification limits (e.g., limiting condition for operation windows), and physical work control rules, thereby guiding the MIP toward cost-optimal, safety-compliant solutions.We construct anonymized test sets by mapping real maintenance work packages onto a hypothetical high-pressure injection system comprised of three trains. The framework is validated on three weekly workloads (A-, B-, and C-train task sets), each examined under three backlog policies.With a 16-h wall-clock limit and interim checkpoints at 30 min, the framework proves optimality in three of nine scenarios and terminates within 10% of the best bound in all nine, with the backlog-enabled scenarios remaining the most numerically challenging (gaps of 3.32% to 9.10%), reflecting the added combinatorial difficulty of optional task selection.In a representative comparison against a schedule hand constructed by methods used in current practice, the optimized A-train plan satisfies all operational requirements at substantially lower labor cost ($28 920 versus $36 612) while respecting out-of-service limits and PRA guardrails.These results demonstrate that integrating MIP with configuration risk screening can reduce operating and maintenance costs without sacrificing safety margins, and represent a promising direction for further development toward routine, cost aware maintenance planning in NPPs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2732612','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2732612',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02054-6','T-DDFM: an advanced denoising diffusion fusion model for high-precision neutron imaging','T-DDFM: 고정밀 중성자 이미징을 위한 고급 노이즈 제거 확산 융합 모델','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Yuan-Yu Liu; Dun-Kai Yang; Kun Zhu; Jing-Jing Lu; Li-Zhen Liang; Xian-Cai Meng; Yu-Zhong Qian; Shuai Li; Xu-Wen Xiong; Sheng-Yu Xing; Dong-Peng Song; Bing Hong','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02054-6','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02054-6',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02069-z','Study on the method of simultaneous regulation of 222Rn/220Rn progeny activity concentration in 220Rn chamber','220Rn 챔버에서 222Rn/220Rn 자손 활성 농도의 동시 조절 방법에 관한 연구','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Tao Ao; Ya-Song Xiao; Jing-Yi Xu; Jing-Yue Pei; Yu-Fan Liu; Jia-Lu Feng; Ke-Xin Wang; Li-Dan Lv; Zheng-Zhong He','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02069-z','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02069-z',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02071-5','Level-anticrossing and a new relationship in the B(E2) anomaly','B (E2) 이상에서 레벨 항균 및 새로운 관계','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Tao Wang; Yu-Xin Cheng; Dong-Kang Li; Xiao-Shen Kang; Suo-Chang Jin; Tie Wang; Zhi-Qi Zhang; Chen-Guang Zhang; Zhi-Xin Zhang','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02071-5','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02071-5',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02070-6','Experimental study on aerosol resuspension induced by erosion and denudation in containment','격리 중 침식 및 분해에 의해 유발된 에어로졸 재현탁에 관한 실험적 연구','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Jia-Xuan Tang; Yang Yang; Zhuo Liu; Lu-Teng Zhang; Jia-Long Li; Liang-Ming Pan; Li Gao; Yi-Dan Yuan','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','2026-10-01','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02070-6','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02070-6',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104741','On-line quantification of delayed neutron precursor drift reactivity in molten salt reactors: A shadow-precursor observer verified against closed-form benchmarks in Modelica/TRANSFORM','용융염 원자로에서 지연된 중성자 전구체 드리프트 반응성의 온라인 정량화: Modelica/transform에서 닫힌 형태의 벤치마크에 대해 검증된 그림자 전구체 관찰자','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Jaejin Lee; SeungYop Paek','2026-10-01','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','In molten salt reactors the delayed neutron precursors drift with the fuel salt. The steady-state consequences — a reduced effective delayed neutron fraction — are well captured by system codes, but the reactivity of the drift has been available only on a single exponential mode or, on-line, only at constant power, where it equals the inventory reading β 0 − β eff ( t ) . In power-varying transients that reading conflates the flow effect with ordinary precursor lag, and the built-in reactivity of the codes deliberately omits the drift channel. This paper derives a shadow-precursor observer that isolates the drift component as an on-line equivalent reactivity for arbitrary power histories — one differential equation per precursor group, non-intrusive — together with an exponential-mode closed form and the circulating-fuel inhour relation for the core–loop geometry. A three-tier, experiment-free benchmark set executed in Modelica/TRANSFORM verifies all three against closed-form references in the code’s own discrete equations: the observer recovers the constant-power reading exactly and matches the inhour and exponential-mode references in free-power flow transients. Under a ＋50 pcm step at constant flow, the observer exposes a drift modulation of + 67.1 pcm, and the common static- β eff substitution overestimates the period of that insertion by + 28 % .','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104741','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104741',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104758','Investigation on organic Rankine cycle technology for utilizing low-temperature waste heat sources from fusion reactors','핵융합 원자로의 저온 폐열원 활용을 위한 유기 랭킨 사이클 기술 조사','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Shuling Xu; Mingzhun Lei; Pinghui Zhao; Kun Lu; Chunyuan Li','2026-10-01','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','Fusion energy is recognized as one of the cleanest base-load power sources with abundant fuel reserves, inherent safety and near-zero carbon emissions, which is expected to fundamentally address global fossil energy depletion and climate change. Fusion reactors generate multi-grade waste heat covering wide temperature intervals: high-temperature heat from blanket modules can be matched with steam Rankine or supercritical CO 2 Brayton cycles, while massive low-temperature cooling waste heat below 200 °C is produced from divertor cooling loops and vacuum vessel heat dissipation. Such low-grade heat cannot be efficiently recovered by conventional high-temperature power cycles, resulting in substantial energy loss and constraining the overall energy utilization efficiency of fusion facilities. To address this bottleneck, this paper establishes an Organic Rankine Cycle (ORC) thermodynamic model coupled with the REFPROP fluid property database for recovering fusion low-temperature waste heat, and systematically performs thermal performance evaluation and component-level exergy analysis on ten typical organic working fluids including alkanes, dimethyl ether and fluorinated refrigerants within the heat source range of 80-180 °C. The simulation results indicate that evaporating temperature serves as the dominant parameter governing cycle thermal efficiency, exergy efficiency and circulating mass flow rate. With the rise of evaporator outlet temperature, thermal efficiency and exergy efficiency increase rapidly, whereas the required working fluid mass flow rate decreases monotonically. Under identical operating conditions, R1234ze(E) requires the maximum circulation flow rate of 10.349 kg/s, while pentane and isopentane exhibit the lowest flow rates of 3.359 kg/s and 3.505 kg/s repectively. For full-range heat sources (80-180 °C), pentane, isopentane and R123 deliver balanced superior thermodynamic performance; R123 exhibits the maximum thermal efficiency of 16.86 % at at an evaporation temperature of 170 °C.R1234ze(E), R134a, R152a and dimethyl ether are alternative candidates exclusive to heat sources below 100 °C. R245fa owns mature industrial supporting technology but is limited by its high Global Warming Potential (GWP) and narrow applicable temperature range. Sensitivity analysis reveals that the variation of expander isentropic efficiency imposes far more significant impacts on system performance than pump efficiency. Second-law exergy decomposition indicates that evaporator and condenser are the two dominant exergy destruction sources of the whole system, while pump exergy loss remains negligible. Comprehensive comparison covering thermodynamic characteristics, environmental friendliness and operation adaptability suggests pentane and isopentane are the optimal matching working fluids for the proposed fusion waste heat ORC system, featuring low total exergy dissipation, minimal circulation flow and mild environmental hazards. This work provides quantitative reference for working fluid screening and heat exchanger structural optimization of fusion low-grade heat recovery ORC systems, and offers clear optimization priorities targeted at core irreversible loss components.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104758','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104758',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104762','Development of an improved solidification model for molten salt reactor applications','용융염 원자로 적용을 위한 개선된 고화 모델 개발','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Oktari Zaidi; Yun Je Cho; Byong Jo Yun; Jae Jun Jeong','2026-10-01','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','The freezing of molten salt in flow systems is one of the major safety concerns for molten salt reactors (MSRs), since solidification in drain lines or passive heat removal systems can obstruct emergency cooling lines and trigger uncontrolled temperature excursions in the reactor core. To predict this behavior, an improved solidification model is developed, which can be adopted in thermal-hydraulic system codes. Building on an existing fuel salt freezing formulation, the present model adds an energy equation for the pipe wall to restore the wall thermal inertia that the earlier model neglects. The governing equations are cast in control-volume form with semi-implicit numerical solution and solved in a MATLAB program for assessment. The model is first applied to the conceptual FLiBe and water cases, where it reproduces the existing model without the wall and predicts slower freezing once the wall thermal inertia is included. The model is then validated against dynamic and static water-freezing experiments and showing better agreement with measured data than the reference models. The results indicate that the proposed model captures the physics of molten salt freezing and provides a useful basis for MSR safety analysis within the MARS code.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104762','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104762',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115237','Partially closed nuclear fuel cycle strategy integrating a NuScale-like reactor and an Accelerator Driven System (ADS)','NuScale 유사 원자로와 가속기 구동 시스템 (ADS) 을 통합한 부분 폐쇄형 핵연료 사이클 전략','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Keferson de A. Carvalho; Graiciany Barros; Geovana L. Cruz; Matheus H.S. Araujo; Tiago Augusto Santiago Vieira; Rebeca Cabral Gonçalves; Higor Fabiano Pereira de Castro; Vitor Silva; Andre A. Campagnole dos Santos','2026-10-01','','2026-12','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This study proposes a partially closed nuclear fuel cycle that integrates a NuScale-like reactor with an adapted Accelerator-Driven System (ADS) through a three-stage approach. NuScale first produces spent fuel, which is reprocessed using the GANEX technique and loaded into the ADS-SMR, a smaller version of the ADS reactor geometrically adapted to match the NuScale dimensions and to incorporate the seed-blanket-unit (SBU) concept. Initially, the ADS-SMR arrangement contains reprocessed fuel in the seed region and thorium dioxide in the blanket region, aiming at fuel regeneration. This thorium-after-breeding fuel is then progressively loaded back into the three batch positions of the NuScale core designed for fresh fuel insertion during reshuffling, thereby resulting in three models with distinct fuel loading patterns. Results showed that the effective multiplication factor from the ADS-SMR dropped slightly over ten years, even without additional fissile input during the operation time. It also generated significant 233 U, reaching about 5.82 wt% fissile content. Back to the NuScale reactor, the three models exhibited early criticality increases due to in-situ fissile breeding, with one of the models nearly doubling energy output per kgHM compared to the reference case. Overall, the study highlights a feasible path for a partially closed nuclear fuel cycle strategy integrating ADS and SMR technologies. The Serpent code version 2.1.32, developed by VTT, and the ENDF/B-VII.0 nuclear data library have been used to perform the simulations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115237','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115237',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','BR','BR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115238','Impact of neutron spectrum and burnability on the selection of spectral shift absorbers for space nuclear reactors','중성자 스펙트럼과 연소성이 우주 핵 원자로의 스펙트럼 이동 흡수체 선택에 미치는 영향','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Baihui Jiang; Jiayi Zhang; Ding She; Jun Sun; Yu Ji; Jing Zhao; Zhihong Liu; Lei Shi','2026-10-01','','2026-12','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','To ensure subcriticality during launch abort accidents while minimizing operational reactivity penalties, Spectral Shift Absorbers (SSAs) are essential for space nuclear reactors. However, existing SSA selection studies are often limited to specific reactor designs and neglect the effects of lifetime burnability, thereby limiting the general applicability and reliability of their conclusions. In this work, the comparative analysis of SSA effectiveness is conducted for three representative reactors with different neutron energy spectra. Five candidate SSAs, including 151 Eu 2 O 3 , 155 Gd 2 O 3 , 157 Gd 2 O 3 , 10 B 4 C, and 151 Eu 10 B 6 , are evaluated. Two mission profiles, 1 MWth and 5 MWth for 10 years, are considered to analyze burnability effects. The results indicate that SSA effectiveness is strongly dependent on the reactor neutron spectrum. The effectiveness ranking can be explained by a proposed spectral crossover mechanism, which governs the balance between accident flux suppression and operational flux penalty. Furthermore, SSA burnability influences end-of-life performance, thereby changing the SSA effectiveness rankings. As a result, 10 B 4 C surpasses 151 Eu 2 O 3 as the superior SSA in the Reactor C with high burnup profiles. Besides, although 157 Gd 2 O 3 exhibits poor burnability in the fast spectra, it offers superior performance in the Reactor B where the crossover energy aligns with the resonance region. These findings demonstrate that both spectrum characteristics and burnability behavior have important influences in SSA selection, providing generalized guidance for future space reactor designs.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115238','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115238',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115254','Experimental study on thermal cycling phenomena and load response in downward-horizontal (DH) stagnant branch pipes of nuclear power plants','원자력 발전소의 하향 수평 (DH) 정체 분기 파이프에서 열 사이클링 현상 및 부하 반응에 대한 실험적 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Gao Qile; Gao Chang; Chen Hong''en; Deng Ke; Chen Zhenmao; Wang Hongliang','2026-10-01','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Thermal cycling phenomena refer to periodic fluctuations of the cold-hot interface in pipes of nuclear power plants, which induce temperature fluctuations and cause fatigue damage, threatening long-term operational safety. The downward-horizontal (DH) stagnant branch pipe is commonly found in nuclear power plants and is particularly susceptible to this phenomenon. Several related incidents have been reported internationally, making it necessary to study its characteristics for developing engineering protection strategies. This study investigated thermal cycling phenomena in a DH stagnant branch pipe using a high-temperature, high-pressure thermal-hydraulic test facility. The geometry of the test section was designed through numerical simulation and iterative debugging to capture thermal cycling in a large stagnant branch pipe, and pipe wall temperatures and strains at key locations were measured synchronously. The synchronous measurement provides direct experimental evidence of the cyclic loading induced by thermal cycling, which in previous studies was mainly inferred from numerical simulations. Experiments covered steady and pulsating flow conditions, with temperatures ranging from 60 to 260 °C and main pipe flow velocities from 3.1 to 10 m/s. analysis of data from 14 test cases shows that, under typical conditions, thermal cycling exhibits a sawtooth-shaped fluctuation characterized by rapid rise, temporary stabilization, and slow decline, with superimposed multi-time-scale variations. Under thermal cycling, pipe wall stresses at the elbow and horizontal sections show highly synchronized periodic fluctuations with temperature, confirming that the phenomenon generates significant fatigue loading on the structure. The cold-hot mixing region can be divided into three distinct zones along the pipe, whose extents are influenced by the temperature and flow velocity of the main pipe. Excessively low or high temperature differences between the main and branch pipes both dampen the fluctuations, the former for insufficient mixing drive and the latter for buoyancy-dominated suppression. Within a sensitive intermediate temperature-difference range, however, the cold-hot interface becomes unstable due to turbulent penetration and heat dissipation, leading to complex flows and intensified fluctuations. A higher steady main pipe velocity enhances turbulent penetration, while a pulsating main flow causes the cold-hot interface to undergo repeated reconstruction-breakdown-reconstruction cycles, amplifying flow instability and significantly increasing temperature and load fluctuations. Dynamic flow variations should therefore be avoided during plant operation. The results provide experimental data and a mechanistic basis for the numerical validation, fatigue assessment, and engineering protection of DH stagnant branch pipes against thermal cycling','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115254','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115254',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115240','Corrigendum to “An artificial neural network assisted approach for developing onset of significant void correlations in subcooled flow boiling” [Nucl. Eng. Des. 457 (2026) 115036]','Corrigendum to “An artificial neural network assisted approach for developing onset of significant void correlations in subcooled flow boiling” [Nucl. Eng. Des. 457 (2026) 115036]','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Thanh-Binh Nguyen; Yoshiyasu Hirose; Akira Satou; Satoshi Abe; Yasuteru Shibamoto; Tomio Okawa','2026-10-01','','2026-10','정오표','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115240','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115240',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115243','A comparative study on MELCOR and MAAP simulations of a severe accident scenario in a Nordic boiling water reactor','북유럽 끓는 물 원자로에서 심각한 사고 시나리오의 MELCOR 및 MAAP 시뮬레이션에 대한 비교 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Björn Engström; Roberta Concilio Hansson; Weimin Ma','2026-10-01','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study juxtaposes the results from two independent simulations of a station blackout scenario in a Nordic boiling water reactor (BWR) using the MAAP and MELCOR codes. The purpose is to better understand and analyse code differences in general and the existing MELCOR and MAAP models of a Nordic boiling water reactor (BWR) in particular. The figures of merit in the comparative study are chronology of events till the actuation of filtered containment venting (FCV), corium temperature and relocation, reactor pressure vessel (RPV) pressure, containment pressure and hydrogen generation. Observed from the limited scope of comparisons, the overall accident progression and the failures of fuels and RPV lower head are consistent with the findings of the MAAP-MELCOR crosswalk study previously performed by EPRI and Sandia National Laboratories ( Luxat et al., 2016 ; Andrews et al., 2017 ). The MELCOR model predicted a later vessel breach and melt ejection into the containment than the MAAP model did, while the MAAP model predicted earlier actuation of the FCV system even though the MELCOR model showed a faster containment pressure increase after RPV failure due to greater hydrogen accumulation. The two codes also differed in their predictions of post-venting containment response, with the MELCOR simulation featuring a significant containment pressure oscillation with a cyclic period of 3–4 h, caused by difference in modelling of pool hydrodynamics in the lower drywell and the wetwell. Since containment pressure evolution is important to safety, this phenomenon merits further investigation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115243','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115243',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','SE','SE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112893','Simulation and exergy analysis of the EPR nuclear power plant','EPR 원자력 발전소의 시뮬레이션 및 엑서지 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Dana Al Ghoul; Patrice Paricaud','2026-10-01','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','A detailed energy and exergy assessment of the European Pressurized Reactor (EPR) plant is conducted to evaluate its thermodynamic performance and identify opportunities for efficiency improvement. Simulations of both the primary and secondary circuits were performed using the DWSIM process simulation software with the CoolProp property package. The predicted overall energy efficiency of the plant reaches 39% at a condenser temperature of 30°C, while the exergy efficiency of the secondary circuit is estimated at 77%. When the reactor core is included in the analysis, the overall exergy efficiency declines to 39%, close to the energy efficiency, revealing that most of the exergy destruction arises from irreversible nuclear-to-thermal energy conversion. The study highlights the contrast between energy and exergy perspectives: most energy losses occur at the condenser, while the secondary circuit is highly optimized in terms of exergy, and the nuclear reactor is the site of the largest exergy destruction. Coupling the EPR with a Rankine bottoming cycle using appropriate working fluids allows significant recovery of condenser waste heat, yielding a substantial increase of the electrical power output.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112893','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112893',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112883','Mass analysis of supercritical nitrous oxide and helium in a recompression Brayton cycle utilizing in-situ resources for lunar base energy system','달 기지 에너지 시스템에 대한 현장 자원을 활용하는 재압축 브레이튼 사이클에서 초임계 아산화질소 및 헬륨의 질량 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Xinyu Miao; Yongfa Zhang; Ling Chen; Haochun Zhang','2026-10-01','','2027-02','연구논문','핵연료·재료','The Moon is the only natural satellite of the Earth and also the closest celestial body to the Earth. The Moon is regarded as an outpost of deep space exploration. The construction of lunar base infrastructure, polar exploration, and rovers constitutes the first step for humans to venture into the Moon. In the process of constructing a lunar base, it is essential to establish an energy system that can fully utilize local resources. This system will reduce the weight of materials transported from Earth and ultimately solve the energy shortage problem on the Moon. A recompression Brayton cycle that utilizes in-situ resources, with supercritical nitrous oxide and helium as the working media, and evaluates the mass of the energy system. A small modular reactor is applied to predict the minimum-mass reactor suitable for the given cycle conditions. The system mass and specific mass optimization explored the trade-offs among the reactor, radiation shield, Brayton cycle unit, recuperator, and radiator to obtain the minimum mass of the lunar base energy system. The results indicate that the specific mass of the energy system is 17.37 kg∙kWe −1 . In addition, it is found that, by utilizing in-situ lunar base resources, the mass and volume of the radiation shield for the reactor can be reduced by 3.55% and 14.20%, respectively. In conclusion, the proposed energy system scheme offers several advantages, including light weight, high efficiency, and continuous electricity supply, for application in lunar bases.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112883','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112883',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112882','Interpretability study on generalization ability of data-driven fault diagnosis methods under domain shifts for nuclear power plants: From the perspective of data representations','원자력 발전소에 대한 영역 이동 하에서의 데이터 기반 고장 진단 방법의 일반화 능력에 대한 해석성 연구: 데이터 표현의 관점에서','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zhenfeng Niu; Jiangkuan Li; Jiaoshen Xu; Meng Lin; Chenxin Zhu; Taixi Zhang; Sichao Tan; Ruifeng Tian','2026-10-01','','2027-02','리뷰·관점','기타 원자력','The generalization ability of data–driven fault diagnosis models is critically challenged in Nuclear Power Plants (NPPs) due to domain shifts arising from varying operating conditions. In existing studies, model generalization ability is primarily enhanced through modifications to model architectures or learning algorithms, whereas the impact of data representations on generalization ability is rarely investigated. To address the above limitations, an integrated framework is proposed to analyze the impact of data representations on generalization ability and the potential mechanisms. By constructing different representations of the raw data through various feature scaling methods, the impact of data representations on model generalization ability is assessed via systematic training and evaluation. Furthermore, the mechanisms by which data representations influence model generalization ability are elucidated by SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations)-based interpretability analysis from both global and local perspectives. Distinct feature–dependence patterns across trained models are induced by disparities in the relative distributions of Domain–Invariant Features (DIFs) and Domain–Sensitive Features (DSFs), thereby resulting in variations in generalization ability. By systematically characterizing the influence of data representations on model generalization ability and elucidating the potential mechanisms that lead to performance variations, novel insights and practical guidance are provided for enhancing the generalization ability of fault diagnosis models in NPPs, which can be achieved by obtaining more generalizable data representations through optimized feature scaling methods.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112882','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112882',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112821','Adaptive spatial convolution weight window smoothing for global variance reduction in deep-penetration Monte Carlo simulations','심층 침투 몬테카를로 시뮬레이션에서 전체 분산 감소를 위한 적응형 공간 컨볼루션 가중치 윈도우 스무딩','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Dengjian Wu; Junjun Gong; Zifu Hao; Junxiang Mao; Yuhang Zhang; Chengqiang Liang','2026-10-01','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','In deep-penetration Monte Carlo simulations, the efficiency of the weight window global variance reduction (WWGVR) method critically depends on the accuracy of the lower weight window bounds. Statistical fluctuations during the initial iterations of self-coupled Monte Carlo method often lead to biased weight window estimates, triggering long-history problems. Conventional practice relies on empirical parameters as mandatory constraints. However, these parameters exert limited influence on Figure-of-Merit (FOM) within reasonable ranges, indicating that the efficiency bottleneck lies not in parameter fine-tuning but in the rationality of the weight window distribution. To address this, an Adaptive Spatial Convolution Weight Window Smoothing (ASCWWS) method is proposed, which employs an error-adaptive neighbourhood convolution kernel to achieve low-pass filtering and regularization of the weight window field, transforming point estimation into field estimation to suppress high-frequency noise and restore physically consistent importance gradients. Validation on the HBR-2 and EURACOS benchmarks shows that ASCWWS improves the FOM by factors of 1.86 and 4.06 compared to the conventional MAGIC method, respectively, with the incidence of importance inversion reduced by over 31%. By enhancing weight window distribution quality, ASCWWS reduces reliance on empirical parameters and can be directly integrated into existing self-coupled Monte Carlo method frameworks as a post-processing tool, offering a new pathway for efficient WWGVR simulation of deep-penetration problems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112821','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112821',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106632','Thermal-hydraulic analysis of rotated wire wrap in LFR assembly under normal operation and flow blockage conditions','정상 작동 및 유동 차단 조건에서 LFR 어셈블리에서 회전 와이어 랩의 열수력 분석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Zhibo Gao; Di Wu; Jinchao Li; Jie Cheng; Xu Han; Xiaobo Zeng; Jianjun Wang','2026-09-30','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study presents a CFD investigation of thermal-hydraulic behavior in a 19-pin wire-wrapped lead-based fast reactor (LFR) fuel assembly under normal operation and flow blockage conditions. The numerical model is validated against the NACIE-UP ADP10 experiment using the SST k-ω turbulence model, with temperature and pressure drop comparisons confirming grid independence. Two heating modes (uniform and central) and four rotation angles of the central wire wrap (60° and 120° clockwise and counterclockwise) are considered. Results show that wire rotation modifies radial coolant paths and degrades near-wall heat transfer, causing localized temperature rises that are more pronounced under central heating. Subsequently, two blockage cases are simulated under central heating at different axial positions. Although blockage effects on temperature distribution become negligible after flow recovery, at the blockage end, peak temperatures can increase by up to 51 K depending on rotation angle and axial location, and the extent of the disturbed flow region also varies. These findings underscore the need for enhanced attention to local thermal-hydraulic safety when rotated wire wraps and blockage accidents coexist.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106632','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106632',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106634','Operational characteristics of the experimental test facility for the passive cooling system of spent fuel pools','소비 연료 풀의 수동 냉각 시스템을 위한 실험 테스트 시설의 작동 특성','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Ta Van Thuong; S.M. Glukhov; O.L. Tashlykov; D.E. Shumkov; Yu.V. Volchikhina; Nguyen Dinh Khuong','2026-09-30','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Ensuring reliable removal of residual heat from spent fuel pools is a key safety requirement for nuclear facilities, particularly for research reactors where the safe storage of spent fuel assemblies must be maintained under both normal and accident conditions. This paper presents the results of experimental studies of a test facility for a passive residual heat removal system designed for spent fuel assemblies in the spent fuel pool of a research nuclear reactor. The study employed both theoretical and empirical methods. The article describes the main thermal-hydraulic parameters and design features of the test facility and provides a description of the experimental methodology. The results of tests carried out under various operating modes of the facility are presented, including operation with full and partial filling of the circuit with the working fluid and operation in an annular thermosyphon mode. The experimental results confirm the operability of the proposed design and demonstrate the capability of the system to provide effective heat removal under different thermal conditions. In addition, three-dimensional modeling of the test facility was performed, which made it possible to identify design characteristics of components not accessible to visual inspection and to optimize the configuration of the evaporator module to ensure a more uniform distribution of the working fluid flow. A theoretical assessment of the impact of using this facility as part of a passive heat removal system on nuclear safety when installed in a spent fuel pool is also provided. The obtained results indicate that the installation of the proposed system does not lead to a violation of nuclear safety requirements and can serve as a basis for the development of a full-scale passive cooling system for spent fuel pools of research reactors.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106634','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106634',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','RU;VN','VN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106638','Impact of possible nuclear phase-out strategies in Spain for a sustainable energy transition','지속 가능한 에너지 전환을 위한 스페인의 가능한 핵 단계적 폐기 전략의 영향','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Iván Merino Rodríguez; Francisco Álvarez-Velarde; Alejandro Prada Valverde; Pablo Romojaro; Constanza Mora Inzunza; Victor J. Casas-Molina','2026-09-30','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Spain''s long-term energy strategy combines rapid renewable expansion with the progressive phase-out of nuclear power by 2035. Since the timing of reactor retirements can significantly affect the long-term electricity balance, this study compares four nuclear phase-out scenarios: the current official retirement schedule (SCN_40) and three lifetime-extension pathways allowing reactor operation up to 50, 55, and 60 years (SCN_50, SCN_55, and SCN_60, respectively). All scenarios use the same demand and renewable deployment trajectories. A target-driven daily simulation developed with LEAF-EB combines historical generation and demand patterns with projections derived from the PNIEC and Spain''s long-term decarbonization strategy. For each scenario, 1000 Monte Carlo simulations estimate clean electricity surpluses and the raw clean generation gap. Surpluses are allocated to BESS charging, exports, and synthetic methane production, while the gap is covered by BESS discharge, cross-border imports, methane reconversion, and residual backup. Over 2028–2050, extending reactor operation from the official schedule to 60 years reduces the modeled cumulative clean generation gap by 39.1% and electricity imports by 38.5%, while exports increase by 72.4%. BESS discharge covers 7.2–11.4% of the gap, while imports account for approximately 21% across all scenarios. Electricity recovered from stored synthetic methane increases from 77.2 to 153.2 TWh, raising its contribution from 8.1% in SCN_40 to 26.5% in SCN_60. The residual backup requirement decreases by 61.0%, from 599.3 to 233.5 TWh, but still covers 40.4% of the gap in SCN_60 and is required on 14.0% of simulated days. Extending nuclear operation therefore reduces the magnitude and frequency of balancing requirements but does not eliminate the need for firm backup generation under the modeled assumptions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106638','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106638',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CL;ES;BE','CL','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106635','Design of liquid lead-bismuth eutectic flow velocity measurement based on contactless inductive flow tomography','비접촉 유도 유동 단층 촬영을 기반으로 한 액체 납-비스무트 공융 유속 측정 설계','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Zhen Zhang; Jiangtao Jia; Zhen Wang; Mingyue Li; Jie Yu','2026-09-30','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','liquid lead-bismuth eutectic (LBE) serves as the coolant for lead-cooled fast reactors (LFR), its velocity distribution is a critical parameter in thermal-hydraulic research. However, the high-temperature corrosivity and opacity of LBE pose significant challenges to the application of traditional flow velocity measurement methods. To address this issue, this study applies Contactless Inductive Flow Tomography (CIFT) and designs a measurement system applicable for LBE flow velocity measurement. The validity of the proposed measurement scheme is verified by comparing the reference velocity field with the velocity field reconstructed via the reconstruction algorithm. Maintaining a comparable total number of sensors, we compare three spatial arrangements: 12×4, 10×5, and 8×6. The results indicate that the 8×6 arrangement achieves the highest degree of agreement between the reconstructed and reference velocity field. Furthermore, the applicability of this measurement system is verified under noisy condition and within complex flow field. The proposed design scheme and sensor configuration analysis provide a valuable reference for the future application of CIFT in LBE flow measurement.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106635','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106635',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106627','Conceptual study of a supercritical CO2-cooled, triply periodic minimal surface lattice-based microreactor','초임계 CO2 냉각, 삼중 주기적 최소 표면 격자 기반 미세 원자로의 개념 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Nicolas Martin; Silvino Balderrama Prieto; Paul Ferney','2026-09-30','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Advancements in additive manufacturing (AM) processes have made it increasingly feasible to consider optimized shapes such as triply periodic minimal surface (TPMS) lattices for heat transfer applications, ranging from heat exchanger designs to nuclear fuel elements. This study introduces a TPMS-lattice-shaped nuclear core and compares its performance against that of a traditional pin-based design. A publicly available design that relies on typical fuel pin elements for a fast spectrum, supercritical CO 2 (sCO 2 )-cooled reactor with a direct Brayton cycle was selected as the reference design. The same core materials were used in the TPMS core to ensure a fair comparison between both geometries. Due to the complexity of this type of geometry, innovative modeling strategies were introduced. The thermal performance of the TPMS fuel element was analyzed using a computational scheme that combined high-fidelity computational fluid dynamics (CFD) with Multiphysics Object-Oriented Simulation Environment (MOOSE)-based 1D thermal hydraulics, coupled with 3D heat transfer. Monte Carlo reactor physics analyses using unstructured meshes in Serpent were employed to characterize the core performance and verified against a native constructive solid geometry TPMS lattice implementation in OpenMC. When it comes to fast spectrum reactors, TPMS geometries are neutronically equivalent to pin geometries. However, TPMS-based fuel elements offer improved heat transfer performance, enabling the power density to be increased up to 59% while still meeting the peak material temperature requirements. A downside of TPMS lattices is the additional pressure drop per unit length, which may be manageable when factoring the pumping power costs into the total energy generated by the proposed microreactor concept.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106627','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106627',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2737542','Network Algorithm-Based Implications of Nuclear Energy Capacity Expansion for Climate Mitigation','기후 완화를 위한 원자력 에너지 용량 확대의 네트워크 알고리즘 기반 시사점','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Kyung Bae Jang; Chang Hyun Baek; Tae Ho Woo','2026-09-30','2026-09-29','2026-09-29','연구논문','AI·디지털','This study aims to develop an advanced, AI-driven System Dynamics model utilizing the Internet of Everything (IoE) to evaluate the impact of tripling nuclear energy capacity on climate change mitigation in alignment with the 28th Conference of the Parties (COP28) objectives. The Internet of Things (IoT), a network of interconnected devices, has been employed for computer system communication. The IoE extends this concept to encompass a more interconnected world, integrating processes, data, objects, and individuals. A dynamic simulation of 100 months was conducted, examining the interactions of Things, People, Data, and Processes. While the classification of Things increased steadily, the People category exhibited two distinct peaks at the 30th and 55th months, with false positives (FP) outnumbering Ttue positives (TP), false negatives (FN), and true negatives (TN). FN and TN demonstrated comparable trends. The Data category increased gradually across all classifications, while Processes declined with sporadic drops. A comparison of Recall (RC) and Precision (PC) shows consistently higher RC values, with People achieving the highest overall. These findings offer actionable insights for large-scale IoT and IoE systems in energy, manufacturing, transportation, and smart cities. Trends like steady growth in Things and Data, human-system volatility, and the importance of recalibration help organizations optimize system design, reduce errors, and improve smart infrastructure adaptability.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2737542','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2737542',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2726097','ForewordSpecial Issue on Tools and Methods for Spent Nuclear Fuel Management','FOREWORD소모 핵연료 관리를 위한 도구 및 방법에 관한 특별호','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Harish Reddy Gadey','2026-09-30','2026-09-29','2026-09-29','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Used nuclear fuel management remains one of the nuclear industry’s most persistent and consequential challenges. As of 2025, an estimated 447 000 metric tons of heavy metal (MTHM) of used fuel had ...','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726097','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726097',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104752','Five-Year Trend of Workplace Ambient Radiation Level at the Philippine Nuclear Research Institute - Radioactive Waste Management Facility','필리핀 원자력 연구소 - 방사성 폐기물 관리 시설의 작업장 주변 방사선 수준 5년 추이','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Lenlen S. Desoloc; John Wilkin F. Lim; Angelo A. Panlaqui; Ronald E. Piquero; Kristine Marie R. Dean','2026-09-30','','2026-09','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104752','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104752',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104754','Comprehensive Atomistic Investigation of the Structural and Thermodynamic Properties of CrUO4 and Cr2UO6','CrUO4 및 Cr2UO6의 구조적 및 열역학적 특성에 대한 포괄적인 원자적 조사','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Hengfeng GONG; Daxi GUO; Lixiang WU; Mingzhou CHEN; Jiwei WANG; Jiaxiang XUE; Haixiang HU; Pengliang LIU; Yuxiang ZHANG; Liutao CHEN; Guoliang ZHANG','2026-09-30','','2026-09','연구논문','핵연료·재료','ABSTRACT In this study, spin-polarized DFT+U calculations were performed to investigate thermo-mechanical properties and irradiation-induced defect evolution of CrUO 4 and Cr 2 UO 6 compounds within the Cr-U-O system. It should be noted that these two phases are treated as independent, hypothetical chemical entities in the present work. The calculated lattice parameters deviate from experimental and theoretical data by 1-2%, an acceptable range for actinide oxide simulations. Both compounds exhibit distinct mechanical anisotropy: orthorhombic Cr 2 UO 6 strongly resist uniaxial compression, while hexagonal CrUO 4 has orientation-dependent elastic stiffness. Plasticity indices ( δ = B / C 44 ) confirm their good ductility, and 3D analyses further verify anisotropy in elastic moduli, Poisson’s ratio and hardness. Total and partial density of states reveal the bonding contributions of Cr 3 d , U 5 f and O 2 p orbitals. We also calculated thermodynamic parameters and point defect energies. Chromium interstitials are energetically favorable in both phases, unlike oxygen interstitials dominant in pure UO 2 . Interstitial defects show negative trap energies, where uranium vacancies possess the highest values. This work offers fundamental theoretical data for understanding the intrinsic behaviors of CrUO 4 and Cr 2 UO 6 themselves, which may provide indirect reference for broader studies on advanced Cr-doped UO 2 nuclear fuel systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104754','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104754',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115246','Research on irradiation-Thermo-mechanical coupled analysis for HTGR fuels','HTGR 연료에 대한 조사-열-기계적 결합 분석에 관한 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Hao Yang; Bin Zhang','2026-09-30','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Predicting the thermo-mechanical response of TRISO particle fuel is important for fuel performance assessment in high-temperature gas-cooled reactors. This study developed CoaPAC (COated fuel Performance Analysis Code), a spherical TRISO fuel performance code that couples implicit heat transfer, fission gas and CO release, viscoelastic coating mechanics, gap evolution, and pressure-vessel (PV)-type failure models. First, CoaPAC was benchmarked against the IAEA CRP-6 mechanical test case, and its results were compared with published results from other fuel performance codes for the HFR P4, HFR-EU1, and NPR-1 irradiation conditions. The results show that CoaPAC reproduces the principal evolution trends of key thermo-mechanical variables, and the comparisons support the consistency of the basic physical modules and their coupled implementation. CoaPAC was then applied to a complex full-life-cycle scenario involving irradiation, storage, and accident heating. The results demonstrate that, under a continuous and complex operating history, CoaPAC can reasonably describe the coupled responses of TRISO particles, including heat transfer, gas composition, coating stress, and failure behavior at different stages. Therefore, the verification and comparison analyses conducted in this study support the accuracy and reliability of the code, demonstrate the reasonableness of its thermo-mechanical model implementation and its capability to handle complex conditions, and further clarify priorities for future code development.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115246','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115246',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112876','Numerical study on direct contact condensation of countercurrent subcooled water-steam flow in a steam-filled vertical rectangular narrow channel','증기 충진 수직 직사각형 좁은 채널에서 역류 부냉 수증기 흐름의 직접 접촉 응축에 대한 수치 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yan Li; Gaokui Xie; Jihang Ouyang; Tao Lu','2026-09-30','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','A two-dimensional computational fluid dynamics (CFD) model was developed to investigate direct contact condensation (DCC) during counter-current flow of subcooled water and steam in a steam-filled vertical rectangular narrow channel. The model incorporates the Volume of Fluid (VOF) method, Lee phase-change model, Continuum Surface Force (CSF) model, and RNG k–ε turbulence model. The effects of subcooled-water and steam inlet velocities on flow evolution, pressure response, and counter-current flow limitation (CCFL) were systematically analyzed. The results show that the channel pressure exhibits pronounced periodic pulsations. Increasing the inlet velocities of both phases strengthens interfacial shear and flow disturbances, thereby intensifying interfacial instability, promoting condensation-induced water hammer (CIWH), and increasing the pressure oscillation intensity. The maximum pressure is mainly controlled by the subcooled-water inlet velocity and increases monotonically with it, while steam injection markedly amplifies the pressure peak compared with single-phase liquid injection. The average pressure increases with either inlet velocity, with the liquid velocity exerting a stronger effect. Flooding and liquid-bridge formation are observed during counter-current flow, triggering CCFL. As the subcooled-water-to-steam velocity ratio increases, CCFL weakens, whereas higher steam velocities lead to earlier liquid-bridge formation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112876','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112876',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106631','Numerical study on debris bed formation characteristics following the FCI of a nuclear reactor severe accident with the EMPS method','EMPS 방법으로 원자로 중증 사고의 FCI에 따른 잔해층 형성 특성에 대한 수치 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Jinhua Que; Yunlong Liao; Gen Li','2026-09-29','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Debris bed formation during fuel-coolant interaction (FCI) is a key process in the analysis of severe nuclear reactor accidents. Existing numerical studies typically decouple melt jet breakup and debris bed formation, relying on idealized fragment shape assumptions. The present study conducts a continuous numerical simulation of the FCI process by coupling the Explicit Moving Particle Semi-implicit (EMPS) method with a Contoured Continuum Surface Force (CCSF) model, a fragment identification model, and a Passively Moving Solid (PMS) model. The integrated approach tracks the dynamic evolution from initial melt injection and solidification to final bed accumulation. The established numerical model is validated against experimental data, with macroscopic predictions showing consistency with physical measurements. Parametric analyses reveal the mechanisms governing debris bed morphology. Increasing the LBE temperature, jet velocity, and water temperature increases the spreading area. High LBE and water temperatures induce edge crust remelting and secondary expansion. Furthermore, the debris bed accumulation height decreases as these three parameters increase. The total porosity increases with elevated LBE temperatures and jet velocities, and decreases under higher cooling water temperatures. The proposed modeling approach provides quantitative insight into debris bed formation and may support the development of severe accident management strategies.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106631','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106631',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104753','Evaluation of time-dependent background in neutron time-of-flight transmission measurements using a 6Li-glass scintillation detector','6Li-유리 섬광 검출기를 사용한 중성자 비행 시간 전송 측정의 시간 의존적 배경 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Jaehong Lee; Fabiana Rossi; Kota Hironaka; Cebastien Joel Guembou Shouop; Tomooki Shiba; Tadafumi Sano; Kazushi Terada; Jun-ichi Hori','2026-09-29','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Accurate evaluation of time-dependent background is essential for reliable neutron time-of-flight (TOF) transmission measurements in neutron resonance analysis (NRA). In this study, we experimentally investigated the time-dependent background in neutron transmission measurements utilizing a 6 Li-glass scintillation detector at the Kyoto University, Institute for Integrated Radiation and Nuclear Science - Linear Accelerator (KURNS-LINAC). A comparative analysis was conducted on three background evaluation techniques, namely the black resonance, neutron absorber, and pulse-height (PH) gate techniques under identical measurement conditions. The results demonstrated that background levels obtained with resonance filters or neutron absorbers can be underestimated due to gamma-ray attenuation by the inserted materials. Conversely, the PH gate technique can overestimate the background in the thermal energy range due to gamma-rays produced by the capture of scattered thermal neutrons. Herein, the characteristics, advantages, and limitations of each technique are discussed, and practical guidance for selecting appropriate techniques and corrections to achieve accurate background evaluation in neutron transmission measurements using a 6 Li-glass scintillation detector is presented, supporting improved resonance analysis for future NRA applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104753','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104753',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115233','Core characteristics of a modified pebble-bed high-temperature gas-cooled reactor design','변형된 조약돌 베드 고온 가스 냉각 원자로 설계의 핵심 특성','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Xuelin Li; Songyang Liu; Lang Wang; Jingsong Guo; Sanping Xiao; Wei Liu','2026-09-29','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','As a promising candidate of Small Modular Reactors (SMRs), high-temperature gas-cooled reactor (HTGR) proves its technical superiority and maturity with the successful commercial operation of Chinese High Temperature gas-cooled Reactor Pebble-bed Module (HTR-PM) in Shidao Bay, Shandong. HTR-PM employs an online-refueling pebble-bed reactor design. Spherical fuel elements enter the core through the top fueling tube, gradually move downward through the pebble bed, and are discharged via the bottom defueling tube. Simultaneously, the coolant enters the pressure vessel and flows around its periphery before reaching the cold helium plenum at the top of the core. It then cools the pebble core in a top-down flow, merges in the hot helium plenum at the bottom, and finally exits the pressure vessel. Based on the design of the HTR-PM, a modified core design (HTR-UD) is proposed, featuring a top-down movement of spherical fuel elements and a bottom-up flow of coolant. This design leverages the strong negative temperature feedback in HTGR to flatten the axial power distribution within the core. A comparative analysis of the core characteristics between the two designs is conducted, and two core upgrading schemes are investigated for the HTR-UD. The analysis results indicate that the HTR-UD can significantly reduce the maximum fuel temperature by approximately 175 °C under depressurized loss of forced cooling (DLOFC) accident. Furthermore, it demonstrates the potential to increase the thermal power by approximately 40% or increase the reactor outlet coolant temperature to 900 °C compared to the original HTR-PM design.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115233','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115233',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115180','An evaluation of diffusivity and resolution models for fission gas release in UO2','UO2에서 핵핵분열기체 방출에 대한 확산도 및 분해능 모델 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Kaylee M. Cunningham; Christopher Matthews; Michael R. Tonks','2026-09-29','','2026-12','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Gas atom behavior is of particular interest to nuclear reactor designers as it plays a key role in determining fission gas release and fuel swelling. Various models have been developed for both the diffusivity and resolution of fission gas in UO 2 for use in fuel performance codes, including both empirical models fitted to experimental data and mechanistic models that represent physical behaviors. This work establishes a consistent methodology for comparing empirical and mechanistic diffusivity and resolution models by evaluating their impact on calculated fission gas release in BISON for several integral light water reactor irradiation experiments. Model accuracies are assessed by comparing the BISON-calculated release with the final fission gas release from the irradiation experiments. Bland–Altman analyses of each combination of models indicate that the mechanistic combination of Matthews diffusivity and Setyawan resolution, with other input parameters fixed, has a lower bias of -0.028% FGR than the historically used empirical pairing, the Turnbull-D1–D2–D3 diffusivity with White resolution, which produces a bias of -1.938% FGR. These results provide a comparative basis for selecting diffusivity and resolution models and suggest that mechanistic models can improve agreement with integral irradiation experiments while offering a more physically based framework for predicting fission gas release beyond the existing experimental database.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115180','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115180',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112878','Numerical study of flow distribution and the effect of unsteady flow of liquid sodium coolant in annular rods scalloped-wall fuel assembly','환형 로드 스캘럽 벽 연료 어셈블리에서 유동 분포 및 액체 소듐 냉각수의 비정상적인 유동의 영향에 대한 수치 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ayodeji A. Ala; Oluwaseun Talabi; John Njoroge','2026-09-29','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','The core of small sodium-cooled fast reactors is designed to be compact, meeting various regulatory and economic objectives. Heat removal in a compact core can be enhanced by using a tightly arranged annular rod fuel assembly within a scalloped-wall duct. This study investigates the steady and periodic flow of liquid sodium coolant through the triangular tight lattice ( P/D = 1.08) annular rod scalloped-wall fuel assembly. The scalloped wall reduced the temperature difference between the center subchannel and gaps by up to 30% compared to a flat-walled fuel assembly. The flow split between the inner and outer subchannels is 10% – 13% in the fuel assembly. The relationship between the Reynolds number and flow friction resistance aligns with previous results for a light water reactor fuel assembly. Periodic flow intensifies the turbulence distribution within the subchannels. A new correlation was proposed for the flow split between the inner and outer subchannels in the tight triangular-lattice scalloped-wall annular rod fuel assembly.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112878','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112878',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112880','Effects of corrosion-product particle deposition on flow-induced vibration of an LBE-cooled wire-wrapped fuel rod bundle','LBE 냉각 와이어로 감싼 핵연료봉 다발의 유동성 진동에 대한 부식-제품 입자 증착의 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Haolin Ning; Mei Huang; Yiyuan Du; Shuai Zhang; Jitong Sun; Aonan Li; Junliang Lin','2026-09-29','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Corrosion-product particles generated in lead–bismuth eutectic (LBE) coolant may be retained on wire-wrapped fuel assemblies, and different particle-laden conditions associated with wall retention may modify local fluid excitation. A computational fluid dynamics–discrete phase model–flow-induced vibration (CFD-DPM-FIV) framework combining the shear stress transport (SST) k–ω model and one-way fluid–structure coupling is developed for a seven-pin LBE-cooled wire-wrapped fuel assembly to investigate the effects of particle mass flow rate, inlet velocity, and diameter. Under the reference particle condition, 73.87% of wall-trapped particles are located on the fuel-rod cladding surface, while 12.68% and 13.46% are located on the wire-wrap surface and hexagonal duct wall. Particle diameter and inlet velocity mainly alter the surface distribution of retained particles, whereas particle mass flow rate mainly changes the particle supply to the bundle. Although the global thermal–hydraulic parameters vary only slightly, the vibration response is sensitive to particle-retention conditions. Compared with the particle-free case, the high particle mass-flow-rate and large-particle cases increase the maximum total deformation from 85.208 μm to about 99.0 μm and the maximum von Mises stress from 0.2976 MPa to about 0.360 MPa. At the center-rod midspan, the fluctuating root-mean-square (RMS) displacement increases from 12.573 to about 22.96 μm in the X direction and from 33.774 to about 63.13 μm in the Z direction, while the dominant response frequency remains near 22 Hz. These results indicate that deposition-prone particle conditions can amplify the predicted FIV response before severe macroscopic blockage develops.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112880','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112880',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112860','An enquiry into noise-induced reactivity shifts in the point-kinetics equations','점 동역학 방정식에서 노이즈 유발 반응성 변화에 대한 문의','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Benjamin Dechenaux','2026-09-29','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Neutron noise analysis within the point-kinetics model is traditionally formulated using linear response theory under small-amplitude sinusoidal perturbations. Although this approach has proven successful in providing a conceptual foundation for neutron noise measurement and diagnostics, it neglects potential non-linear effects that may, for example, modify the stationary state of the reactor. In particular, effective reactivity shifts can be generated by non-linear interactions, which are not captured by the standard linearized treatment. These effects are nevertheless generally assumed to remain negligible under deterministic forcing. This assumption may break down in the presence of stochastic fluctuations. Multiplicative noise can indeed induce systematic drift terms in the effective dynamics, leading to noise-induced reactivity shifts that drive the mean neutron population away from stationarity. The present work investigates the impact of non-linear neutron noise within the point-kinetics model, considering both deterministic and stochastic excitations. The magnitude of the resulting reactivity shifts is quantified, and the respective roles of stochastic forcing and delayed neutron precursors are analysed, providing an assessment of their potential operational significance. • Sinusoidal perturbations induces a reactivity shift of the neutron population. • Another reactivity shift is observed in the case of multiplicative noise. • Delayed neutrons introduce correlation-dependent drift.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112860','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112860',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','FR','FR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106633','Theoretical design and parametric sensitivity analysis of a passive containment cooling system based on separated heat pipes','분리된 히트 파이프를 기반으로 한 수동 격납 냉각 시스템의 이론적 설계 및 파라메트릭 민감도 분석','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Weiyu Chu; Dufeng Lv; An Cao; Zhaoming Meng; Baihui Duan','2026-09-28','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','A design-oriented inverse methodology is developed for a separated heat pipe passive containment cooling system (SHP-PCS) to determine feasible system configurations from prescribed accident heat removal requirements. A steady thermal-hydraulic sizing model is established by coupling heat transfer characteristics, two-phase flow pressure losses, natural circulation constraints, and engineering design limitations. The resulting configuration is further evaluated using a one-dimensional steady-state analysis model to investigate the effects of working fluid inventory, heat exchanger geometry, and riser dimensions on system performance. Two system-level heat removal requirements are considered, including a 50 MW high-pressure and high-temperature accident condition and a 12 MW long-term cooling condition. The designed separated heat pipe module is analyzed as the basic heat removal unit, and multiple modules can be integrated to satisfy the overall system requirements. The results show that the optimized configuration demonstrates the capability of passive heat removal under a relatively small source-sink elevation difference. The working fluid inventory exhibits a significant influence on system performance, with an optimal range of approximately 30–40%. The heat exchanger diameter shows an optimum due to the competition between hydraulic resistance reduction and heat transfer degradation, while riser diameter mainly affects system performance by changing vapor-side flow resistance. The proposed inverse-design framework provides a systematic approach for determining SHP-PCS configurations from required heat removal duties and provides engineering guidance for the optimization and application of separated heat pipe passive containment cooling systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106633','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106633',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106609','High-fidelity prediction of LBE mixed convection heat transfer via gradient-balanced physics-informed neural networks','그라디언트 균형 물리 정보 신경망을 통한 LBE 혼합 대류 열전달의 고충실도 예측','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Yuefeng Guo; Xingkang Su; Yunxiang Li; Guan Wang; Long Gu','2026-09-28','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Mixed convection in liquid metals, such as lead-bismuth eutectic (LBE), presents intricate flow and heat transfer characteristics due to the strong coupling of forced and natural convection in low Prandtl number fluids. Accurately predicting these phenomena is paramount for the thermal-hydraulic safety and design of advanced nuclear reactors. In this study, a novel Mixed Convection Heat Transfer Physics-Informed Neural Network (MCHT-PINN) is proposed to conduct progressive case studies across a two-dimensional backward-facing step, a two-dimensional circular pipe, and a three-dimensional 19-pin fuel assembly. To address the highly coupled multi-physics fields, the MCHT-PINN architecture integrates the GradNorm adaptive-weight algorithm, which dynamically balances the loss gradients associated with the Partial Differential Equations (PDEs) and boundary conditions. The results demonstrate that the MCHT-PINN model achieves accurate predictions of both velocity and temperature fields, demonstrating excellent agreement with OpenFOAM reference solutions. The average relative L 2 errors are consistently maintained below 3% across all cases. Furthermore, the model accurately resolves complex coupled thermo-fluid phenomena, capturing not only buoyancy-driven velocity profile distortions but also the localized lifting of the thermal boundary layer and subsequent flow field evolution. Ultimately, these findings not only verify the robustness of the MCHT-PINN across varying geometries but also provide a reliable computational tool for evaluating complex thermal-hydraulics in liquid metal reactor components.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106609','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106609',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2735544','High-Fidelity Multiphysics Modeling of the Molten Salt Fast Reactor with Applications for Reduced-Order Models','주문 감소 모델에 적용된 용융염 고속 원자로의 고충실도 다물리 모델링','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Maximiliano Dalinger; Alex Nellis; Saya Lee; Casey Emler; Stefano Terlizzi; Elia Merzari','2026-09-28','2026-09-28','2026-09-28','연구논문','열수력·유체','The molten salt fast reactor (MSFR) is one of the six Generation-IV reactor designs. In the MSFR, the liquid fuel is also the coolant, which moves throughout the primary circuit. This complex phenomenology requires multiphysics modeling. In this paper, a high-fidelity model of the MSFR is developed in the multiphysics code Cardinal, accounting for neutronics–thermal-hydraulic feedback and the transport of delayed neutron precursors (DNPs) and decay heat precursors (DHPs).NekRS solves the mass, momentum, energy, and DNP and DHP transport equations. NekRS uses a Reynolds-averaged Navier-Stokes k−τ turbulence model. DNPs and DHPs are modeled using a convective diffusion equation with modified source terms that account for radioactive decay. OpenMC is used to solve the neutronics equation. Current limitations in OpenMC do not allow for the modification of delayed neutron source locations. Ongoing efforts look to include this feature in future work to introduce DNP feedback in OpenMC.The Cardinal results showed reasonable behavior for temperature, heat source, velocity, DNPs, and DHPs. In addition, the fission matrix (FM) method is used as a reduced-order neutronics model. The NekRS-FM model is analyzed and compared with the NekRS-OpenMC model. The results showed good agreement between the codes.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2735544','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2735544',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02057-3','Start-to-end commissioning simulation for the Hefei advanced light facility storage ring','허페이 첨단 조명 설비 저장 링을 위한 시운전 시뮬레이션','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Ke-Min Chen; Zhe Wang; Tao He; Duo-Hui He; Wei Xu','2026-09-28','2026-09-28','2026-09-28','연구논문','핵연료주기·폐기물','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02057-3','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02057-3',0,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115234','Topology optimization of the NaK78 inlet distributor for a liquid-cooled space nuclear reactor heat exchanger','액체 냉각 우주 원자로 열교환기에 대한 NaK78 입구 분배기의 토폴로지 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Asim Shehzad; ZhaoMing Meng; ChuanChang Dong; Amir Ali; Wajahat Hussain','2026-09-28','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Liquid-metal-cooled space nuclear reactors coupled with closed Brayton cycles are promising candidates for high-power deep-space missions. In these systems, the NaK78-to-He dual-fluid heat exchanger is critical. Yet, the concentrated liquid-metal inlet causes severe flow maldistribution, which can consume the limited pressure head (only 10–20% of that available from mechanical pumps) from electromagnetic pumps driving the NaK78 loop. Existing remedial measures rely on trial-and-error modifications to predefined geometric forms, offering no guarantee of optimality. In this work, we apply density-based topology optimization to autonomously determine the optimal solid baffle distribution within the NaK78 inlet plenum of a prototype space nuclear heat exchanger. The optimization is implemented in COMSOL Multiphysics 6.3 using Brinkman penalization and adjoint-based sensitivity analysis to minimize the integral of squared outlet velocity deviation. The inlet slot width is fixed at 8 mm ( Re ≈ 1980), ensuring the laminar flow assumption is strictly valid for this proof-of-concept study. Parametric investigations over solid volume fraction (φₛ = 0.3–0.7) and a uniformity-pressure-drop trade-off coefficient (C1 = 0–0.1 m −1 ) are conducted using β-continuation. The base-case optimized distributor achieves a coefficient of variation CV = 5.08% (uniformity index η = 0.949) and a pressure drop ΔP = 7.68 Pa, with φₛ = 0.5 identified as optimal. Notably, the uniformity-only objective (C1 = 0) is Pareto-dominant; increasing the pressure-drop penalty degrades both metrics simultaneously, a finding explained by the dual flow-organizing function of the curved baffles in the thin rectangular plenum. The optimizer autonomously discovers a curved bifurcating baffle topology physically analogous to wedge-shaped designs previously derived by empirical enumeration, yet obtained here rigorously and without geometric preconditioning. While the present 2D laminar model serves as a proof-of-concept, the discovered topology provides a physically meaningful baseline for future 3D turbulent validation under rated operating conditions. The present operating point corresponds to a thermal duty of approximately 6.8 kW; an order-of-magnitude assessment shows that remain laminar up to ∼500 kW(th) and only reaches transition at 1000 kW(th), while the inlet plenum becomes turbulent. This study establishes topology optimization as a systematic tool for inlet distributor design in liquid-metal nuclear heat exchangers, addressing the hydraulic root cause of maldistribution-induced thermal degradation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115234','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115234',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112879','Adaptive TD3-PID control for once-through steam generator using hardware-in-the-loop simulation','하드웨어-인-더-루프 (hardware-in-the-loop) 시뮬레이션을 사용하는 원스루 스팀 발생기를 위한 적응형 TD3-PID 제어','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','YuLong Wang; Qi Zhang; Yehu Yang; Peiwei Sun; Xinyu Wei','2026-09-28','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This paper presents a adaptive hybrid control framework that integrates Twin Delayed Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient (TD3) reinforcement learning with PID. This approach addresses the critical challenges of pronounced non-linearity, significant time delays, and wide-ranging operating conditions in the pressure control of Once-Through Steam Generators (OTSGs). By employing a TD3 agent to dynamically optimize PID within predefined safety bounds, the proposed strategy substantially improves system adaptability without compromising the inherent stability of the baseline PID structure. Extensive hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) experiments on an industrial distributed control system (DCS) demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed strategy. Quantitative results show that the TD3-PID control reduces settling times by more than 50% during setpoint tracking. Moreover, under large-scale load transients, the intelligent agent suppresses pressure overshoot by 73%-90% and effectively attenuates associated temperature fluctuations. These results validate the robustness and practical feasibility of the proposed TD3-PID architecture, offering a viable pathway for the deployment of intelligent control systems in advanced nuclear energy applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112879','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112879',1,'2026-10-04','2026-10-05','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106645','Geometric fidelity, contact-point treatment, and thermal hydraulics in pebble-bed FHR: A review of pebble-bed modeling strategies','페블베드 FHR의 기하학적 충실도, 접촉점 처리 및 열수력: 페블베드 모델링 전략 검토','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Guangyuan Jin; Chaoyi Chen; Yongxing Li; Hongye He; Yandong Hou','2026-10-11','','2027-01','리뷰·관점','열수력·유체','Fluoride-salt-cooled high-temperature reactors (FHRs) combine tri-structural isotropic (TRISO) fuel with low-pressure liquid-salt cooling, but their pebble-bed thermal hydraulics are unusually sensitive to how the packed geometry is generated and regularized for computation. This review connects five modeling decisions—packing generation, contact-point treatment, wall-effect representation, transport-model selection, and experimental validation—to the quantities used in reactor design. Ordered simple-cubic, body-centred-cubic and face-centred-cubic beds are distinguished from confined random beds because their channel connectivity, anisotropy and wall layering arise through different mechanisms. Contact regularization is assessed by separating global geometry changes from local gap, overlap, bridge, cap and hybrid treatments. In a published structured-bed benchmark, the selected treatment changed pressure drop by about 30% and the conduction-only maximum pebble temperature by 23%; the corresponding differences fell below 0.5% for full-power thermal metrics and to 0.3% when convection was included. These values are study-specific sensitivity indicators, not universal correction factors. Evidence from pressure-drop, velocity and heat-transfer experiments is mapped to the model scale and operating range that it can support. The synthesis shows that no single contact treatment is optimal for every quantity of interest: hydraulic screening, local hot-spot prediction and passive-loss-of-forced-circulation analysis require different levels of geometric and thermal-contact fidelity. A decision framework is therefore proposed to link geometry, regularization, physics, validation and engineering use while making transferability limits explicit.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106645','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106645',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104779','Transient Dynamic Response of a Thorium-Based Molten Salt Reactor Under Reactivity Insertion followed by Loss of Flow and Loss of Heat Sink','반응성 삽입 후 유동 손실 및 히트 싱크 손실이 뒤따르는 토륨 기반 용융 염 원자로의 일시적인 동적 반응','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Xiao-Sheng Li; Tao Zhou; Jian-Quan Liu; Meng-Bin Li; Yu-Bo Cheng','2026-10-11','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','ABSTRACT In molten salt reactors the mobile fuel couples neutronics and thermal-hydraulics so closely that a second failure can change the outcome of an accident qualitatively. A nonlinear transient code couples lumped-parameter thermal-hydraulics with point kinetics retaining both the loss and the delayed return of drifting precursors, and resolves the structural wall separately from the salt. Validated against Molten Salt Reactor Experiment data, it was applied to a 200 MWth U-233 thorium-based molten salt reactor (TMSR) for reactivity insertions of 10–500 pcm followed by loss of flow (LOF) or loss of heat sink (LOHS). Temperature feedback always shuts the reactor down, but decay heat then carries the structure past the 800 °C Hastelloy N limit. For a 100 pcm insertion the limit is reached at 2299 s under LOF, where stagnation opens a 59 K fuel–wall temperature difference, and at 5557 s under LOHS, where circulation retains the loop inventory as thermal ballast. This ordering reverses between 200 and 300 pcm, above which neither configuration protects the structural boundary. Inherent feedback therefore bounds the fuel temperature but does not ensure structural integrity, and margins assessed against the salt temperature overstate the available response time by up to a factor of five.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104779','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104779',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;BD','BD','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104777','Interpreting Representative Parameter Values in Safety Assessment: Implications for System Evolution in Deep Geological Repositories','안전성 평가에서 대표 파라미터 값 해석: 심층 지층처분장의 시스템 진화에 대한 시사점','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Myeongjin Kang; Kunok Chang','2026-10-11','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','A safety case is the collection of arguments and evidence to demonstrate the safety of a facility. The safety case includes safety assessments, and representative parameter values are widely used in safety assessments to simplify time-dependent repository conditions in performance assessment modeling. In existing safety assessments, time-dependent repository conditions are commonly represented by a single representative parameter value selected to simplify transport calculations. Repository conditions, however, evolve over time through coupled thermal, hydraulic, mechanical, and chemical processes, and a single representative parameter value may not adequately represent all stages of repository evolution. This study reviews existing safety case approaches, examines the relationship between repository evolution and parameter applicability, and proposes a decision process for evaluating representative parameter values. The analysis indicates that existing modeling approaches remain analytically valid, but representative parameter values should be interpreted and applied with explicit consideration of repository evolution and stage-specific system conditions. Explicit evaluation of representative parameter values with respect to repository evolution stages provides a clearer basis for judging whether representative parameter values remain appropriate for a given stage of repository evolution.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104777','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104777',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112927','Experimental study of void fraction and its distribution characteristics in vertical narrow rectangular channels','수직 좁은 직사각형 채널에서 공극 분율과 그 분포 특성에 대한 실험적 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Teng Wang; Yuhao Zhang; Yuepeng Ma; Lu Liu; Tao Zhang','2026-10-11','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Two-phase flow in narrow rectangular channels is of continued interest in multiphase flow research because of its importance in compact heat transfer applications. Gas-liquid flow in these geometries exhibits complex interfacial behavior and flow-regime transitions driven by the interactions of inertial, viscous, and capillary forces, which strongly affect heat and mass transfer performance. In this study, visualization experiments using high-speed photography were conducted to investigate vertical upward gas–liquid two-phase flow in narrow rectangular channels with cross-sectional dimensions of 15 × 2 mm 2 and 50 × 2 mm 2 . A MATLAB-based image-processing procedure was used to identify flow patterns and extract two-phase flow parameters. Four distinct flow patterns were identified, and the corresponding local void fraction distributions and probability density functions (PDFs) of instantaneous cross-sectional void fraction were obtained. The results showed that the void fraction increased consistently from the wall toward the channel center. At a fixed liquid flow velocity, increasing the gas flow velocity shifted the PDF from a sharp peak at low void fraction to a broader distribution at higher void fraction, with the dominant peak gradually evolving into a bimodal distribution. A modified drift-flux model was developed to predict the time-averaged cross-sectional void fraction, and the predicted values agreed well with the experimental data, with errors within 10 % for both channels.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112927','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112927',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106640','Nuclear data-induced uncertainties in the neutron source for vessel fluence evaluations: Application to TVA-watts bar unit 1 cycle 1','선박 플루언스 평가를 위한 중성자원의 핵 데이터 유발 불확실성: TVA-watts bar unit 1 cycle 1에 적용','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Iñigo Gayo; Emilio Castro; Nuria García-Herranz; Oscar Cabellos; Kostadin Ivanov','2026-10-10','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Accurate reactor pressure vessel (RPV) fluence prediction is essential for long-term operation licensing and relies on the so-called industrial, two-step workflow: an in-core multi-physics calculation to determine the neutron source, followed by an ex-core fixed-source transport calculation through surrounding structures. Nuclear data uncertainties propagate across both steps and may therefore affect the Best Estimate Plus Uncertainty (BEPU) assessment of RPV fluence, starting from the impact on the in-core neutron source. In this work, a random sampling uncertainty propagation procedure is applied to a nodal full-core model of the OECD/NEA TVA–Watts Bar Unit 1 (TVA-WB1) Cycle 1 benchmark using the in-house SEANAP computational system, after verification and validation against plant measurements and CASL/VERA reference results. Nuclear data-induced uncertainties are propagated specifically to the three-dimensional neutron source, a key input for subsequent RPV fluence analyses, although the propagation of the source uncertainties in the fluence calculation is not performed. Three evaluated libraries are considered, ENDF/B-VII.1, ENDF/B-VIII.1, and JEFF-3.3, with the analysis targeting the dominant contributors to the fission source term, namely U-235, U-238, Pu-239, as well as H-1 thermal scattering in light water. The study focuses on fuel assemblies in the peripheral region of the core, quantifying both total uncertainties and the individual contributions from isotopes and dominant reaction channels. Results show that, for all evaluated libraries, propagated uncertainties in neutron source intensity remain below 4%. Uncertainties are higher in the early cycle and generally decrease with burnup. Spatially, the upper and lower axial regions exhibit larger relative uncertainties than the mid-plane, and corner assemblies present the highest uncertainties among peripheral locations. The analysis identifies U-235 ¯ 𝜈 and U-238 inelastic scattering as leading contributors in specific evaluations, while ENDF/B-VIII.1 yields the lowest overall uncertainty levels. The framework enables future assessments of technological-parameter-induced uncertainties and additional nuclear data evaluations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106640','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106640',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','ES;US','ES','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106643','A new method for calculating the weak source startup of reactor based on Monte Carlo method','몬테카를로 방식에 기반한 원자로의 약한 시동을 계산하는 새로운 방법','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Conglong Jia; Yuanhao Gou; Kan Wang; Shichang Liu','2026-10-10','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Weak source startup represents a reactor startup regime in which neutron population evolution is dominated by stochastic effects and cannot be adequately described using conventional deterministic or point-kinetics approaches. The weak source startup approach, which operates without an external neutron source, eliminates the need for costly neutron source procurement and improves the economic performance of nuclear power plants. In this study, a Monte Carlo based method is developed for simulating weak source startup processes. The proposed approach enables direct time-dependent simulation of stochastic neutron transport and allows the transition from stochastic to deterministic behavior to be identified through the evolution of the fission rate. Unlike traditional stochastic neutron kinetics methods, which are typically limited to simplified geometries, the present method is applicable to realistic three-dimensional reactor configurations. The method is demonstrated using both a KRUSTY heat-pipe-cooled reactor and a small pressurized water reactor. The results show that the transition time during weak source startup exhibits inherent statistical variability and that the spatial distribution of maximum neutron flux gradually becomes concentrated as the neutron population increases. The proposed framework provides a practical computational tool for analyzing weak source startup phenomena in engineering-scale reactor systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106643','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106643',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104780','Experimental Study on Spray Activation in a Containment Atmosphere with Superheated Steam Conditions during a Design Basis Accident','설계 기초 사고 중 과열된 증기 조건을 가진 격납 분위기에서의 스프레이 활성화에 관한 실험적 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Myeong-Seon Chae; Domenico Paladino; Mira Jreissaty; Jean-Luc Vacher','2026-10-10','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','ABSTRACT This study presents experimental results on large-scale containment thermal-hydraulics driven by the combined effects of steam injection and spray activation under a postulated design basis accident scenario, such as a main steam line break. The experimental campaign consisted of two experiments, identified as P1A1_5 and P1A1_6, which form part of the P1A1 series conducted within the OECD/NEA PANDA project to investigate PWR containment spray systems. The experiments were conducted in the facility, which consists of a large-scale cylindrical vessel. Initial conditions involved pressurization with air and steam up to 2.5 bar under superheated conditions. The spray system was activated using a single nozzle. The experiments were divided into three phases: steam injection only, combined steam and spray injection, and spray only injection. The results show that during containment depressurization, steam remains superheated above the spray nozzle, whereas below the nozzle the measured fluid temperature closely follows the saturation temperature. This behavior may be associated with enhanced condensation near the vessel wall and possible spray-induced flow recirculation. Upon spray activation, pressure and temperature gradients below the spray nozzle decrease more rapidly over time than during Phase 2, possibly reflecting spray-induced mixing and droplet dynamics.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104780','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104780',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CH','CH','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112924','Power reconstruction in hexagonal-assembly small reactor using thin-plate spline and in-core detector response','얇은 플레이트 스플라인 및 인코어 검출기 응답을 사용하는 6각형 조립 소형 원자로의 전력 재구성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hao Yang; Tianxiang Wang; Zhuo Li; Shengli Chen','2026-10-10','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The three-dimensional power distribution (3DPD) of a reactor core is an important indicator of reactor operating conditions, and its accurate reconstruction is essential for core monitoring and safe operation. Compared with conventional large reactors, small reactors with hexagonal fuel assemblies exhibit stronger neutron leakage and more complex spatial power characteristics, increasing the difficulty of power reconstruction. To address this issue, this study investigates 3DPD in a hexagonal-assembly small pressurized water reactor using the thin-plate spline (TPS) method combined with in-core detector response functions. The results show that the in-core detector response exhibits strong spatial localization characteristics. Radially, the detector response is mainly concentrated within the third ring of neighboring assemblies (∼15 cm). Neglecting detector response leads to significant reconstruction errors. By incorporating detector response functions, the TPS method effectively suppresses reconstruction deviations under different burnup levels, keeping all post-reconstruction relative errors within the commonly adopted 8% acceptance criterion. The proposed method demonstrates good applicability to hexagonal fuel assembly 3DPD reconstruction in small reactors.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112924','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112924',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106644','Impact of residual nuclides on the transmutation of Np and Am in a lead-cooled fast reactor','납 냉각 고속 원자로에서 잔류 핵종이 Np 및 Am의 변형에 미치는 영향','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Yue Jiang; Zhiwen Wen; Shiyu Song; Junkui Xu; Yiwei Gong; Xiaoqin Tang; Yuxuan Huang; Xu Zhou; Liyingran Zeng; Xiang Hu; Jianling Ran; Sen Song; Peng Luo','2026-10-09','','2027-01','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Partitioning and Transmutation (P&T) is recognized as an effective strategy for mitigating the burden associated with the geological disposal of minor actinide (MA) nuclides. This study investigates the impact of three types of residual nuclides, namely, rare earth elements (REs), uranium, and plutonium, that remain in MA fuels during the partitioning process. Based on a 500 MW th lead-cooled fast reactor (LFR) developed using OpenMC, the effects of these residuals on the transmutation performance of 237 Np, 241 Am and 243 Am are systematically analyzed. The results reveal that the effective delayed neutron fraction varies non-monotonically within the 0-50 wt.% residual nuclide content range, and no significant decrease is observed. Spectral analysis demonstrates that RE 2 O 3 (rare earth oxide) and UO 2 induce spectrum softening, whereas PuO 2 hardens the spectrum. Transmutation calculations further show that for all three MAs, both the transmutation rates and capture-to-fission ratios increase approximately linearly with an increasing RE 2 O 3 and UO 2 content, whereas they decrease with an increase in PuO 2 content. This research elucidates the distinct mechanisms of these residuals in LFRs, providing a foundational basis for developing transmutation strategies for impure MA fuels.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106644','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106644',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106639','Experimental study on flow patterns and pressure oscillation characteristics of vertical upward steam jets at low water temperatures','저수온에서 수직 상향 스팀젯의 유동 패턴 및 압력 발진 특성에 관한 실험적 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Weiyu Chu; Jidong Cong; Zhaoming Meng; Ping Song; Yinghua Chai','2026-10-09','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Experiments were conducted to examine flow-regime transitions and pressure responses of vertically upward steam jets at low water temperatures (0–50 °C) and steam mass fluxes of 40–550 kg/(m 2 ·s). By combining high-speed imaging with high-frequency dynamic-pressure measurements, a flow-regime map was constructed. Within the investigated parameter range, seven regimes were identified and their observed operating regions were mapped. The maximum positive pressure excursion, p max , was used as a descriptive peak metric over each displayed time interval. For the three displayed 5-s chugging records, p max increased from 4.94 to 20.53 kPa as pool-water temperature increased from 0 to 20 °C. Among the displayed 50-ms records, hemispherical condensation oscillation reached 88.53 kPa, ellipsoidal condensation oscillation reached 149.85 kPa, and the stable-jet cases ranged from 5.16 to 10.56 kPa. These values are single-run, non-duration-normalized maxima.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106639','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106639',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2739693','Effects of Activation Energy and Joule Heating on Reactive MHD Micropolar Nanofluid Flow Over a Permeable Stretching Sheet','투과성 스트레칭 시트에 대한 반응성 MHD 극소극성 나노유체 흐름에 대한 활성화 에너지 및 줄 가열의 효과','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Sreedhar Sarma Gobburu; Govardhan Kamatam','2026-10-09','2026-10-09','2026-10-09','연구논문','열수력·유체','In this work, the effect of combined Joule heating and activation energy on steady magnetohydrodynamic micropolar nanofluid flow along a permeable stretching surface is investigated. The novelty of this model is the coupling of micropolar microrotational physics with thermal radiation, viscous dissipation, Dufour diffusion, and temperature-dependent chemical kinetics. The governing nonlinear partial differential equations are converted to a set of coupled ordinary differential equations by similarity transformations and then numerically solved by the fourth-order Adams-Moulton method with a shooting technique. The results indicate that there was significant improvement in the thermal field by the Joule heating effect, which caused the surface heat transfer rate to decrease by 4.17% due to the Joule heating. On the other hand, for a higher activation energy, chemical reaction kinetics decreases, and thus, the number of nanoparticles increases as the rate of mass transfer decreases by 15.02%. Moreover, the effect of viscous dissipation and thermal radiation increases the thermal boundary layer thickness while the cross-diffusion transport of the species is dominated by Brownian motion and thermophoresis. These insights provide practical design mechanisms for optimizing advanced nanofluid thermal management systems in high-temperature engineering applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2739693','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2739693',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104776','Exploring the effects of dual-layered Cr/Nb coating thickness on the corrosion and annealing response characteristics of an accident-tolerant Zr fuel cladding material','듀얼 레이어 Cr/Nb 코팅 두께가 사고 내성 Zr 연료 피복관 재료의 부식 및 어닐링 응답 특성에 미치는 영향 탐구','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Ubong Eduok; Jerzy Szpunar','2026-10-09','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','Cr-coated Zr alloys are accident-tolerant fuel (ATF) cladding materials that offer practical solutions to nuclear challenges due to their inherent benefits. Nonetheless, drawbacks remain, including Cr-Zr interdiffusion, which accelerates coating degradation, especially where the role of interlayer coating thickness is not clearly defined. In this study, an Nb interlayer barrier is fabricated between a Cr topcoat and Zircaloy-4 to investigate how corrosion and annealing response characteristics change with varying thickness. Annealing at 1200 °C for 5 min led to microcrack formation at the coating/alloy interfaces, interfacial voids (in thicker coatings), and adhesion loss (in thinner coatings). This was followed by an average thickness loss of up to 1.1 μm for the former and 2.3 μm for the latter. The present study was conducted under thermal conditions simulating a near-serious accident scenario to observe potential interfacial changes at a relatively accelerated rate. While high-temperature electrochemistry remains relatively unexplored in nuclear research as an approach to studying coolant chemistry, the conditions for the present electrochemistry and Zr-release studies were chosen only to test corrosion performance, and not to simulate reactor conditions. The long-term research objective is to develop safe, reliable ATF cladding materials for use in light-water reactors (LWRs) under varying conditions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104776','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104776',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115250','Surrogate-based engineering evaluation and service-life enhancement of a pleated 316 L metal-fiber cartridge for lead‑bismuth coolant purification','납 비스무트 냉각수 정제를 위한 주름 316 L 금속 섬유 카트리지의 대리석 기반 엔지니어링 평가 및 서비스 수명 향상','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Zilong Li; Jianfeng Wang; Yanmin Zhou; Haoliang Ren; Haifeng Gu; Zexiang Chen','2026-10-09','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Corrosion-product control in lead‑bismuth eutectic (LBE) coolant loops is important for maintaining hydraulic reliability, reducing impurity accumulation, and extending the service life of purification components. However, engineering-scale data on the filtration efficiency, dust-holding capacity, and pressure-drop evolution of pleated metal-fiber cartridges for LBE systems remain limited. In this study, a pleated 316 L sintered metal-fiber cartridge was experimentally evaluated using a water-SiO 2 surrogate system, and the applicability of the surrogate was assessed through mechanism-based similarity analysis. The results show that both the surrogate and the target PbBi-Fe3O4 system operate in the creeping-flow regime (Re f 95%) and a dust-holding capacity of 1668 g/m 2 at a terminal pressure drop of 300 kPa. Continuous segmented regression revealed a two-stage pressure-drop/loading relationship with a transition at approximately 1027–1050 g/m 2 , corresponding to a shift from pleat-internal loading to outer-surface cake growth. This transition provides a practical maintenance indicator for cartridge replacement. Structural optimization showed that reducing the packing density of the sintered medium increased dust-holding capacity by 6.86%, while introducing an outer loose-fiber layer further delayed rapid pressure-drop growth. The best configuration, a 3 mm-compressed coating with an 8 μm fiber diameter, increased the corrected dust-holding capacity from 2048 to 3052 g/m 2 , corresponding to a 49.05% improvement. The present work establishes a surrogate-based engineering framework for evaluating and optimizing pleated metal-fiber cartridges for corrosion-product removal in LBE coolant purification systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115250','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115250',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115236','Sodium-cooled fast reactors: design evolution, safety innovations, and economic competitiveness challenges and sustainability outlook','소듐 냉각 고속 원자로: 설계 진화, 안전 혁신, 경제 경쟁력 과제 및 지속 가능성 전망','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Zhiwen Dai; Shu Wang; Nuerlan Areai; Donghui Zhang; Zhiwei Zhou; Xiuli Xue; Chao Lin; Xintai Yu; Dalin Zhang; Songping Wang; Yeqiang Xu; Yizhe Liu; Mo Wang; Yuting Yang','2026-10-09','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115236','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115236',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115242','GT-833 and NeuSys: an auditable neuro-symbolic framework for nuclear regulatory constraint extraction and consistency checking','GT-833 및 NeuSys: 핵 규제 제약 추출 및 일관성 검사를 위한 감사 가능한 신경 기호 프레임워크','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Gyu-Hyun Lim; Yuchul Jung','2026-10-09','','2026-12','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115242','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115242',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115245','Experimental and numerical study on aerosol mass concentration attenuation in reactor containment during LBB events','LBB 사건 중 원자로 격납에서 에어로졸 질량 농도 감쇠에 대한 실험적 및 수치적 연구','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Bifan Liu; Yue Miao; Yonglong Cui; Junlian Yin; Dezhong Wang','2026-10-09','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','Under Leak-Before-Break (LBB) accident conditions, containment ventilation systems can operate under elevated air exchange conditions, introducing forced convection that modifies aerosol transport behavior. Large internal structures in engineering-scale compartments further disturb the flow field and generate spatially heterogeneous flow and turbulence structures. Many existing aerosol attenuation and deposition models were developed and validated either for sealed, quiescent environments dominated by natural convection, or for obstacle-free chambers under low-to-moderate ventilation rates. Their applicability to LBB-relevant conditions therefore remains uncertain. This study investigates aerosol attenuation in a mechanically ventilated compartment with representative nuclear-island obstacle layouts at an air change rate of 12 h −1 , intended to represent compact containment layouts adopted in integral pressurized water reactor and small modular reactor concepts. Experiments were combined with numerical simulations comparing an Eulerian approach incorporating the Lai–Nazaroff deposition formulation and a Lagrangian Discrete Phase Model with Discrete Random Walk (DPM–DRW) framework. The measured average total aerosol removal rate was 25.4 h −1 , of which deposition contributed 13.4 h −1 . This deposition component exceeds values commonly reported under conventional indoor ventilation conditions and is comparable to the ventilation removal contribution. When coupled with a near-wall-resolving turbulence closure—specifically the Shear Stress Transport (SST) k–ω model—the DPM–DRW framework reproduced the observed attenuation trend with a predicted decay coefficient of 22.8 h −1 , within 10.2% of the measured 25.4 h −1 . By contrast, wall-function-based models (realizable k–ε) overpredicted removal by over a factor of two, while both the well-mixed single-zone model and the Lai–Nazaroff formulation systematically underestimated deposition-associated attenuation under the present geometric and flow conditions. These results indicate that deposition may remain an important removal mechanism even under elevated ventilation conditions in compactly arranged containment compartments. The findings suggest that conventional ventilation-dominated attenuation assumptions do not fully capture aerosol removal under the present conditions, and that deposition should therefore be considered when selecting an aerosol attenuation model for such compact configurations.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115245','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115245',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/s0029-5493(26)00514-5','Editorial Board','편집위원회','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','','2026-10-09','','2026-12','편집물','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0029-5493(26)00514-5','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0029-5493(26)00514-5',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112918','Structural improvement of tilting-pad thrust bearings in nuclear reactor coolant pumps based on thermal elastohydrodynamic lubrication analysis','열탄소 수력학 윤활 분석을 기반으로 한 원자로 냉각수 펌프의 틸팅 패드 스러스트 베어링 구조 개선','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Fengyu Lin; Xiaojun Liu; Yuyan Zhang; Pengcheng Du; Lina Si; Tao Wu','2026-10-09','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','As a core supporting component of a nuclear main pump, the tilting-pad thrust bearing carries a large axial load, and its lubrication performance directly affects the operational reliability of the pump. This study develops a fluid–structure coupled thermal elastohydrodynamic lubrication model for an oil-lubricated point-supported tilting-pad thrust bearing by considering the contact effect at the pad-back pivot. Within each physical time step, partitioned iterative coupling is implemented between the oil-film lubrication field and the thermoelastic deformation field of the pad. Based on this model, improved schemes for the pad pivot position and pad surface profile are determined, and the lubrication performance of the bearing under extreme accident conditions is evaluated. The results show that thermoelastic deformation of the pad significantly affects the distributions of oil-film pressure, film thickness, and temperature. Considering the maximum oil-film pressure, minimum oil-film thickness, and maximum oil-film temperature, the bearing investigated in this study exhibits the best comprehensive lubrication performance when the radial offset coefficient is 0.51, the circumferential offset coefficient is 0.57, and the height of the parabolic pad surface profile is 6 μm. The optimized structure also improves the pressure and film thickness distributions during coast-down condition, thereby enhancing the oil-film safety margin. This study provides a theoretical basis and numerical method support for thermal elastohydrodynamic lubrication analysis, structural parameter optimization, and transient shutdown safety evaluation of tilting-pad thrust bearings in reactor coolant pumps.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112918','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112918',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112907','In-depth design and construction of an integrated thermal-hydraulic facility (INTALI) for a prismatic gas-cooled micro reactor','프리즘 가스 냉각 초소형원자로용 통합 열수력 설비 (INTALI) 의 심층 설계 및 시공','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zheng Huang; Miaoxin Jiao; Jian Jiao','2026-10-09','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','To support the development of an innovative gas-cooled micro reactor (GMR), an integrated thermal-hydraulic facility (INTALI) has been designed to investigate heat transfer and fluid behaviors under both prototypical operating conditions and representative accident scenarios, thus providing a basis for thermal-hydraulic code validation. The INTALI facility consists of a helium circulation loop and a test section containing a scaled-down simulated reactor and a passive core cooling system (PCCS). This paper aims to finalize the facility design and corresponding experimental methodology. Firstly, the overall configuration and layout of the apparatus were described. An analytical model was developed to predict the helium temperature distribution along the primary loop, which is critical to facility operational control and piping integrity. A pre-test calculation under nominal conditions indicates that all helium temperatures throughout the loop remain below the piping safety limit. Parametric calculations were performed to study the influences of both heating power and the flow rate ratio of the main flow to the protective flow. Secondly, the detailed structural designs of the test section were elaborated. Specific internal components within the reactor were designed, including tenon-mortise joints for fuel assembly alignment and core baffles to suppress bypass flow. Structural analysis confirms that incorporating four reinforced ribs improves the PCCS dome’s stiffness. The layout and the installation of thermocouples (TCs) within both the reactor and the PCCS were described. A comparative calculation demonstrates that the mixer effectively enhances mixing of the main and the protective flows, thus lowering the temperature at the reactor outlet. Thirdly, an experimental methodology was proposed to simulate an anticipated transient without scram (ATWS) accident initiated by loss of forced coolant. To incorporate the temperature-reactivity feedback, a computational module solving the neutron point kinetics model was developed and validated. Furthermore, dedicated data processing along with uncertainty analysis methods were formulated to derive key physical quantities from experimental measurements: 1) friction factor of helium through a coolant channel, 2) heat exchange rate between the reactor and the PCCS, and 3) convective heat transfer coefficient on the reactor pressure vessel (RPV) wall. Finally, the current status of facility construction and the planned testing program in the next stage are outlined.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112907','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112907',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112831','Experimental study and modeling Investigation on counter-current flow limitation phenomenon in reactor downcomer with DVI injection','실험 연구 및 모델링 DVI 주입이 있는 원자로 강수관의 역류 유량 제한 현상에 대한 조사','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Qiqi Yan; Yiran Xiong; Ren Liang; Zhikang Lin','2026-10-09','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','During the refilling phase of a large-break loss-of-coolant accident (LBLOCA), the large upward flow of steam generated in the core region enters the reactor downcomer, causing the cooling water to fail to descend into the reactor core in time. This results in counter-current flow limitation (CCFL). The passive safety injection system of the HPR1000 reactor incorporates direct vessel injection (DVI) technology in the reactor pressure vessel (RPV). DVI has different injection characteristics compared to traditional loop injection, leading to differences in the phenomena and processes during a LBLOCA. To investigate the gas–liquid two-phase characteristics of the CCFL behavior in the RPV downcomer section with DVI injection under LBLOCA conditions, an RPV integral test facility was designed and constructed based on scaling criteria and the design features of the prototype reactor, and experimental and modeling studies were then performed. Emergency core coolant (ECC) experimental data were obtained under different inlet ECC flow rates, core steam flow rates, etc. Based on these experimental results, a conservative analysis was performed using the LBLOCA-specific analysis code — CATHARE GB. The results indicate that lowering the axial height of the DVI nozzle and installing a DVI flow diversion structure can effectively suppress ECC bypass. The CATHARE GB model used in the analysis of the LBLOCA analysis with DVI injection is conservative, and the current reactor incorporates DVI technology within the RPV. The ECC design can maintain an adequate safety margin.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112831','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112831',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112922','Critical heat flux prediction in water-cooled vertical tubes using fuzzy-clustering-assisted AdaBoost and random forest models','퍼지 클러스터링 지원 AdaBoost 및 랜덤 포레스트 모델을 사용하는 수냉식 수직 튜브의 임계 열 플럭스 예측','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Farhan Labib Arnab; Tamim Muhammad Rayeed; Ali Mahdi; S.M. Nymul Hasan Anik','2026-10-09','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Accurate prediction of critical heat flux (CHF) in water-cooled vertical tubes is essential for thermal–hydraulic safety, yet many empirical and mechanistic methods are valid only within restricted operating ranges. This study evaluates whether fuzzy c-means (FCM) clustering improves data-driven CHF prediction using 4,384 experimental observations from vertical round tubes. Six predictors were considered: tube diameter, heated length, pressure, mass flux, inlet subcooling, and exit quality. Elastic Net, k-nearest neighbors, random forests (RF), AdaBoost, FCM-assisted RF, and FCM-assisted AdaBoost were evaluated using a common fixed 70:30 training-test partition. Hyperparameters of the standalone models were optimized by five-fold cross-validation within the training set, whereas the FCM-assisted models used an internal fitting-validation split for joint optimization of the clustering and regression components. FCM membership values were used to decompose the CHF target without including CHF in the clustering inputs. FCM-assisted AdaBoost achieved the best test performance, with a relative root-mean-square error (rRMSE) of 18.1 % and a root-mean-square relative error (RMSRE) of 11.7 %. FCM markedly reduced the RMSRE of RF, from 65.9 % to 16.4 %, whereas the improvement over standalone AdaBoost was smaller (RMSRE: 16.1 % to 11.7 %). These results demonstrate that fuzzy pre-clustering can improve predictive performance for the present heterogeneous CHF dataset, although the physical interpretation of the resulting fuzzy partitions requires further investigation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112922','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112922',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','BD','BD','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112888','Adaptive mesh refinement for Monte Carlo unstructured mesh tallies: Studies from rod bundles to a whole core','몬테카를로 비정형 메쉬 탈리에 대한 적응형 메쉬 개선: 로드 번들에서 코어 전체에 이르는 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Kevin C. Sawatzky; Ebny Walid Ahammed; Paul P.H. Wilson; Patrick C. Shriwise; Paul K. Romano; April J. Novak','2026-10-09','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112888','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112888',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112896','A buoyancy-adaptive reduced-order surrogate for heated rod-bundle transients using gauge-consistent deep orthogonal decomposition','게이지 일관성 깊은 직교 분해를 사용하는 가열된 로드 번들 과도 현상을 위한 부력 적응 감소 주문 대리인','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Xinheng Zhao; Minjun Peng; Guangliang Chen; Xiang Zhang','2026-10-09','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Heated rod-bundle transients couple changes in flow rate, temperature, and buoyancy-driven secondary motion, making them difficult to represent with a fixed global reduced basis. Proper orthogonal decomposition (POD) works well for nearly linear forced-convection hydraulics, but the transverse structures that develop under mixed convection vary with the buoyancy state and require a basis that adapts to the operating condition. This study develops a buoyancy-adaptive reduced-order surrogate for transient rod-bundle thermal-hydraulics using gauge-consistent deep orthogonal decomposition (DOD). The surrogate reconstructs the three velocity components and the temperature field, and is coupled with a coolant-residence-time-based thermal-lag model with a data-calibrated prefactor and a quasi-steady hydraulic closure. It is evaluated against processed steady operating states and transient CFD simulations. Compared with a global POD using the same coefficient mapper, the DOD surrogate gives more accurate reconstructions of the buoyancy-sensitive transverse velocity components. Heated flow-decrease and flow-increase tests show that the surrogate captures the main axial-flow response and temperature evolution under both uniform and skewed heating conditions. These results demonstrate the benefit of buoyancy-adaptive reduced bases for reconstructing nonlinear transverse flow structures in heated rod-bundle transients and establish a practical route for extending real-time rod-bundle digital twins from isothermal hydraulics to heated buoyant transients.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112896','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112896',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106641','Thermo-fluid characteristics at the points of onset of nucleate boiling and onset of significant void in vertical upward boiling flows','수직 상향 비등 흐름에서 핵산염 비등의 개시 및 상당한 공극의 개시 시점에서의 열유체 특성','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Shichang Dong; Takashi Hibiki','2026-10-08','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','The onset of nucleate boiling (ONB) and the onset of significant void (OSV) are critical transition points that demarcate heat transfer regimes and govern the development of two-phase flow in subcooled boiling flows. Accurate prediction of these two characteristic points is of great significance for the thermal-hydraulic design and safety analysis of industrial heat exchange equipment, such as nuclear reactors and steam generators. This study focused on the local characteristics at the ONB and OSV points in vertical upward flow channels. Firstly, a low-pressure ONB experimental database covering various channel geometries (including circular tubes, rectangular channels, and rod bundles) was compiled, and the existing classical ONB prediction models were systematically evaluated. The results indicated that the existing models exhibited considerable scatter and significant deviations. To address this issue, a new ONB correlation was developed based on a correlation analysis of the active nucleation site density with dimensionless parameters. The developed correlation reduced the mean absolute relative deviation for wall superheat prediction at ONB to 19.7%, outperforming existing models. Secondly, for the OSV point, a comprehensive drift-flux model was employed to analyze the cross-sectional void fraction and its axial development rate, revealing an exponential correlation between these parameters and the modified dimensionless Sauter mean diameter. Furthermore, by incorporating a bubble layer thickness model, the local parameters of the bubble layer (i.e., bubble layer thickness and void fraction) at the OSV point were quantitatively characterized for both externally heated channels and internally heated annular channels, and corresponding predictive correlations were established. The results demonstrated that the average void fraction within the bubble layer remains essentially constant (approximately 0.1) in externally heated channels, whereas it increased exponentially with the cross-sectional void fraction in internally heated annular channels. The quantitative relationships established in this study addressed the deficiency of existing bubble coalescence-based OSV models in terms of closure relations for local parameters, thereby providing crucial theoretical support for the accurate modeling and engineering applications of subcooled boiling two-phase flows.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106641','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106641',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','HK','HK','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02050-w','Separating baryon number from valence-quark charge','바리온 번호와 원자가-쿼크 전하 분리','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Xia-Qing Li; Shu-Zhe Shi; Peng-Fei Zhuang','2026-10-08','2026-10-08','2026-10-08','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02050-w','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02050-w',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02077-z','Design and integration of a crab-waist interaction region for the Super Tau-Charm Facility','Super Tau-Charm Facility를 위한 게-허리 상호작용 영역의 설계 및 통합','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Lin-Hao Zhang; Tao Liu; Ye Zou; Peng-Hui Yang; De-Min Zhou; Jian-Cong Bao; Ze Yu; Yu-Han Jin; Yi-Hao Mo; Sang-Ya Li; Tian-Long He; Qing Luo; Jing-Yu Tang','2026-10-08','2026-10-08','2026-10-08','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02077-z','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02077-z',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;JP','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104750','Design of a ZnO:Ga/SiPM array alpha detector for associated particle imaging','ZnO 설계: 관련 입자 이미징을 위한 Ga/SiPM 어레이 알파 검출기','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Xinjian Wang; Xu Zhang; Changsheng Dai; Yan Lu; Tiancheng Zhong','2026-10-08','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','A compact associated alpha detector based on a ZnO:Ga scintillator coupled to a 121-channel SiPM array was proposed for associated particle imaging (API) applications. Monte Carlo simulations were performed to evaluate the detector response, position reconstruction capability, and timing performance. The simulation results show that scintillation light is shared among several neighboring SiPM channels, providing sufficient information for position and timing reconstruction. Position reconstruction was investigated using the COG method together with two-dimensional correction and CNN-based correction methods, achieving a spatial resolution better than 0.6 mm over most of the effective detection area. The timing performance was evaluated using an amplitude-weighted timing method combined with time-walk and flight-distance corrections, resulting in a timing resolution of 81.5 ps. These results demonstrate the feasibility of the proposed detector concept and indicate that it is a promising SiPM-based solution for high-resolution API applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104750','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104750',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104746','Biokinetic modelling of uranium retention and committed organ doses from groundwater ingestion in Chengalpattu District, Tamil Nadu, India','인도 타밀나두 (Tamil Nadu) 첸갈파투 (Chengalpattu) 지구의 지하수 섭취로 인한 우라늄 보유 및 커밋된 장기 선량의 생체 동력학 모델링','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','S. Palani; Satyanarayan Bramha; S. Chandrasekaran; P. Jayaprakash; J. Venkatmuthukumar; A. Vidyasakar; R. Ravisankar','2026-10-08','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Groundwater samples collected from Chengalpattu District were analyzed for uranium using an LED fluorimeter. The measured values ranged between 0.02 μg L −1 and 2.814 μg L −1 , with an average concentration of 0.347 μg L −1 . All measured values were within the permissible limits recommended by the World Health Organization and the International Commission on Radiological Protection. The study evaluated organ-specific uranium retention and committed equivalent doses for adults under chronic ingestion conditions using a hair-based compartmental biokinetic model. The results further confirm the previously reported non-uniform distribution of uranium among human organs and tissues, with tissue-specific retention characteristics governing its accumulation and residence time. Skeletal tissues, particularly cortical and trabecular bone volumes, exhibited the highest accumulation due to the strong affinity of uranyl ions for phosphate groups in hydroxyapatite, leading to prolonged retention and the largest contribution to internal radiation dose. In contrast, soft tissues, gastrointestinal tract segments, kidneys, and liver showed lower retention due to faster transfer and elimination rates. The gastrointestinal tract acts as the primary entry pathway, while the kidneys and urinary bladder play key roles in uranium clearance. Excretion analysis indicates that faeces elimination is the dominant pathway, followed by urinary and minor hair excretion. The highest committed equivalent doses were observed in bone surfaces, followed by other soft tissues, the lower large intestine wall, kidneys, upper large intestine wall, small intestine wall, stomach wall, and liver. The overall effective dose is mainly influenced by skeletal retention; however, the estimated doses across all locations remain low and well within international safety limits. These findings suggest minimal radiological health risk from chronic uranium ingestion in the study area and demonstrate that the hair compartmental biokinetic model is a reliable tool for long-term exposure and risk assessment.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104746','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104746',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IN;US','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112895','Reactor turbine coordinated control strategy for nuclear power plants based on thermal-mismatch','열 불일치를 기반으로 한 원자력 발전소의 원자로 터빈 조정 제어 전략','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ming Du; Zhiyuan Yao; Xiaofei Sun; Xiangtian Hou; Tao Yang; Yuguang Niu','2026-10-08','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','As power systems increasingly rely on flexibility resources, nuclear power will inevitably participate in grid load-following services. To improve the dynamic response performance of nuclear power plants during load-following operation, this paper proposes a reactor turbine coordinated control strategy based on thermal-mismatch analysis. The energy transfer characteristics between the primary and secondary loops of a pressurized water reactor (PWR) nuclear power plant operating in the “one reactor-two turbines” mode are analyzed. An energy-demand signal for the secondary loop and an energy-supply signal for the primary loop are constructed, and their difference is defined as the thermal-mismatch signal. By incorporating the pressure-power fitting coefficient and a control rod sensitivity coefficient, the thermal-mismatch signal is introduced into the reactor power control system as a feedforward signal. Furthermore, the heat-storage calculation methods of different regions in the once-through steam generator are analyzed. The boundary lengths are determined based on mass conservation on the secondary side, and the solution approach for the thermal storage coefficient is ultimately established. Finally, simulation results under operating conditions demonstrate that the strategy significantly improves the dynamic response of the primary-loop temperature during load variations. This paper provides an effective coordinated control scheme for enhancing the flexibility of PWR nuclear power plants in load-following operation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112895','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112895',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106637','Experimental study of a ten sodium heat pipe bundle array with various failure modes','다양한 고장 모드가 있는 10개의 소듐 히트 파이프 번들 어레이에 대한 실험적 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Pei-Hsun Huang; Taehwan Ahn; Annalisa Manera; Victor Petrov','2026-10-07','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Alkali metal heat pipes are key components for high-temperature heat removal in microreactors, where multiple heat pipes are embedded directly within the reactor core. Their collective thermal behavior, including interactions under off-normal conditions, remains insufficiently characterized. This study investigates the performance of a ten-heat-pipe array under a range of operating conditions, including simulated failure scenarios. Under steady-state operation, the vertical configuration produced more uniform vapor temperatures among the heat pipes, albeit with slightly longer startup times and marginally higher average operating temperatures compared to the horizontal orientation. System uncertainties associated with the heat pipe array configuration were quantified to support future model validation. Complete loss-of-function conditions were simulated by replacing one or two sodium heat pipes with empty tubes. In these cases, neighboring heat pipes redistributed the thermal load, resulting in increased local heat fluxes and a corresponding rise in system temperature. This localized overloading further amplified thermal stresses on adjacent heat pipes. The experimental results provide data for characterizing thermal interactions within heat-pipe arrays, offering useful guidance for the design of future experiments and the validation of numerical models used in the analysis of heat-pipe-cooled microreactor systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106637','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106637',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US;CH','CH','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2672883','Void Avoidance in Underwater Acoustic Sensor Networks with Deformable Bi-Level Routing Attention-Based Multiagent Adaptive Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient Routing Protocol','변형 가능한 2단계 라우팅 주의 기반 다제제 적응형 심층 결정적 정책 그라디언트 라우팅 프로토콜이 있는 수중 음향 센서 네트워크에서 회피','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Ashok Battula; S. Emalda Roslin','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Underwater acoustic sensor networks (UASNs) have gained increasing importance in various military and civilian applications due to their ability to facilitate communication in challenging underwater environments. However, routing in UASNs faces unique challenges stemming from the harsh characteristics of underwater acoustic communication caused by water currents and node mobility. This work suggests a comprehensive routing framework that uniquely integrates void avoidance with intelligent, deep reinforcement learning–based routing techniques.The contribution from this research is the performance of void avoidance and routing for the effective transmission. Specifically, a novel HH-VBF (hop-by-hop vector-based forwarding) method is employed to detect and eliminate the void nodes, thereby enhancing reliability and reducing packet loss. Furthermore, the proposed deformable bi-level routing attention-based multi-agent adaptive deep deterministic policy gradient (DBRAMADDPG) algorithm, optimized using the improved nuclear reaction optimization algorithm (ImNROA), dynamically learns optimal routing paths to reduce end-to-end delay and energy consumption by avoiding the void area.This unified approach can effectively mitigate void-induced disruptions while balancing energy efficiency, extending the network lifetime, and improving the quality of service. Extensive simulations demonstrated that our model outperformed existing methods, reducing delay by up to 7%, while taking the number of nodes as 10, the delays of the IR2P (intelligent reinforcement learning routing protocol with integrated power-control), HMERP (hybrid message encoding-based routing protocol), ROAR (resource-optimized adaptive routing), VAHR (void-aware hybrid routing), and the proposed ImNROA-DBRAMADDPG were 0.8948%, 0.8639%, 0.84533%, 0.80878%, and 0.78594%, respectively, ensuring more stable data delivery in complex underwater scenarios.These advancements contribute to the state of the art by offering robust routing strategies capable of dynamically adapting to underwater environmental challenges and void formations. The findings provide potential implications for designing resilient and energy-efficient UASNs, paving the way for improved real-time underwater monitoring and secure acoustic communication systems. These findings pave the way for more reliable, sustainable, and intelligent underwater sensor networks, with significant implications for real-time marine exploration, defense, and environmental monitoring.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2672883','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2672883',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2735598','Research on an Improved Reconstruction Approach for Local Transmission Imaging in TGS','TGS의 국소 투과 영상을 위한 개선된 재구성 접근법에 관한 연구','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Xing-Yu Li; Yu-Cheng Yan; Jin-Qi Yuan; Yu Zhao; Ding Yang; Ji-Biao Han; Wang-Rui Ma','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Tomographic gamma scanning is a nondestructive γ-ray measurement technique that utilizes computed tomography–based reconstruction methods to analyze the internal distribution of radioactive waste materials. To address the insufficient reconstruction accuracy of local regions under sparse-angle transmission measurement conditions, a geometry-guided global-to-local adaptive reconstruction method is proposed in this study.A surface layer voxel model of a radioactive waste container was established according to the practical configuration of low- and intermediate-level radioactive solid waste steel containers. The surface region was divided into 25 square voxel grids, with each a voxel size of 12 × 12 cm. Concrete filling material was placed at the 16th voxel position, and two models were constructed, in which the concrete occupied one-ninth and one-half of the initial voxel volume, respectively.Based on the source-detector scanning geometry, a geometric relationship X = H-2W was introduced to determine the minimum voxel partition length and the required number of subdivisions in the local region of interest. The Alternating Direction Method of Multipliers (ADMM)–Orthogonal Matching Pursuit (OMP) reconstruction framework was employed to reconstruct sparse-angle transmission projection data and improve the transmission image quality. Monte Carlo simulations were performed to validate the proposed reconstruction framework.The results demonstrated that under sparse-angle sampling conditions, the OMP method produces relatively poor reconstruction performance, with peak signal-to-noise ratio (PSNR) values of approximately 30 and structural similarity index measure (SSIM) values of around 0.6. In contrast, the ADMM-OMP framework effectively improved the reconstruction results, achieving PSNR values close to 40 and SSIM values close to 1, thereby improving the quality of the reconstructed transmission images.Finally, the global reconstructed image and the locally refined reconstruction results were fused, effectively alleviating the degradation of local reconstruction quality caused by the filling material occupying only a small fraction of the initial voxel in the region of interest.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2735598','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2735598',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2735584','Application of Nuclear Technology in Agriculture and the Role of Isotopes in Increasing Productivity, Food Security, and Sustainable Development in Türkiye','농업에서의 원자력 기술의 적용과 튀르키예의 생산성, 식량 안보 및 지속 가능한 개발 증가에 있어 동위 원소의 역할','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Mansur Mustafaoğlu; Fazil Hacımüftüoğlu','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Nuclear technology has emerged as an important scientific approach for improving agricultural productivity, strengthening food security, and supporting sustainable development. However, despite the increasing global use of isotopes and irradiation techniques in agriculture, there is limited comprehensive research focusing on their applications, benefits, and future potential in Türkiye. Therefore, this study was carried out to examine the role of nuclear technology and isotope applications in Turkish agriculture, particularly in areas such as food irradiation, pest control, soil and water management, crop improvement, and sustainable resource utilization. The study was conducted using a qualitative and comparative review methodology based on scientific literature, international reports, institutional publications, and recent case studies related to nuclear applications in agriculture and food systems. Relevant studies from organizations such as the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA), the Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO), and recent international academic publications were systematically analyzed to evaluate current practices and developments in Türkiye and other countries. The analysis demonstrates that isotope and irradiation technologies contribute significantly to increasing agricultural productivity, improving fertilizer and water-use efficiency, reducing post-harvest losses, extending food shelf life, and decreasing dependence on chemical pesticides. Furthermore, the findings indicate that Türkiye has made notable progress in integrating nuclear techniques into agriculture through collaborations among universities, TENMAK, FAO, and IAEA. Nevertheless, challenges such as limited infrastructure, public awareness, regulatory development, and investment capacity still remain. The study concludes that nuclear and isotope technologies can play a strategic role in achieving sustainable agriculture and long-term food security in Türkiye. It is recommended that Türkiye strengthen interdisciplinary research, expand international cooperation, improve regulatory frameworks, and invest in scientific infrastructure and public awareness programs to support the safe and effective application of nuclear technologies in agriculture.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2735584','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2735584',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02058-2','Triple-energy computed tomography in the megavoltage range with an inverse Compton scattering light source','역 콤프턴 산란 광원을 가진 메가 전압 범위의 트리플 에너지 컴퓨터 단층 촬영','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Zhi-Jun Chi; Sheng-Yuan Liu; Hong-Ze Zhang; Jia-Yi Sun; Hao Ding; Jin Lin; Xuan-Qi Zhang; Qi-Li Tian; Zhi Zhang; Ying-Chao Du; Wen-Hui Huang; Chuan-Xiang Tang','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02058-2','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02058-2',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02049-3','Frontier questions and emerging directions in nuclear science and technology','원자력 과학 및 기술 분야의 새로운 방향에 대한 프론티어 질문','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Yu-Gang Ma','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02049-3','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02049-3',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02063-5','Enhancing point kernel code POKER using CAD-based geometries and GPU acceleration for radiation shielding simulation','방사선 차폐 시뮬레이션을 위한 CAD 기반 지오메트리 및 GPU 가속을 사용하여 포인트 커널 코드 포커 향상','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Jun-Yi Chen; Cheng-Hao Cao; Rui-Han Li; Shao-Ning Shen; Jin-Gang Liang','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02063-5','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02063-5',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02047-5','Correction: Development of a pixelated prompt gamma imaging detector with LaBr3–BGO in a wedged configuration','보정: 쐐기형 구성의 LaBr3-BGO가 있는 픽셀화된 프롬프트 감마 이미징 검출기 개발','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Jin-Long Wang; Li-Wang Yang; Xiao-Guang Wu; Zi-Yang He; Yun Zheng; Cong-Bo Li; Tian-Xiao Li; Zi-Hao Zhao; Ming Zheng; Jin-Ze Li; Yun-Qiu Li; Rui Hong; Jia-Nan Zou; Shao-Xiong Guan; Jing Shi','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02047-5','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02047-5',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02052-8','Application of Bayesian optimization to synchrotron slow extraction tuning','싱크로트론 느린 추출 튜닝에 베이지안 최적화 적용','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Ze-Jiang Wang; Hong-Juan Yao; Xiao-Yu Liu; Wen-Bo Ye; Yang Xiong; Shu-Xin Zheng; Mao-Cheng Wang; Di Wang; Min-Wen Wang; Ye Yang; Wo-Long Liu; Ming-Tong Zhao; Yi-Hua Yan; Zhong-Ming Wang','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02052-8','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02052-8',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02056-4','A novel neutron texture diffractometer analysis method based on convolutional neural networks for face-centered cubic materials','얼굴 중심 입방 재료에 대한 컨볼루션 신경망을 기반으로 한 새로운 중성자 텍스처 회절 분석 방법','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Bo-Kai Zhao; Wei-Min Gan; Dan-Min Liu; Xiao-Long Liu; Yu-Han Hou; Yu-Qing Li; Tian-Fu Li; Kai Sun; Xue-Shen Jiao; Mei-Juan Li; Dong-Feng Chen; Ying-Xun Zhang','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','2026-10-07','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02056-4','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02056-4',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;DE','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104769','Selecting a project-delivery structure for Indonesia''s first nuclear power plant: an expert AHP-weighted anchored-rating analysis of the bankability–strategic-control trade-off','인도네시아 최초의 원자력 발전소를 위한 프로젝트 납품 구조 선정: 은행성-전략적-통제 트레이드오프에 대한 전문가 AHP 가중치 고정 등급 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Agus Aryanto; Soojin Park','2026-10-07','','2026-10','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','Indonesia''s energy policy and supply plan include nuclear generation, shifting attention from adoption to delivery. This study evaluates five case-anchored delivery configurations against 14 criteria covering ownership, contractual risk allocation, strategic national value, and financing feasibility, using a hybrid AHP-weighted anchored-rating model: 19 purposively selected Indonesian experts derived criterion weights by pairwise comparison and rated each configuration on an anchored nine-point scale; each respondent''s weights and ratings were combined before aggregation. All 95 pairwise matrices met CR ≤ 0.10 under software-enforced consistency requirements, whereas agreement on dimension priorities was weak (Kendall''s W = 0.187). Within this panel and under the administered profiles, a host-majority public–vendor joint venture scored highest (0.710), ahead of a state-utility configuration (0.638); its margin arose from perceived bankability, construction-risk allocation, and funding access, not from strategic national value, the largest-weighted dimension (34.4%). Priority heterogeneity alone reversed the group choice for no respondent; assessment heterogeneity reversed it for five. A1 led in over 98% of resampling and weight-variation draws, but the lead reversed when its seven contracting and financing ratings were lowered together by more than about 1.2 points. Newcomer delivery choices should weigh the risk bearer''s control rights, exposure, and loss-absorption capacity, not nominal allocation alone.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104769','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104769',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104770','Response Characteristics and Interference Evaluation of RAD7 Radon Measurement within 50,000 ppm CO2 Concentration Threshold','50,000ppm CO2 농도 임계값 내 RAD7 라돈 측정의 반응 특성 및 간섭 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Yilin Deng; Ruomei Xie; Zhongkai Fan; Jiaxin Li; Jiale Cheng; Yehe Zhou; Xiangming Wu; Haoyu You; Yuyang Lu; Hongzhi Yuan; Yanliang Tan','2026-10-07','','2026-10','연구논문','방사선·계측','RAD7 is a core instrument for geological onsite radon measurements. When measuring the exhalation rate of radon from surface soil using closed accumulation chambers, concurrently exhaled carbon dioxide accumulates within the chamber. Similarly, during in-situ degassing for water-borne radon extraction, high concentrations of carbon dioxide in water are released together with radon. Under these conditions, CO 2 concentrations typically reach tens of thousands of ppm. To evaluate this conventional field concentration range''s impact on RAD7, this study focused on CO 2 interference below 50000 ppm, established a closed-loop circulation experimental system with a dual-machine parallel comparison function. RAD7-4101 acted as the reference instrument measuring CO 2 -free radon; RAD7-4103 acted as the experimental instrument, undergoing six dynamic tests across five CO 2 gradients (10000 – 50000 ppm). Paired-ratio analysis revealed an overall negative offset but no statistically detectable dependence on CO 2 concentration, consistent with the small response predicted by existing models. At 50,000 ppm, the projected incremental interference could not be statistically resolved within the experimental precision, indicating no detectable concentration-dependent CO 2 -induced suppression under the present conditions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104770','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104770',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104772','Experimental Optimization of Filler Geometry for Vacuum Leak Mitigation in 200 MHz RFQ Section Brazing','200MHz RFQ 섹션 브레이징에서 진공 누출 완화를 위한 필러 형상 실험 최적화','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Kyung Hyun Kim; Han Sung Kim; Hyeok Jung Kwon; Jung Goo Hong','2026-10-07','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','Vacuum integrity is critical in the fabrication of radio-frequency quadrupole (RFQ) structures for high-intensity proton accelerators. This study investigated vacuum leak issues observed after section brazing of a 200 MHz RFQ at the Korea Multi-purpose Accelerator Complex (KOMAC) through experimental optimization of filler geometry. Specimen experiments were conducted to evaluate the effects of filler inclination angle and layout on the flow and redistribution behavior of molten Ag72Cu28 filler metal during high-vacuum brazing. The results showed that filler inclination angle strongly affects capillary-driven flow and gravity-induced redistribution. An effective inclination angle range of 15°–45° was identified, with 15° exhibiting the strongest preferential redistribution toward the critical vacuum seal area. Accordingly, 15° was selected for RFQ fabrication considering both filler redistribution and practical constraints, including bolt-hole interference, groove-machining space, and re-brazing accessibility. A ring-shaped filler layout was also introduced around bolt regions to reduce local filler deficiency and improve sealing continuity. The optimized design was validated through X-ray CT analysis and helium leak testing, demonstrating satisfactory vacuum integrity in the specimen experiments. The optimized layout was subsequently applied to full-scale RFQ section brazing. The fabricated RFQ sections exhibited satisfactory brazing appearance and satisfied the vacuum leak criterion of less than 1 × 10 -9 torr·L/s. These findings provide practical guidelines for controlling filler flow during large-scale vacuum brazing of RFQ structures.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104772','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104772',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104771','Corrigendum to “Novel bricks based lightweight Vietnam''s white clay minerals for gamma ray shielding purposes: An extensive experimental study” Journal: Nuclear Engineering and Technology Volume 56, Issue 2, February 2024, Pages 666–672','Corrigendum to “감마선 차폐 목적의 신규 벽돌 기반 경량 베트남의 백토 광물: 광범위한 실험 연구” Journal: Nuclear Engineering and Technology Volume 56, Issue 2, February 2024, Pages 666–672','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Ta Van Thuong; O.L. Tashlykov; K.A. Mahmoud','2026-10-07','','2026-10','정오표','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104771','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104771',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','RU;EG','RU','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115239','F-MNet: flux-modulated network for radial power prediction of space reactors','F-MNet: 우주 원자로의 반경 방향 전력 예측을 위한 플럭스 변조 네트워크','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Yaotang Li; Yuting Cheng; Wenjun Shao; Xu Sun','2026-10-07','','2026-12','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Rapid and accurate prediction of radial power distribution is crucial for the design and operation of space nuclear reactors. However, traditional Monte Carlo methods incur prohibitively high computational costs, while conventional data-driven surrogate models face severe overfitting and insufficient generalization capabilities under small-sample and data distribution shift conditions. Addressing the problem of radial power prediction for rod-controlled space reactors, this paper proposes F-MNet (Flux-Modulated Network), a physics-informed neural network architecture. F-MNet employs the Feature-wise Linear Modulation (FiLM) mechanism to take the core-average neutron flux as a conditioning signal and dynamically adjust hidden-layer feature transformations, thereby learning the nonlinear sensitivity function of local assembly power with respect to flux—a relationship intrinsically constrained by the control rod differential worth. To evaluate the extrapolation performance under small-sample conditions, four dataset partitions with distinct characteristics of control rod position distributions were constructed. Ablation experiments demonstrate that F-MNet consistently outperforms all baseline models (Plain MLP, Res + FiLM, Res Only) across all partition schemes. Notably, in the challenging extrapolation scenario Case 1, F-MNet increased the R 2 from 0.4540 for Plain MLP to 0.9429, with the MAE, RMSE, and MAPE all reduced to approximately one-third. Furthermore, a cross-criticality case experiment was conducted, spanning subcritical (keff ≈ 0.62) to supercritical (keff ≈ 1.05) states, where the maximum relative deviation for all assemblies remained below 1.55%, further validating the engineering applicability of the model. The aforementioned results indicate that F-MNet is an efficient, accurate, and physically consistent model framework, providing a reference design paradigm for surrogate models dealing with small-sample and data distribution shift scenarios.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115239','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115239',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115252','Experimental investigation on the thermal-hydraulic performance of an air–water parallel passive residual heat removal system','공기-물 병렬 수동 잔류 열 제거 시스템의 열수력 성능에 대한 실험적 조사','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Hecheng Liang; Xiaobo Zeng; Yifu Wang; Jinchao Li; Di Wu; Meng Wang; Xu Han; Jie Cheng; Jianjun Wang','2026-10-07','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','To enhance the safety and long-term cooling performance of passive residual heat removal systems (PRHRS) in offshore floating nuclear power plants, an air–water parallel passive residual heat removal system (AWPRHRS) is proposed and experimentally investigated. The system combines an air-cooled heat exchanger (AHX) and a water-cooled heat exchanger (WHX) in parallel, enabling efficient redistribution of thermal loads under varying heat conditions and reducing reliance on stored cooling water. The experimental facility was designed to evaluate key operational characteristics, including pressure response, natural circulation behavior, and thermal–hydraulic performance. Results demonstrate that the AWPRHRS can maintain high heat removal capacity under early-stage high heat load and achieve stable, long-term cooling without excessive water consumption. Under heat loads ranging from 35 to 45 kW, the system reaches a quasi-steady-state pressure of 0.65–0.66 MPa, while the air-cooled subsystem consistently carries approximately 37% of the total flow. The AWPRHRS effectively integrates the advantages of water- and air-cooled subsystems, providing both rapid initial decay heat removal and reliable long-term operation in the freshwater-limited OFNP environments.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115252','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115252',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112885','Reliability-assessed machine learning for high flux flow regime classification','높은 플럭스 흐름 체제 분류를 위한 신뢰성 평가 기계 학습','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Maria Pantopoulou; Charie A. Tsoukalas; Akshay Khandelwal; Mamoru Ishii; Lefteri Tsoukalas','2026-10-07','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Thermal-hydraulic systems in nuclear engineering require reliable monitoring, accurate characterization and models capable of handling nonlinear, time-dependent behavior. High-void-fraction multiphase flows introduce significant diagnostic challenges, as the chaotic, nonlinear nature of interfacial transitions makes conventional modeling and rigid thresholding approaches less practical. This study develops a diagnostic framework for classifying annular gas–liquid flow sub-regimes using centerline conductivity probe measurements. Continuous experimental runs were partitioned into short temporal segments, with feature vectors constructed from volumetric, frequency-domain and morphological characteristics to represent the geometric structure of the flow. Four supervised learning architectures, K-nearest neighbors (KNN), support vector machines (SVM), random forest (RF) and gradient boosted trees (GBT), were evaluated. Feature selection reduced the initial six-feature configuration to an optimal three-feature subset, improving classification performance across most architectures. The RF model achieved the best overall results, with a macro F1 score of 0.9263 at the local segment level and perfect balanced accuracy under global run-level majority voting. Probabilistic evaluation using expected calibration error (ECE), maximum calibration error (MCE) and Brier scores confirmed that the RF model produced the most reliable confidence estimates among all evaluated classifiers. Overall, the study shows that machine learning can be applied to flow characterization problems to address challenges that traditional methods handle poorly. The results also highlight the importance of understanding model behavior, not just predictive accuracy, through analysis of evaluation methodology and calibration of predicted probabilities.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112885','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112885',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112897','Multi-objective optimization of thermo-hydraulic performance for dimpled–protruded tubes of an intermediate heat exchanger in SCO2 gas fast reactor using machine learning and NSGA-II','기계 학습 및 NSGA-II를 사용하여 SCO2 가스 고속 원자로에서 중간 열교환기의 딤플 돌출 튜브에 대한 열수력 성능의 다중 목표 최적화','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Samuel Olaoluwa Oke; Puzhen Gao; Adebimpe A. Amosun; Olatomide G. Fadodun; Deborah Boluwatife Omowunmi','2026-10-07','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','The thermo–hydraulic performance of heat exchangers is governed by coupled interactions among geometry, flow conditions, and fluid properties. This study develops a hybrid framework integrating computational fluid dynamics (CFD), machine learning (ML) and multi-objective optimization framework to predict and optimize the thermo-hydraulic and exergy performance of supercritical CO 2 (SCO 2 ) flowing through dimpled-protruded tubes (DPTs) for intermediate heat exchangers in SCO 2 gas-cooled fast reactors. A CFD dataset comprising 504 cases was generated by varying Reynolds number ( Re ), Prandtl number ( Pr ), diameter of dimple-protrusion ( d / D ), and dimple-protrusion orientation parameter ( θ / ω ). Random forest (RF), extreme gradient boosting (XGB), and K-nearest neighbours (KNN) models were developed to predict Nusselt number ( Nu ), Poiseuille number ( fRe ), performance evaluation criterion ( PEC ), and exergy efficiency ( η W - S ). All models demonstrated good agreement with CFD results, with XGB achieving the highest predictive accuracy, followed by RF. At Re = 10 , 000 , d / D = 0.15 , and θ / ω = 0.33 , increasing Pr from 0.84 to 1.30 increased Nu by 56 % and PEC by 10 % . Increasing d / D from 0.10 to 0.25 enhanced Nu by 68 % but reduced PEC by 16 %, demonstrating the trade-off between heat-transfer enhancement and hydraulic performance. The best-performing XGB surrogate was coupled with the non-dominated sorting genetic algorithm II (NSGA-II) to simultaneously maximize Nu and η W - S while minimizing fRe . The resulting Pareto-optimal solutions identify parameter combinations balancing heat-transfer enhancement, exergy performance, and hydraulic losses. The proposed CFD–ML–MOOP framework provides an efficient data-driven approach for the thermo-hydraulic design and optimization of advanced heat exchangers for next-generation nuclear energy systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112897','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112897',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;NG','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112915','LUT anchored target source calibration for critical heat flux prediction under source shift','소스 이동 시 임계열유속 예측을 위한 LUT 앵커 대상 소스 보정','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Mehmet Yoladi','2026-10-07','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','The public NUREG derived set of 24,283 critical heat flux (CHF) measurements from 60 dryout dominated sources is studied under source shift. The tabulated outlet quality reconstructs the measured CHF from the heat balance (correlation 0.99989) and is excluded as target leakage. Under a leave one source out protocol the leakage safe model reaches 23.2 percent error and an inlet solved 2006 Groeneveld look up table 21.2 percent. A zero shot conformal interval gives a pooled coverage of 0.916 but source conditional coverage as low as 0.40 on biased sources, for the learned model and the table alike. A backbone agnostic calibration is proposed in which a few labelled target points correct a multiplicative bias and recalibrate an empirical conformal interval. A strict split protocol that separates adaptation from calibration restores near nominal empirical source conditional coverage with twenty to thirty target points, a cross conformal variant with about ten. Anchored on the look up table the calibration reaches about eleven percent error with the sharpest intervals, an in sample figure because the table was derived from this working set; re-deriving the table with the source held out costs about three points, and held out analogues anchor the calibration at seventeen to nineteen percent, near the learned backbone. All coverage values are empirical. The budget is stable over fifty target draws and under grouping by laboratory or network, but coverage falls to 0.83 to 0.93 when the labelled points cover only one mass flux or pressure block.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112915','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112915',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','TR','TR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112913','Design and thermal–hydraulic analysis of a directly heated test facility simulating plate type fuel with narrow rectangular channel for nuclear research reactors','원자력 연구용 원자로의 직사각형 채널이 좁은 판형 연료를 시뮬레이션하는 직접 가열 시험 시설의 설계 및 열수력 해석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Vijaya Kumar Veluri; Samiran Sengupta; Aniruddha Ghosh','2026-10-07','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Nuclear research reactors often use plate type fuel assemblies where coolant is passed through a set of narrow rectangular channels to transfer the heat from the reactor core. The channel gap between fuel plates strongly influences hydraulic resistance, fuel temperature, and the available margin to boiling, making it one of the key design parameters governing reactor safety during normal operation, anticipated operational occurrences, and accident conditions. This paper presents the design and development of the Heat-transfer Experiment Loop for Plate geometry (HELP), an out-of-pile test facility built to reproduce the thermal–hydraulic behaviour of plate-type fuel assemblies for research reactors. The facility employs a directly heated Inconel-625 test section with channel gaps of 1.7 mm, 1.8 mm, 2.0 mm, 2.2 mm and 2.4 mm, covering a large range of narrow gaps commonly adopted in research reactors. A steady-state design framework was established predicting hydraulic and thermal performance of a Directly Heated Test Facility simulating narrow rectangular channels. Pressure drop, wall temperature, heat-transfer coefficient, axial temperature distribution, and margin to onset of nucleate boiling (ONB) were evaluated using established friction-factor and heat-transfer correlations, including Shah-London, Blasius, Petukhov, Gnielinski, Dittus-Boelter, Sudo, and the SULTAN-JHR closures proposed by Ghione et al. The comparison highlights the variation among available correlations and defines the expected operating envelope of the facility. The resulting framework provides the theoretical basis for subsequent experimental measurements for validation of CFD simulations for narrow rectangular cooling channels representative of plate-type fuel for research reactors.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112913','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112913',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112881','Adaptive coupling of transport and depletion using the neutronically weighted inventory deviation (NWID) metric','중성 가중 재고 편차 (NWID) 메트릭을 사용한 운송 및 연소의 적응형 결합','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Abdullah M. Alharbi; Justin K. Watson; Paul K. Romano; Saqr M. Alshogeathri','2026-10-07','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Most depletion engines solve transport at every depletion interval (fully transport-coupled depletion), this is the highest-fidelity option but impractical for many-interval histories. Some engines also offer a cheaper transport-independent mode that loses accuracy as the spectrum drifts. This paper introduces adaptive coupling as a new option that applies to both within-interval and across-interval depletion problems, triggering transport recalculation only when the Neutronically Weighted Inventory Deviation (NWID) tracking metric exceeds a user-defined tolerance. NWID quantifies inventory drift weighted by neutronic importance and is computed after each depletion interval at negligible cost. Demonstrations on PWR and SFR pin cells depleted at an irregular schedule to 45 and 131 MWd/kg, respectively, show that end-of-life baseline NWID differs by an order of magnitude between the two systems (145% for the PWR versus 14% for the SFR), mirroring the gap in their fully independent inventory errors and consistent with the spectral rigidity of fast systems. At 3% NWID tolerance simulations for both cases, the PWR recovers 0.61% maximum actinide error, 0.58% maximum fission product error, and - 45 pcm k eff deviation throughout the depletion history all relative to the fully coupled reference. While the SFR achieves 0.11% actinide error, 0.10% fission product error, and a k eff deviation of only - 19 pcm. Benchmarking results presented above were achieved while reducing the number of transport solves by 2.3 x and 14.3 x for PWR and SFR, respectively, with proportional reductions in runtime.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112881','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112881',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US;SA','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106642','Can small modular reactors clear the cost screen for Greek noninterconnected islands: A benchmark screening assessment against oil based supply with illustrative renewable storage evidence','소형모듈원자로(SMR)가 그리스의 비연결 섬에 대한 비용 화면을 지울 수 있습니까: 예시적인 재생 가능 저장 증거가 있는 석유 기반 공급에 대한 벤치마크 선별 평가','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Ioanna Ananiadou; Demetrios Papacostas','2026-10-06','','2027-01','연구논문','핵연료주기·폐기물','Greek noninterconnected islands remain economically distinctive because several still depend on autonomous oil based generation while facing pressure to decarbonize through renewables, storage, and interconnections. This article addresses a limited screening question. Do small modular reactors (SMRs) sit above or below the regulator documented cost of continued autonomous island supply, and how should that result be positioned against alternative decarbonization pathways. Using Greek regulatory data, peer reviewed SMR cost anchors, and an eighteen scenario levelized cost of electricity (LCOE) matrix for a 300 MWe proxy unit, the study identifies a central benchmark of 193.57 EUR per MWh and scenario results of 74.7 to 157.9 EUR per MWh. This favorable outcome holds only under the high technical availability assumed as a plant parameter. When Scenario S1 is translated into a more realistic island utilization of 40 to 50 percent, cost rises toward the benchmark, reaching about 187.9 EUR per MWh at 40 percent once the illustrative adders are applied. The discussion adds an illustrative comparison drawn from verified Greek island studies of photovoltaic and storage performance, presented as directional evidence that is not directly commensurate with plant level SMR LCOE. The article does not establish deployment feasibility or superiority over renewable systems with storage. It indicates only that SMRs cannot be excluded on cost screening grounds when the counterfactual is oil based island generation, while the margin narrows sharply under realistic low island utilization.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106642','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106642',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','GR;US','GR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2737549','Optimization of the Heat Transfer Model for Superheated Steam Condensation Inside Tubes and Its Evaluation with the SPACE Code','스페이스 코드로 튜브 내부의 과열된 스팀 응축을 위한 열전달 모델 최적화 및 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Ho Sik Kim; Hae Min Park; Jong-Hyuk Lee','2026-10-06','2026-10-06','2026-10-06','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study focuses on condensation heat transfer of superheated steam inside tubes of once-through steam generators, which are utilized in various small modular reactors (SMRs). This work specifically investigates innovative SMR (i-SMR) and its passive auxiliary feedwater system (PAFS). The primary objective is to implement an optimized heat transfer model for superheated steam condensation into the Safety and Performance Analysis Code for Nuclear Power Plants (SPACE) code and subsequently validate it. To achieve this, a review of previous studies on superheated steam condensation heat transfer inside tubes was conducted to identify the best existing model for the PAFS operating conditions. The model identified from the literature review was first implemented in the SPACE code and evaluated against relevant experimental data. This evaluation revealed a key weakness, as the model underpredicted heat transfer in the high-superheat region. To address this shortcoming, an optimized model was developed by improving the single-phase forced convection heat transfer correlation for superheated steam based on a previous experimental study. This optimized model was subsequently implemented in the SPACE code. Validation calculations confirmed that the optimized model offers significantly improved prediction accuracy, especially in the high-superheat region, establishing it as the final model for the i-SMR PAFS.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2737549','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2737549',0,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104765','Rate kinetics determination of cerium oxides conversion used as surrogate of specific heavy metal for process development','공정 개발을 위한 특정 중금속의 대용으로 사용되는 세륨 산화물 전환율 동역학 측정','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Ram Balak Yadav; Gattu Suneel; P.K. Sharma; S.K. Satpati','2026-10-06','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','Specific heavy metal (SHM) nitrates generated during the back end of the nuclear fuel cycle are typically converted to metal oxalates using oxalic acid, followed by calcination to produce the metal oxides. Cerium was employed as actinide surrogate to investigate continuous precipitation and thermal decomposition relevant to process development and preliminary equipment design. A cerium nitrate solution containing 20 g/l Ce in 1M HNO 3 and 1M oxalic acid continuously fed to precipitator at a volumetric flow rate ratio of 3:1. The resulting cerium oxalate precipitate filtered using stainless steel filter and subjected to thermal analysis. Thermogravimetric and differential thermogravimetric analysis were performed from 303 - 1173K at heating rates of 5–25 K/min under inert atmosphere. Three distinct thermal decomposition stages were identified, corresponding to dehydration and two successive decomposition steps leading to CeO 2 formation. Apparent kinetic parameters for the individual stages were evaluated using nonisothermal Kissinger analysis. The experimentally observed mass losses were compared with theoretical values derived from the proposed decomposition steps. The results provide quantitative thermal and apparent kinetic information for cerium oxalate decomposition and establish an experimental basis for further mechanistic, heat & mass-transfer, and scale-up studies toward continuous drying and calcination of SHM oxalates.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104765','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104765',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104735','Observations regarding the construction of multipoint kinetics models from observational data','관측 데이터에서 다지점 동역학 모델의 구성에 관한 관측','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','K.G. Howey; Giorgio Valocchi; Dean Price','2026-10-06','','2026-10','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The multipoint kinetics (MPK) equations extend point kinetics models by tracking neutron populations in lumped reactor regions, offering improved spatial resolution at modest computational cost. However, determining the coupling coefficient matrix $K$ from transient data remains an open problem without established experimental procedures. This work provides some commentary on the task of recovering $K$ from observable forward flux measurements during reactor transients. Analytical solutions to the Kobayashi MPK formulation in the case of no precursors and with a single precursor family are derived in spectral form, enabling a mathematically rigorous investigation of eigenmode behavior and parameter observability. Coupling coefficient recoverability is investigated using modal sensitivity analysis and the Hessian condition number of the spectral recovery problem. The inclusion of delayed neutron precursors delays this eigenmode divergence but may be insufficient for enabling practical recovery of $K$ in many scenarios. In conclusion, capturing the behavior of nondominant eigenmodes without oversampling the dominant eigenmode is critical to the recoverability of $K$ through transient data.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104735','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104735',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104766','High-efficiency 160-way cavity combiner: 170 kW CW validation for the IFMIF-DONES RF Power System','고효율 160웨이 캐비티 컴바이너: IFMIF-DONES RF 전원 시스템에 대한 170kW CW 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','C. de la Morena; D. Regidor; D. Iriarte; E. Ugarte; S. Dragaš; A.J. Martínez; J. Peral; J.A. Rama; D. Jimenez-Rey','2026-10-06','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','Solid-state (SS) amplification has become a compelling alternative to vacuum-tube technology for mid-range radiofrequency (RF) power systems, particularly at frequencies below a few hundred megahertz. This is the case of the RF Power System of IFMIF-DONES (International Fusion Materials Irradiation Facility – DEMO (DEMOnstration power plant) Oriented Neutron Source), composed of 56 RF Stations at 175 MHz based on SS technology. IFMIF-DONES is one of the key facilities of the European roadmap towards fusion electricity, necessary for the validation and qualification of the materials capable of withstanding the harsh conditions inside future fusion reactors. Nevertheless, achieving high power with SS technology requires combining the output of many transistor-based amplifier modules. Resonant cavity combination offers a compact and highly efficient single-step alternative to conventional corporate schemes. This work presents the latest validation campaign of the 160-input 175 MHz resonant cavity combiner developed for the IFMIF-DONES prototype SS RF Station. The device has been experimentally tested in continuous-wave (CW) mode up to 170 kW, extending previous validation experiments and providing new insight into the thermal behavior, efficiency evolution, and tuning characteristics of the system. The results confirm the suitability of resonant cavity combination for high-power SS RF sources and represent a significant step toward the full-power validation required for IFMIF-DONES.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104766','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104766',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','ES','ES','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104768','An Intelligent Quality Assurance Pipeline for Large-Scale Personal Dosimetry Services Using Unsupervised Machine Learning-Based Anomaly Detection on Multi-Element TLD Readouts','다중 요소 TLD 판독에서 비감독 기계 학습 기반 이상 탐지를 사용하는 대규모 개인 선량측정 서비스를 위한 지능형 품질 보증 파이프라인','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Habib Abdul Ghani; Zico Pratama Putra; Teguh Sulistyo; Muhammad Lintang Saujana; Rofiq Syaifudin; Irma Dwi Rahayu; Mutia Muharani; Isnaini Farida; Raden Sumarbagiono; Ahmad Musyafa; Baskan Hanurajie','2026-10-06','','2026-10','연구논문','AI·디지털','Large-scale national personal dosimetry programs require stringent data quality assurance (QA) to prevent false exposure reports. Traditional QA relies on manual review or scalar thresholds, which fail to detect multi-dimensional anomalies. This paper presents an intelligent QA pipeline evaluating six unsupervised machine learning models against physics-grounded reference labels. We compiled a unified dataset of 14,732 records by programmatically matching raw reader outputs with dose spreadsheets (2024–2026), recovering 8,487 missing barcodes at a 99.1% matching rate via floating-point response fingerprinting. Evaluation against 379 physical anomalies proved that Isolation Forest achieved the highest performance (F1 = 0.580 at 1.5% contamination; F1 = 0.743 and Recall = 0.744 at 2.85% contamination), significantly outperforming One-Class SVM, Local Outlier Factor, and Elliptic Envelope (pairwise McNemar''s tests with continuity correction, p < 0.001). Feature ablation confirmed that combining element shares, ratios, and operational metrics maximizes detection for Isolation Forest, while sensitivity analysis proved stable performance. The consensus intersection model yielded an operational precision of 0.592. This pipeline demonstrates the feasibility of integrating unsupervised learning into routine radiation protection workflows to safeguard national occupational dose registries.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104768','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104768',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','ID','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115251','Corrigendum to “Regulating artificial intelligence for CANDU software qualifications” [Nucl. Eng. Des. 443 (2025) 114322]','Corrigendum to “Regulating artificial intelligence for CANDU software qualifications” [Nucl. Eng. Des. 443 (2025) 114322]','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Samer Dahaweer; Issam Hammad; Karthik Thiyagarajan','2026-10-06','','2026-10','정오표','AI·디지털','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115251','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115251',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115249','Analysis of synergistic transport characteristics and selection of key nuclides for insoluble fission products in molten salt reactors','용융염 원자로에서 불용성 핵분열 생성물의 시너지 수송 특성 분석 및 주요 핵종 선택','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Liang Chen; Xin-Yu Zhong; Rui Yan; Yang Zou','2026-10-06','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','In liquid-fueled Molten Salt Reactors (MSRs), the non-uniform distribution of insoluble fission products (IFPs) significantly affects source term characterization, decay heat evaluation, and reactor safety. However, the single-atom transport assumption for IFP migration becomes invalid under high-power operations due to significant particle agglomeration. To clarify the relative importance of IFPs across various physical effects and alleviate computational bottlenecks in multiphysics simulations, this study evaluates the evolution characteristics of IFPs in a 150 MWth MSR under a conservative bounding accumulation assumption. By quantitatively screening four macroscopic physical parameters—mass deposition, radioactivity, decay heat, and core neutron absorption—using a hybrid cutoff criterion, this study reduces hundreds of dynamically evolving isotopes to a core inventory of 24 key nuclides. This reduction preserves over 95% of these original system''s core physical features characteristics while significantly minimizing computational cost. Analysis of this reduced inventory reveals several critical transport phenomena: First, the macroscopic deposits are driven by a primary framework composed of high-yield, long-lived nuclides (primarily Mo, which accounts for >40%, alongside Ru). Second, a significant disparity between mass and activity/decay heat is observed, wherein trace high-risk nuclides (such as 95 Nb, 103 Ru) undergo coupled transport exclusively through attachment to these Mo Ru particles. Third, from a neutronics perspective, the spatial redistribution of long-lived solid poisons ( 103 Rh, 99 Tc) driven by particle migration induces non-negligible positive reactivity perturbations. Furthermore, decay chains (e.g., 95 Nb 95 Mo, 103 Ru 103 Rh) tightly couple early-stage thermal and safety issues with medium-to-long-term multiphase deposition and neutronics. In conclusion, the IFP transport characteristics and the 24-nuclide benchmark inventory established in this paper provide physically self-consistent inputs for future high-fidelity multiphysics coupled simulations, online purification system design, and surrogate material selection for non-radioactive experimental loops.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115249','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115249',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112910','Scattering-coupled adaptive source biasing for deep-penetration neutron arrival-spectrum calculations','깊은 침투 중성자 도달 스펙트럼 계산을 위한 산란 결합 적응 소스 바이어싱','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Linhe Du; Xiaoqiang Li; Peng Li; Yanbin Wang; Xinliang Pang; Xiong Zhang','2026-10-06','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Reliable neutron arrival spectra are needed for space radiation assessment and radiation protection, but deep-penetration Monte Carlo calculations often yield highly uneven uncertainties across energy groups. In analog Monte Carlo simulations, the nonuniform source spectrum and the energy-dependent transport behavior of neutrons can lead to relative uncertainties that differ by tens or even hundreds of times among arrival energy groups. To address this imbalance in arrival-spectrum uncertainties for deep-penetration transport, this study proposes a scattering-coupled adaptive source biasing (SC-ASB) method that uses a source-to-target response matrix to retain scattering-induced coupling from high-energy source neutrons to lower-energy arrival groups. The biased source distribution is derived by minimizing the sum of relative statistical errors (RSEs) subject to normalization and two-sided error-balance constraints, while the original source expectation is preserved by weight correction. Atmospheric neutron transport calculations showed that SC-ASB improved the relative-error distribution and increased computational efficiency. For a 15 km source height case, the figure of merit was 276 times that of analog simulation. Compared with uniform source biasing, SC-ASB showed better adaptability across source heights. In contrast to the WW variance-reduction method, SC-ASB provides more effective balancing of the RSEs across different energy groups. The method provides a variance-reduction framework for spectrum-resolved deep-penetration neutron transport.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112910','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112910',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112829','Experimental study on discharge behavior in automatic depressurization system: overall discharge characteristics of the sparger','자동 감압 시스템의 배출 거동에 관한 실험적 연구: 분사기의 전반적인 배출 특성','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zhengrun Shang; Dufeng Lv; Pei Yu; Zhaoming Meng; Zhongning Sun','2026-10-06','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','To investigate the high pressure two phase discharge characteristics of the sparger during the actual operation of automatic depressurization system (ADS), based on the discharge parameter conditions of the prototype sparger, the pressure oscillation behavior caused by the jet condensation of the racetrack orifices sparger was experimentally studied in this paper. The results show that under the condition of single phase discharge, the maximum oscillation increases first and then decreases with the increase of water temperature. With the increase of steam mass flow rate, it increases in the middle and high water temperature, and does not change significantly in the low water temperature. Under the condition of two phase discharge, when the water temperature is higher than 90 °C, the maximum oscillation increases with the increase of two phase mass flow rate and the decrease of equilibrium quality. Under single phase discharge conditions, the maximum oscillation appears in the condensation oscillation regime map, which is 123 kPa. Under the two phase discharge condition, it appears in the incomplete condensation regime map, which is 398 kPa. The maximum oscillation of the two phase condition is higher than that of the single phase condition. For the oscillation propagation law in the water tank, the maximum oscillation in the radial direction decreases with the increase of the distance from the sparger orifices, and the decrease amplitude decreases with the increase of the distance. In the axial direction, it shows a trend of decreasing first and then increasing.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112829','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112829',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/s0306-4549(26)00790-5','Editorial Board','편집위원회','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','','2026-10-06','','2027-01','편집물','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0306-4549(26)00790-5','https://doi.org/10.1016/s0306-4549(26)00790-5',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112912','A strongly connected component-based block solver for accelerated multi-node flowing-fuel depletion calculations','가속화된 다중 노드 유동 연료 연소 계산을 위한 강력하게 연결된 구성 요소 기반 블록 솔버','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yunfei Zhang; Guifeng Zhu; Rui Yan; Yang Zou','2026-10-06','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Spatially resolved depletion calculations for circulating-fuel systems couple nuclide transmutation with inter-node transport and generate large sparse spatial–nuclide matrices. Repeated factorization of the complex shifted systems can therefore dominate the computational cost of the Chebyshev rational approximation method (CRAM). This study develops a direct block solver based on strongly connected component (SCC) decomposition and implements it in MACT. The off-diagonal graph of the global depletion matrix is decomposed into SCCs and topologically ordered, transforming each CRAM shifted system into block lower-triangular form. Because the pole-dependent shifts affect only the diagonal entries, the same graph structure can be reused for all CRAM poles. The resulting block-forward solution retains all transmutation and migration couplings and is algebraically equivalent to the monolithic solution in exact arithmetic. The method was assessed for powered-node fraction, spatial scale, flow rate, zero-power decay, and a source-term history derived from the Molten-Salt Reactor Experiment (MSRE) model. For burnup calculations, the solver speedup increased with spatial scale and reached 420.8 for the 30-node case, whereas zero-power decay showed more modest acceleration. In the 30-node MSRE-derived source-term history comprising nine burnup and 15 post-shutdown decay steps, the unmerged SCC solver (SCC-RAW) achieved a solver speedup of 318.7; the maximum relative error among the reported aggregate inventories was 2.41 × 10 −10 at decay step 14, and the maximum all-nuclide decay-heat error was 5.87 × 10 −7 at decay step 15. The remaining runtime was dominated by factorization of the largest SCC. The method therefore provides an efficient structure-preserving solver for coupled depletion and transport calculations, although further treatment of dominant SCCs is required for larger systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112912','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112912',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115253','Passive optical fiber sensor system for water level monitoring with implementation of human-machine interface module','인간-기계 인터페이스 모듈 구현을 통한 수위 모니터링을 위한 수동 광섬유 센서 시스템','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Gitae Kim; Jinjong Seo; Jaeyul Choo; Hoon-Keun Lee','2026-10-05','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','In this paper, we demonstrate a remote passive optical fiber sensor system based on space division multiplexing for water level monitoring targeting to extreme environments, such as a spent fuel pool in nuclear power plant. The proposed system is evaluated under laboratory conditions to demonstrate its feasibility for future nuclear safety instrumentation applications. It employs a broadband light source as a seed light and a 1 × 4 optical splitter for multiplexing/demultiplexing multiple optical fiber sensors. Four sensors are vertically installed in a water pool at predefined heights. By measuring the reflected optical power from each sensor with an optical receiver, the discrete water level state corresponding to the predefined sensor positions can be determined in real-time. To mitigate the effect of Rayleigh backscattering in remote sensing, a simple dual-path configuration is introduced. Experimental results show that the proposed system can monitor water levels over a distance of approximately 19 km, limited by the performance of the detector. On the other hand, providing intuitive and real-time information for water level monitoring to operators remains a significant challenge. To address this issue, a human-machine interface (HMI) module is also implemented. By providing real-time information on the discrete water level states and system status through the HMI display, it enables operators to intuitively monitor the current water level status, as well as perform trend analysis and abnormal condition detection.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115253','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115253',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115235','Impact of flow-induced excitation type on fretting wear behavior of steam generator tubes','증기발생기 튜브의 프레팅 마모 거동에 대한 유동 유도 여기 유형의 영향','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Salim El Bouzidi; Anne McLellan; Mohammed Alziadeh; Brendan St. Pierre; Fabrice Guérout','2026-10-05','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','High-temperature impact fretting wear tests have been conducted worldwide since the 1970s, providing insights into the wear characteristics of nuclear power plant components. These tests typically reproduce component interface geometries, materials, and process conditions such as fluid medium, temperature, pressure, and chemistry. Most approaches assume that work rate is the primary parameter governing fretting wear dynamics, consistent with Archard’s equation. However, it is unclear whether a wear coefficient derived under one excitation type (e.g., periodic) can reliably predict component life under another (e.g., random). To address this, an experimental study was conducted using the high-temperature fretting wear rig at Chalk River Laboratories to examine the effect of excitation type on wear behavior. The study focused on a nickel alloy steam generator tube in contact with a stainless-steel support featuring a broached hole geometry. Tests were performed for 500 h in water at 280 °C under two excitation conditions. The first employed periodic excitation to simulate tube vibration from vortex-induced vibration and fluidelastic instability, while the second applied random excitation generated from empirically derived force spectra to represent turbulence-induced vibration. Tube motion and contact forces were monitored to control work rate and investigate impact statistics. Wear was assessed using profilometry and mass change to derive wear coefficients, and SEM imaging was used to assess the wear mechanisms. Results showed that, at the same work rate, random excitation caused significantly greater wear and broader impact distributions across impact angles, forces, and sliding parameters. These findings indicate that fretting wear behavior depends on excitation type as well as work rate.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115235','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115235',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115241','Coherence-to-multiscale transition of shear-layer vortex shedding in a closed side-branch junction','밀폐된 사이드 브랜치 접합에서 전단층 와류 쉐딩의 일관성 대 다중 스케일 전이','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Yunhao Zhang; Xinying Wang; Lang Liu; Haijun Wang','2026-10-05','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','This paper investigates a coherence-to-multiscale transition of shear-layer vortex shedding in a closed side-branch junction and quantifies how geometric perturbations modify (i) the spectral distribution of pressure fluctuations across frequencies and (ii) the spatial footprint of the dominant-frequency oscillations. Large-eddy simulations are analyzed using spectral proper orthogonal decomposition (SPOD) for 16 geometries with side-branch diameters D side = 24, 32, 40, and 48 mm and lip fillet-chamfer diameters D cham = 0, 10, 20, and 30 mm. After statistically steady states are reached, we characterize the dominant shedding frequency, the temporal standard deviation of pressure fluctuations, the leading SPOD-mode energy fraction and its spatial footprint, and the time-averaged shear-layer length and thickness. Increasing the geometric dimensions reduces the dominant shedding frequency and amplifies pressure fluctuations, while the main-frequency energy fraction decreases and the dominant-response region becomes markedly more spatially dispersed. These trends indicate that the shear layer evolves from a dominant narrowband shedding state, with a strong leading SPOD mode at the shedding frequency, to a broader-band state in which energy is distributed among higher-order modes and broadband fluctuations. This reduction in single-frequency dominance may lower the propensity for lock-in when a flow-acoustic feedback pathway is present. An equivalent characteristic length derived from the shear-layer statistics accounts for the combined effects of the side-branch and lip fillet-chamfer diameters. The resulting Strouhal numbers range from 0.9 to 1.3, supporting a common convective time-scale interpretation of the dominant shedding frequency across the investigated geometries.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115241','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115241',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112916','Experimental and computational investigation of radiation shielding performance of high-strength copper-based alloys','고강도 구리계 합금의 방사선 차폐 성능에 대한 실험 및 계산 조사','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Hemn Salh; Ş.Nevin Balo; Hawbir Swara Ahmed Manguri; Dedawan S. Saleh; Ari Maghdid Hamad','2026-10-05','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The radiation shielding performance of four high-strength copper-based alloys, namely CuBe 2 , CuCoNiBe, CuNi 2 SiCr, and CuCrZr, was investigated against gamma rays, fast neutrons, and charged particles (protons and helium ions). Gamma-ray attenuation coefficients were experimentally measured at photon energies of 0.511–1.332 MeV using a NaI(Tl) detector and theoretically evaluated over the energy range 0.2–10 MeV using the Phy-X/PSD. The calculated results were validated through comparison with WinXCom calculations and experimental data, showing good agreement. The mass stopping power and projected range of protons and helium ions were evaluated using SRIM Monte Carlo simulations. The CuCrZr alloy demonstrates the best gamma-ray shielding performance, while CuNi 2 SiCr exhibits the highest mass stopping power for both protons and helium ions. Fast neutron shielding evaluation, based on the fast neutron effective removal cross section (FNERCs) software, indicates that CuCoNiBe provides the most effective neutron attenuation. The results highlight the potential of high-strength copper-based alloys as multifunctional materials for radiation shielding applications involving mixed radiation fields.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112916','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112916',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IQ;TR','IQ','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112869','DEM-based analysis of fine-debris migration, retention and pore-network deposition in gas-swept Li4SiO4 breeder pebble beds','가스 스윕된 Li4SiO4 육종가 페블베드에서 미세 잔해 이동, 유지 및 기공-네트워크 침착에 대한 DEM 기반 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jian Wang; Mingzhun Lei; Haoxi Wang; Zhiyuan Liu; Haishun Deng; Wei Wen; Gang Shen','2026-10-05','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Fine debris can migrate through connected pores in ceramic breeder beds before bed-scale structural degradation becomes measurable. We combine particle-resolved DEM tracking with DEM-derived pore reconstruction in a stiff Li 4 SiO 4 bed of 10,000 1 mm pebbles and evaluate outlet breakthrough, local deposition, connected-pore loss and pressure response as distinct observables. Across the terminal drive, inventory and internal-release cases, the migration and deposition channels responded differently, while the largest resolved connectivity loss was 5.3 × 1 0 − 4 . Localized release separated a retained bulk from a sparse leading population, showing why outlet arrival is not a hydraulic-failure measure by itself. Same-mesh OpenFOAM calculations provide an independent debris-free pressure reference and a prescribed resistance-loading response. The resulting staged workflow can select cases for finer pore reconstruction, coupled flow analysis or pressure measurement. Its interpretation is limited to the studied parameter space, fixed-bed one-way DEM assumptions and finite voxel resolution; predicting a clogging transition requires resolved gas–solid feedback and hydraulic validation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112869','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112869',1,'2026-10-11','2026-10-12','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02060-8','Study on temperature-assisted dynamic liquid chromatography and its application in uranium isotope separation','온도 보조 동적 액체 크로마토그래피 및 우라늄 동위원소 분리에서의 응용에 관한 연구','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Yu-Jie Fu; Tao Yu; Yu-Xiang Li','2026-10-17','2026-10-16','2026-10-16','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02060-8','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02060-8',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02079-x','Improved model and structure–energy database for hydrogen–nanovoid interactions in tungsten','텅스텐에서 수소-나노보이드 상호작용을 위한 개선된 모델 및 구조-에너지 데이터베이스','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Kang-Ni He; Xiang-Shan Kong; Jun Lin; Liang Chen','2026-10-17','2026-10-16','2026-10-16','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02079-x','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02079-x',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02068-0','Hybrid adaptive RSM-GA Monte Carlo optimization method (HRG-MCO) and its application in the design of moderator–collimator systems for accelerator-based thermal neutron radiography','하이브리드 적응형 RSM-GA 몬테카를로 최적화 방법 (HRG-MCO) 및 가속기 기반 열 중성자 방사선 촬영을 위한 조정자-조정자 시스템 설계에 적용','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Chen-Xiao Yang; Si-Ze Chen; Lian-Xin Zhang; Chuan Peng; Dan Xiao','2026-10-17','2026-10-16','2026-10-16','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02068-0','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02068-0',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02075-1','Generation of mode-locked EUV and soft X-ray radiation via coherent Thomson scattering from a density-modulated electron bunch','밀도 변조 전자 다발로부터 일관된 톰슨 산란을 통한 모드 잠금 EUV 및 연질 X선 복사의 생성','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Zhen-Hong Wang; Si Chen; Hai-Xiao Deng','2026-10-17','2026-10-16','2026-10-16','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02075-1','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02075-1',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02074-2','Analysis with the Lindblad equation and the instantaneous-pulse approximation: quantum Zeno/anti-Zeno effects in a three-level system','린드블라드 방정식과 순간-펄스 근사치를 이용한 분석: 3-레벨 시스템에서 양자 제노/안티-제노 효과','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Chen-Xu Wu; Pei-Wei Wen; Cheng-Jian Lin; Chang Xu; Lei Yang; Hui-Ming Jia; Feng Yang; Nan-Ru Ma','2026-10-17','2026-10-16','2026-10-16','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02074-2','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02074-2',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02064-4','3DTNN-based TRPCA reconstruction approach for compressed ultra-fast photography of a velocity interferometer system for any reflector','모든 반사경을 위한 속도 간섭계 시스템의 압축 초고속 사진을 위한 3DTNN 기반 TRPCA 재구성 접근법','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Hua-Quan Gan; Feng Wang; Yun-Bao Huang; Zan-Yang Guan; Yu-Long Li; Hai-Yan Li','2026-10-17','2026-10-16','2026-10-16','연구논문','기타 원자력','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02064-4','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02064-4',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104790','Toward Reliable Probabilistic CHF Prediction: Physical Interpretation and Evaluation of Epistemic–Aleatoric Uncertainty Decomposition','신뢰할 수 있는 확률적 CHF 예측을 향하여: 인식적-대립적 불확실성 분해의 물리적 해석 및 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Chanyeong Yoon; Mooneon Lee; Juhyung Lee; Hyouk Kwon; Kyung Mo Kim','2026-10-17','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','Critical heat flux (CHF) is a key thermal-hydraulic phenomenon in reactor safety; however, its accurate prediction remains challenging due to highly nonlinear behavior. Accordingly, data-driven models have been developed to overcome limitations of conventional correlations. Although probabilistic neural networks provide uncertainty estimates alongside predictions, the reliability of their calibration and consistency with the underlying data distribution remain unclear. A unified framework is proposed to evaluate uncertainty reliability using 24,579 CHF data points and three probabilistic approaches: Bayesian neural networks, Monte Carlo Dropout, and Deep Ensembles. Calibration is assessed using AUSE, CE, and NLL, while uncertainty consistency is evaluated through Spearman correlation between epistemic uncertainty and data sparsity measures. The results reveal that epistemic uncertainty across models is more strongly influenced by prediction magnitude than data sparsity, indicating limited consistency with the underlying data distribution. To improve the uncertainty calibration and consistency of the probabilistic framework, a pruned diversified deep ensemble (PDiv-DE) is proposed. The PDiv-DE preserves predictive performance while improving calibration accuracy and strengthening the consistency between epistemic uncertainty and data sparsity. Therefore, the proposed framework provides a practical step toward more reliable uncertainty quantification for CHF prediction and supports the development of data-driven models for safety-relevant thermal-hydraulic applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104790','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104790',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104792','Public valuation of a partial transition from large reactors to enhanced-safety small modular reactors: Evidence from South Korea','대형 원자로에서 강화된 안전 소형 모듈형 원자로로의 부분 전환에 대한 공공 평가: 한국의 증거','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Moon-Ki Min; Bo-Min Seol; Seung-Hoon Yoo','2026-10-17','','2026-10','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This study estimates South Korean households’ willingness to pay (WTP) for a proposed partial transition from conventional large reactors to enhanced-safety small modular reactors (SMRs). The scenario maintains total capacity at 1,400 MW while replacing 700 MW of conventional large-reactor capacity with SMRs. A nationwide contingent valuation survey of 1,000 household heads or spouses, conducted in early 2026, employed one-and-one-half-bound dichotomous-choice questions and a spike model to accommodate zero WTP responses. Mean monthly WTP was KRW 2,677 (USD 1.74) in the model without covariates and KRW 2,591 (USD 1.68) in the covariate model. WTP was positively associated with household income and prior SMR knowledge and negatively associated with the presence of children. The treatment of stated zero responses materially affects the estimated welfare measure, and the high prevalence of payment-vehicle protests underscores the importance of financing design and perceived institutional responsibility. The results indicate that the proposed transition has measurable non-market value; however, the estimate reflects households’ valuation of the bundled policy scenario—including changes in reactor technology, unit scale, capacity composition, and safety-related characteristics—rather than the marginal value of passive safety or any individual SMR attribute.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104792','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104792',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104778','A reliability data aggregation method for fusion-oriented research facilities','융합형 연구시설에 대한 신뢰성 자료 집계 방법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','H. Ortiz; J.E. Ruiz-Castro; C. Acal; K. Kowal; J. Chiachío; A.M. Aguilera','2026-10-17','','2026-10','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This paper aims to develop a statistical method for integrating multiple incomplete data sources to improve the estimation of the failure-rate probability distribution of fusion-specific devices. The data aggregation approach proposed in this work is to support the Reliability, Availability, Maintainability, and Inspectability (RAMI) studies for fusion-oriented research facilities. This work focuses on developing a procedure for handling missing or incomplete data from multiple sources, as well as formulating a statistical framework for combining data from different sources that refer to the same equipment type and failure mode. Specifically, a Bayesian result is adopted under the assumption of a constant failure rate over time. This framework motivates the use of the Gamma distributions to model the failure-rate parameter of each device. Subsequently, two alternative procedures are introduced to approximate, using a single Gamma distribution, the weighted mixture formed by combining Gamma distributions corresponding to the same equipment type across multiple data sources. The proposed method is validated through an extensive simulation study and further illustrated by application to the accelerator systems of the IFMIF-DONES facility. Finally, the proposed algorithm has been implemented in the open-source software R to facilitate its use in the nuclear fusion community.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104778','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104778',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','ES;PL','ES','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115274','Modelling fluidelastic instability in two-phase cross-flow using indicial functions','내부 함수를 사용하여 2상 교차 흐름에서 유체 탄성 불안정 모델링','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Loay Alyaldin; Njuki W. Mureithi','2026-10-17','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115274','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115274',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112951','Numerical study of thermal mixing characteristics in lead-bismuth parallel triple-jet based on detached eddy simulation','분리된 EDDY 시뮬레이션을 기반으로 한 납-비스무트 평행 삼중 제트에서의 열 혼합 특성에 대한 수치 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Wenzhen Qiao; Xingchen Wang; Weijie Tang; Rui Zhang; Jianquan Liu; Mingchen Xia; Yuanhao Liu','2026-10-17','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','In lead-cooled fast reactors (LFRs), the temperature difference between hot and cold lead–bismuth eutectic (LBE) streams from different fuel assemblies can exceed 100 K. Their interaction in the upper plenum generates complex turbulent jets, which may cause thermal striping and thermal fatigue in structural components, making thermal mixing critical to reactor safety. Conventional RANS methods struggle to reliably capture transient temperature fluctuations, while pure LES incurs prohibitively high computational cost for multi-condition engineering studies. Detached eddy simulation (DES), which combines near-wall Reynolds-averaged Navier–Stokes modeling with large eddy simulation in separated regions, strikes a practical balance between eddy-resolving capability and computational efficiency, providing an efficient approach for resolving large-scale turbulent structures and temperature fluctuations. In this study, DES was used to investigate the thermal mixing of hot and cold LBE coolant jets in a parallel triple-jet configuration. The method was validated against liquid-sodium triple-jet experimental data and then applied to examine the effects of inlet velocity and temperature difference. The results show that higher inlet velocity enhances jet inertia, delays near-inlet mixing, and broadens the frequency range of temperature fluctuations, whereas a larger temperature difference mainly increases temperature gradients and fluctuation intensity, with little influence on the overall flow structure and dominant frequency range. A reference comparison with LES data further demonstrates that DES can reproduce the overall dependence of temperature fluctuation intensity on the operating parameters with comparable fluctuation amplitude ranges, while requiring approximately 94 % lower estimated computational cost.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112951','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112951',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112952','Numerical simulation of Gamma-Induced background current in cobalt Self-Powered neutron detectors','코발트 자체 동력 중성자 검출기에서 감마 유도 배경 전류의 수치 시뮬레이션','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Xiong Wu; Zhihong Liu; Jiasi Yu; Jieqiong Jiang; Li Cai; Xiangju Zhang; Zhiqiang Cui','2026-10-17','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112952','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112952',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106647','Proactive maintenance and structural modifications of VVER-1000 steam generator blowdown systems to ensure long-term safety','장기적인 안전을 보장하기 위해 VVER-1000 증기발생기 블로우다운 시스템의 사전 유지 보수 및 구조 수정','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Karel Vidlák; Vladimír Mózer','2026-10-16','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Steam generators of VVER-1000 pressurized water reactors play a crucial role in separating the primary and secondary circuits and safely removing heat from the reactor core. This paper systematically evaluates the degradation mechanisms on the secondary side of the steam generator, focusing on the continuous blowdown and sludge removal systems in the context of ensuring long-term safety functions. Based on operational data and experience from a reference nuclear power plant, a transition from reactive to proactive preventive maintenance is proposed. This approach combines continuous diagnostics, water chemistry management, technical modifications to piping layouts, and risk-based planning. The study identifies dominant damage mechanisms (pitting corrosion, stress corrosion cracking, sludge accumulation in inspection pockets, and foreign material ingress), quantifies their impact on the integrity of heat transfer tubes, and proposes practical measures to maintain the barrier function of the steam generator. The benefits include a reduced probability of failures, stabilization of the water chemistry regime, shortened outage durations, and improved long-term reliability of Safety Class 1 components.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106647','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106647',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CZ','CZ','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106649','Numerical study on effects of tube bundle geometry and arrangement on external steam-air condensation','튜브 다발 형상 및 배열이 외부 증기-공기 응축에 미치는 영향에 대한 수치 연구','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Daiyong Song; Nan Zhang; Ruihan Jing; Qianru Liu; Zhongning Sun; Haozhi Bian','2026-10-16','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Condensation of steam mixed with non-condensable gases (NCGs) is a key physical process governing containment depressurization and thermal removal during severe nuclear reactor accidents. Previous studies on steam condensation with NCGs outside tube bundles have mostly focused on bundle structures with a single length and pitch. This paper examines the effects of bundle length, pitch, inclination angle, arrangement, and tube rows number on steam-air condensation outside tube bundles via numerical simulation. The coupling effects between tube length and arrangement, as well as tube pitch and inclination angle, are also analyzed. Calculations indicate that for tubes of different lengths and arrangements, the condensation heat transfer coefficient (CHTC) first decreases and then stabilizes as the tube length increases. Furthermore, the CHTC of different tubes within the bundle increases with larger tube pitch. At a tube pitch of 1.5d, tube innermost tube exhibits the poorest heat transfer performance. At a tube pitch of 3d, its heat transfer capacity becomes 2.55 times that under the 1.5d condition. Inclination induces more obvious overlap effect with narrow tube pitch, at a pitch of 2d, and the overall CHTC of the bundle increases with a larger inclination angle. Additionally, the overall CHTC for a 1m tube bundle gradually increases with increased tube rows, the CHTC surpasses that of a single tube when the number of rows exceeds 10. For 3m and 5m tube bundles, it initially decreases and then tends to stabilize as the number of rows increases.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106649','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106649',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106646','Effects of curvature and inclination on external steam condensation with non-condensable gases under natural convection','자연 대류 하에서 비응축성 가스로 외부 증기 응축에 대한 곡률 및 경사의 영향','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','Ruihan Jing; Shuhang Zhou; Daiyong Song; Xu Zhang; Chao Jiang; Haozhi Bian; Jianjun Wang','2026-10-16','','2027-01','연구논문','열수력·유체','Steam-air condensation is a significant heat transfer process within the thermal-hydraulics field. Previous research has predominantly focused on heat transfer tubes with large curvatures, resulting in experimental correlations that are largely limited to circular tubes and often neglect the effects of curvatures and inclinations on external condensation performance of tubes with limited curvatures or even flat plates. This study, conducted on the COAST (condensation and species transport) experimental facility, investigated steam condensation with non-condensable gases (NCGs) outside circular tubes/plates of different curvatures, covering a pressure range of 0.2∼1.6 MPa and an NCG concentration range of 7∼90%. The plate configurations included both upper-condensing plate and lower-condensing plate, with the influence of inclination angles also incorporated. The results show that the condensation heat transfer coefficient ( h c ) increases significantly with greater curvature, and the rate of this increase itself grows. The h c of the 100 mm tube shows an improvement of less than 10% compared to flat plate, whereas the 19 mm tube exhibits an average enhancement of approximately 50% compared to the 100 mm tube. Furthermore, the h c increases notably with decreasing inclination, although the magnitude of this improvement gradually diminishes. For the 19 mm tube, the h c of the horizontal tube is 18∼27% higher than that of the vertical tube. For the 100 mm tube, the improvement is only about 5∼15%. The influence of inclination angles on plate condensation differs from that on tubes. For upper-condensing plate, the h c is weaker in the horizontal orientation than in the vertical orientation. While that of the lower-condensing plate initially enlarges and then diminishes from horizontal to vertical orientation. Moreover, the h c of the lower-condensing plate consistently surpasses that of the upper plate. Finally, an experimental correlation applicable to heat transfer tubes and plates with different curvatures and inclination angles was developed. A comparison with existing correlations demonstrates that the proposed correlation has a predictive accuracy within ±20%.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106646','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106646',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104782','High-throughput gamma-ray spectrometry using 1-GS/s current-pulse acquisition and FPGA-based cascaded pile-up recovery','1-GS/s 전류 펄스 획득 및 FPGA 기반 캐스케이드 파일 업 복구를 사용한 고속 감마선 분광법','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Lei Yan; Guo-qiang Zeng; Qiang Li; Li He; Jian Yang; Yang Hou; Song Qing','2026-10-16','','2026-10','연구논문','방사선·계측','Long decay tails introduced by charge-sensitive preamplifiers increase the probability of pulse pile-up and limit the output count rate of conventional gamma-ray spectrometers under high-count-rate conditions. This work presents a high-throughput gamma-ray spectrometer based on current-pulse readout, 1-GS/s waveform digitization, and field-programmable gate array (FPGA)-based pile-up recovery. The 16-bit analog-to-digital converter (ADC) stream is processed using four parallel 250-MHz preprocessing lanes, event-driven variable-length packetization, dynamic allocation among eight first-in, first-out (FIFO)-backed recovery channels, and 16-stage cascaded template subtraction. The system was evaluated using a 1.5-inch LaBr 3 :Ce detector and a 137 Cs source. The measured single-pulse rise time and decay-time constant were 33 and 47 ns, respectively. For a representative isolated pulse, the normalized root-mean-square error relative to the average template was 0.0134. Noise-injection simulations yielded a standard deviation of 0.776 ns for timing deviations obtained using digital constant-fraction discrimination. For the investigated pulse separations and amplitude ratio, template-alignment errors between −3 and +3 ns resulted in a maximum absolute relative error below 1.8% in the mean recovered secondary-pulse amplitude. Using the estimated input rates, valid-event throughputs of 95.6% and 82.1% were obtained at 1 and 4.96 Mcps, respectively, with corresponding energy resolutions of 3.14% and 5.27% at 661.7 keV under their respective operating conditions. A system-level comparison showed that the proposed spectrometer maintained a more nearly linear input–output count-rate response and a smaller rate-dependent degradation in energy resolution than the conventional charge-sensitive configuration over the common measurement range.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104782','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104782',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115270','Benchmarking CAPRIX pin behaviour under irradiation with high plutonium content: comparison with experimental data','높은 플루토늄 함량으로 조사 중인 CAPRIX PIN 행동 벤치마킹: 실험 데이터와의 비교','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','M.-M. Desagulier; D. Jaramillo-Sierra; B. Burger; L. Argeles; M. Stefanowska-Skrodzka; J. Lavarenne; V. Dupont; E. Deveaux; A. Del Nevo; E. Brunetto; A. Scolaro; J. Gado; K. Sturm; A. Rineiski; L. Luzzi; A. Magni; D. Pizzocri; K. Mikityuk; A. Jiménez-Carrascosa; S. Lemehov; V. Matocha; S. Bebjak; C. Strmensky; V. Blanc; N. Chauvin','2026-10-16','','2026-12','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This paper presents the results of the second phase of the benchmark exercise in the Plutonium Management for More Agility project (PuMMA), which aims to enhance the reliability of fuel performance codes (FPCs) for Mixed Oxide (MOX) fuels with high plutonium content. This phase involved the simulation of the CAPRIX irradiation (45% of Pu) carried out in the PHENIX reactor in France. Thirteen organizations from nine countries participated, using eight different fuel performance codes. In this phase, 7 codes then improved its modelling by optimizing parameters and/or improving the formulation of some models involved in the computation. A comparative analysis was then conducted between the codes and the post-irradiation experimental (PIE) results, with the objective of identifying the improvements made, the discrepancies still observed, and to define future areas for improvement and development. The present paper demonstrates the results for the CAPRIX pin. The main results despite the discrepancies noted between the codes and/or with the experimental data, the work carried out through this benchmark has demonstrated the capacity of the codes to optimise/improve their simulation in order to approximate the PIE. Moreover, the methodology employed yielded a comprehensive and precise analysis, thus facilitating the suggestion of approaches to the development of specific models. This finding thus demonstrates the potential of fuel performance codes modelling pins with high Pu contents.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115270','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115270',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112933','Thermal-hydraulic assessment of microencapsulated phase change material slurry for natural-circulation loops','자연 순환 루프용 마이크로 캡슐화 상 변화 재료 슬러리의 열수력 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Si Yang; Hangbin Zhao; Kaiwen Qin; Tingxiang Lv; Xiaobin Tang','2026-10-16','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112933','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112933',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112930','Radiation dose analysis in the IR-IECF device: numerical analysis with geant4 simulation and experimental measurements','IR-IECF 장치에서의 방사선량 분석: geant4 시뮬레이션 및 실험 측정을 통한 수치 분석','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Maryam Ghapanvary; Fatemeh Bakhshoodeh Pour; Morteza Sedaghat Movahed; Alireza Aslezaeem','2026-10-16','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This study presents a combined experimental and Geant4-based assessment of the radiation field and shielding performance of the Iranian Inertial Electrostatic Confinement fusion device (IR-IECF) operating in deuterium–deuterium (D–D) mode and producing 2.45 MeV neutrons. A detailed Geant4 model of the IR-IECF device, its surrounding borated-polyethylene shielding, and the relevant dosimetry locations was developed to calculate neutron and gamma dose distributions. Experimental gamma doses were measured using GR-200 (LiF:Mg,Cu,P) thermoluminescent dosimeters, whereas neutron ambient dose-equivalent rates were measured using a Berthold LB6411 rem counter. In the Geant4 model, neutron dose scoring was performed using LiF-based virtual dosimeters positioned at the corresponding monitoring locations, allowing the numerical results to be compared with the experimental neutron measurements. The simulated neutron and gamma dose values showed good agreement with the corresponding experimental data, supporting the reliability of the developed Geant4 model for radiation-field characterization. In addition, a dedicated secondary-particle scoring analysis was performed to characterize the secondary radiation generated during neutron transport. Electrons, protons, and photons were the dominant recorded secondary particles, while secondary neutrons accounted for approximately 1.69% of the recorded secondary tracks. Overall, the combined experimental and numerical approach provides a practical framework for radiation-field characterization and shielding assessment of IECF-based neutron sources.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112930','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112930',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112937','Multivariable control of large-scale pressurized water reactor based on LPV-MPC algorithm over a wide operating range','광범위한 작동 범위에서 LPV-MPC 알고리즘에 기반한 대규모 가압수형 원자로의 다변수 제어','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Jinhong Mo; Peiwei Sun; Xinyu Wei','2026-10-16','','2027-02','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','For energy conservation, large-scale Pressurized Water Reactors (PWRs) are required to participate in grid peak shaving. Compared to traditional PID control, Model Predictive Control (MPC) algorithm offers advantages in handling multivariable control problems. However, PWR systems exhibit strong nonlinearity under wide-range operation, limiting conventional MPC performance. Therefore, Linear Parameter Varying (LPV) models, valued for their nonlinear approximation capability and low computational cost, are employed in nonlinear MPC. This paper proposes an LPV model-based MPC algorithm to enhance the control of a nonlinear HPR1000 model. An iterative optimization strategy is adopted for LPV model identification: first, initial local models are identified using the asymptotic method; then, parameters of the weighting functions are estimated via least squares; finally, the LPV model is optimized iteratively based on the total data. The local models demonstrate good performance in both time-domain and frequency-domain validation. The optimized LPV model shows high similarity to the plant’s step responses at both high and low loads, confirming its suitability for MPC controller. The LPV-MPC is compared with both the original control system and a fixed-model MPC (F-MPC) through test scenarios at 100 % and 50 % FP. The results indicate that the LPV-MPC controller offers comparable performance at 100 % FP, but exhibits faster regulation speed and stronger capability in suppressing SG water level fluctuations at 50 % FP. The comparison with F-MPC demonstrates that the LPV-MPC possesses stronger adaptability and robustness. Meanwhile, a large-scale transition scenario was implemented. The comparative analysis confirms that the LPV-MPC controller possesses superior load-following performance.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112937','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112937',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112925','Impact of regional climate and SMR operation mode on techno-economic performance of nuclear renewable hybrid energy systems for middle scale data centers','중규모 데이터 센터를 위한 원자력 재생 하이브리드 에너지 시스템의 기술 경제적 성능에 대한 지역 기후 및 SMR 운영 모드의 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Shuo Wang; Yiyang Shen; Zhenqin Xiong','2026-10-16','','2027-02','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112925','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112925',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2745314','Safety Culture in Licensed Indonesian Irradiation Facilities: Evaluating Key Attributes Through the IAEA Harmonized Model','허가된 인도네시아 방사선 조사 시설의 안전 문화: IAEA 조화 모델을 통한 주요 속성 평가','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Agus Teguh Pranoto; Nunik Madyaningarum; Khusnul Khotimah; Siti Alimah; Ratih Luhuring Tyas; Ika Wahyu Setya Andani; Chevy Cahyana; Budi Santoso; Joko Waluyo; Edwin Yoga Pratama; Hadi Suntoko; Agus Aryanto; Sriyana; Kurnia Anzhar; Fepriadi','2026-10-15','2026-10-15','2026-10-15','연구논문','열수력·유체','The growing deployment of industrial irradiation technology utilizing high-activity sealed sources and high-energy accelerators escalates radiological risks. Comprehensive safety culture evaluations are critical to prevent radiological consequences and maintain the credibility of the national nuclear safety infrastructure. This study assesses key attributes within licensed Indonesian irradiation facilities using the IAEA Harmonized Safety Culture Model, addressing the lack of empirical evidence in this sector. A quantitative, exploratory study was conducted across multiple organizational levels (operators, supervisors, management, HSE, and administrative personnel), yielding 39 respondents. The questionnaire evaluated 43 attributes grouped into ten IAEA-defined characteristics. Data were analyzed using descriptive statistics, including frequency distributions, mean scores, and standard deviations, supported by validity and reliability testing of the instrument. Workplace communication, facilities reflect respect, learning from experience, training, and resolution emerged as relatively strengths; conversely, respect is evident, free flow of information, benchmarking, recognize and question assumptions, and question uncertainty were identified as priority areas for improvement. The findings provide an empirical baseline and context-specific insights for operators and regulators to strengthen targeted safety strategies. While exploratory and perception-based, this study establishes a foundation for progressive safety maturity. Future research should integrate objective safety performance indicators, larger datasets, and complementary qualitative approaches to systematically examine the causal relationships driving organizational safety performance.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2745314','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2745314',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','ID','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2743954','A 2D Defense-in-Depth Waypoint Graph Framework for Evaluation of Physical Protection Systems at Research Reactors','연구용 원자로의 물리적 보호 시스템 평가를 위한 2D 심층 방어 웨이포인트 그래프 프레임워크','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Nizar Kamil Perwira; Sihana; Muhammad Subekti; Dinan Andiwijayakusuma','2026-10-15','2026-10-15','2026-10-15','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Research reactors represent potential targets for sabotage scenarios with severe radiological consequences, requiring rigorous evaluation of the effectiveness of physical protection systems (PPSs). Traditional evaluation tools based on the Estimate of Adversary Sequence Interruption model and its extensions employ one-dimensional adversary sequence diagrams (ASDs) that abstract facility geometry into sequential protection layers, limiting the spatial analysis of alternative adversary routes. This study presents a two-dimensional waypoint graph framework for evaluating the effectiveness of PPSs. Facility layouts are represented as sparse waypoint graphs encoding spatial coordinates, probability of detection PD, and barrier delay times td, with adversary movement constrained by the progression of the defense-in-depth layer. A backward Dijkstra-based pathfinding formulation with exhaustive critical detection point enumeration is used to identify the most vulnerable path under a conservative adversary strategy, without relying on heuristic assumptions. The global pathfinding solution was independently verified through full enumeration of feasible adversary paths. A Monte Carlo simulation was integrated to quantify the influence of the detection probability variability on the probability of interruption distribution. A hypothetical research reactor case study demonstrates that the proposed framework identifies more vulnerable adversary paths than the ASD-based approach under equivalent spatial traversal conditions, resulting in probability of interruption PI values up to 4.25% lower under varying response force timing scenarios. The complete evaluation demonstrated computational tractability suitable for iterative PPS evaluation. Analysis of modified PPS configurations showed where the greatest vulnerability lies within the facility.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2743954','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2743954',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','ID','ID','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104783','Parametric Study of Sn Electrorefining in a LiCl-KCl-CaCl2 Eutectic: A Surrogate System for Pu Electrorefining','LiCl-KCl-CaCl2 Eutectic에서 Sn 전기정제에 대한 파라메트릭 연구: Pu 전기정제를 위한 대리 시스템','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','George Ankrah; Bryant Johnson; Anderson Fuller; Ricardo Rodriguez-Ceron; Addison Omdahl; Gabrielle R. Dangel; Molly Garner; Tatiana Ayers; Devin Rappleye','2026-10-15','','2026-10','연구논문','AI·디지털','Molten-salt electrorefining (ER) is essential for purifying chemically active metals, including plutonium, that cannot be processed in aqueous systems. However, systematic experimental studies linking operating parameters to ER performance and reliable process-monitoring criteria remain limited. In this work, tin–nickel (Sn-Ni) electrorefining in a LiCl-KCl-CaCl 2 eutectic is employed as a non-radioactive surrogate to investigate the effects of anode composition, temperature, and SnCl 2 seeding concentration. Kilogram-scale ER experiments were conducted using an automated operating protocol that monitored voltage, current, static refining resistance, and back-electromotive force (back-emf) as run termination indicators. Product yield, faradaic efficiency, and refined-metal purity were quantified through post-run mass balances and chemical analysis. All conditions produced refined Sn with ≥99.5 wt.% purity. Increasing SnCl 2 seeding concentration and operating temperature improved product yield, whereas increasing Ni impurity in the anode feed from 2 to 3 wt.% significantly reduced yield and faradaic efficiency. Comparison of monitoring metrics showed static refining resistance to be more consistent and reliable than back-emf for identifying run completion, as back-emf exhibited false positives and missed late-stage transitions. These results provide practical guidance for ER process control and reinforce the Sn-Ni system as a surrogate for molten-salt electrorefining of plutonium.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104783','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104783',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104787','Gaussian Process Regression-Based Prediction of Spatial Source-Term Distributions in Activated Bioshield Concrete Using Limited Sampling Data','제한된 샘플링 데이터를 사용하여 활성화된 바이오실드 콘크리트에서 공간 소스-항 분포의 가우시안 프로세스 회귀 기반 예측','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Seok Jun Hong; Nak Woong Yang; Chang Je Park','2026-10-15','','2026-10','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Reliable reconstruction of spatial source-term distributions is important for the radiological characterization of activated bioshield concrete during nuclear power plant decommissioning. Although full-field neutron transport calculations remain necessary, performing mesh-wise activation calculations or radiochemical analyses over an entire structure is computationally and practically demanding. This study developed a Gaussian Process Regression (GPR) approach to reconstruct spatial source-term distributions from limited data. The OPR-1000 bioshield concrete region was discretized into 7,500 mesh cells, and reference specific-activity fields for Co-60, Eu-152, and U-234 were generated using MCNP6.3 and SCALE6.3/ORIGEN. Reconstruction performance was compared among a coordinate-only GPR (CO-GPR) using spatial coordinates, a flux-only log-linear regression (FO-LR) baseline, and a flux-informed GPR (FI-GPR) incorporating total neutron flux. CO-GPR reproduced the overall spatial trends but retained localized residual errors as the number of training points increased. FI-GPR reproduced the reference fields with 10–20 training points and reduced both average and maximum errors. It achieved lower errors than FO-LR for Eu-152 and U-234, while maintaining high accuracy for Co-60, demonstrating consistent reconstruction performance across the three radionuclides. It also yielded narrower GPR posterior prediction intervals associated with sparse-data reconstruction, although empirical coverage differed among the radionuclides. The proposed method therefore reduces the number of required mesh-wise ORIGEN calculations while retaining the full-field MCNP flux calculation.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104787','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104787',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115273','Mechanical pump shaft seals: Dynamic stability and dynamic sealing considerations','기계식 펌프 샤프트 씰: 동적 안정성 및 동적 씰링 고려 사항','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Robert H. Lumsden; Changqing Zhang','2026-10-15','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','The majority of power reactor designs utilize pumps to circulate the primary coolant past the fuel to transfer heat away and provide the thermal power to generate electricity. Mechanical shaft seals are critical nuclear components used to prevent leakage between a rotating pump shaft and the stationary housing for the pump. Success is usually achieved by finding the right balance of providing sufficient leakage to lubricate the seal, without overwhelming the collection system. Mechanical pump seals have two lapped-flat faces in close proximity, one rotating and the other stationary, across which a small amount of leakage (lubricant) is driven by the pressure being sealed (hydrostatic seals) or leakage is driven by the shaft rotation (hydrodynamic seals). This paper will discuss design aspects associated with hydrostatic seals. The gap between these seal faces can change over operation due to intermittent rubbing from loss of film uniformity as a result of: shaft tilt, eccentricity, misalignment, elastomeric seal friction, and vibration. This intermittent rubbing can cause a loss of the initial convergence set during manufacturing, which can cause unstable dynamic response, such as hard rubbing (unlubricated seal face operation). Additionally, this paper will discuss considerations related to the design of dynamic elastomeric seals, which observe the same shaft operating challenges, but also need to move along the shaft without affecting the lubricating film.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115273','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115273',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115256','Finite element model updating of building structures under seismic excitation: A parallelized latent space-based Bayesian framework','지진 여기 하에서 건물 구조물의 유한 요소 모델 업데이트: 병렬화된 잠재 공간 기반 베이지안 프레임워크','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Taro Yaoyama; Sangwon Lee; Minoru Matsubara; Kenzo Kodera; Takeshi Ugata; Tatsuya Itoi','2026-10-15','','2026-12','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Enhancing seismic fragility and risk assessment of nuclear power plants relies on accurate prediction of reactor building responses to seismic hazards, which can be further improved through dynamic analysis of high-fidelity finite element (FE) models. However, FE models often exhibit non-negligible discrepancies from actual structures due to various sources of uncertainty, necessitating FE model updating with rigorous quantification of associated uncertainties. This paper presents a GPU-accelerated latent space-based Bayesian framework for FE model updating of building structures. In the proposed framework, high-dimensional structural response data (e.g., time histories or frequency response functions) are projected into a low-dimensional latent space using a multimodal variational autoencoder (MVAE), thereby enabling efficient and tractable likelihood evaluation without explicit modeling in the original observation space. Once trained, the surrogate enables amortized inference, allowing posterior sampling to be performed without additional simulator evaluations. We specifically employ a sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) sampler, whose population-based formulation allows parallel evaluation of the approximate likelihood on GPUs, resulting in computational efficiency and robustness against multimodal and complex posterior distributions. The proposed framework is evaluated through numerical benchmarking using a shear-type building structure with a multimodal posterior distribution. The results indicate that the proposed approach can recover the major posterior modes while achieving efficient inference through GPU-based parallel evaluation. We further apply the framework to experimental data from a shaking table test of a reinforced concrete building structure. The results suggest that the inferred posterior distributions and posterior predictive responses are consistent with the observed data, even in the presence of sparse observations that induce complex posterior distributions.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115256','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115256',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112911','Startup-to-criticality, transient dynamics, and power-dependent dynamics of a Molten Salt Research Reactor model in OpenModelica','OpenModelica에서 용융염 연구 원자로 모델의 시작-중요성, 일시적 역학 및 전력-의존적 역학','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ondrej Chvala; Visura Pathirana; Jonathan Scherr; Tomomichi Umetani; Kevin Clarno','2026-10-15','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112911','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112911',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','','','OpenAlex: country unavailable');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112932','Reliability assessment of nuclear powered zero-liquid-discharge cogeneration systems with thermal energy storage','열에너지 저장 장치가 있는 원자력 발전 제로 액체 방전 열병합 발전 시스템의 신뢰성 평가','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Asher Jewell; Michael J. Wagner; Saeed Alhadhrami; Steven Prescott; Ben Lindley','2026-10-15','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Nuclear power has the potential to simultaneously address demand for clean electricity, freshwater scarcity, and demand for valuable minerals, such as lithium, if it is thermally integrated with zero liquid discharge desalination (ZLD). ZLD is an energy-intensive process that desalinates seawater, mining its minerals and extracting freshwater such that no liquid is discharged. However, such nuclear-thermal integration could present challenges for the reliability of the combined system, given both nuclear and desalination are capital-intensive technologies. In this paper, the reliability of such a system is assessed for different maintenance strategies. Additionally, the impact of using thermal energy storage (TES) to decouple designs to maintain thermal independence and reduce downtime is investigated. The system is modeled in Event Modeling Risk Assessment using Linked Diagrams (EMRALD). We determined that performing preventative maintenance on degrading system components can reduce reactor downtime by as much as 40% and that introducing TES to decouple the power cycle from the ZLD reduces reactor downtime by as much as 65%. The impact of decoupling on reducing reactor downtime was found to depend on the component failure rates of the ZLD system, with such a strategy being less impactful for a higher reliability process heat application. High component reliabilities in the TES were found to be necessary to prevent increased downtime in the ZLD system, as failure in the TES could otherwise drive the ZLD system offline. Seeing these changes in system performance, this research shows how EMRALD can be used to compare the reliabilities of different cogenerating plant designs and maintenance strategies.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112932','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112932',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112940','Numerical investigations on heat transfer characteristics and melting behaviour of a PHWR pressure tube under combined LOCA and moderator voiding','결합된 위치 및 조정자 무효화 하에서 PHWR 압력관의 열전달 특성 및 용융 거동에 대한 수치 조사','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Omkar Pathak; Abhinav; Shivanshu; Amrik Kundu; Subodh Kumar Yadav; Mushtaque Momin; Mukesh Sharma','2026-10-15','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Failure of the Pressure tube under severe Loss of Coolant Accident (LOCA) with Emergency Core Cooling System (ECCS) failure and complete moderator voiding is a serious issue in Indian Pressurized Heavy Water Reactors (IPHWRs). The present study investigates the thermal behaviour, heat transfer characteristics, and melting progression of a single fuel channel of the 220 MWe IPHWR using ANSYS 2023 R1. The steady-state simulations were performed for heat fluxes ranging from 900 to 4950 W/m 2 to determine the temperature distributions and to identify the melting initiation heat flux for the onset of melting, while the heat flux ranges 4400–4950 W/m 2 were used for the transient phase change simulations to determine the melting rate. The results show that there is a significant temperature asymmetry within the pressure tube-calandria tube assembly. The peak temperature of the pressure tube was raised from 396.25°C to 2080.60°C and the melting initiation heat flux was predicted to be approximately 4400 W/m 2 . With increasing heat flux, the complete melting time decreased from 80 s to 8 s, with an increase of about ten in the Melting Rate Index (MRI), thus representing very non-linear melting behaviour. The proposed PT-CT Thermal Coupling Index (TCI), Normalized Temperature Ratio (NTR) and Melting Rate Index (MRI) are quantitative assessments of the thermal vulnerability and melting progress. The proposed approach will be useful for severe accident analysis and safety assessment of Indian PHWR systems for engineering applications.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112940','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112940',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IN','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112923','Nuclear ship Mutsu and the 1974 radiation leak Incident: Technical background and management lessons','핵선 무츠호와 1974년 방사능 누출 사고: 기술적 배경 및 관리 교훈','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Akira Sakai; Shuichi Ishida','2026-10-15','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','During its experimental voyage in September 1974, Japan’s first nuclear-powered ship, Mutsu, experienced abnormal radiation during a low-power reactor test conducted approximately 800 km east of Cape Shiriya in Aomori Prefecture. The immediate technical mechanism involved fast-neutron streaming and secondary gamma-ray generation caused by an inadequate shielding configuration. Although the event did not involve major fuel damage or a large release of radioactive material, it developed into a serious operational and political problem, leading to resistance to the ship’s return and to a government investigation. This paper reconstructs the incident and reviews the technical and organizational conditions that shaped its occurrence and subsequent handling. Drawing on official reports, technical records, and prior studies, it examines how inadequate project integration, limited design review, contractual separation, and communication failures complicated what began as a shielding-design problem. Using action system theory of management as a heuristic framework, we organize key task-level findings and relate them to recurrent patterns in major public technology projects. The case indicates that, in prototype nuclear systems, technical adequacy alone is insufficient: integrated review, clear responsibility, and effective communication are also essential to safe development and testing.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112923','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112923',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','JP','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112949','Nuclear reactor cladding enhancement via magnetron sputtering: Examining the effects of increasing Mo content in high-entropy coating on Zircaloy-4','마그네트론 스퍼터를 통한 원자로 피복관 향상: 고엔트로피 코팅의 Mo 함량 증가가 Zircaloy-4에 미치는 영향 검토','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ubong Eduok; Jerzy Szpunar','2026-10-15','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Single-metal interlayer coating systems reliably protect standard Zircaloy tubes, making them suitable candidates for accident-tolerant fuel (ATF) cladding in nuclear service environments. However, they also deplete during interfacial metallic interactions (e.g., during Nb-Zr interdiffusion) and co-precipitate (e.g., when Mo interlays between Cr and Zr), thereby losing their availability as protective coatings for long-term use. In the quest to address these shortcomings, the present study explores a multiple-metal-engineered high-entropy alloy (HEA) coating (CrFeNiMoAl), proposed as a reliable alternative, particularly based on Mo as a refractory metal, for testing under high-thermal conditions. Four coating variants with Mo content ranging from 0 to 30 % (HEAMo0-3) were deposited on Zircaloy-4 via magnetron sputtering. To examine their corrosion behavior, these coatings were comparatively tested under conditions simulating Pressurized Water Reactor (PWR) cooling systems via electrochemistry in LiOH/H 3 BO 3 , by accelerated annealing (1200 °C at atmospheric pressure for 5 min), and subcritical corrosion tests at 360 °C in 18.6 MPa steam. In addition to material strengthening, improved barrier performance is attributed to the optimal Mo content, which supports the presence of predominantly body-centered cubic (BCC) nanocrystalline multiphase structure. Barrier performance depends largely on Mo content in the following order of increasing strengths: HEAMo1 (with 10.1 % Mo) ˃ HEAMo2 (with 20.7 % Mo) ˃ HEAMo3 (with 30 % Mo) ˃ HEAMo0 (with 0 % Mo). Higher Mo content oversaturated the internal coating structure, leading to coating degradation, increased Mo-ion release, and the formation of additional pathways for corrosive ions to reach the Zr surface. This work does not aim to investigate interfacial elemental diffusion, as ample research already addresses this topic. The essential insight from the present study concerns the impact of coolant chemistry and coating content on the performance and durability of ATF-cladding materials for next-generation nuclear reactor fuel systems.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112949','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112949',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112920','Modeling (α,n) neutron source terms in the ALEPH depletion code','ALEPH 연소 코드에서 중성자 선원항 모델링 (α, n)','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Alexey Stankovskiy; Yurdunaz Çelik; Nadia Messaoudi; Gert Van den Eynde','2026-10-15','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The modeling of ( α ,n) neutron source terms in the ALEPH depletion code is assessed for two contrasting systems: spent nuclear fuel, a heavy actinide-oxide matrix, and an americium-beryllium (AmBe) source, a light low-Z matrix. In each, the source intensity and alpha spectrum are computed both by the analytic thick target yield and by direct alpha transport. For the spent fuel the yield from MCNP, ALEPH’s transport solver, falls 16% below the thick target yield, whereas for AmBe the two agree to within about 1%. The discrepancy is traced to MCNP’s internal stopping power table, which deviates from the validated SRIM and NIST ASTAR data in the heavy matrix but not the light one. The thick target yield is therefore at present the only reliable route to ( α ,n) source terms within ALEPH: MCNP alpha transport should not be used in heavy matrices, and an explicit transport estimate should come from a code with validated stopping powers, such as PHITS. A separate, matrix-independent energy-binning artifact in the MCNP alpha fluence spectrum is also identified; it redistributes fluence between neighboring bins without biasing integral quantities, and matters only when a differential spectrum is tallied. The neutron emission spectra from JENDL-5, JEFF-4.0 and TENDL-2025 are assessed through their effect on the ambient dose equivalent rate H*(10), computed for the AmBe source in a PHITS model of a shielded calibration laboratory and benchmarked against the reference ISO 8529-1 spectrum. The comparison supports JENDL-5 as the ALEPH default.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112920','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112920',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','BE','BE','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2736428','Selected Papers from the 13th Japan–U.S. Seminar on Two-Phase Flow Dynamics','제13회 일본-미국 2단계 흐름 역학 세미나에서 선정된 논문','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Shuichiro Miwa; Steven Ceccio; Gretar Tryggvason; Shu Takagi; Koji Okamoto; Xiaodong Sun','2026-10-14','2026-10-14','2026-10-14','연구논문','열수력·유체','It is our great pleasure to introduce this special issue of Nuclear Technology featuring selected papers from the 13th Japan–U.S. Seminar on Two-Phase Flow Dynamics (JP-US STPFD’25). Hosted by the ...','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2736428','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2736428',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','JP;US','JP','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2726096','Foreword Special Issue on the MARVEL Microreactor: Analysis, Design, Testing, and Applications','서문 마블 마이크로리액터의 특수 문제: 분석, 설계, 테스트 및 응용','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Abdalla Abou-Jaoude; John Jackson; Carlo Parisi; Mark Messner','2026-10-14','2026-10-14','2026-10-14','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','This special issue of Nuclear Technology focuses on the MARVEL (Microreactor Applications Research, Validation & Evaluation) project. Led by Idaho National Laboratory under the auspices of the U.S....','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726096','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2726096',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104786','Interfacial dissolution behavior of UO2 in carbonate-based groundwater environments','탄산염 기반 지하수 환경에서 UO2의 계면 용해 거동','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Chan-Yong Jung; Jeong Eun Kim; Hee-Kyung Kim; Wansik Cha; Sang-Ho Lee; Sang-Eun Bae','2026-10-14','','2026-10','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','ABSTRACT Understanding the dissolution behavior of UO 2 in carbonate-bearing groundwater is critical for predicting the long-term release of uranium from spent nuclear fuel in geological disposal environments. This study investigates the pH-dependent interfacial dissolution of UO 2 in these environments to identify distinct reaction regimes governed by surface chemistry. Two uranium oxide models with contrasting structural characteristics were examined: structurally disordered electrodeposited UO 2+x films and well-crystallized sintered UO 2 pellets exhibiting terrace-step morphologies. Dissolution processes were monitored using a combination of quartz crystal microbalance (QCM), atomic force microscopy (AFM), Raman spectroscopy, and inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry (ICP-MS). Both materials exhibit consistent biphasic dissolution kinetics, characterized by an initial rapid uranium release followed by a slower, steady-state regime. Dissolution is accelerated under mildly acidic carbonate conditions (pH 6.0) and suppressed under highly alkaline conditions (pH 12.0). Under representative groundwater conditions (pH 8.0), the UO 2 surface develops a relatively stable interfacial layer involving partial oxidation and surface-bound carbonates. These findings demonstrate that pH-controlled interfacial chemistry and initial defect density fundamentally dictate uranium dissolution, providing critical mechanistic insights for predicting radionuclide release in deep geological repositories.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104786','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104786',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104748','Health risk and dominant factors of indoor radon concentrations in Souq Al-Khamees and Ka''am, Libya','리비아 Souq Al-Khamees 및 Ka ''am의 실내 라돈 농도 건강 위험 및 지배적 요인','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','M.M. Al Bosta; A.M. Ismail; A. Okasha','2026-10-14','','2027-02','연구논문','안전·사고·리스크','This study assessed indoor 222Rn concentrations and their determinants in Souq Al-Khamees and Ka’am, Libya, to quantify public health risks and identify mitigation strategies. Passive dosimeters were deployed in 55 dwellings for 90 days. Multiple Linear Regression (MLR) with advanced feature engineering analyzed 17 variables, including functional transformations. Arithmetic Mean (AM) concentrations were 77 Bq/m³ in Souq Al-Khamees and 116 Bq/m³ in Ka’am. While geometric means (39 and 44 Bq/m³) reflect a stable regional background, WHO reference level exceedance rates reached 18.4% and 21.3%, respectively. The MLR model (R² = 0.692) identified the reciprocals of modified ventilation (1/(V+2)) and storey level (1/(S+2)) as the primary significant predictors. To address single-season sampling bias (March–June), a regional Mediterranean seasonal correction factor of 1.29 was integrated, showing that true annual exposures, Annual Effective Dose Equivalents (AEDE), and lifetime health risks exceed measured seasonal parameters. Consequently, 222Rn exposure increases estimated lifetime lung cancer risk for never-smokers to 16 and 20 per 1,000, respectively, escalating synergistically to 276 and 352 per 1,000 for current smokers. Increasing daily ventilation past 2–4 hours provides a critical, cost-effective regional mitigation strategy.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104748','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104748',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','EG;LY','EG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104775','Characterisation of Annular UO2 Pellets Fabricated Using Spark Plasma Sintering and Conventional Sintering','스파크 플라즈마 소결 및 기존 소결을 사용하여 제작된 환형 UO2 펠릿의 특성 분석','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Anil Prasad; Andrew Bergeron; Charles Liu; Victoria Szlachta; Reeghan Osmond; Lukas Bichler','2026-10-14','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','Internally and EXternally cooled Annular Fuel (IXAF) is a novel nuclear fuel concept that is being researched due to several advantages such as enhanced heat transfer, lower Peak Fuel Temperature (PFT), and lower fission gas release. The fuel concept has gained some momentum recently due to its enhanced accident tolerance. In this study the fabrication of IXAF by two different processing routes are compared. Spark Plasma Sintering (SPS) is a novel powder consolidation technique with good near net shaping ability as compared to Conventional Sintering (CS). This publication compares the results obtained from the characterisation of annular pellets fabricated from Spark Plasma Sintering to that from conventional sintering. The as-sintered pellets were characterised to compare their densities, dimensional change, microstructure, and grain size. The internal diameter of the as-sintered pellets was measured by a novel replicate technique and compared. Unexpectedly, the SPS technique proved to be a less viable alternative to CS in improving the near net shaping of the IXAF.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104775','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104775',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CA','CA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104785','Catalyzed deuterium fusion neutron source for the transmutation of minor actinides, production of tritium, and electrical power generation','부차적인 악티늄의 핵변환, 삼중수소 생산 및 전력 발전을 위한 촉매화된 중수소 융합 중성자 공급원','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','John Slough','2026-10-14','','2026-10','연구논문','열수력·유체','The accumulated inventory of spent nuclear fuel in the United States exceeds 90,000 metric tons, with long-term radiological hazards dominated by minor actinides that require isolation for thousands of years. This study details a possible solution to these challenges that also provides significant electrical power. The method employs a fusion system operating in catalyzed deuterium (Cat-D) mode producing the high neutron flux required for this task. It is based on the Compact Field Reversed Configuration Fusion Reactor (CFR2), where the plasma is sequentially compressed to fusion conditions remote from the burn chamber and then translated into the chamber surrounded by the fission blanket. A Monte Carlo neutronics analysis of a subcritical actinide transmutation blanket and the design was optimized. The optimized blanket employs FLiNaK eutectic fluoride salt enriched to 90% 6 Li and containing 17.53 mol% transuranic fluorides as the combined coolant, moderator, and fissile medium. The design achieves keff=0.9695 with a blanket volume of 13.4 m 3 . The FRC is pulsed at 4Hz with a tritium fraction of 4%, yielding a neutron flux of 4×10 18 n/s. This fission system burns 683 kg/yr of TRU, produces 9.6 kg/yr of tritium and 1,431 MWth, requiring only 17.5 MWe to power the CFR2.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104785','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104785',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115257','Numerical simulation and validation of submerged isothermal liquid metal jets','수중 등온 액체 금속 제트의 수치 시뮬레이션 및 검증','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Broderick Sieh; Artur Kucharewicz; Hitesh Bindra','2026-10-14','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','A key phenomenon under examination in liquid metal (LM) cooled nuclear reactors is the formation and evolution of submerged, axisymmetric, round LM jets in the upper plenum region, with particular emphasis on the influence of geometric configuration and density stratification on the development and stability of these flow structures. Experimentally, characterization of the optically opaque LM flow fields is performed using ultrasonic Doppler velocimetry (UDV). The primary objective of this study is to employ existing experimental data to validate computational models that can subsequently be used as predictive tools for simulating other LM coolant applications. Using computational fluid dynamics (CFD) software, the evolution of neutrally buoyant jets is analyzed and compared against theoretical descriptions. Unobstructed and obstructed inlet configurations are investigated over a range of injection flow rates and assessed relative to classical free-shear round jet theory. A modified k– ɛ turbulence model, with coefficients specifically calibrated for axisymmetric jet flows, is applied to characterize the behavior of confined pipe jets and obstructed LM jets over a range of inlet conditions, yielding results consistent with established empirical pipe jet correlations. For the Gallium Thermal–hydraulic Experiment (GaTE), good agreement between CFD predictions and theoretical expectations was obtained when reduced effective inlet diameters were adopted, as opposed to the assumptions of isothermal, unconfined round jet theory in an infinite domain. CFD models for obstructed jet flow were further validated experimentally in the presence of the upper internal structure (UIS) of the GaTE facility, with agreement demonstrated against the available experimental velocity measurements. The mean relative deviation between the experimental and computational results is determined to be less than 15%.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115257','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115257',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115271','Corrigendum to “Experiment Design for the Neutron Irradiation of PM-HIP alloys for nuclear reactors” [Nucl. Eng. Des. 402 (2023) 112114]','Corrigendum to “Experiment Design for the Neutron Irradiation of PM-HIP alloys for nuclear reactors” [Nucl. Eng. Des. 402 (2023) 112114]','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','D.P. Guillen; J.P. Wharry; G.K. Housley; C.D. Hale; J.V. Brookman; D.W. Gandy','2026-10-14','','2026-10','정오표','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115271','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115271',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112935','Effect of geometric protrusions and depressions on critical heat flux density of the heating surface','가열 표면의 임계 열속 밀도에 대한 기하학적 돌출부 및 함몰부의 영향','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zihao Wang; Yanxu Huang; Yunyu Qiu; Bin Tan; Byeongnam Jo; Jinbiao Xiong; Kai Wang','2026-10-14','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','In the “Melted Reactor Retention and External Pressure Vessel Cooling (IVR-ERVC)” strategy for nuclear power plants, the Critical Heat Flux (CHF) serves as the critical limit for ensuring pressure vessel integrity. Traditional safety assessment procedures rely on an ideal flat surface assumption, neglecting macroscopic irregularities caused by corrosion and manufacturing defects during long-term operation. To address this issue, this study systematically investigated the impact mechanism of macroscopic irregularities on CHF using a self-developed saturated pool boiling experimental system and high-speed imaging technology. Results demonstrate that as the system approaches boiling crisis, macroscopic convex and concave defects reduce average CHF by approximately 27.4% and 16.7%, respectively. Mechanism analysis demonstrates that concave defects form a “steam trap, ”the vapor retention is attributed primarily to triple-phase contact line (TPL) pinning at the sharp machined edges, leading to bubble retention and localized drying; whereas convex defects impede bubble detachment through “mechanical obstruction,” resulting in premature CHF. Once validated under conditions more representative of IVR-ERVC, a “surface degradation penalty coefficient” may be considered in future nuclear safety analyses as a possible conservative option.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112935','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112935',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;KR','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112921','Counterpart test for LSTF SBLOCA at the RPV upper head using ATLAS test facility','ATLAS 시험 시설을 사용하여 RPV 상부 헤드에서 LSTF SBLOCA에 대한 대응 시험','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yusun Park; Byoung-Uhn Bae; Jae Bong Lee; Jongrok Kim; Seok Cho; Kyoung-Ho Kang','2026-10-14','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study presents a comprehensive analysis of the OECD-ATLAS2 B5.1 test, the counterpart for the LSTF SB-PV-07 test. This test simulates a 1% small-break loss-of-coolant accident (SBLOCA) with the break at the reactor pressure vessel (RPV) upper head. The transient scenario considered a total failure of the high-pressure injection (HPI) system. But it incorporated the accident management (AM) actions to mitigate the accident and considered the inflow of non-condensable nitrogen gas from the accumulators following coolant depletion of accumulator (ACC). This test scenario is distinguished by its complex coolant distribution and depressurization characteristics compared to typical cold-leg break accident. This test was designed to investigate the thermal–hydraulic response of the ATLAS (Advanced Thermal-hydraulic Test Loop for Accident Simulation) facility compared to the LSTF test result. In addition to that, the effectiveness of the accident management actions considered in this test scenario was another objective of this study. From the test results, the ATLAS facility successfully reproduced the essential thermal–hydraulic phenomena that can be expected in the SBLOCA conditions including loop seal clearing (LSC) and core heat-up even though several differences were found with the LSTF test result. Critically, the study demonstrated that manual accident management actions − comprising manual HPI actuation and rapid secondary-side depressurization − effectively mitigated the accident progression and cooled down the system successfully even under the influence of non-condensable gases.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112921','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112921',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112917','A note on neutron point kinetics with delayed neutrons and prompt neutrons as separate populations','지연된 중성자 및 프롬프트 중성자를 별도의 모집단으로 사용하는 중성자 점 동역학에 대한 메모','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Zi Liang Tan','2026-10-14','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This note describes the development of a theory of point kinetics with delayed neutrons and prompt neutrons as separated populations. The separated point kinetics are demonstrated to be consistent with the original point kinetics, and are used in three novel applications to: (1) visualise the separate evolution timescales of the two neutron populations, (2) allow us to comment quantitatively on the ‘delayed neutron fraction’ versus ’relative yield’ definitions of the parameter β in favour of the latter, and (3) suggest a possible deficiency that the use of reactivity as a parameter may not be able to accurately model the true physical effects of perturbations to fission production.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112917','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112917',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','SG','SG','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106648','Radiological characterization for research reactor decommissioning: Application of lessons learned from the VVR-S reactor to the WWR-M facility','연구용 원자로 해체를 위한 방사선학적 특성 분석: VVR-S 원자로에서 얻은 교훈을 WWR-M 시설에 적용','Progress in Nuclear Energy','0149-1970','D. Gurau; Yu.M. Lobach; I.A. Maliuk','2026-10-13','','2027-01','연구논문','핵연료·재료','Radiological characterization is a key element of the decommissioning of any nuclear facility, providing the information required for dismantling planning, radiation protection, radioactive waste management, and final site release. This paper presents a characterization strategy developed for the decommissioning of the WWR-M research reactor in Ukraine, integrating historical records, radiological surveys, in situ measurements, laboratory analyses, activation assessments, and radionuclide inventory determination. The proposed approach covers three main stages of decommissioning: dismantling, radioactive waste management, and final cleaning of premises. Particular attention is given to the characterization of activated structures, contaminated systems and components, radioactive waste streams, and residual contamination in building materials. The methodology incorporates lessons learned from the successful decommissioning of the VVR-S research reactor in Romania, including activation assessment, dose-rate mapping, radionuclide inventory determination, and waste classification. By combining direct measurements with analytical and modelling techniques, the proposed program provides the information necessary for safe and efficient decommissioning implementation while reducing uncertainties and optimizing characterization efforts. The approach may serve as a practical framework for other research reactors undergoing decommissioning.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106648','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pnucene.2026.106648',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','RO;UA','UA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1080/00295450.2026.2740309','Coriolis Force and Inclination Angle Influences of MHD Flow Over a Spinning Plate Using bvp4c and ANN Prediction','코리올리 힘 및 경사각은 bvp4c 및 ANN 예측을 사용하여 회전 플레이트를 통한 MHD 흐름의 영향','Nuclear Technology','0029-5450','Mohammed Almakki; Shweta Mishra; Wuriti Sridhar; Muhammad Imran Khan; Mohammed El Khider; Gurram Dharmaiah','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','연구논문','열수력·유체','Rotating heat-exchanger surfaces, disc-type cooling systems, and inclined rotating machinery in industrial processes require accurate prediction of heat and mass transfer under combined electromagnetic and rotational effects, a problem that has not previously been addressed in a single unified model together with a fast prediction tool. This study investigates the electro-magnetohydrodynamic flow of a rotating Newtonian nanofluid over an inclined, spinning stretching sheet, incorporating Coriolis force, Lorentz force, viscous dissipation, Joule heating, and a heat source/sink, together with Brownian motion and thermophoresis. This combination of effects is directly representative of rotating heat-exchanger and disc-cooling configurations, where inclination and rotation act simultaneously and cannot be modeled independently. Coriolis force and the surface inclination angle are incorporated into the Navier–Stokes equations governing the flow, and the resulting system of partial differential equations is reduced, via a suitable similarity transformation, to a system of ordinary differential equations, which is solved using the bvp4c solver in MATLAB. The adaptability, robustness, and precision of this method make it an effective tool for addressing such fluid-flow problems. The effects of the Coriolis force, surface inclination angle, heat generation, Prandtl number, and Grashof number on the temperature, concentration, and velocity fields are examined in detail. The present results show highly satisfactory agreement with existing published results. The numerical (bvp4c) results are further used to train an artificial neural network (ANN) model, enabling near-instant prediction of key engineering quantities—skin friction, Nusselt number, and Sherwood number without repeated numerical solution of the governing equations; the ANN predictions show excellent agreement with the bvp4c results. The findings of this study are directly applicable to the design of cooling systems for large industrial machinery and consumer electronics such as laptops and cellphones, as well as to rotating heat-exchanger and disc-cleaning applications, food processing, and other rotating-machinery systems where nanofluid-based cooling is employed.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2740309','https://doi.org/10.1080/00295450.2026.2740309',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','AE;IN;PK','IN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02053-7','Development and optimization analysis of the cryogenic automatic sample changer for neutron scattering at CSNS','CSN에서 중성자 산란을 위한 극저온 자동 시료 교환기 개발 및 최적화 분석','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Ji-Xin Chen; Bo Bai; Fa-Liang Cheng; Yuan Sun; Hui Cheng; Bao Yuan; Meng-Jia Dou; Chen-Yang Wang; Quan Lin; Zi-Cong Lu; Lin-Jin Deng; Xin Tong; Hai-Tao Hu','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02053-7','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02053-7',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02055-5','Design of a Lamb-shift polarimeter for pulsed high-intensity polarized H$$^+$$/D$$^+$$ ion sources','펄스 고강도 편광 H $ $ ^ + $ $/D $ $ ^ + $ $ 이온 소스를 위한 램 시프트 편광계 설계','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Yao-Jie Zhai; Sheng Zhang; Bo-Xing Gou; Xue-Zhen Zhang; Yu-Guo Liu; Qian-Yu Jin; Liang-Ting Sun','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','연구논문','설계·운전·경제','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02055-5','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02055-5',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1007/s41365-026-02067-1','Design and offline test of a dual MCP time-of-flight detector with forward–backward secondary electron collection for isochronous mass spectrometry at HIAF-SRing','HIAF-SRING에서 등시성 질량 분석을 위한 전후 2차 전자를 수집하는 이중 MCP 비행 시간 검출기의 설계 및 오프라인 테스트','Nuclear Science and Techniques','1001-8042','Hong-Yang Jiao; Chao-Yi Fu; Meng Wang; Xing Xu; Hong-Fu Li; Jia-Hao Lv; Min Zhang; Xin-Liang Yan; Qi Zeng; Wen-Jia Huang; Rui-Jiu Chen; Ming-Ze Sun; Min Si; Peng Shuai; Qian Wang; Yuan-Ming Xing; Yu-Hu Zhang; Xiao-Hong Zhou; Xu Zhou; Zu-Yi Chen; Ting Liao; Yin-Fang Luo; Jin-Yang Shi; Yu-Nan Song; Yue Yu','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','2026-10-13','연구논문','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02067-1','https://doi.org/10.1007/s41365-026-02067-1',0,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;HK','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104767','Trap-Assisted Carrier Loss and Transient Signal Degradation in Diamond Radiation Detectors','다이아몬드 방사선 검출기의 트랩 지원 캐리어 손실 및 과도 신호 저하','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Hongyun Wang; Wuqi Chen; Shengyi Hao; Baowen Tian; Long Fan; Yu Zhao; Yuheng She; Hanwen Zhang; Wenyi Shao; Xiaochuan Xia; Hongwei Liang','2026-10-13','','2026-10','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Diamond radiation detectors are promising for neutron and charged-particle detection owing to their radiation hardness, fast charge collection, and stability in harsh environments. However, traps introduced during growth, fabrication, irradiation, or long-term operation can act as trapping and recombination centers, causing transient signal degradation that remains insufficiently quantified. This work incorporates traps into an SRIM–TCAD–Garfield++ multi-physics framework to model trap-driven degradation in planar diamond detectors. The framework couples charged-particle energy deposition, electric-field-dependent carrier transport, trap-assisted capture and recombination, and Shockley–Ramo-induced current calculation. Furthermore, we construct an effective-lifetime model to evaluate effects of trap concentration, capture cross-section, and bias voltage. Results show that a strong-capture trap causes the transient response to evolve from a plateau-like waveform into a spike-like waveform as its concentration increases from 0.1 to 1000 ppm, decreasing signal duration from ∼9 ns to 0.5 ns. In contrast, a weak-capture trap barely distorts waveform collapse over the same concentration range, indicating trap density alone cannot determine signal degradation. Increasing the applied bias partially compensates for carrier loss by shortening transit time and suppressing diffusion, but this compensation becomes limited when trapping dominates. These results guide trap tolerance evaluation and bias optimization in diamond radiation detectors.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104767','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104767',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115247','Assessment of sensitivity methodologies for a pressurized and depressurized loss of forced cooling in the high temperature gas-cooled test reactor','고온 가스 냉각 시험 원자로에서 강제 냉각의 가압 및 감압 손실에 대한 감도 방법론 평가','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Jonathan L. Barthle; Robert F. Kile; Nicholas R. Brown','2026-10-13','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','The goal of this study is to perform a preliminary assessment of loss of forced cooling events in the High Temperature Gas-cooled Test Reactor (HTGR-TR). This assessment is a demonstration of a sensitivity analysis framework that can be readily built upon. The framework employed two different sensitivity methodologies to highlight the necessity and benefits of including multiple metrics by comparing the predicted coefficients. An analysis will be performed for both a pressurized loss of forced cooling (PLOFC) and a depressurized loss of forced cooling (DLOFC). In both cases, the study will include the subsequent conduction cooldown in the reactor core. In particular, we will focus on a small, non-exhaustive, group of thermal properties within the HTGR-TR. The sensitivity study was used to exemplify how the framework can help determine which thermal properties have the most impact on the transient peak fuel temperature and 8-day (“late stage”) coolant outlet temperature. This study will include the calculation of both non-variance-based sensitivity coefficients and moment-independent Delta indices through the use of Monte Carlo sampling to compare the findings of both methodologies. An envelope of predicted fuel temperatures was generated through the sampling of the parameters during the sensitivity study. A peak fuel temperature of approximately 1500 K was predicted for both the PLOFC and DLOFC. The peak temperature was dominated by steady-state conditions, resulting in the same peak temperature for both transients. After the onset of both transients, a subsequent peak temperature was observed to be 1300 K for the PLOFC and 1400 K for the DLOFC. The fuel temperature did not exceed the steady-state temperatures during either transient. In both the PLOFC and DLOFC, the coolant inlet temperature and thermal conductivity were identified as most important for the transient fuel temperature. The Delta indices also identified these parameters as important with respect to the transient fuel temperature distribution. For example, the thermal conductivity had a Delta index of 0.28 and 0.5 for the PLOFC and DLOFC, respectively. In addition, an analysis of the 8-day coolant outlet temperature indicated a shift in parameter importance between the PLOFC and DLOFC with respect to nominal coolant pressure and moderator thermal conductivity. For example, a vastly differing Delta index of 0.1 and 0.7 was computed for the thermal conductivity during PLOFC and DLOFC, respectively. Discrepancies between the sensitivity studies highlight the potential strengths and weaknesses of different sensitivity approaches, emphasizing the value of including different methodologies during sensitivity analyses.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115247','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115247',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112929','Neutron activation analysis at the Moroccan TRIGA MARK II reactor: state of the art, methodological advances, applications and future perspectives','모로코 TRIGA MARK II 원자로에서의 중성자 활성화 분석: 최첨단 기술, 방법론적 진보, 응용 및 미래 관점','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Iliasse Aarab; Hamid Bounouira; Hamid Amsil; Abdelwahab Badague; Abedessamad Didi; Fouad Taous','2026-10-13','','2027-02','리뷰·관점','원자로물리·해석','Neutron Activation Analysis (NAA) is a powerful nuclear analytical technique widely used for multi-elemental characterization due to its high sensitivity, accuracy, and non-destructive nature. This review provides a comprehensive synthesis of studies conducted at the Moroccan TRIGA MARK II research reactor (CNESTEN), highlighting the applications and methodological advances of Instrumental Neutron Activation Analysis (INAA). Environmental monitoring, food safety, medicinal plant analysis, and geochemical investigations emerge as the main application domains. The implementation of the k 0 -standardization method has significantly improved analytical performance and reproducibility. In parallel, the development of Prompt Gamma Neutron Activation Analysis (PGNAA), currently in a simulation-based phase, is discussed as a strategic extension of analytical capabilities. The integration of INAA and PGNAA is expected to enable a complementary analytical platform for both trace-level and real-time bulk analysis.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112929','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112929',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','MA','MA','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112939','Measurement of the Zr-90(n, 2n) Zr-89 reaction cross section using fast neutron spectrum at the Tehran Research reactor (TRR)','Tehran Research reactor (TRR) 에서 고속 중성자 스펙트럼을 이용한 Zr-90 (n, 2n) Zr-89 반응 단면 측정','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','S.M. Mohammadi; S. Bagheri; H. Khalafi; R. Khodabakhsh','2026-10-13','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Accurate determination of threshold neutron-induced reaction cross sections at relatively high threshold energies is of fundamental importance for nuclear model development and practical applications in physics. In addition, the evaluation and re-evaluation of such cross sections are relevant to ongoing efforts to improve the prompt fission neutron spectra of U-235 and U-238 within the IAEA CIELO project. In this work, the reaction cross sections of natural zirconium isotopes were investigated, with particular emphasis on the threshold reaction Zr-90(n,2n) Zr-89, which has a threshold energy above 10 MeV, in the neutron spectrum of the Tehran Research Reactor. Zirconium and monitor foils were irradiated in an irradiation box located in the reactor core. After an appropriate cooling period, the induced activities of the irradiated samples were measured using a high-purity germanium detector. To accurately estimate the neutron flux on the foils, the reactor core was modeled using the MCNPX code while accounting for burnup effects. The calculated foil reaction rates were then compared with the experimental values to validate the computed neutron flux. The spectrum-averaged cross section of the Zr-90(n,2n) Zr-89 reaction was measured to be 1.73 × 10 −5 barn with an uncertainty of 11%. The corresponding spectrum-averaged cross sections for the Zr-94(n,γ) Zr-95 and Zr-96(n,γ)Zr-97 reactions were 4.18 × 10 −2 and 8.04 × 10 −2 barn, respectively.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112939','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112939',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112908','Experimental investigation of central blockages in a narrow rectangular channel using PIV: comparative study of square and diamond blockages','PIV를 이용한 좁은 직사각형 통로의 중심 막힘에 대한 실험적 조사: 사각형 및 다이아몬드 막힘에 대한 비교 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Dongdong Yuan; Zheng Cong; Feng Qiu; Xiangyu Yun; Huiyong Zhang; Sichao Tan','2026-10-13','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','This study investigates the flow characteristics in a rectangular channel with center square and diamond blockages ( α =30%) at varying Reynolds numbers ( Re = 1268 – 4438) using particle image velocimetry (PIV). Time-averaged analysis, turbulence statistics, and proper orthogonal decomposition (POD) were employed to examine the effects of blockage geometry on vortex evolution and turbulent kinetic energy dissipation. Key findings demonstrate that the diamond blockage induces localized high-vorticity zones due to its sharp vertices, resulting in stronger vortex cores. In contrast, the square blockage triggers flow stagnation due to its right-angled geometry, exhibiting broader turbulent kinetic energy dissipation and imposing stronger disturbances on the wake fluid. POD analysis and flow field reconstruction confirm the periodic vortex shedding in both blockage conditions. The present results can provide effective experimental data for blockage accident simulations of plate-type fuel assemblies.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112908','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112908',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112875','Enabling long-cycle, high-burnup light water SMRs with LEU+ fuel: A coupled core and fuel performance comparison of boron free and borated designs','LEU + 연료로 장주기, 고연소 경수 SMR 활성화: 붕소 무함유 및 붕소 설계의 결합 코어 및 연료 성능 비교','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Chansoo Lee; Jooil Yoon; Youho Lee','2026-10-13','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Recent development of the LEU+ fuel supply chain enables new pathways to extend discharge burnup in light water SMRs, whose burnup is often reactivity-limited due to high neutron leakage. This study investigates LEU+ fueled core concepts for an i-SMR-based SMR with the objective of reducing annual spent fuel assembly discharge by approximately 30 % relative to the reference i-SMR with U-235 enrichment below 5 %, which corresponds to extending the cycle length from 730 to 1043 EFPD while maintaining the same number of feed fuel assemblies. Two variants are designed and assessed: a soluble-boron-free (SBF) core and a soluble-boron-used (SBU) core. For the SBF design, increased reliance on burnable absorbers and control rods motivates adoption of a 17 × 17 assembly with 28 guide tubes and 1 instrumentation tube, together with multiple IGD absorber options including enriched gadolinium configurations. Although a carefully designed shuffling scheme in the SBF core can effectively mitigate hoop stresses, control rod-driven axial depletion non-uniformity increases the peak nodal burnup to 80 MWd/kgU at rod average burnup below 65 MWd/kgU, accelerating fission gas release and rod internal pressure at high local burnup. In the SBU design, soluble boron provides cycle-long global reactivity control, reducing reliance on control rod insertion, yielding more uniform depletion behavior with moderated peak nodal burnup and fuel performance trends. Overall, the results support the technical viability of LEU+ for long-cycle SMR from the standpoint of neutronics and fuel performance under normal operation; however, the SBF implementation may induce increasing control rod-induced depletion non-uniformity when pursuing additional burnup extension beyond the burnup levels evaluated in this study (65 MWd/kgU).','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112875','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112875',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112931','A Geant4 based study of the response of surface barrier detector for alpha-particles','알파 입자에 대한 표면 장벽 검출기의 반응에 대한 Geant4 기반 연구','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Mishel Nasir; Rubina Nasir; Shakeel Mahmood; Sikander M. Mirza','2026-10-13','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','This study presents a Geant4 based comprehensive characterization of a silicon Surface Barrier Detector (SBD) for charged particle spectroscopy, with a specific focus on alpha particle detection. This work investigates the fundamental properties governing detector response, including the Bragg curve, Range and absolute detection efficiency. The Geant4 simulated Bragg curves have been found in good agreement with the corresponding TCAD-SRIM based data. For the 1–10 MeV domain of energy values of α-Particles, the Range in Silicon is found to exhibit a quadratic behavior. The Geant4 simulated absolute efficiency of SBD in parallel, coaxial source–detector configuration has been found in agreement with the corresponding experimental data. The Geant4 simulated absolute efficiency data has also been found in good agreement with the corresponding numerical/theoretical values for various values of source dimensions and for various values of source-to-detector axial distances. The Geant4 based absolute efficiency values show a gradual decrease with increasing radial displacement for fixed value of axial distance.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112931','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112931',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','PK','PK','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104744','High-energy field-of-view completion in dual-source dual-energy CT using measurement-conditioned frequency-decoupled learning','측정 컨디셔닝된 주파수 디커플러닝 학습을 사용한 듀얼 소스 듀얼 에너지 CT에서의 고에너지 시야 완성','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Sanghyun Cho; Woosung Kim; Hyosung Cho','2026-10-12','','2027-02','연구논문','방사선·계측','This study proposes a measurement-conditioned framework for high-energy field-of-view (FOV) completion in dual-source dual-energy computed tomography (DECT). The model uses a full-FOV low-energy image, a measured central high-energy seed, and its support mask, while hard data consistency preserves the measured seed. A frequency-decoupled objective combines image-domain reconstruction, high-frequency adversarial supervision, and wavelet-based low-frequency attenuation constraints. Because true high-energy references are unavailable outside the physical high-energy FOV, a controlled seed–halo setting was used by withholding an annular region within the measured FOV for paired supervision and evaluation. Leave-one-patient-out experiments were conducted on thoracoabdominal DECT data from three patients. In the held-out halo, the proposed method achieved the lowest MAE and RMSE of 28.56 ± 6.23 HU and 40.86 ± 8.32 HU, respectively, and the highest SSIM of 0.9420 ± 0.0220 among the evaluated methods. It also more closely reproduced tissue-specific HU values and local intensity variation. In virtual monoenergetic imaging, it achieved the lowest MAE at all evaluated energies. Although true outer-FOV accuracy could not be directly validated, the results support the feasibility of the proposed approach for high-energy FOV completion and downstream spectral imaging.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104744','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104744',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','KR','KR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.net.2026.104781','Corrigendum to “Evaluation of dose distribution from 12C ion in radiation therapy by FLUKA code” [NUCL ENG TECHNOL 52 (2020) 2410-2414]','Corrigendum to “FLUKA 코드에 의한 방사선 치료에서 12C 이온으로부터의 선량 분포 평가” [NUCL ENG TECHNOL 52 (2020) 2410-2414]','Nuclear Engineering and Technology','1738-5733','Jamshid Soltani-Nabipour; Abdollah Khorshidi; Faezeh Shojai','2026-10-12','','2026-10','정오표','방사선·계측','','','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104781','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.net.2026.104781',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','IR','IR','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115267','Onset of flooding data at variable pressure in a large diameter tube for air-water and saturated steam-water fluid pairs','공기-물 및 포화 증기-물 유체 쌍에 대한 대직경 튜브의 가변 압력에서 홍수 데이터의 시작','Nuclear Engineering and Design','0029-5493','Karen Vierow Kirkland; Nicholas Wynne; David Aumiller','2026-10-12','','2026-12','연구논문','열수력·유체','An experimental investigation to acquire flooding data for steam-water and air-water fluid pairs in a large-diameter vertical tube at above-atmospheric pressures has been conducted. The experimental program presented herein is the first to use a single test section with controlled boundary conditions for these pairs in a large-diameter vertical tube, enabling consistent comparisons of flooding characteristics. Many data exist for air-water flooding in annular flow within a large-diameter vertical tube and at various pressures. Steam-water flows are of interest for reactor applications, but insufficient data are available to enable reliable analysis. Evaluation of the effect of the fluid pair is performed to understand the applicability of the air-water data to steam-water applications. The pressure range was investigated by obtaining data at nominal pressures of 0.1, 0.2, 0.3 and 0.4 MPa (0, 15, 30 and 45 psig) for air-water and steam-water flow conditions. Water subcooling was minimized to the extent possible in the steam-water tests to reduce the effect of phase change and permit a more level comparison with the air-water data. All data reported herein were taken at the onset of flooding, that is, conditions when flow reversal of the liquid phase first occurs. Flooding characteristics are presented in terms of the dimensionless Kutateladze parameter. The saturated steam-water flooding data over the pressure range closely trend with the air-water data.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115267','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2026.115267',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','US','US','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112884','The effect of pulsating liquid sodium coolant inlets on flow structures and thermal mixing in a T-junction','T-접합부에서 액체 소듐 냉각제 유입구를 유동 구조 및 열 혼합에 맥동시키는 효과','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ayodeji A. Ala; John Njoroge; Oluwaseun Talabi; Junjie Mao; Bin Ye','2026-10-12','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Mixing of two pipe streams at different temperatures features in the secondary circuit of compact sodium-cooled fast reactors. This study presents the numerical simulation of flow features and mixing characteristics in the T-junction with the inlets subjected to co-pulsating and out-of-phase pulsating flows over a 4-s flow cycle. The main and branch pipe inlets are subjected to sine-sine and sine-cosine velocity variations. The momentum ratio is constant (3.57) in the first case, but varies between 1.73 and 7.38 in the second. The velocity magnitude profile in both cases gradually recovers to its pre-mixing shape after the T-junction; however, the profiles differ between the two half-cycles in Case 2. Turbulence intensity varied more in the upper part than in the lower part of the main pipe. The 90 o out-of-phase pulsating flow at the inlet resulted in increased temperature and turbulence intensity fluctuations along the flow axis. Momentum interactions dominate thermal mixing in the upper part of the pipe, while the lower half is dominated by gradual convection in the shear layers. The lower temperature mixing degree in 75% of the flow cross-section and 20% reduction in the temperature difference at the outlet show that more thermal mixing was achieved in Case 2. The 90° out-of-phase difference between the mixing inlets also causes the position of the thermal fluctuation to be momentarily away from the wall, which has implications for the extent of damage expected at the junction.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112884','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112884',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN;BJ','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112887','Development of an equivalent homogenization method with anisotropic scattering few-group constants in the RMC code','RMC 코드에서 이방성 산란 소집단 상수를 갖는 동등한 균질화 방법의 개발','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Yaodong Li; Dacai Zhang; Peng‑Fei Shen; Ganglin Yu; Kan Wang','2026-10-12','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','The Legendre expansion, widely adopted for representing anisotropic scattering in Monte Carlo multi-group cross section generation, suffers from truncation artifacts that can lead to negative scattering cross sections. This paper develops an angle-discretized macroscopic scattering matrix representation, generated by direct track-length tallying during continuous-energy Monte Carlo transport and used as the working representation throughout a complete Monte Carlo two-step workflow in the Reactor Monte Carlo code RMC. The representation is non-negative by construction across all angular bins, avoiding the negative scattering cross sections that arise from Legendre truncation. Supporting engineering elements required for the complete workflow—including a full-core tallying scheme that mitigates environmental-effect errors associated with reflective single-assembly boundary conditions, and a Monte Carlo–adapted SPH iteration for use within the workflow—are also described. The methodology is validated on a PWR assembly, a MOX fuel assembly with control-rod insertion and withdrawal, a four-assembly mini-core, and the C5G7 benchmark. Reference solutions are obtained from continuous-energy RMC simulations, and the angle-discretized scattering matrices are compared against OpenMC Legendre-expansion results to illustrate the non-negativity property of the proposed representation. Key results include a reduction of the mini-core eigenvalue deviation from approximately 600 pcm under reflective-boundary group constants to 6 pcm under full-core group constants.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112887','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112887',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112926','Development and validation of the premixing-phase model in the three-dimensional fuel–coolant interaction code SEINA-3D','3차원 연료 냉각수 상호 작용 코드 SEINA-3D에서 프리믹싱 단계 모델의 개발 및 검증','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Ruiyu Sun; Qianxi Xiao; Ronghua Chen; Kui Zhang; Wenxi Tian','2026-10-12','','2027-02','연구논문','열수력·유체','Premixing during a fuel–coolant interaction determines the three-dimensional melt–water–vapor state available to a subsequent steam explosion. This study develops and validates the premixing-phase model of the three-dimensional fuel–coolant interaction code SEINA-3D. The model advances five coupled Eulerian material fields—liquid coolant, vapor, connected melt jet, melt droplets, and melt fragments—in one pressure-based framework. Mixed finite-volume/finite-difference discretization, explicit/implicit advancement, and improved SIMPLEPC pressure coupling form the numerical core; VOF–PLIC interface geometry and continuum-surface-force capillarity resolve the connected interfaces; and interphase exchange, breakup, and phase-change closures couple the fields. The Ransom faucet problem, SPHERIC Test 2, and a three-dimensional rising-bubble benchmark verify the transport, free-surface, and capillary treatments, while FARO L-24 validates the complete model under prototypical corium–water conditions. On the finest SPHERIC grid, the median NRMSE is 0.159 over the four water-level records and 0.139 over the eight pressure records, and the first P1 impact amplitude is reproduced within 10.2 %. The rising-bubble calculation preserves the gas volume and reproduces the published centroid, velocity, sphericity, and directional-size endpoints to within 5 %. In the 15-point FARO pressure comparison, the steam-only calculation has an RMSE of about 0.18 MPa and reproduces the approximately 2.2 MPa peak near 1.6 s; adding the reported L-24 hydrogen source raises the late-time pressure by about 0.48 MPa and quantifies the coupled sensitivity of the steam, noncondensable-gas, and headspace closures. The calculation also yields the material inventories, energy partition, void, azimuthal asymmetry, and a debris-size distribution consistent with the post-test recovery. These results establish the premixing capability of SEINA-3D and provide three-dimensional mixture states for steam-explosion load analysis.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112926','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112926',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
INSERT INTO "papers" VALUES('10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112909','A Bayesian regularized MLEM hybrid approach for reactor fast-neutron spectrum adjustment','원자로 고속 중성자 스펙트럼 조정을 위한 베이지안 정규 MLEM 하이브리드 접근법','Annals of Nuclear Energy','0306-4549','Cong Liu; Laiming Wang; Yixue Chen; Bin Zhang','2026-10-12','','2027-02','연구논문','원자로물리·해석','Precise characterization of the fast-neutron energy spectrum constitutes a fundamental requirement for evaluating radiation damage in reactor pressure vessels (RPV). Conventional MLEM iterative adjustment algorithms applied to high-precision spectrum adjustment often result in potential spectral artifacts due to the inability to rigorously propagate off-diagonal covariance terms. A novel Bayesian Regularized Maximum Likelihood Expectation Maximization (BR-MLEM) framework is proposed to address these challenges by integrating hierarchical Bayesian priors with adaptive regularization. This methodology systematically incorporates covariance matrices associated with the prior spectrum, response functions, and measurements, employing singular value decomposition (SVD)-based Monte Carlo sampling to mitigate noise amplification. Application to the H. B. Robinson Unit 2 benchmark demonstrates the algorithm’s capability to produce physically consistent spectra while effectively suppressing non-physical distortions observed in standard MLEM iterations. The adjusted calculated specific activity exhibits excellent agreement with experimental dosimetry data, achieving consistency comparable to generalized least-squares methods but with superior stability in high-energy regions. Posterior uncertainty analysis reveals a significant reduction in relative standard deviations across primary fast-neutron energy groups. These findings confirm that the BR-MLEM framework enhances the fidelity of fluence estimation and provides a robust tool for RPV lifetime management.','OpenAlex','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112909','https://doi.org/10.1016/j.anucene.2026.112909',1,'2026-10-18','2026-10-19','active','Crossref + OpenAlex','CN','CN','OpenAlex authorship institutions');
